ercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/6298a60f15f9d5ea4048736fe65bf836f19824fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:07:48Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:07:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: warn when advertised ssrRemoteEntry is missing from emit (#507)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Why\n\nUpstream `@module-federation/vite` had a crash class (vite#1403, fixed\nin 1.23.2): `mf-manifest.json` advertised `metaData.ssrRemoteEntry`\nafter a client-only `vite build` even when no SSR entry was emitted. An\nSSR host that prefers that field then fails at runtime. Stale output\ndirs can produce the same state with any plugin version.\n\nmfdoctor previously parsed and checked only `metaData.remoteEntry`.\nPutting that SSR case on the existing **error** rule would fail CI for\nevery client-only `@module-federation/vite` <1.23.2 producer (including\nthe examples pinned at 1.22.1), even though CSR hosts never load\n`ssrRemoteEntry`.\n\n## What\n\n- Parse `metaData.ssrRemoteEntry` (same `{ name, path, type? }` shape as\n`remoteEntry`) into manifest facts.\n- Keep **`artifact/manifest-remote-entry-missing`** (`error`) exactly as\non main: client `remoteEntry` only.\n- Add **`artifact/manifest-ssr-remote-entry-missing`** (`warning`) when\nthat SSR entry is advertised but absent from collected emit.\n- Keep host manifests with an empty `remoteEntry` object silent, as\nbefore.\n\n## False-positive guards (SSR rule)\n\nThe client `remoteEntry` check stays scoped to the manifest’s own output\nso another directory cannot satisfy it. `ssrRemoteEntry` is searched\nacross **all collected** `emittedAssets`, `assetSizes`, and per-build\nemit lists. The SSR warning stays silent when:\n\n- emit evidence is missing (`capabilities.emittedAssets` is false),\n- the manifest exposes no modules (consumer-only host; nobody loads this\ncontainer’s SSR entry),\n- or this is a Nitro/Nuxt dual-env app and no **server output root** has\nbeen collected yet (`.output/server`, `.nuxt/dist/server`, Nitro’s\n`node_modules/.nitro/vite/services/ssr`). Vite client closes often\nrecord `targetKind=node` from default `ssr.target` while writing\n`.output/public`; that is not treated as the SSR environment.\n\nA split `dist/client` + `dist/server` (or Nitro public/server) layout\nthat the doctor actually collected does not fire. After a server output\nroot is collected, a missing SSR entry is reported as a warning.\n\nRemediation mentions cleaning/rebuilding, building the SSR environment,\nand upgrading `@module-federation/vite` to `>=1.23.2` when\n`metaData.pluginVersion` looks like the 1.x Vite plugin below that.\n\nClient-only Vite producer examples keep the client `remoteEntry` error.\nThe new SSR rule is a warning, so those cells do not need a suppression\n(default CI `failOn` is `error`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- (a) `ssrRemoteEntry` present and emitted → no finding\n- (b) advertised on a client-only **producer** emit → SSR warning;\nclient `remoteEntry` rule stays quiet\n- (c) emitted in a separate server output the doctor collected → no\nfinding\n- (d) manifest without `ssrRemoteEntry` → unchanged `remoteEntry`\nbehavior\n- consumer-only host advertising `ssrRemoteEntry` → no finding\n- missing emit capability → no finding\n- Nitro client close (`targetKind=node` on `.output/public`) → silent;\nafter `.output/server` with no SSR asset → warning\n\nNo version bump / publish. Changeset included because this is a\nuser-visible rule change. Do not merge until CI is green.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-9ce34619-f370-53f9-9943-e14f6a8f933f?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-9ce34619-f370-53f9-9943-e14f6a8f933f&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"224058ba1c1ff04074956029f4a6298c331743f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/224058ba1c1ff04074956029f4a6298c331743f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/6298a60f15f9d5ea4048736fe65bf836f19824fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 224058ba1c1ff04074956029f4a6298c331743f3\nparent e8fe4e34bdf91c6e026d8602842c8165c028a1fb\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1791191268 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791191268 +0200\n\nfix: warn when advertised ssrRemoteEntry is missing from emit (#507)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Why\n\nUpstream `@module-federation/vite` had a crash class (vite#1403, fixed\nin 1.23.2): `mf-manifest.json` advertised `metaData.ssrRemoteEntry`\nafter a client-only `vite build` even when no SSR entry was emitted. An\nSSR host that prefers that field then fails at runtime. Stale output\ndirs can produce the same state with any plugin version.\n\nmfdoctor previously parsed and checked only `metaData.remoteEntry`.\nPutting that SSR case on the existing **error** rule would fail CI for\nevery client-only `@module-federation/vite` <1.23.2 producer (including\nthe examples pinned at 1.22.1), even though CSR hosts never load\n`ssrRemoteEntry`.\n\n## What\n\n- Parse `metaData.ssrRemoteEntry` (same `{ name, path, type? }` shape as\n`remoteEntry`) into manifest facts.\n- Keep **`artifact/manifest-remote-entry-missing`** (`error`) exactly as\non main: client `remoteEntry` only.\n- Add **`artifact/manifest-ssr-remote-entry-missing`** (`warning`) when\nthat SSR entry is advertised but absent from collected emit.\n- Keep host manifests with an empty `remoteEntry` object silent, as\nbefore.\n\n## False-positive guards (SSR rule)\n\nThe client `remoteEntry` check stays scoped to the manifest’s own output\nso another directory cannot satisfy it. `ssrRemoteEntry` is searched\nacross **all collected** `emittedAssets`, `assetSizes`, and per-build\nemit lists. The SSR warning stays silent when:\n\n- emit evidence is missing (`capabilities.emittedAssets` is false),\n- the manifest exposes no modules (consumer-only host; nobody loads this\ncontainer’s SSR entry),\n- or this is a Nitro/Nuxt dual-env app and no **server output root** has\nbeen collected yet (`.output/server`, `.nuxt/dist/server`, Nitro’s\n`node_modules/.nitro/vite/services/ssr`). Vite client closes often\nrecord `targetKind=node` from default `ssr.target` while writing\n`.output/public`; that is not treated as the SSR environment.\n\nA split `dist/client` + `dist/server` (or Nitro public/server) layout\nthat the doctor actually collected does not fire. After a server output\nroot is collected, a missing SSR entry is reported as a warning.\n\nRemediation mentions cleaning/rebuilding, building the SSR environment,\nand upgrading `@module-federation/vite` to `>=1.23.2` when\n`metaData.pluginVersion` looks like the 1.x Vite plugin below that.\n\nClient-only Vite producer examples keep the client `remoteEntry` error.\nThe new SSR rule is a warning, so those cells do not need a suppression\n(default CI `failOn` is `error`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- (a) `ssrRemoteEntry` present and emitted → no finding\n- (b) advertised on a client-only **producer** emit → SSR warning;\nclient `remoteEntry` rule stays quiet\n- (c) emitted in a separate server output the doctor collected → no\nfinding\n- (d) manifest without `ssrRemoteEntry` → unchanged `remoteEntry`\nbehavior\n- consumer-only host advertising `ssrRemoteEntry` → no finding\n- missing emit capability → no finding\n- Nitro client close (`targetKind=node` on `.output/public`) → silent;\nafter `.output/server` with no SSR asset → warning\n\nNo version bump / publish. Changeset included because this is a\nuser-visible rule change. Do not merge until CI is green.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-9ce34619-f370-53f9-9943-e14f6a8f933f?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-9ce34619-f370-53f9-9943-e14f6a8f933f&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2jkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAgsQAD59TI0MQrHyPFvsqtyeA9W/\nfwNmgHoqkRpfCmHx0XBYwPyczCw5Op2VhEWx6xj+O7fNFgHm8oT85kmRYSDkhPWP\ntLa7aOJy7Oqgx/UOoT8woG+hl6RNLcQQQemVpY3O6uihmd+sjcQmlojoLZX7ZGN3\nVntEbxjXciyo1l70nqYEdArw+Lwvv592boxuRaaXrh1LBCh1QEC9VLpcPds/NZId\nM9xE/O3Lvq+WzpugAVUJG3O9vAzcm8LeWxCB+u3T6xtqCIY3TpJ1r6YMsBlz1i3F\nsMv6Ouiexdi2oikY4BHFpULMIn2SxCnfkfkVn+oQgaiBJfqeyDiNJ6kr4CipZ/mp\nkGil2zF5promenAY7lYnXzIecJwjMrFudsRcGZKjFPQx5aS5Pl21ykZCqW3fwuJ8\n1Ltas76dOCyQiqkvomwUDqFwiD6QRZgjp7csHxY6J56rJbva+dANKS8ySDqpN/WE\n2rF0S4Hw0rf7uEUK/Z7xW1iM9whf8Q0q3zcafvNHA5W67JAiRYhR1lryV5+J56++\nhd7d89RkvGPF5R2uu5s4k223a0Z6KSaKA7Jp56ft7/VtdtsaLG7NV4W2le1r4Pjd\nc3xz/h4SzsT8ZdNnJrdJF+cr/9miPTxshG7HJSMvzXSNAhCOnAjvAOpWF5QGQkjo\nDzFQf2E5v/lji05PB5Yk\n=W284\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T09:07:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","h