ation-doctor/commit/eb69a69ef5c60bfca5f65eb4323e3decefd170e6","node_id":"C_kwDOTjIi_9oAKGViNjlhNjllZjVjNjBiZmNhNWY2NWViNDMyM2UzZGVjZWZkMTcwZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/4a7f1e828bc2decf7e334c1a8fe1a9372e7cb3c8","sha":"4a7f1e828bc2decf7e334c1a8fe1a9372e7cb3c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/4a7f1e828bc2decf7e334c1a8fe1a9372e7cb3c8"}],"sha":"eb69a69ef5c60bfca5f65eb4323e3decefd170e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/eb69a69ef5c60bfca5f65eb4323e3decefd170e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/4a7f1e828bc2decf7e334c1a8fe1a9372e7cb3c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:38:27Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:38:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: SARIF and finding remediations for agents (#501)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\nWave 2 on top of #499: make how-to-fix guidance show up where agents\nactually read reports, without starting Wave 3.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Findings now keep the rule catalog `fix` when a rule does not pass a\nfinding-specific suggestion, so JSON/`mfdoctor prompt` see the same\nhow-to-fix as the terminal `fix:` line.\n- SARIF `results.sarif` includes `help.text`, result `properties.fix`,\nand `runs[0].properties.incompleteReasons[]` plus invocation\nnotifications for incomplete-reason remediations.\n- Plugin incomplete failures, diagnostics `summary.md`, and prompt\ncompleteness text include those remediations.\n- Engine stderr no longer dumps `mfdoctor could not complete` when the\nfailure report was already written (or the structured terminal report\nwas printed).\n- Tightened a few catalog fixes (`artifact/expose-missing`,\n`shared/eager-without-singleton`, `federation/name-conflict`,\nmissing-config `doctor/partial-analysis`).\n- Agent playbook (`AGENTS.md` / `skills/mfdoctor/SKILL.md`) tells agents\nto read those remediations instead of scraping engine stderr.\n\nJSON `status.incompleteReasons` stays the stable code list (no report\nschema change). Fingerprints are unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Unit tests for SARIF remediations, quieter failure stderr, plugin\nincomplete remediations, default finding suggestions, and catalog fix\nquality.\n- Regenerated rule docs, inventory fixture, and analysis-cost golden\nsuggestion strings.\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-85800909-bb1f-53d6-b478-8feb5da71d07?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>