2","sha":"4642782c4e18537db5003a9a191c5a6c75c065b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/4642782c4e18537db5003a9a191c5a6c75c065b2"}],"sha":"4a7f1e828bc2decf7e334c1a8fe1a9372e7cb3c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/4a7f1e828bc2decf7e334c1a8fe1a9372e7cb3c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/4642782c4e18537db5003a9a191c5a6c75c065b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:23:15Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T19:23:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: actionable CLI error remediations for agents (#499)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nWave 1 focused on **error outputs with concrete fix suggestions** (CLI +\nreport next-action + plugin policy failures), so users and coding agents\ncan tell **what is wrong and how to fix it**.\n\nUsage/I/O failures no longer dump the full help blob. They print a\nstructured stderr block aligned with `mfdoctor capabilities` error\ncodes:\n\n```text\nerror: usage-error\nUnknown command: chek\nDid you mean: check\n\nfix: Replace `chek` with `check`. …\nnext: mfdoctor check --help\n\nUsage:\n  mfdoctor check [root]\n```\n\nAlso:\n\n- `mfdoctor <command> --help` prints focused usage (exit 0)\n- Unknown options/rules/commands get nearest-match hints (`--ui` is\ncalled out as a documented non-goal)\n- `prompt --finding` miss lists available rule ids and a retry command\n- Terminal `Next action:` names `mfdoctor prompt --finding <ruleId>` and\nmaps `status.incompleteReasons` to remediations\n- Plugin `failAfterCollect` policy failures include the same prompt\ncommand\n- Engine `doctor/analysis-failed` suggestions are phase-specific\n- Capabilities `errorCodes.*.fix` is an additive remediation string\n(schema-optional, always present in live payload)\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: `cli`, `cli-errors`, `reporters`, `capabilities`,\n`failures`, `collect-all`, `run-status`, `agent-prompt` — **113 passed**\n- [x] `vp lint --deny-warnings` and `vp fmt --check` on the branch\n(pre-commit)\n- [x] `vp pack` CLI build\n- [x] Smoke: `node dist/cli.js chek` (exit 2, structured remediations),\n`node dist/cli.js check --help` (exit 0, focused usage), `node\ndist/cli.js rules config/name-requird` (did-you-mean), `node dist/cli.js\ncapabilities` (`errorCodes.usage-error.fix` present)\n- [x] `changeset:check` and `schema-contract` passed\n\n## Notes\n\n- Patch changeset included (user-facing CLI/report/capabilities\nmessaging).\n- No dependency bumps. Verify-mfdoctor skill maps unchanged.\n- Branched from `main` @ `74d7d2e`.\n- Left for Wave 2: per-rule suggestion quality pass, incomplete-reason\ncopy in SARIF, quieter engine stderr when a report was already written.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-85800909-bb1f-53d6-b478-8feb5da71d07?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=ope