,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/d29b0efac299ca7b0b0755de98414b9de3f13520","node_id":"C_kwDOTjIi_9oAKGQyOWIwZWZhYzI5OWNhN2IwYjA3NTVkZTk4NDE0YjlkZTNmMTM1MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/ba4f684bc4a51ac745890af715be21318f291205","sha":"ba4f684bc4a51ac745890af715be21318f291205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/ba4f684bc4a51ac745890af715be21318f291205"}],"sha":"d29b0efac299ca7b0b0755de98414b9de3f13520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/d29b0efac299ca7b0b0755de98414b9de3f13520"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/ba4f684bc4a51ac745890af715be21318f291205/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T22:10:08Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T22:10:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(runtime): remove redundant completeness gate (#477)\n\n## Why\nWhen runtime shared evidence is absent, `sharedCompletenessFor` returns\n`\"unknown\"` regardless of runtime version or source contract. The\nversion gate therefore duplicated the final return value.\n\n## Scope\nRemove the unreachable version check and its obsolete comment. Reports\nwith shared evidence still use the existing complete or partial\nbranches, and reports without it still return `\"unknown\"`.\n\n## Blast Radius\nThe runtime-trace test covers partial and old-runtime reports, and\nrepository search confirmed the remaining semver use serves unrelated\nruntime classification. No network or probe behavior is involved.\n\n## Verification\n- Baseline: 45 focused tests passed before editing\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/runtime-trace.test.ts`\n- `pnpm typecheck`\n- `pnpm knip`\n- `pnpm build`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Comment-quality review: pass\n\nThe repository-wide docs build and final package CLI assertion remain\nexisting trunk blockers documented in the cleanup audit.","tree":{"sha":"46b8f8aea888b27440055f3671badb5b17723b87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/46b8f8aea888b27440055f3671badb5b17723b87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/ba4f684bc4a51ac745890af715be21318f291205","verification":{"payload":"tree 46b8f8aea888b27440055f3671badb5b17723b87\nparent 0531a3c67076b7e5af49619e5a991c77e0621737\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1789769408 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789769408 -0700\n\nrefactor(runtime): remove redundant completeness gate (#477)\n\n## Why\nWhen runtime shared evidence is absent, `sharedCompletenessFor` returns\n`\"unknown\"` regardless of runtime version or source contract. The\nversion gate therefore duplicated the final return value.\n\n## Scope\nRemove the unreachable version check and its obsolete comment. Reports\nwith shared evidence still use the existing complete or partial\nbranches, and reports without it still return `\"unknown\"`.\n\n## Blast Radius\nThe runtime-trace test covers partial and old-runtime reports, and\nrepository search confirmed the remaining semver use serves unrelated\nruntime classification. No network or probe behavior is involved.\n\n## Verification\n- Baseline: 45 focused tests passed before editing\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/runtime-trace.test.ts`\n- `pnpm typecheck`\n- `pnpm knip`\n- `pnpm build`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Comment-quality review: pass\n\nThe repository-wide docs build and final package CLI assertion remain\nexisting trunk blockers documented in the cleanup audit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrbbACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj9AQAEbdApLFzgpFbP/+gnGCCkVT\nlRk7ZyyoyxUZlH/QOC3EmqcBUTouEF/bzMC7gUEALEHKHSwu0ryJCJ2Mx0mNLX5x\noo+uZMkdOTC3VG2RH5xTLNm4QTn7iZYbPQDd/69UkFe0fUi/WXVW0FLwbZ/MOQc3\nJkoB5CgZOHmxVPC90AhHFcdrKeb3AItaFN4OUV145NZxtcCxrEjfbVG6krHSkdlb\n+yT3SNuQysOT48s0khUcUVn9XCpg2r9x6oJTC3OSKYfK9t0USLHeX5tTcps0jf4u\nXKRtN8kW08ji1jqeMScYioiOim9PiNzURQZikiyMZw2qZIFJFtJj3iCEEV5VPXVU\n9qGtgH9JMLNADVk7B8d/bSEe7FUS2WuptyBo/JNZsAwJcJYIgy6lSYs5g27fYe6c\n/Op3HoNJWAK6C/z1d0r7r+1iD951V0+R+J4svQRuuA18r5KitPwHVHrNTZmU9cm6\nnTOQUzYVGHzW2d2n1Z9JK3JeQI2HfMtng+fq8oB7isrbID1g97d8jR2Lwg10BCWJ\n4h8akFq0qGCbfmt8hsW4RtccigYzQy36ndfH/gEWWPFOlAzKVdWzBGaeoK3d7i7u\nEcXAcDCuFOudzqbbR42j1iAi930znj4iYpdN1bq6P2aPEnf/03yTg9PoYA/9+o1R\nKwUTFQ4+lbFd4P6xH6na\n=F4TG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","ver