cc7\nparent 575e130d2a9541698f1434040fbecb4ca91ebb9e\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1789769314 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789769314 -0700\n\nrefactor(cache): narrow internal version constants (#473)\n\n## Why\nThe cache identity version markers are used only inside\n`src/analysis-cache.ts` and are not part of any supported package entry\nor root export.\n\n## Scope\nRemove only the two internal `export` modifiers. Cache identity values\nand runtime behavior remain unchanged.\n\n## Blast Radius\nRepository search covered source, tests, scripts, docs, fixtures,\ngenerated declarations, and package exports. The built package no longer\ndeclares these names while the cache identity still contains the same\nvalues.\n\n## Verification\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/analysis-cache.test.ts`\n- `pnpm typecheck`\n- `pnpm knip`\n- `pnpm build`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Comment-quality review: pass\n\nThe repository-wide docs build and final package CLI assertion remain\nexisting trunk blockers documented in the cleanup audit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrbZiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+oMQAGhQlmogGgWhxIGQOgD2oSCr\nUxm3cfD+rmZOU0+lnSxqdLrCY4G5j6QzWd4SgSxuPkz1YL00ZVdJJQV35AoPoS/f\nHC1uOBJOVh9WCK/uKHSRKhas+i9X1wzhhFxI5jKfZbkftRCYRzkbP/VcjeURwPTQ\nvyaIz2VefIvWaPD2+CzJO1qTx7YhERrU5C3p0y88YEyuYp+8ZBfb2zq0yYeZuHrA\nN3tMW7muZsk+emZ4PbIwsbNcuEoWPuO7+e7Tud9EFAs6KH3722bxaymPiWsCVgKR\n0dIl9AQAd6SyR8NlkSdyyIYF/XqAJCRQdT63OLLf4vqNfsLY5WUD80UA8LnkRJ7w\nNAUxxU81L7z18cpqF6Brx4s8okF+oJeE+XYIG7gVd3T24llKVwt9Hbh1JEEkqVM/\n2CtzebPRW3qTxvY302+n/ItuhQiBo1+rWQTekHtzXa+5xu93WMUfZu3pGrIUWmT8\nJEgE78/xvGF33Qmn3INhcchee/5pJv9MhpoWG4Da02DsXodkySBB0O0uhlALaypT\ntS8YCPFKVGK/GLWO3Bhn4sUz4+hOY6HzoMKuQc5Z9DJZDFJT2X3zWRMmqeTG0mDw\nL/ee39QBCQMIMJv7fzD2riXcP2r3riPbZWNScZ3N7bk+EkUsNqx0TibwwxY7eO5r\nI1Q+IOQE6HPSB5NQoQJQ\n=Jxzb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T22:08:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/27c61a9eb46fd43c86fe01b6cd416848b49a2564","node_id":"C_kwDOTjIi_9oAKDI3YzYxYTllYjQ2ZmQ0M2M4NmZlMDFiNmNkNDE2ODQ4YjQ5YTI1NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/575e130d2a9541698f1434040fbecb4ca91ebb9e","sha":"575e130d2a9541698f1434040fbecb4ca91ebb9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/575e130d2a9541698f1434040fbecb4ca91ebb9e"}],"sha":"27c61a9eb46fd43c86fe01b6cd416848b49a2564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/27c61a9eb46fd43c86fe01b6cd416848b49a2564"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/575e130d2a9541698f1434040fbecb4ca91ebb9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T18:23:55Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T18:23:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): pin probe requests to validated DNS addresses (#470)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Resolve every probe/compare host before connecting and reject any\nrestricted address.\n- Pin the validated address into the Node HTTP(S) socket lookup hook to\nprevent DNS rebinding between policy validation and connection.\n- Preserve manual redirect checks and add a regression test for public\nhostnames resolving to loopback.\n- Add a patch changeset for `@tonoizer/mfdoctor`.\n\n## Security context\n\nThe security audit identified an SSRF gap in `probe`/ `compare`:\nhostname and literal-IP checks happened before `fetch`, but a public\nhostname could resolve to a private or cloud-metadata address afterward.\nThe default transport now performs the check and uses the checked\naddress for the socket. Explicit custom `fetch` transports remain\ncaller-owned policy boundaries.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit`\n- `pnpm run lint`\n- `pnpm run build`\n- `pnpm run pack:check`\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/probe.test.ts --testTimeout=30000`\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit --testTimeout=30000 --maxWorkers=2`\n(94 files, 1,221 tests) ✅","tree":{"sha":"4f4174b1c1025903392cc44d6a2e860d895d6d28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/4f4174b1c1025903392cc44d6a2e860d895d6d28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/575e130d2a9541698f1434040fbecb4ca91ebb9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f4174b1c1025903392cc44d6a2e860d895d6d28\nparent 50d1a6df9308a1c97f6da0e86ca0ff1c7e8c2fe2\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1789755835 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789755835 -0700\n\nfix(security): pin probe requests to validated DNS addresses (#470)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Resolve every probe/compare host before connecting and reject any\nrestricted address.\n- Pin the validated address into the Node HTTP(S) socket lookup hook to\nprevent DNS rebinding between policy validation and connection.\n- Preserve manual redirect checks and add a regression test for public\nhostnames resolving to loopback.\n- Add a patch changeset for `@tonoizer/mfdoctor`.\n\n## Security context\n\nThe security audit identified an SSRF gap in `probe`/ `compare`:\nhostname and literal-IP checks happened before `fetch`, but a public\nhostname could resolve to a private or cloud-metadata address afterward.\nThe default transport now performs the check and uses the checked\naddress for the socket. Explicit custom `fetch` transports remain\ncaller-owned policy boundaries.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit`\n- `pnpm run lint`\n- `pnpm run build`\n- `pnpm run pack:check`\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/probe.test.ts --testTimeout=30000`\n- `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit --testTimeout=30000 --maxWorkers=2`\n(94 files, 1,221 tests) ✅","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrYG7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcfsQAASvJAgIlCF+ua/KoynSxJFl\nkzz82b+hln+tg49NwT/hT5D+LDggQf7NCveZeLkg+wGY1Ku2zQxMBj/dKPgYUw8W\nCit0B7CnCdwooHQBubWpW2gk8D9i7iCYO/sTNxkvYBP+