"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:04:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(agent): add context-faithful verification contracts (#454)\n\n## Summary\n- Add a versioned verification plan that retains analysis kind, project\ndirectory, required artifacts, rebuild requirement, unknown build\ncommands, operation follow-up, and completeness conditions.\n- Add bounded and redacted repair context with rule family, fingerprint,\nreport path, JSON pointer, and typed-detail metadata.\n- Add a versioned CLI operations contract and derive legacy\ndiscovery/network command metadata from it.\n- Preserve legacy evidence rollout defaults, suppressions policy, and\nthe existing `src/cli.ts` and `src/reporters.ts` files.\n\n## Testing\n- [x] `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/agent-prompt.test.ts\ntest/unit/capabilities.test.ts test/unit/finding-details.test.ts\ntest/unit/schema-contract.test.ts`\n- [x] `pnpm run test:unit`\n- [x] `pnpm run test:integration`\n- [x] `pnpm run schema:check`\n- [x] `pnpm run fmt:check`\n- [x] `pnpm run lint`\n- [x] `pnpm run typecheck`\n- [x] `pnpm run build`\n- [x] `pnpm run knip`\n- [x] `pnpm run changeset:check`\n\n## Risks\n- The capabilities schema now requires the versioned `operations`\nmember; the checked-in schema fixture was updated with the same\ncontract.\n- Existing CLI callers still need to pass original analysis context when\nthey have a custom operation; diagnostics dumps infer runtime/workspace\ncontext from findings and retain unknown commands rather than inventing\nthem.\n- No networked MFDoctor operation or evidence-rollout default was\nchanged.","tree":{"sha":"4a6a20f84fa69516e1f8593e2d9f32fe7bab5e6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/4a6a20f84fa69516e1f8593e2d9f32fe7bab5e6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/b4892f80439154fb34ca9cf986ad826f2aca917f","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a6a20f84fa69516e1f8593e2d9f32fe7bab5e6e\nparent 8469777f221fedc4828ad3d07fc02a18f0814023\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1789333485 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789333485 -0700\n\nfeat(agent): add context-faithful verification contracts (#454)\n\n## Summary\n- Add a versioned verification plan that retains analysis kind, project\ndirectory, required artifacts, rebuild requirement, unknown build\ncommands, operation follow-up, and completeness conditions.\n- Add bounded and redacted repair context with rule family, fingerprint,\nreport path, JSON pointer, and typed-detail metadata.\n- Add a versioned CLI operations contract and derive legacy\ndiscovery/network command metadata from it.\n- Preserve legacy evidence rollout defaults, suppressions policy, and\nthe existing `src/cli.ts` and `src/reporters.ts` files.\n\n## Testing\n- [x] `pnpm exec vitest run test/unit/agent-prompt.test.ts\ntest/unit/capabilities.test.ts test/unit/finding-details.test.ts\ntest/unit/schema-contract.test.ts`\n- [x] `pnpm run test:unit`\n- [x] `pnpm run test:integration`\n- [x] `pnpm run schema:check`\n- [x] `pnpm run fmt:check`\n- [x] `pnpm run lint`\n- [x] `pnpm run typecheck`\n- [x] `pnpm run build`\n- [x] `pnpm run knip`\n- [x] `pnpm run changeset:check`\n\n## Risks\n- The capabilities schema now requires the versioned `operations`\nmember; the checked-in schema fixture was updated with the same\ncontract.\n- Existing CLI callers still need to pass original analysis context when\nthey have a custom operation; diagnostics dumps infer runtime/workspace\ncontext from findings and retain unknown commands rather than inventing\nthem.\n- No networked MFDoctor operation or evidence-rollout default was\nchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpw/tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl74QACBA2Ct0tRVB75EkpW7ubEi6\n3032EFbxblJIEKCUY7yX/R2PeyweVQzssMIEd573QiMhjrcGARZvARHjQHF7h+HY\ndDqkWt+VPbopl977a8QsLtjM3BeTbQ8YiqY56bKyH/ZyZr8nHPiMzSgVLlzgzdgX\ntLf+chJvhsD2w+