n`runtime/error-correlated`); green exit 0; missing trace exit 2 |\n| plugin-emit | `@mfdoctor-standalone/vite` build writes\n`.mf/doctor/project.json` (`vite@8.1.5`,\n`lifecycle.flavor=rolldown-vite`); core rule IDs present |\n| rules | catalog **127** rules; shared `supportedBundlers` omits\n`unknown`; `vite/server-origin` → `[\"vite\"]`; unknown ID exit 2 |\n\nUnreachable: none. Network `probe` / `compare` remain explicitly\nunmapped.\n\n## Map/evidence corrections (proven drift)\n\n- **plugin-emit:** evidence notes called the standalone Vite cell a\n“Vite Plus cell”. Live emit is `vite@8.1.5` with\n`bundler.lifecycle.flavor=rolldown-vite` (Rolldown engine), not the\n`vite-plus` package. Map now points Vite Plus smoke at\n`examples/compatibility/rolldown`. Optional static `check` still\nincludes `missing-emit` and `partial-bundler`.\n- **capabilities / rules evidence:** refresh for package `2.0.0` and\ncatalog growth 113 → 127 (new rule IDs are not a new CLI surface).\n- **check / prompt / baseline evidence:** default `remote-http-insecure`\nshowcase now also reports `config/js-remote-without-type-urls`\n(warning). Recipes still match; extra findings are expected.\n\n## Out of scope (intentional)\n\n- Product code, suppressions, `probe` / `compare`, HTML UI, in-browser\nagent, general `--fix`\n- Network proofs\n- Version bump / npm publish\n- Driving `examples/compatibility/rolldown` as a separate mapped feature\n(optional path only)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-0cc98caa-a379-4dff-8138-dfa803bff109?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&