ents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/07bdd3127ceb7ea838bdef8e59645ba09098892b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:21:34Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:21:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add dataPrefetch to the configuration audit checklist (#427)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\nImplements **BL-57** only: add a configuration-audit checklist row for\n`dataPrefetch` / prefetch remotes.\n\nPrefetch and preload misconfiguration can break load order, but there is\nno normalize field and a doctor rule would be easy to over-build. This\nPR documents the surface as a review checklist — **no rule, no\nfixture**.\n\nRebased onto latest `main` (includes BL-54 `#428`, `compilerInstance`\naudit row `#417`, and neighbors). Conflict resolution kept those main\nrows and added only the `dataPrefetch` checklist line.\n\n### What changed\n\n- EN + DE `configuration-audit` tables: `dataPrefetch` / prefetch\nremotes row.\n- Official docs link in the row: [Data\nPrefetch](https://module-federation.io/guide/data/data-prefetch.html).\n- Practical fix points at `lazyLoadComponentPlugin` + `prefetch({ id:\n''<remote>/<expose>'' })` and `preloadRemote` load-order testing.\n- Explicitly **not checked automatically** (low confidence), matching\nthe existing `shared[].layer` audit pattern.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- No doctor rule or showcase fixture (later PR, as BL-57 acceptance\nrequires).\n- No version bump, changeset, or npm publish.\n- No HTML UI / in-browser agent / general `--fix`.\n- Skips unrelated work (#356 / #314 / #29).\n\n### Test plan\n\n- [x] EN and DE rows stay in sync (German generator only translates\nheadings).\n- [x] `node scripts/generate-german-docs.mjs --check`\n- [x] `node scripts/check-doc-parity.mjs`\n- [x] `vp fmt --check`\n- [x] Rebased onto latest `main`; conflict resolution kept\n`compilerInstance` / SSR host-init notes from main plus the BL-57 row.\n- [ ] CI required checks (Vercel Pro rate-limit failures are not\nrequired)\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-40644595-4ef7-40cb-a6a2-96c1725b4cb0?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-40644595-4ef7-40cb-a6a2-96c1725b4cb0&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"69174e739c0bb2044b1106165db265ea643c31f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/69174e739c0bb2044b1106165db265ea643c31f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/07bdd3127ceb7ea838bdef8e59645ba09098892b","verification":{"payload":"tree 69174e739c0bb2044b1106165db265ea643c31f7\nparent cdf26e24983bc58