s://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/07bdd3127ceb7ea838bdef8e59645ba09098892b","node_id":"C_kwDOTjIi_9oAKDA3YmRkMzEyN2NlYjdlYTgzOGJkZWY4ZTU5NjQ1YmEwOTA5ODg5MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/cdf26e24983bc5850c3395c80d7cf5ea8583d6be","sha":"cdf26e24983bc5850c3395c80d7cf5ea8583d6be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/cdf26e24983bc5850c3395c80d7cf5ea8583d6be"}],"sha":"07bdd3127ceb7ea838bdef8e59645ba09098892b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/07bdd3127ceb7ea838bdef8e59645ba09098892b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/cdf26e24983bc5850c3395c80d7cf5ea8583d6be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:21:32Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:21:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: incompleteReasons when Enhanced stats are off but remotes exist (#431)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\nImplements BL-50: distinguish Enhanced (Webpack/Rspack/Rsbuild) missing\nstats from Vite’s documented manifest/stats opt-in.\n\n## What changed\n\n- After an Enhanced **emit** (`capabilities.emittedAssets`) with remotes\nand `capabilities.stats: false`, `report.status.incompleteReasons`\nincludes **`missing-stats`**. CLI-only checks stay on `missing-emit` (no\ndouble-count). Explicit `manifest: false` still uses\n`artifact/manifest-disabled` instead of this code.\n- `doctor/partial-analysis` now explains the Enhanced default (`manifest\n!== false` / `mf-stats.json`) when remotes exist and stats were not\ncollected. Vite without `manifest: true` still gets the existing opt-in\nsuggestion — not `missing-stats`.\n- Report schema + docs list the new additive reason code.\n`fixtures/rule-inventory/v1.json` regenerated so `inventory:check`\nmatches the updated `doctor/partial-analysis` remediation.fix.\n- No version bump, changeset, or evidence-v2 default flip.\n\nRebased onto latest `main` (includes #428 / #429).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n| Path | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Webpack/Rspack/Rsbuild emit + remotes + stats false | `missing-stats`\nand Enhanced partial-analysis copy |\n| Enhanced remotes + explicit `manifest: false` | existing\n`artifact/manifest-disabled` |\n| Vite remotes without manifest | documented opt-in; no `missing-stats`\n|\n\n## Proof\n\n- `vp test run test/unit` — 1106 passed (covers the Enhanced vs Vite\ndistinction).\n- CLI `federation` on an Rspack `project.json` with emit + remotes +\n`stats: false` → `status.incompleteReasons: [\"missing-stats\"]`. Same\nshape on Vite → complete, no `missing-stats`.\n- CLI `check` on Webpack remotes with omitted `manifest` → Enhanced\n`doctor/partial-analysis` suggestion (`mf-stats.json` / `manifest !==\nfalse`). Explicit `manifest: false` → `artifact/manifest-disabled`. Vite\n`check` → `missing-emit` only (no `missing-stats`).\n- `node scripts/generate-rule-inventory.mjs --check` — up to date after\nfixture sync.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-2623aeee-2be2-4957-a018-cd60b6ca100d?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-2623aeee-2be2-4957-a018-cd60b6ca100d&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0e2b71d8af0311d82121ed37a5ab9839892cf21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/e0e2b71d8af0311d82121ed37a5ab9839892cf21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/cdf26e24983bc5850c3395c80d7cf5ea8583d6be","verification":{"payload":"tree e0e2b71d8af0311d82121ed37a5ab9839892cf21\nparent dfb1f1ed2f24f133b8ecbc55513dc83728256210\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1788708092 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788708092 +0000\n\nfix: incompleteReasons when Enhanced stats are off but remotes exist (#431)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\nImplements BL-50: distinguish Enhanced (Webpack/Rspack/Rsbuild) missing\nstats from Vite’s documented manifest/stats opt-in.\n\n## What changed\n\n- After an Enhanced **emit** (`capabilities.emittedAssets`) with remotes\nand `capabilities.stats: false`, `report.status.incompleteReasons`\nincludes **`missing-stats`**. CLI-only checks stay on `missing-emit` (no\ndouble-count). Explicit `manifest: false` still uses\n`artifact/manifest-disabled` instead of this code.\n- `doctor/partial-analysis` now explains the Enhanced default (`manifest\n!== false` / `mf-stats.json`) when remotes exist and stats were not\ncollected. Vite without `manifest: true` still gets the existing opt-in\nsuggestion — not `missing-stats`.\n- Report schema + docs list the new additive reason code.\n`fixtures/rule-inventory/v1.json` regenerated so `inventory:check`\nmatches the updated `doctor/partial-analysis` remediation.fix.\n- No version bump, changeset, or evidence-v2 default flip.\n\nRebased onto latest `main` (includes #428 / #429).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n| Path | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Webpack/Rspack/Rsbuild emit + remotes + stats false | `missing-stats`\nand Enhanced partial-analysis copy |\n| Enhanced remotes + explicit `manifest: false` | existing\n`artifact/manifest-disabled` |\n| Vite remotes without manifest | documented opt-in; no `missing-stats`\n|\n\n## Proof\n\n- `vp test run test/unit` — 1106 passed (covers the Enhanced vs Vite\ndistinction).\n- CLI `federation` on an Rspack `project.json` with emit + remotes +\n`stats: false` → `status.incompleteReasons: [\"missing-stats\"]`. Same\nshape on Vite → complete, no `missing-stats`.\n- CLI `check` on Webpack remotes with omitted `manifest` → Enhanced\n`doctor/partial-analysis` suggestion (`mf-stats.json` / `manifest !==\nfalse`). Explicit `manifest: false` → `artifact/manifest-disabled`. Vite\n`check` → `missing-emit` only (no `missing-stats`).\n- `node scripts/generate-rule-inventory.mjs --check` — up to date after\nfixture sync.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-2623aeee-2be2-4957-a018-cd60b6ca100d?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-2623aeee-2be2-4957-a018-cd60b6ca100d&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP S