"received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/7d681b55fc2cef042903a024ba97c8075f507b16","node_id":"C_kwDOTjIi_9oAKDdkNjgxYjU1ZmMyY2VmMDQyOTAzYTAyNGJhOTdjODA3NWY1MDdiMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commit/83d02bb352c90b5ac73a93f01e99d4d0de041be4","sha":"83d02bb352c90b5ac73a93f01e99d4d0de041be4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/83d02bb352c90b5ac73a93f01e99d4d0de041be4"}],"sha":"7d681b55fc2cef042903a024ba97c8075f507b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/7d681b55fc2cef042903a024ba97c8075f507b16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70775490?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tonoizer","id":70775490,"login":"tonoizer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzc1NDkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/83d02bb352c90b5ac73a93f01e99d4d0de041be4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:20:54Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:20:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: preserve shared.layer in normalize (#418)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nBL-42: Webpack/Enhanced `shared[pkg].layer` (and sibling `issuerLayer`)\nwere dropped in `normalize`. Webpack layer sharing is a real failure\nmode — host and remote on different compilation layers do not share —\nbut `NormalizedShared` had no field for it.\n\nConfirmed against the SDK plugin types cited in CONTRIBUTING\n(`module-federation/core@641a0b6` `SharedConfig`):\n\n- `layer?: string` — layer in which the shared module should be placed\n- `issuerLayer?: string` — layer of the issuer\n\nPublic [shared docs](https://module-federation.io/configure/shared.html)\nand Vite’s option normalizer do **not** list `layer`. Confidence on how\noften MF users set it is still low.\n\nThis PR is normalize-and-unknown-field only:\n\n- `layer` / `issuerLayer` round-trip on `NormalizedShared`\n- Extra shared object keys that are not confirmed SDK/`packagePath`\nfields are recorded as canonical `extensions`\n- **No cross-layer mismatch rule.** This repo has no two-project fixture\nwhere both sides declare `layer`. Marked as a follow-up on BL-42.\n\nNo changeset / version bump (additive optional fields; no new finding).\nNo HTML UI, `--fix`, private MF scraping, or npm publish.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: `layer` / `issuerLayer` round-trip through\n`normalizeModuleFederation`; omitted on string-array shared and\nnon-string values\n- [x] Unit: canonical config keeps confirmed layer keys known; unknown\nextra shared keys become extensions\n- [x] Unit: collect facts preserve `layer` on normalized shared and the\ndeclared collection\n- [x] `vp test run test/unit/normalize.test.ts\ntest/unit/canonical-config.test.ts\ntest/unit/canonical-config-bridge.test.ts` — 3 files, 32 tests passed\n- [x] `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit`\n- [x] `vp fmt --check` and `vp lint --deny-warnings` on the pre-commit\nhook\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-460fcd27-91ce-4fe6-bdc5-da8ba3d9f49c?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-460fcd27-91ce-4fe6-bdc5-da8ba3d9f49c&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"02fc12955944e3b7d12cce436c7617a152433b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/02fc12955944e3b7d12cce436c7617a152433b08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/83d02bb352c90b5ac73a93f01e99d4d0de041be4","verification":{"payload":"tree 02fc12955944e3b7d12cce436c7617a152433b08\nparent 1e0f5c3f82d8638ba7f46dcb46cdf32f7f6108f7\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1788704454 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788704454 +0000\n\nfeat: preserve shared.layer in normalize (#418)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nBL-42: Webpack/Enhanced `shared[pkg].layer` (and sibling `issuerLayer`)\nwere dropped in `normalize`. Webpack layer sharing is a real failure\nmode — host and remote on different compilation layers do not share —\nbut `NormalizedShared` had no field for it.\n\nConfirmed against the SDK plugin types cited in CONTRIBUTING\n(`module-federation/core@641a0b6` `SharedConfig`):\n\n- `layer?: string` — layer in which the shared module should be placed\n- `issuerLayer?: string` — layer of the issuer\n\nPublic [shared docs](https://module-federation.io/configure/shared.html)\nand Vite’s option normalizer do **not** list `layer`. Confidence on how\noften MF users set it is still low.\n\nThis PR is normalize-and-unknown-field only:\n\n- `layer` / `issuerLayer` round-trip on `NormalizedShared`\n- Extra shared object keys that are not confirmed SDK/`packagePath`\nfields are recorded as canonical `extensions`\n- **No cross-layer mismatch rule.** This repo has no two-project fixture\nwhere both sides declare `layer`. Marked as a follow-up on BL-42.\n\nNo changeset / version bump (additive optional fields; no new finding).\nNo HTML UI, `--fix`, private MF scraping, or npm publish.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: `layer` / `issuerLayer` round-trip through\n`normalizeModuleFederation`; omitted on string-array shared and\nnon-string values\n- [x] Unit: canonical config keeps confirmed layer keys known; unknown\nextra shared keys become extensions\n- [x] Unit: collect facts preserve `layer` on normalized shared and the\ndeclared collection\n- [x] `vp test run test/unit/normalize.test.ts\ntest/unit/canonical-config.test.ts\ntest/unit/canonical-config-bridge.test.ts` — 3 files, 32 tests passed\n- [x] `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit`\n- [x] `vp fmt --check` and `vp lint --deny-warnings` on the pre-commit\nhook\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-460fcd27-91ce-4fe6-bdc5-da8ba3d9f49c?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-460fcd27-91ce-4fe6-bdc5-da8ba3d9f49c&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnXbGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIPQQAH299O95+f2ZQU1c84VBdRIK\nA1ymXAfUTCbMHpU2mEQo0C1lZLbTTjaxrEYSbmqs4TAH7TrPEcFa8wms4mGQT776\nqSPWjUFuNvL9v4Ikz/UNHDoYII12xwSHqJGCB0UEBhbjmN54idM4vZYXWjjJ3uCl\nuoJlVSmcjOu8Hx3WAbmjlbgNTDhMA2uGoonDQ5ZeXcAuATlAuv6BzDgfvP7BIfcR\ngS5xEaMwm62OU8z02p6L9LHFKbOk30twTVicy93VUwKWuPFH20x44HiWY0IlDeUz\nVo77RftYETLX0EdmotXAicj805Gb9WsXh6ZIs7ngxD2UKmB5KhvPWM3rSy4/Yz1i\nP8z0OV6JvbOLg/PEaoBGnBGQPSncbAJLnZODJWUgDteVB3EdtAXSYS73wXWDXPYR\nkBkF/hB4NEPYN8PvG8CE9d7SqjsvY8rSqqgThKpPOSiRpC7khwFngQOYqaRHxToW\nZW+VZ+QqwOoo27Qmc5uM6L7QMyU7cGif5QoULS8St4JCobf3wCVzyqdTHHbrthCW\nlhA4AlfAZ0FBmHjBZu1M2FB5x6P2g0fjgPQSPg759i6mHyYGqqxqfVras370aFaz\nhqhlmG4/Dzo0tWXVgHsJay4cNpQIWtuWBg51rAIcRwEkE1X49DQeRFJXtB+tmkZy\n46BA1qNVKMrrwiEsqvJn\n=JGEb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T14:20:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte