ithub.com/users/tonoizer/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonoizer","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/commits/8c303a4bcafba68d35d659bfd3f68136cd910cd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:08:31Z","email":"hey@kevinbeier.com","name":"Kevin Beier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:08:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: assert Vite-only rules in mfdoctor rules catalog (#413)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nBL-41: after BL-01 wired `supportedBundlers` from inventory, add a named\ncatalog canary so agents cannot regress Vite-only rules back to “every\nbundler.”\n\n`vite/server-origin.supportedBundlers` is now asserted as `[\"vite\"]` in:\n\n- `ruleCatalog()` (`test/unit/rule-contract.test.ts`)\n- `mfdoctor rules vite/server-origin` (`test/unit/cli.test.ts`)\n\nThe existing `vite/remotes-prefer-module` CLI check stays. Verify-skill\n`rules` evidence already records this (`stdout-vite-only.json`); this PR\ndoes not rewrite that skill.\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npnpm exec vp test run test/unit/cli.test.ts test/unit/rule-contract.test.ts\n# 2 files, 52 passed\npnpm exec vp fmt --check test/unit/cli.test.ts test/unit/rule-contract.test.ts\n```\n\nNo product/runtime change, no changeset, no version bump.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- HTML UI / in-browser agent / general `--fix`\n- #356 / #314 / #29\n- npm publish / GitHub Release\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-2356044e-2e7f-46c5-926e-54303c9083bf?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https:/