reply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: preserve expose object filters in normalize (#405)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nBL-33: Enhanced expose objects were flattened to `Record<string,\nstring>`, so extra fields (filters / don’t-expose-shaped keys)\ndisappeared with no signal.\n\nConfirmed against the SDK types cited in CONTRIBUTING\n(`module-federation/core@641a0b6` `ExposesConfig` and webpack’s matching\ntype): **only `import` and `name` exist**. There is no documented\ndon’t-expose / filter field, so this PR does not invent one.\n\n- Unknown expose object keys are recorded as canonical unknown fields\n(`extensions`)\n- Confirmed `name` (chunk name) is preserved on `exposeObjects`\n- `exposes` stays the **public** map used by `config/expose-key-invalid`\n(confirmed `import` targets only)\n- Extra keys on an object that still has `import` remain public\n(unconfirmed filter is not treated as a hide API)\n- Object entries with no `import` are omitted from the public list and\nkept on `exposeObjects` + canonical extensions\n\nRebased onto latest `main` (includes #395). CI red was a merge-commit\nlockfile (`ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_MISSING_DEPENDENCY` for\n`@module-federation/vite@1.20.7`). After rebase, `vp install\n--frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile` both succeed\nwith no lockfile diff vs `main`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: normalize preserves `name` and unknown keys; public list\nexcludes no-import objects\n- [x] Unit: canonical config records unknown expose keys, not\n`import`/`name`\n- [x] Unit: `config/expose-key-invalid` uses the public list\n- [x] Rebase onto `main`; frozen + unfrozen install; knip\n- [x] quality / adapter / doctor CI green (Vercel Pro rate-limit\nignored)\n\nWebpack/Rspack post-emit doctor only. No HTML UI, `--fix`, private MF\nscraping, version bump, or npm publish.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-13ba1922-7a0f-4b99-af5e-4d7fdd6d84b4?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-13ba1922-7a0f-4b99-af5e-4d7fdd6d84b4&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"89dad2814992988221735dad24020ab00976094a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/trees/89dad2814992988221735dad24020ab00976094a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonoizer/module-federation-doctor/git/commits/c40c8109f6b054f63498e8ddff506cfce49b005e","verification":{"payload":"tree 89dad2814992988221735dad24020ab00976094a\nparent 8ac5eeba014980c01692a70c35b9ef4e06479c80\nauthor Kevin Beier <hey@kevinbeier.com> 1788702601 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788702601 +0000\n\nfeat: preserve expose object filters in normalize (#405)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Summary\n\nBL-33: Enhanced expose objects were flattened to `Record<string,\nstring>`, so extra fields (filters / don’t-expose-shaped keys)\ndisappeared with no signal.\n\nConfirmed against the SDK types cited in CONTRIBUTING\n(`module-federation/core@641a0b6` `ExposesConfig` and webpack’s matching\ntype): **only `import` and `name` exist**. There is no documented\ndon’t-expose / filter field, so this PR does not invent one.\n\n- Unknown expose object keys are recorded as canonical unknown fields\n(`extensions`)\n- Confirmed `name` (chunk name) is preserved on `exposeObjects`\n- `exposes` stays the **public** map used by `config/expose-key-invalid`\n(confirmed `import` targets only)\n- Extra keys on an object that still has `import` remain public\n(unconfirmed filter is not treated as a hide API)\n- Object entries with no `import` are omitted from the public list and\nkept on `exposeObjects` + canonical extensions\n\nRebased onto latest `main` (includes #395). CI red was a merge-commit\nlockfile (`ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_MISSING_DEPENDENCY` for\n`@module-federation/vite@1.20.7`). After rebase, `vp install\n--frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile` both succeed\nwith no lockfile diff vs `main`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit: normalize preserves `name` and unknown keys; public list\nexcludes no-import objects\n- [x] Unit: canonical config records unknown expose keys, not\n`import`/`name`\n- [x] Unit: `config/expose-key-invalid` uses the public list\n- [x] Rebase onto `main`; frozen + unfrozen install; knip\n- [x] quality / adapter / doctor CI green (Vercel Pro rate-limit\nignored)\n\nWebpack/Rspack post-emit doctor only. No HTML UI, `--fix`, private MF\nscraping, version bump, or npm publish.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-13ba1922-7a0f-4b99-af5e-4d7fdd6d84b4?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-13ba1922-7a0f-4b99-af5e-4d7fdd6d84b4&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img\nalt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\"\nsrc=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnW+JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArQQQAFzTSOXSbIAgt2Ehl4VYwt4f\nSREC1R1K2bY7HLg9UiZ4svV6W8BBDHbgK377f2uD+2sNjvf0JpKmoewr9cpRBt2Q\ntVaSPAhac92NgRF9jKRRuyUD91QWfAD7DRDLOmmPBoegW+Ic6gBhz/ZJB7ZDbqtC\nvJ0cwTZs2xlNoRA6ZMXABmGIQWrgfwQKFjsBX84AQVSRsMT3AgPy9DAZV59KnPlD\nX5eC8HWy9T715FZnVhpqgx5fTWI0KqnFB4mrhu2kNv9P5vNv4oiAIkWa3k6TCFpS\ni/oMcI7JK7d72s5DZvTdZTqD+hDjc3i20UlEfSl+6WMbpHzLWfeXop+y3VxOQgOq\nsne1g+LS4iV3XqG8dqyPlze3b3JeNBbYFwjWUTvQ4lF4KNO2rgpTu/abhif1tDZk\n+EFRJdsEWi07jkkECMAjTWxAP3o1/0FbtO+mjV79iUJHP9ZZuSPTu+2KfMVdCSgm\nILhIMOeNa64ITsnvtVSVCcrfxszrqdhWR6yuOAXJxsLVZJY9vfZ5NZFIgvlEcqLa\ndTpGWQtuFhhbyjUGNbBaOLrMvQrpLdmNPF4whCVmH5lcSBLUEN+QOsSJn+EHmauH\ng4A8kxUJKAhs3h7jt63Spqvrltoh6NAIzaf32zaR1wGfW2IdOf7ZeAgIk2LJg2GI\nuSl29M+4FcsjWJZjdrgv\n=Dy4U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T13:50:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f