_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh","id":204504651,"login":"reddy-sh","node_id":"U_kgDODDB-Sw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commit/40ac20002dd61a21d2c948c326929eb2295873d0","node_id":"C_kwDOTjOA8doAKDQwYWMyMDAwMmRkNjFhMjFkMmM5NDhjMzI2OTI5ZWIyMjk1ODczZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commit/f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f","sha":"f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f"}],"sha":"40ac20002dd61a21d2c948c326929eb2295873d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/40ac20002dd61a21d2c948c326929eb2295873d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204504651?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh","id":204504651,"login":"reddy-sh","node_id":"U_kgDODDB-Sw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T00:49:28Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T00:49:28Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"message":"fix(w360): actually file every survey a passbook lists, at its own acreage\n\n\"One record per survey\" wrote one record. The batch was gated on\nmultiSurvey.choice === ''each'', but Add record stayed enabled while the question\nsat unanswered, so pressing it ran the ordinary single-record path and filed\nrow one of twelve. The question now gates the primary, and says why it is\ndisabled rather than greying out in silence.\n\nTwo worse bugs were underneath it:\n\nEvery record got the form''s one extent. A passbook''s areas are per row — this\nROR lists twelve totalling 12.39 acres — and the form had no total to show, so\nall twelve would have been filed at 0.00 ac. Each record now takes its own row''s\nextent through parcelAcres(), which converts rather than relabels. That matters\nmore than it sounds: the drawer''s existing deedExtent() maps \"cents\" onto the\nacres box and converts nothing, so a \"5 Cents\" row would have been filed as five\nacres. Tolerable for one figure somebody eyeballs in a box; silent corruption\nacross twelve nobody checks. parcelAcres is unit-tested for exactly that.\n\nThe batch also stamped the document''s consideration and market value onto every\nrow. Portfolio worth is a plain sum, so one deed''s ₹50 lakh across twelve rows\nreports ₹6 crore. Both fields are now left off the batch entirely, and their\nboxes are hidden while batching rather than left to look like they apply.\n\nAlso:\n- The loop stays strictly sequential, deliberately. _create_record finds the\n  parent passbook with a SELECT on (owner, khata, village) and INSERTs when it\n  misses, outside a transaction with no unique index behind it — run twelve\n  concurrently and all twelve miss and mint twelve passbooks for one khata.\n  The batch refuses to run at all with the khata box empty, for the same reason.\n- Resumable. There is no unique index on (passbook, survey_no) and no\n  idempotency key on saveRecord, so the old \"return on first failure\" left a\n  partial set that a second press would have duplicated wholesale. Written rows\n  are tracked; a retry finishes the job and names the surveys still missing.\n- The passbook is uploaded once and pointed at all N records, not uploaded per\n  record (storage POSTs with onConflict=duplicate, so that meant N byte copies)\n  and not filed against the first only (which left eleven records claiming no\n  papers for the document they were made from). The survey rides in each\n  subtitle so the Vault cards are tellable apart.\n- The batch writes through a non-invalidating, non-toasting saveRecord and\n  refreshes once at the end — api.ts documents this escape hatch for exactly\n  this case. Twelve ordinary saves meant twelve serialised whole-tree refetches\n  and twelve toasts reading \"Nothing has changed\", which was false mid-batch.\n- The drawer reports what it made instead of navigating to the twelfth record.\n  In list view it previously closed with no report at all, since Properties only\n  passes onCreated in map view.\n- Both callout boxes used var(--w-accent-light), which is defined nowhere in the\n  repo, so they rendered with no background. Now --w-accent-wash, via a .callout\n  class rather than inline style.\n- The half-written-batch error gets role=\"alert\", and the discard prompt gets a\n  third branch — after six records it was still saying nothing had been saved.\n\nDeliberately NOT done, both reversible and worth a second opinion:\n- Survey numbers are stored as written (\"119-2\"), not normalised to \"119/2\".\n  Normalising would fix village-map matching, but _survey_parts splits on \"/\"\n  only, so it would split this holding across two conventions against the 44\n  rows already filed and against the phone''s import key. That needs a migration,\n  not a quiet change of shape for new rows.\n- acquisition_source is left at the server default ''sale'' though the paper says\n  inheritance on all twelve, and no parcel_owners row is seeded. RecordInput\n  carries neither field. Fixing it is a ~20 line server change in the parity\n  note band; it is pre-existing behaviour for every record this drawer makes,\n  not a regression from this one, so it is not bundled here.","tree":{"sha":"8d86e1b3f61918d22d032c5268bd6fe5b8288017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/git/trees/8d86e1b3f61918d22d032c5268bd6fe5b8288017"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/git/commits/f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204504651?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh","id":204504651,"login":"reddy-sh","node_id":"U_kgDODDB-Sw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commit/f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f","node_id":"C_kwDOTjOA8doAKGYzYzczODMxZTlhMzYwZWIwYjcwY2ViMzQ4NmM2Y2U4MjU0NGNkNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commit/0bdcef98b24ab73dda799a476731059a0ef22651","sha":"0bdcef98b24ab73dda799a476731059a0ef22651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/0bdcef98b24ab73dda799a476731059a0ef22651"}],"sha":"f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/f3c73831e9a360eb0b70ceb3486c6ce82544cd5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204504651?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh","id":204504651,"login":"reddy-sh","node_id":"U_kgDODDB-Sw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/0bdcef98b24