/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/07944a06a8c6d126ba94eed0b30c2dec886fb6d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T18:28:49Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T18:28:49Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"message":"Integrate platform repair and Web360 expansion","tree":{"sha":"f7b9486e1b1cb141fe5602796b0a4c94e654283e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/git/trees/f7b9486e1b1cb141fe5602796b0a4c94e654283e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/git/commits/07944a06a8c6d126ba94eed0b30c2dec886fb6d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204504651?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh","id":204504651,"login":"reddy-sh","node_id":"U_kgDODDB-Sw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commit/07944a06a8c6d126ba94eed0b30c2dec886fb6d4","node_id":"C_kwDOTjOA8doAKDA3OTQ0YTA2YThjNmQxMjZiYTk0ZWVkMGIzMGMyZGVjODg2ZmI2ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commit/548dbebf55e754d7928f5ec27d5a30e0c96f7819","sha":"548dbebf55e754d7928f5ec27d5a30e0c96f7819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/548dbebf55e754d7928f5ec27d5a30e0c96f7819"}],"sha":"07944a06a8c6d126ba94eed0b30c2dec886fb6d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/07944a06a8c6d126ba94eed0b30c2dec886fb6d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204504651?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reddy-sh","id":204504651,"login":"reddy-sh","node_id":"U_kgDODDB-Sw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/548dbebf55e754d7928f5ec27d5a30e0c96f7819/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:56:22Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:56:22Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"message":"feat(parity): web changes wake the phone, on their own\n\nThe two apps share no code, so every land rule, GraphQL document and token\nexists twice and drifts. It has cost us before: web and iOS grew two tables,\ntwo shelf taxonomies and two names — \"Documents\" and \"Vault\" — for the same\nthing, and nobody could say where a deed was without first asking which\ndevice you were holding.\n\nThree tiers, cheapest first.\n\nThe contract says what crosses and what must never. apps/ios/design.md\nallows exactly three things over from the web system, so a diff full of MUI\nand w360.css is mostly nothing to do; and web360.py hangs off Query.web,\nwhich Queries.swift does not read, so most W360 work cannot reach the phone\nuntil someone decides it should. Both are written down so an agent stops\nrather than invents.\n\nparity-check.ts finds the mechanical half with no model in the loop: a\npackages/core module whose PattadarKit twin did not move, stale vectors, a\nfield Queries.swift names that the schema no longer has — which fails the\nWHOLE query, not just that field — a doc taxonomy that split, and a\ncontractual token that moved on one side. The derived paper ramp is reported\nas info, not error: Palette.ground is allowed to differ, and a checker that\ncries wolf is a checker nobody reads.\n\npost-commit does no work. It classifies and hands off to a detached sweep in\na throwaway worktree, because a second session owns apps/ios and a\nbackground writer under it would clobber its file state. The gate is\nswift test — package only, no simulator, no device. verify.sh installs onto\na physical iPhone, so it is deleted from the worktree outright rather than\nfenced by a permission glob, and put back before anything is staged.\n\nNothing is merged for anyone. Sweeps land on parity/ios-<sha> with a report.\n\nProof it bites: geo.ts had grown placeCandidates and ringCentroid and iOS\nhad neither. Both ported here, with vectors, and the geocoder ladder now\nfails a build instead of quietly aiming the map at the wrong district.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0dddf76239b3ff0e5f30f462e311c3d7de86