/reddy-sh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/commits/23fd2a99ebf372a80b3fce453595e61a5361e9e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T01:24:33Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T01:24:33Z","email":"sankara@reddy.sh","name":"Sankara Reddy Telukutla"},"message":"feat(dev): the phone tests against the laptop — no cloud roll per iteration\n\nphone-local.sh: with start-local.sh running (real gateway, real Cognito,\nMinIO, local Postgres — nothing mocked), it bridges the loopback gateway\nonto the LAN, rebuilds the app with the bundle URL pointed at the\nbridge, installs it on the phone, and stays up until Ctrl-C. project.yml\nis restored on exit however it ends, so the repo never keeps the LAN URL\nand the next verify.sh puts production back on the phone. Test locally,\nthen push the api image and roll ECS once, when it is proven.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"faf42700e829727df9b787600b6380e0c16cd275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/git/trees/faf42700e829727df9b787600b6380e0c16cd275"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/reddy-sh/pattadar-platform/git/commits/23fd2a99ebf372a80b3fce453595e61a5361e9e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204504651?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reddy-sh/followers","following_url":"https://api.gith