:{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:03:40Z","email":"306877576+Triconzor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Triconzor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:03:40Z","email":"306877576+Triconzor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Triconzor"},"message":"feat(watch): align match cards with 5Stack\n\nPort the current 5Stack WEB (a3f2c7a2) ticker cell layout to the /watch\nmatch rail cards, keeping the DEAFCS match identity.\n\n- 5Stack cell size, spacing and hierarchy: status line (live dot, round\n  and map, final, start time; pre-match step or \"you\" on the right), two\n  team rows with series pips and score, and the tag line at the foot.\n- Bottom-left: the tournament name for tournament matches (as upstream);\n  otherwise the full DEAFCS mode badge (Competitive / Wingman / Duel in\n  the existing colours) instead of compact 5V5 / 2V2 / 1V1 labels.\n- DEAFCS map backgrounds and the LIVE / stream indicator are preserved;\n  the card still opens the match page and never embeds a player.\n- Map names use the shared display rule (configured label, else the\n  cleaned source name), so unlabeled official maps read \"Dust2\" or\n  \"Ancient\" instead of de_* ids and workshop maps keep their label.\n\nNo API, tournament, match result, ELO or matchmaking logic changes.\n\nTests: watch-page spec 27/27 (updated for the new card; new checks for\nthe mode badge, tournament-name replacement, map names and pips). Node\nand Vitest failures unchanged from baseline (only the known Highlights\nand pre-existing failures); Nuxt production build passes.\n\nAdapted from 5Stack WEB; MIT Copyright (c) 2025 5Stack.gg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fed544704657abeee5e2b56852aebb1d1e77f8dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEAFCS/deafcs-web/git/trees/fed544704657abeee5e2b56852aebb1d1e77f8dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEAFCS/deafcs-web/git/commits/725f2dec1ab2e368334409d67a791ef2876b5e33","verification":{"payload":null,"reas