epos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Triconzor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Triconzor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Triconzor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Triconzor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEAFCS/deafcs-web/commits/b797b953378733d97abcaa73333e2cfca5b432e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:34:47Z","email":"306877576+Triconzor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Triconzor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:34:47Z","email":"306877576+Triconzor@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Triconzor"},"message":"fix(chat): prevent wrapped emoji overlapping actions\n\nThe React button sits just left of the \"...\" menu (absolute right-6, 16px\nwide), i.e. 24-40px from the row''s right edge, while the message column\nonly reserves pr-6 (24px). A first line that ran the full width, such as\na long or continuation message with an emoji at the line end, rendered\nunderneath the controls (always visible on touch devices, on hover on\ndesktop).\n\nA one-line-tall float spacer (float-right h-[1lh] w-5, aria-hidden) now\nleads the message column whenever the React button exists, so only the\nfirst line wraps before the controls. Later lines keep the full width,\nemoji stay inline, short messages and chats without reactions are\nunchanged, and \"...\" stays where it is.\n\nChecked in a real layout engine with the same geometry at 600/340/300/260px:\nbefore, visible overlap on full-width first lines; after, no overlap with\nthe controls'' icons and no extra wrapping of later lines.\n\nTests: new chat-message-layout spec (4); full Vitest 443 passed; git diff\n--check passes. The chat node scripts that fail are the same pre-existing\nfailures as on origin/main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"270c81d767a15aca66658ce7e48894f39997c7fd","url":"https: