ructure guardrails, Foundry rationale and appendix\n\nTighten the oral-defense deck so each slide argues one idea and the\nappendix reads as a single ordered reference section.\n\nMain slides:\n- Fold \"Guardrails we will not trade away\" into \"From OT Signal to\n  Trustworthy Data\" so the guarantees sit with the pipeline they\n  constrain, instead of standing alone a slide later.\n- Replace the ADR-006 one-liner on \"The Four AI Capabilities\" with an\n  argued case for running the intelligence layer as agents in Azure AI\n  Foundry: governed by construction, tools as the only exit, every call\n  is evidence, EU residency without a rebuild.\n- Drop the ADR-006 line from \"Responsible AI & EU AI Act Governance\" in\n  favour of the human-approval guarantee it was standing in for.\n- Colour the \"Security, Identity & EU Data Residency\" tiles so the five\n  principles are separable at a glance.\n- Move Compliance ahead of Responsible AI so the regulatory frame lands\n  before the controls that answer it.\n- Name the method behind the agent swarm: Spec Kit, Superpowers\n  (BMAD-Method, HVE), McKinsey for business, C4 for architecture.\n- Highlight the two near-term phases on \"Next Steps\".\n\nAppendix:\n- Consolidate the two duplicate \"Why We Do Not Write to the Furnace\"\n  slides into one and lead the appendix with it, stating the\n  outbound-only IEC 62443 zone boundary as the reason.\n- Reorder the appendix into the rationale-then-reference sequence and\n  normalise every heading to the \"Appendix — \" prefix, since the old\n  Backup/Appendix split no longer tracks the ordering.\n- Retire the glass-plant reuse and reproducible-evidence slides.\n\nDeck is now 37 timed slides plus 14 appendix slides; test counts, the\nspeaking budget and the README were updated to match.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 8ea14723-183f-4c7e-a275-4b0dca073f38","tree":{"sha":"9b01191ba3e74ab23c12c775501ac8246e013af4","url"