ml_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/95ea15a17ba8245fdffd1f296fab8afdbea7c9eb","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDk1ZWExNWExN2JhODI0NWZkZmZkMWYyOTZmYWI4YWZkYmVhN2M5ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/e47c59b2400243007e54167313c51fd161f6b8d1","sha":"e47c59b2400243007e54167313c51fd161f6b8d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/e47c59b2400243007e54167313c51fd161f6b8d1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4","sha":"166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4"}],"sha":"95ea15a17ba8245fdffd1f296fab8afdbea7c9eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/95ea15a17ba8245fdffd1f296fab8afdbea7c9eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:39:56Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:39:56Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"feat(capture): import an audio file and play it back before upload\n\nOperators often record a walkthrough on a phone recorder or a handheld\ndictaphone before they get near a workstation, and some shop-floor\nbrowsers refuse getUserMedia outright. Both cases previously dead-ended\nthe capture wizard, so this adds a file-import path alongside live\nrecording.\n\nAn imported file lands in exactly the same `stopped` state a live\nrecording produces, so the existing Review step handles playback with no\nnew player: the operator hears the file, sees its name and duration, and\ncan discard or confirm before anything is uploaded.\n\nNotes worth a reviewer''s attention:\n\n- `src/audio/audioFile.ts` normalises the MIME type before validating.\n  Browsers report perfectly valid audio as `audio/x-wav`, `audio/wave`,\n  `audio/x-m4a`, `video/webm` or `application/octet-stream`, none of\n  which are in the BFF allow-list. When the reported type differs from\n  the normalised one the file is re-wrapped with `File.slice` so the\n  multipart part carries a content type the BFF accepts. `TYPE_ALIASES`\n  and `EXTENSION_TYPES` mirror `_AUDIO_ALLOWED_CONTENT_TYPES` in\n  services/bff-api/src/bff_api/routes.py and must stay in sync with it.\n- Type and size (25 MB, the BFF ceiling) are rejected client-side with a\n  translated message rather than after a 2 MB upload round trip.\n- The import controls are rendered in the idle, error and `unsupported`\n  recorder states, so a browser without a microphone can still complete\n  a capture.\n- Duration probing resolves 0 instead of rejecting, and guards the\n  `Infinity` that MediaRecorder WebM streams report. Duration is review\n  metadata only and must never block an otherwise valid file.\n- The multipart filename extension is now derived from the blob type\n  instead of being hardcoded to `.webm`.\n- nginx''s stock mime.types has no `.wav` entry, which left the sample\n  asset as octet-stream and unplayable when opened directly given the\n  nosniff header; the runtime config now maps wav/weba/oga/opus.\n\nThe bundled sample interview narrates\nservices/knowledge-orchestrator/fixtures/interview_transcript.json\nverbatim, which is the transcript the BFF returns in demo mode, so\nimporting it produces audio and a transcript that actually agree.\nscripts/generate-sample-audio.ps1 regenerates it from that same fixture\nto keep the two locked together.\n\nVerified against the deployed environment: the sample is served as\naudio/wav, uploads through the BFF and returns the matching transcript.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 8ea14723-183f-4c7e-a275-4b0dca073f38","tree":{"sha":"9ff117ba0a6615140750b7f77bd5223ff6d8ace2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/9ff117ba0a6615140750b7f77bd5223ff6d8ace2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDE2NmE2OWVlMWY4Yjc2N2Y0MjRhYjlhYTg4MDE4YmFmZjEwOGM2YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/7567c15c6458d965e46194e4d68ba6f37e5cb4c0","sha":"7567c15c6458d965e46194e4d68ba6f37e5cb4c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/7567c15c6458d965e46194e4d68ba6f37e5cb4c0"}],"sha":"166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/166a69ee1f8b767f424ab9aa88018baff108c6a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/7567c15c6458d965e46194e4d68ba6f37e5cb4c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T10:56:11Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T11:01:12Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"Deploy the operator capture PWA as its own Container App\n\nThe voice-capture PWA had no delivery path: no image, no infrastructure and no\nworkflow, so it only ever ran on a developer machine. This packages it the same\nway as the portal and wires it into the existing CI/CD chain.\n\nContainer:\n- Dockerfile (node build -> nginx on 8080) using the same BuildKit named-context\n  convention as portal-shell, because the app is an npm workspace member and\n  imports the shared design tokens from contracts/.\n- runtime/nginx.conf serves the SPA with a fallback, pins hashed /assets forever\n  and marks config.js and service-worker.js no-store/no-cache so a redeploy can\n  never be pinned to a previous environment.\n- runtime/inject-config.sh writes /config.js on container start from\n  CAPTURE_BFF_BASE_URL, so one image is promotable across environments instead\n  of baking the backend origin into the bundle.\n\nInfrastructure and pipeline:\n- apps.bicep gains the capture Container App, gated on a non-empty captureImage\n  so the estate stays deployable before that image exists. It reuses the portal\n  identity: this is a static site whose only data-plane need is an ACR pull.\n- captureOrigin is appended to BFF_CORS_ORIGINS. The PWA is served from its own\n  origin, so without this every capture API call is blocked by the browser.\n- ci-build-services.yml builds and pushes the image by digest and cd-services.yml\n  promotes it to demo, matching how bff-api and portal-shell are handled.\n\nTwo fixes found by running the flow against the deployed BFF rather than a local\none:\n- config.ts never sent X-Demo-Plants. The BFF rejects any demo identity without\n  an NS-DEMO-* plant claim, so every call returned 401 once deployed. Unit tests\n  that stub fetch cannot see this, so config.test.ts now guards it.\n- The demo persona claimed Knowledge.Publisher. An operator captures and submits\n  for review; approving their own procedure would defeat the human-in-the-loop\n  gate, so it now claims Knowledge.Contributor.\n\nVerified against the deployed estate: static assets, manifest and service worker\nall serve, runtime config injection resolves the BFF URL, CORS preflight passes,\nand the full capture flow (interview -> audio -> transcript -> DRAFT ->\nIN_REVIEW) succeeds while operator approval is still refused with 403.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 8ea14723-183f-4c7e-a275-4b0dca073f38","tree":{"sha":"1d93c2680044499048eade3ee596d7532af3e8a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/1d93c2680044499048eade3ee596d7532af3e8a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/7567c15c6458d965e46194e4d68ba6f37e5cb4c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.co