epos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/e95b77cbb97a612bc0c0ca6e476edc2ab1861f9f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/972673100032f6f17f07e9c15c25aef44157beef","sha":"972673100032f6f17f07e9c15c25aef44157beef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/972673100032f6f17f07e9c15c25aef44157beef"}],"sha":"8127cd375dfc097e8439089d83c32cf40836c3b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/8127cd375dfc097e8439089d83c32cf40836c3b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/972673100032f6f17f07e9c15c25aef44157beef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:50:39Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T09:50:39Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"Add operator voice-capture PWA and wire the real Speech-to-Text path\n\nOperators had no way to record a procedure: the Knowledge Hub could create a\nconsent-bound interview, but the BFF injected a hardcoded fixture WAV and the\nAzureSpeechFastTranscriptionAdapter was never instantiated, so the capture\nflow only ever simulated transcription.\n\nFrontend (new apps/operator-capture-mfe):\n- Installable mobile-first PWA: consent gate, MediaRecorder capture with live\n  level meter, local review/retake, multipart upload, transcript polling, and\n  DRAFT creation with submit-for-review.\n- IndexedDB retry so a recording survives a failed upload on a weak network.\n- Hand-written service worker caches the app shell but bypasses every\n  /v1/knowledge/ request so audio and transcripts are never cached.\n- i18n en/fr/de/nl/es, ARIA-labelled controls, dependency versions pinned to\n  analytics-mfe.\n\nBackend:\n- POST /v1/knowledge/interviews/{id}/audio (multipart, 25 MB cap,\n  content-type allow-list, consent-gated) and POST .../draft.\n- New AudioStorageAdapter port with local and Azure Blob implementations;\n  audioRef is opaque and never a SAS URL.\n- Speech and audio-storage adapters now selected from environment config,\n  falling back to local so demo mode stays free of cloud dependencies.\n\nAuthorization fix: operators held Knowledge.Contributor on the new endpoints\nbut interview creation, transcript read, and :submit were still\nKnowledge.Publisher-only, which broke the flow at step one. Those three now\naccept the capture role. :approve and :reject stay Publisher-only, so the\nhuman-in-the-loop gate is unchanged.\n\nVerified with a live end-to-end run (real WAV through transcript, DRAFT, and\nIN_REVIEW in the Knowledge Hub) plus the backend and frontend suites.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 8ea14723-183f-4c7e-a275-4b0dca073f38","tree":{"sha":"cacee33db4b20380f2984ac3152f1f93546e9bab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/cacee33db4b20380f2984ac3152f1f93546e9bab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/972673100032f6f17f07e9c15c25aef44157beef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":n