unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/d67dffd1a69c312f6106fe010b3f1aeb6f1f38bf","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKGQ2N2RmZmQxYTY5YzMxMmY2MTA2ZmUwMTBiM2YxYWViNmYxZjM4YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0","sha":"fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0"}],"sha":"d67dffd1a69c312f6106fe010b3f1aeb6f1f38bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/d67dffd1a69c312f6106fe010b3f1aeb6f1f38bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T14:16:04Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T14:16:04Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"docs(architecture): design the Copilot -> Fabric data agent path\n\nThe Copilot panel cannot reach da-novasteelv3 today, so the usecase-driven\nquestions written for the data agent have nowhere to run. This weighs the\noptions before any code is written.\n\nHeadline finding: ADR-011 deliberately gives the chat no tools and no\nretrieval of operational values, so every option here amends an accepted\ndecision. The native Foundry Fabric tool is ruled out because it requires\nOn-Behalf-Of user identity -- service principals are not supported -- which\nwould force every demo evaluator to hold a Fabric account with READ on the\nlakehouse, the KQL database and the semantic model.\n\nRecommends instead treating the data agent as a third grounding provider in\ncopilot_adapter.chat(), alongside the online and steel corpora. That seam\nalready exists, keeps the BFF as the authorization boundary, leaves ADR-012\nuntouched, works with the offline LocalCopilotChatAgent and carries no\npreview dependency. MCP stays on the roadmap for the operations-agent\nsurface, where tool-level role and site checks already live.\n\nAlso records that the agent''s current description omits the ontology, so an\nMCP orchestrator would never route a genealogy question to it, and proposes\nblending 2 Fabric-backed chips into 6 screens rather than replacing the 275\nexisting suggestion strings.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"f75fde71eaa84d379d90b557ef6fcea093100e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/f75fde71eaa84d379d90b557ef6fcea093100e2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKGZkZTEwNjdmYWM3NjVhNTRlY2MwNGY5ZmE2ZGFhYTkwYTg2ZDNlZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/0586ea43f8855c02cf2033df3dc5ecba198c1c0c","sha":"0586ea43f8855c02cf2033df3dc5ecba198c1c0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/0586ea43f8855c02cf2033df3dc5ecba198c1c0c"}],"sha":"fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/fde1067fac765a54ecc04f9fa6daaa90a86d3ed0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/0586ea43f8855c02cf2033df3dc5ecba198c1c0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T13:26:40Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T13:26:40Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"docs(demo): add a Data Agent question script tied to usecase.md\n\nEvery headline number in docs/usecase/usecase.md is already a row in\ndim_kpi_target, but nothing connected the two for a presenter, and the Data\nAgent prompt never mentioned the business narrative — so \"are we on track\nfor the 14% energy reduction?\" only worked if the model happened to guess\nKPI-ENE-01.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n* The agent prompt gains a business-narrative section: the five challenges\n  (energy at 35% of cost, ETS pressure, the EUR 8M lining failure, high-grade\n  quality, retiring operators), the explicit kpi_id -> outcome -> fact-table\n  mapping for all four committed outcomes plus the three adoption and\n  governance targets, and where each AI infusion point''s evidence lives. It\n  is now told to resolve target-versus-actual questions through\n  dim_kpi_target rather than quoting a number from memory, and to give the\n  actual, the target, the gap and the direction of travel.\n\n* A new presenter script, docs/demo/data-agent-question-script.md, with 33\n  copy-pasteable questions grouped by usecase.md section, the GQL behind the\n  ontology questions, a verified July 2026 KPI scorecard, presenter notes and\n  troubleshooting. It complements docs/demo/demo-runbook.md, which drives the\n  web application; this one drives the agent chat.\n\nThe prompt also gains a data-window guardrail. The gold history ends\n2026-07-29 while the real date is 2026-08-02, so \"today\" and \"this week\"\nreturn nothing from the facts while the same phrasing against KQL is fine.\nThe agent now says so and answers for the most recent period that has data.\nEvery question in the script is phrased to land inside a window that has\nrows.\n\nFigures in the script were verified against the live SQL endpoint rather than\nasserted: energy 10.63 GJ/t, CO2 1.019 tCO2e/t, high-grade first-pass yield\n0.9494 against a 0.972 target, dispatch adoption 0.862, and the BE-EAF-01\nalert episode that fires at exactly 21.0 days of remaining life on 2026-06-19\nagainst a predicted failure of 2026-07-10, with unplanned_outage_flag false\nthroughout. Quality is deliberately left amber — a demo where every KPI is\ngreen reads as a mock-up.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"de8f766b65ecb613d4f110dba7ac7bdd48f4d9da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/de8f766b65ecb613d4f110dba7ac7bdd48f4d9da"},