rl":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/1a136fa0b050df74ffc824c1ae62f095bcbccfec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T21:04:50Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T21:04:50Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"Merge origin/main: converge energy agent on the ADR-019 manifest\n\nmain landed ADR-019 (two Foundry projects, a declarative agent manifest, a\ndeny-by-default tool catalogue and a release-time reconciler) while this branch\nwas in flight. It already hosts `novasteel-energy-advisor` over\n`simulate_energy_dispatch`, which is the same capability this branch built by\nhand as `novasteel-energy-dispatch-agent`.\n\nRather than keep both, this merge drops this branch''s implementation and keeps\nmain''s, because main''s is stronger where it counts:\n\n* Its tool bodies run in the BFF closed over the request''s validated\n  `UserContext` and re-apply `require_any_role` / `require_site`. This branch''s\n  `BffDispatchPort` was bound once at startup and had no per-caller check, so\n  keeping it would have added a second, weaker path to the optimizer.\n* The roster is reviewable data applied at release time, instead of agents\n  created lazily on first request.\n\nThis branch''s Copilot-panel routing is dropped for the same reason: ADR-011\nstates the chat surface receives no tools, and the slide deck advertises that\nas a guardrail. Routing dispatch questions from the chat into the solver would\nhave revoked it silently. `POST /v1/agents/ask` is the intended surface and\nalready exists.\n\nRemoved: `energy_agent.py`, `bff_api/dispatch_port.py`,\n`tests/knowledge/test_energy_agent.py`, `ensure_energy_dispatch_agent()`,\n`HostedEnergyDispatchAgent` and the duplicate client-side tool loop.\n\nKept: the documentation, rewritten to describe the architecture that actually\nships. `MILP_PuLP_CBC.md` still answers the original question in plain language\nand now points at ADR-019; FAQ Q85-Q90 and the optimizer README were corrected\nto match.\n\nValidation: 682 passed, 3 skipped (knowledge + backend); 221 passed\n(presentation + infra + contract).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 8e03b894-1831-4d5c-86d7-4a63eb87645a","tree":{"sha":"fc530789154df9ca829c6043e9aaefafc2be5b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/fc530789154df9ca829c6043e9aaefafc2be5b35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/1a136fa0b050df74ffc824c1ae62f095bcbccfec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/1a136fa0b050df74ffc824c1ae62f095bcbccfec","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDFhMTM2ZmEwYjA1MGRmNzRmZmM4MjRjMWFlNjJmMDk1YmNiY2NmZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/7bdf3582c7fd9583f0d579030ba7ae71c9c47c1f","sha":"7bdf3582c7fd9583f0d579030ba7ae71c9c47c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/7bdf3582c7fd9583f0d579030ba7ae71c9c47c1f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/e0feab8e649ec4dbb3ed3aa87a11a4b5d838c9b1","sha":"e0feab8e649ec4dbb3ed3aa87a11a4b5d838c9b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/e0feab8e649ec4dbb3ed3aa87a11a4b5d838c9b1"}],"sha":"1a136fa0b050df74ffc824c1ae62f095bcbccfec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/1a136fa0b050df74ffc824c1ae62f095bcbccfec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/6c379df8b5e009dace594ca1799c744ced089ac4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T09:11:54Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T09:11:54Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"feat(fabric): restore steel class genealogy inside the IQ ontology\n\nThe consolidation that retired ns-steel-ontology also removed the abstract\nknowledge model, so the Data Agent could no longer answer class or process\ngenealogy questions (\"what does a blast furnace feed\", \"what kind of\nproduction unit is this\", \"what does continuous casting produce\"). Rather\nthan resurrect the standalone ontology_* Delta tables — which nothing could\nreach — the knowledge model is now expressed natively inside the Fabric IQ\nOntology item, so it is queryable with GQL and visible in the ontology UI.\n\nThe ontology now carries two layers joined by a bridge:\n\n* ABox (instances)  Plant -[hasAsset]-> Asset -[hasSensor]-> Sensor, Grade,\n  plus real process genealogy Asset -[supplies]-> Asset derived from\n  dim_asset.parent_asset_id.\n* TBox (vocabulary) EquipmentClass (12, with a -[specializes]-> hierarchy\n  and an IsAbstract flag), ProcessStep (7), ProductType (7), Signal,\n  AlarmType (6), wired by feeds / executes / produces / triggeredBy / halts.\n* Bridge            Asset -[instanceOf]-> EquipmentClass and\n  Sensor -[measures]-> Signal, so a question can walk from a real asset up\n  to its class, reason abstractly, then come back down to instances or join\n  the gold facts on the shared *_key columns.\n\nTwo corrections were made deliberately. The retired notebook asserted\nBlastFurnace -feeds-> ContinuousCaster, which is metallurgically wrong; the\nrestored chain is BlastFurnace -> BasicOxygenFurnace -> ContinuousCaster ->\nReheatFurnace / RollingMill and the original question is answered with a\nfeeds*1..3 path. And the product class is labelled ProductType because\n\"Product\" is a GQL reserved word and is rejected as a node label.\n\nAlso fixes a Fabric behaviour that is easy to miss: the GraphModel item is\nauto-created when an Ontology is first published but is never re-projected\nafterwards, and RefreshGraph only reloads tables already present in its\ndefinition. Every new label therefore failed with \"syntax error or access\nrule violation\" while the old ones worked. The projection is now derived\nfrom the ontology tree by generate-graphmodel-definition.py and published by\nDeploy-GraphModel.ps1, so the two can no longer drift.\n\nVerified live: 9 node types / 11 edge types loaded, all 20 count assertions\nand all 8 demo questions pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"be204b319318acfc5ac7965a38e0caa32f83a16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/be204b319318acfc5ac7965a38e0caa32f83a16e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/6c379df8b5e009dace594ca1799c744ced089ac4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/6c379df8b5e009dace594ca1799c744ced089ac4","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDZjMzc5ZGY4YjVlMDA5ZGFjZTU5NGNhMTc5OWM3NDRjZWQwODlhYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1","sha":"c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1"}],"sha":"6c379df8b5e009dace594ca1799c744ced089ac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/6c379df8b5e009dace594ca1799c744ced089ac4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:02:15Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T22:02:15Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"refactor(fabric): give the gold facts a single authority and cut 11 notebooks to 8\n\nThe workspace had two independent paths MERGEing the same gold facts on the\nsame natural keys, so the last writer won. Live proof before this change:\nfact_energy_daily for 2026-06-10 / NS-DEMO-LUX-01 carried the medallion\ncalculation_version at 0.48 GJ/t, against 17.5-20.7 GJ/t for every other day\nof that integrated-route plant - a corrupt point sitting in the middle of the\nenergy chart.\n\nThe two paths cannot be collapsed into one. The 24-month analytical programme\nis gold-grain BY CONTRACT (contracts/data/gold.v2.json: it \"emits gold facts\ndirectly from the scenario and runs NO SCD2 dimension load\"), so there is no\nevent-level source to replay through bronze. Instead the boundary is now\nexplicit and enforced:\n\n- ns-silver-to-gold gains PROGRAMME_END_DATE and enforce_ownership(). The\n  programme owns every date up to its scenario end_date; the medallion owns\n  everything after. Skipped rows are reported per table in the run summary.\n- ns-validate-data-quality gains DQ-GOLD-004, which fails the gate if any row\n  inside the programme window carries the medallion calculation_version.\n- The medallion pipeline passes PROGRAMME_END_DATE to both notebooks.\n\nNotebook consolidation, 11 -> 8:\n\n- ns-load-operational-envelopes is folded into ns-seed-bronze-from-pack. Both\n  only landed the demo pack and neither was orchestrated. All nine BFF\n  datasets plus manifest are still produced identically - the BFF hard-codes\n  that list in services/bff-api/src/bff_api/fabric_source.py.\n- ns-steel-ontology is retired along with ontology_entity, ontology_relationship\n  and ontology_property. Nothing read them: not the BFF, not the frontend, not\n  the semantic model, not a test. The Fabric IQ ontology item supersedes them\n  for instance-level questions, and the data agent prompt is updated to route\n  structural questions to the graph.\n- ns-ontology-bindings is now an orchestrated activity after Data_Quality_Gate\n  instead of a manual run.\n\nCapability genuinely lost: the data agent can no longer answer abstract class\nquestions such as \"what does a blast furnace feed\", because the graph models\nPlant->Asset->Sensor containment, not process genealogy.\n\nVerified live: analytical loader re-run repaired the corrupt row; all four\nprogramme facts now report exactly one calculation_version; silver-to-gold\nre-ran and wrote zero rows into them; the data-quality gate passes 11/11\nincluding the four new DQ-GOLD-004 checks.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"de2afb937bb053eda464316571fbc40747ba2af5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/de2afb937bb053eda464316571fbc40747ba2af5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKGMwOTY2YWNjZmRmMjljNmZhZGM2OWYxMWE3MDBkMWZiZmQ3ODYwYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80","sha":"8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80"}],"sha":"c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/c0966accfdf29c6fadc69f11a700d1fbfd7860a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:19:13Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T20:19:13Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"feat(fabric): add Fabric IQ ontology between semantic model and data agent\n\nAdds a real Fabric IQ Ontology item (onto_novasteelv3) as the AI-facing\nsemantic layer sitting between the gold star schema and the data agent,\nreplacing the table-only ontology as the agent''s structural entry point.\n\n- fabric/items/onto-novasteelv3.Ontology: 20-part item definition with\n  entity types Plant, Asset, Sensor, Grade and relationship types\n  hasAsset (Plant->Asset) and hasSensor (Asset->Sensor), each with data\n  bindings and overviews.\n- fabric/notebooks/ns-ontology-bindings.Notebook: builds nine onto_*\n  serving tables. Needed because fact_telemetry.event_ts is a string\n  (ontology time-series bindings require a real timestamp) and the dim_*\n  tables are SCD2 (raw binding would duplicate instances).\n- .azure/fabric/Deploy-Ontology.ps1: walks the item tree, base64-encodes\n  every file into a definition part and creates-or-updates via the LRO.\n- tools/fabric/generate-ontology-definition.py: regenerates the tree.\n- Registers the ontology and its companion GraphModel in the deployment\n  manifest, parameters and schema, and makes the data agent depend on it.\n- Teaches the data agent the graph: adds the graph datasource and GQL\n  routing guidance to dataAgent.json.\n\nRelationship types deliberately avoid the name \"contains\" - it is a GQL\nreserved word and fails to parse unless back-quoted, which would be a\ntrap for an agent generating queries at runtime.\n\nVerified live: 4 Plants, 8 Assets, 100 Sensors, 3 Grades, 8 hasAsset and\n100 hasSensor edges, and the two-hop Plant->Asset->Sensor traversal all\nreturn through the GQL query API.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"91c012620a008a4c0c0aeb1410fbd97c839625bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/91c012620a008a4c0c0aeb1410fbd97c839625bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDhjNDRjZmUwNmJlOGRiM2Y3Yjg0N2EyYmM1NWM5Mzg3N2VjNTJhODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e","sha":"959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e"}],"sha":"8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/8c44cfe06be8db3f7b847a2bc55c93877ec52a80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T18:42:14Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T18:42:14Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"feat(fabric): make the medallion produce every silver fact\n\nThe demo workspace only ever had telemetry in bronze, because bronze is fed\nby the Eventstream and the Eventstream only carries whatever a device\nsimulator streamed at the time. Everything downstream of the other event\nfamilies was therefore empty, and three of the silver handlers had never\nactually been run against real payloads - so they had drifted away from the\nevent contracts without anyone noticing.\n\n- Add v3-seed-bronze-from-pack: expands the committed operational envelope\n  pack into landing.bronze_event_envelope with an idempotent MERGE on\n  event_id. Demo/dev/test only, and deliberately skips heat_batch,\n  operator_knowledge, maintenance_event and truth_ledger - those are\n  documents, not event envelopes.\n- Fix the energy handler: the contract emits consumption_mwh/price/\n  grid_carbon_intensity_kgco2e_per_mwh, not energy_gj/spot_price/\n  grid_carbon_kg_per_mwh, so all 96 intervals were quarantined as\n  SCHEMA_INVALID. Read both vocabularies and derive the warehouse columns.\n- Fix the alarm handler: the simulator emits alert_id/status/reason and no\n  transition identifier at all. Map them, and hash alarm+state+transitioned_at\n  into a stable transition_id.\n- Fix the model-inference handler: the quantiles are nested under\n  prediction and the drivers come as a top_factors array; there is no flat\n  p50/prediction_type/top_factors_json in the envelope.\n- payload_column now coalesces payload_json over payload. Both columns\n  coexist once file-seeded and streamed rows share the table, and the\n  Eventstream''s inferred struct silently drops every field except `type`\n  for anything that is not telemetry.\n- Put Load_Reference_Data into the medallion pipeline. It is a hard\n  prerequisite for bronze-to-silver - without the dimensions every event\n  quarantines as UNKNOWN_ASSET - but the pipeline never ran it.\n- Commit the per-sector peer-relative furnace RUL scoring: the old constants\n  were calibrated against SIGNAL_REGISTRY bounds (35-190) while the physics\n  model emits 476-3113 kW/m2, so risk saturated at 0.99 and rul_p50\n  collapsed to 3 days, failing DQ-DEMO-001.\n- Reconcile the KQL database name drift (kql-ns-operations is the live one)\n  and give the Data Agent its authored system prompt.\n- Two parameter tests asserted a workspace that no longer exists: the\n  semantic model is deployed now, and the live KQL database was already\n  named kql-ns-operations.\n\nVerified against the live workspace: bronze carries all five event families,\nsilver has telemetry 2708 / energy 96 / quality 20 / alarm 1 / inference 6,\nquarantine is down to the 16 deliberately malformed envelopes, both pipelines\nrun green end to end, and all 7 data-quality rules pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"4c4a75216b61c4eb43b1eee334684d3d0a3b20b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/4c4a75216b61c4eb43b1eee334684d3d0a3b20b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDk1OWI5ZDhiNWNhNWFkMzFjZDhhOTAzODJmNjdmMzkyZWI1YjY1M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75","sha":"991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75"}],"sha":"959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/959b9d8b5ca5ad31cd8a90382f67f392eb5b653e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T16:50:50Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T16:50:50Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"feat(fabric): seed reference dimensions and key the sensor registry by channel\n\nNothing in the repo ever populated dim_plant/dim_asset/dim_sensor/dim_grade/\ndim_calendar, so bronze-to-silver quarantined 100% of events as UNKNOWN_ASSET\n(DQ-REF-001) and every silver fact table stayed empty.\n\n- simulator: new `python -m simulator generate-reference` exports the five\n  dimensions from the existing PLANTS/ASSETS/SIGNAL_REGISTRY/GRADES config.\n- new v3-load-reference-data notebook loads them idempotently from OneLake\n  Files with a reference_load_audit table for observability.\n- dim_sensor grain is now (sensor_id, signal_code): the generator truncates the\n  signal code to four characters when building a furnace sensor_id, so one\n  sensor_id legitimately carries several channels with different canonical\n  units. Keying on sensor_id alone mis-resolved 312 of 598 telemetry events as\n  DQ-UNIT-001. Contract, catalog and the bronze-to-silver join updated to match.\n- loader conformance tests now assert the suffix-based environment guard.\n\nVerified in NovaSteelV3-Demo: dim_* rows 4/8/100/3/5844, fact_telemetry 598,\nquarantine_event down from 614 to the 16 deliberately malformed envelopes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"d8bd981a08f9aed92103cd3bf50131e094195cb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/d8bd981a08f9aed92103cd3bf50131e094195cb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/frkim","id":74252080,"login":"frkim","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MjUyMDgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDk5MTc5MGVjNTNkNzM3NzZlNWNiM2ZkZGMyNTRiZWRiMTljZjljNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0","sha":"b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0"}],"sha":"991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/991790ec53d73776e5cb3fddc254bedb19cf9c75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1693627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-copilot-cli","id":223556219,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDODVMyew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:58:22Z","email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot App"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:58:22Z","email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot App"},"message":"fix(fabric): parse RFC 4180 quotes and audit per-table gold load outcomes\n\nThe analytical gold loader aborted the whole Spark session on\nfact_furnace_rul. Its top_factors_json column holds a JSON array, which\nthe simulator writes with Python''s csv.writer -- so an embedded quote is\nescaped by doubling it, per RFC 4180. Spark defaults the CSV `escape`\noption to a backslash, so the field never closed and FAILFAST killed the\nrun. Set quote and escape explicitly to the double-quote character.\n\nThe failure was also effectively undiagnosable: the Fabric Jobs API only\nreports \"System_Cancelled_Session_Statements_Failed\" with no Python\ndetail, and the Livy session APIs returned nothing for the run. Catch\nper-table errors, keep loading the remaining datasets, and persist the\noutcome to a gold_load_audit Delta table that can be read straight from\nOneLake. The notebook still fails the job at the end if any table failed,\nso a partial load cannot be mistaken for success.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"e1d4050868ec7cef22ff10858101396ebd4a4b83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/e1d4050868ec7cef22ff10858101396ebd4a4b83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1693627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-copilot-cli","id":223556219,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDODVMyew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKGI2OWZhMDljM2UzYTM3MDQ5ZDYxYjBhZGRjNGJkYzg5MTdhOGM2YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa","sha":"47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa"}],"sha":"b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/b69fa09c3e3a37049d61b0addc4bdc8917a8c6b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1693627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-copilot-cli","id":223556219,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDODVMyew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:28:38Z","email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot App"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:28:38Z","email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot App"},"message":"fix(fabric): deploy notebooks as ipynb so cell content actually persists\n\nFabric''s REST API accepts a notebook definition in the fabricGitSource\n(.py) format with HTTP 202 and a long-running operation that reports\nSucceeded, then silently discards every cell. A subsequent getDefinition\nreturns a three-line stub and getDefinition?format=ipynb returns an empty\ncells array. This was reproduced with the minimal example from the\nMicrosoft Learn docs, so it is not specific to our payloads. Every\nnotebook in the workspace was therefore an empty shell: jobs reported\nSUCCESS in ~33s while writing nothing, leaving lh_novasteelv3_core with\nzero tables.\n\nConvert notebook-content.py to a Jupyter document at deploy time and\npublish with format ipynb, which round-trips faithfully. The converter\nsplits on the CELL/MARKDOWN/METADATA markers, maps per-cell META blocks\nonto cell metadata and the header block onto the kernelspec, and is\nverified to reproduce each cell body byte-for-byte.\n\nAlso pin the Fabric definition sources to LF in .gitattributes and\nnormalize line endings during payload construction, so a Windows\ncheckout with core.autocrlf=true cannot reintroduce marker mismatches.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"987acfc3a11f2f296f3b859ed2103d319b89c4b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/987acfc3a11f2f296f3b859ed2103d319b89c4b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1693627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-copilot-cli","id":223556219,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDODVMyew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa","node_id":"C_kwDOTjwLXNoAKDQ3ZWIyNWJhOWJkNzBkZWE0MzUxMDY5YzlmNzcwY2ZhNWQ2OGE5YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/frkim/NovaSteel3/commit/d90d63f7a8f311f1f8bff7fa642dc1dba811247d","sha":"d90d63f7a8f311f1f8bff7fa642dc1dba811247d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/d90d63f7a8f311f1f8bff7fa642dc1dba811247d"}],"sha":"47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/47eb25ba9bd70dea4351069c9f770cfa5d68a9aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1693627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-copilot-cli","id":223556219,"login":"Copilot","node_id":"BOT_kgDODVMyew","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/d90d63f7a8f311f1f8bff7fa642dc1dba811247d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:07:30Z","email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot App"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:07:30Z","email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Copilot App"},"message":"fix(fabric): deploy loader notebooks, fix OneLake upload and env guard\n\nWire the two previously-undeployed loader notebooks into the deployment so the\ncore lakehouse is actually populated:\n\n- Add notebookLoadOperationalEnvelopes and notebookLoadAnalyticalGold to the\n  items manifest and parameters. These create the nine envelope tables the BFF\n  reads (BFF_DATA_SOURCE=fabric) and the multi-month gold facts respectively.\n  Neither was ever deployed, which is why lh_novasteelv3_core was empty.\n- Load-AnalyticalGold.ps1: replace the ''az storage fs file upload'' fallback with\n  direct OneLake DFS REST (create/append/flush). The blob endpoint rejects\n  OneLake with EndpointUnsupportedAccountFeatures, and the old loop swallowed\n  the error and still reported success.\n- Relax the dev/test/demo environment guard in the three guarded notebooks to\n  accept suffixed environment names such as ''novasteelv3-demo'' while still\n  blocking production. The exact-match set silently failed every run.\n- Add a .platform to the semantic model so updateDefinition?updateMetadata=true\n  stops failing with ''UpdateMetadata is true but .platform file was not provided''.\n- dataAgent.json: ground the agent in the ontology_* tables, the envelope tables\n  and the gold star schema, and add explicit source-routing guidance. The system\n  prompt previously claimed ontology access the wiring never provided.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 25799989-97ab-47a1-8e70-b2840101a6f7","tree":{"sha":"17e586481e440551ad2a1bf20c922cf5f1976f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/17e586481e440551ad2a1bf20c922cf5f1976f39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/d90d63f7a8f311f1f8bff7fa642dc1dba811247d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","sig