nizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/commits/910a331b248dd7de4ea7463d5380099715a1c222/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T14:02:38Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T14:02:38Z","email":"frkim@live.fr","name":"François-Xavier Kim"},"message":"Fix the five defects that deploying the agents exposed\n\nDeploying the merged multi-agent work to a real Foundry estate surfaced five\nbugs that 1129 passing tests did not, because every one of them lived at a\nboundary the tests stubbed out.\n\n- Tool types were imported from `azure.ai.agents.models`, the *classic* SDK.\n  That package has no `WebSearchTool` at all, so the web-search agent raised\n  ImportError the first time it was reconciled. The project-model home for\n  these is `azure.ai.projects.models`.\n- Both Bicep estates gave the operations project the *knowledge* project''s\n  connection names. Connection names are unique per Foundry account, not per\n  project, so the deployment failed with \"Connection ... already exist, and\n  can only be updated by the workspace that created it\". Capability hosts\n  reference connections by name, so the ops capability host has to name the\n  ops connections.\n- `OperationsAgentAdapter.ask()` called `FoundryAgentService(project=...)`,\n  which is not a parameter of that class. Every agent request would have\n  500''d. The service takes a project *endpoint*; `_build_service()` now\n  resolves it the same way the orchestrator''s own hosting path does.\n- The model was never told who was asking, so with `strict=True` tool schemas\n  it guessed `site: \"unknown\"` and `assetId: \"main furnace\"` and every tool\n  call was refused by the authorization layer. Caller scope (server-validated\n  sites and their assets) is now sent as a `developer` message on operations\n  turns only, and the two advisor prompts are told to use those exact ids and\n  never invent one. The scope is derived from the validated `UserContext`, not\n  from the request body, so it cannot be spoofed by the caller.\n- The Cosmos account in `agent-platform.bicep` did not declare\n  `enableAutomaticFailover`, so redeploying the module would have silently\n  turned off failover that is on in the live estate.\n\nVerified against live Azure, not just in tests: all four agents reconcile,\nboth operations agents answer through the deployed BFF with real tool output\nand correct site/asset ids, a caller without the role is refused at the tool\nboundary, a caller asking about a site outside their scope is refused before a\ntool is called, and re-running what-if on the module now reports no changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 19c453da-57c8-48ea-b6e5-9c5f118ffc30","tree":{"sha":"7aa3aa6364495488569acc55400d47dcdc8d2aab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/trees/7aa3aa6364495488569acc55400d47dcdc8d2aab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/frkim/NovaSteel3/git/commits/910a331b248dd7de4ea7463d5380099715a1c222","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74252080?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frkim/gists{/gist_id}","gravat