muelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/e4493b83e06b6461117bef9b4b1be7f8a083d71e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T21:33:21Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T21:33:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app): harden hosting, offline recovery and request reporting (#94)\n\n﻿chore(git): keep local agent instructions untracked\r\n\r\nIgnore the root AGENTS.md alongside the existing local planning documents. Verified with git check-ignore; the guide itself stays off the remote.\r\n\r\nfix(hosting): serve public integrations with compatible headers\r\n\r\nAllow cross-origin iframe embedding and Module Federation imports while keeping the application protected from framing. Stable entries cache for 600 seconds; only hashed assets receive one-year immutable caching. Resolve the iframe API URL from the build environment for Docker. Verified Nginx syntax, response headers, and a cross-origin iframe using the real local API.\r\n\r\nfix(theme): tolerate unavailable browser storage\r\n\r\nFall back to the system theme when storage reads fail and apply theme changes even when persistence fails. Regression tests cover blocked reads and quota errors.\r\n\r\nfix(pwa): preserve the valid offline shell after server errors\r\n\r\nCache only successful HTML navigations and await cache writes without allowing storage errors to break network responses. Regression tests cover HTTP 500 followed by offline navigation, non-HTML responses, failed storage and excluded paths.\r\n\r\nfix(observability): report unexpected request failures safely\r\n\r\nInject query and mutation failure reporting while preserving session redirects and expected client-error handling. Report HTTP status or schema issue codes and paths without request variables, API bodies or original error messages. Tests cover exhausted retries, schema drift, mutation failures, cancellation and telemetry filtering.","tree":{"sha":"16ecabc03d95a816f59f0e623bd73fd7b43f4ac6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/16ecabc03d95a816f59f0e623bd73fd7b43f4ac6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/e4493b83e06b6461117bef9b4b1be7f8a083d71e","verification":{"payload":"tree 16ecabc03d95a816f59f0e623bd73fd7b43f4ac6\nparent f2d46af8d9b1a1e78bd784c1aa28e5e3ea3c8deb\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788816801 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788816801 -0300\n\nfix(app): harden hosting, offline recovery and request reporting (#94)\n\n﻿chore(git): keep local agent instructions untracked\r\n\r\nIgnore the root AGENTS.md alongside the existing local planning documents. Verified with git check-ignore; the guide itself stays off the remote.\r\n\r\nfix(hosting): serve public integrations with compatible headers\r\n\r\nAllow cross-origin iframe embedding and Module Federation imports while keeping the application protected from framing. Stable entries cache for 600 seconds; only hashed assets receive one-year immutable caching. Resolve the iframe API URL from the build environment for Docker. Verified Nginx syntax, response headers, and a cross-origin iframe using the real local API.\r\n\r\nfix(theme): tolerate unavailable browser storage\r\n\r\nFall back to the system theme when storage reads fail and apply theme changes even when persistence fails. Regression tests cover blocked reads and quota errors.\r\n\r\nfix(pwa): preserve the valid offline shell after server errors\r\n\r\nCache only successful HTML navigations and await cache writes without allowing storage errors to break network responses. Regression tests cover HTTP 500 followed by offline navigation, non-HTML responses, failed storage and excluded paths.\r\n\r\nfix(observability): report unexpected request failures safely\r\n\r\nInject query and mutation failure reporting while preserving session redirects and expected client-error handling. Report HTTP status or schema issue codes and paths without request variables, API bodies or original error messages. Tests cover exhausted retries, schema drift, mutation failures, cancellation and telemetry filtering.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqny2hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7iQQAGmY8UwVHIx+gRWVYn0iEQf7\nQwb3vp+xl2biUv1QObamMGY4UPF/D3xWLkI6LzedrSl5xCxiUK4j93uLsvdxPdJS\nubAWr6N7ynWN2SXkLgDPOEyfkRL56igQj+SpJPXykw+Sk/I4JRZDKeZuXSbgyfPj\nrrFDFkvRSZwIECqXh+3rao4JP2nQaEd0HswkKC8umCXk1g90wLt08OMGCYyfmNyI\n/qs4wk05EOO6aJgqdncRFQeGxZNNMKohpFjPN3uwmYikLff4T+qP6FUQL9gyBktz\nxMVPhsAJ1ciDEj7rr6BzfWJwA+6dco0zGwfyHK2zeGuOZVVxQG6Tt6fsrCujPyzD\nQzlGRjCKsHokDDkQpadXFFYRs7QW0wHfNGdnLADhARY110TJaEpeLYEBiN4SffCT\nz8TwP30CXqYH0UNSrCy8kRQsxYYyEPduVPWbUAeQqb8AlEq34pQDC5a/8tdLDyHz\nMz2NtMpev19XLfZGI0ro8o55iu47gj8lqJMWw180px/RbB56pax2elGizFxGkny5\natWtoPK7Iq30xtKPIDyPVTB4EKWgzYdr2aaEqtneRwH0OEmh9rj/NgFlJTD7ZrKb\nxUlyD7yANdm24uoRIfLa06OTyZCaLmWLbNhs81WxmADwjZbh3Xwtu69jbTWCq3pO\nIQBh2y483YHwlpJMU7YL\n=2jUV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T21:33:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/e4493b83e06b6461117bef9b4b1be7f8a083d71e","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGU0NDkzYjgzZTA2YjY0NjExMTdiZWY5YjRiMWJlN2Y4YTA4M2Q3MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/f2d46af8d9b1a1e78bd784c1aa28e5e3ea3c8deb","sha":"f2d46af8d9b1a1e78bd784c1aa28e5e3ea3c8deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f2d46af8d9b1a1e78bd784c1aa28e5e3ea3c8deb"}],"sha":"e4493b83e06b6461117bef9b4b1be7f8a083d71e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/e4493b83e06b6461117bef9b4b1be7f8a083d71e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f2d46af8d9b1a1e78bd784c1aa28e5e3ea3c8deb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:36:27Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:36:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(profile): offer the mailed code when there is no password to type (#93)\n\nThe delete dialog asked for a password, which an account created by signing in\nwithout one does not have — its hash is random bytes, so no password is ever\ncorrect and the dialog was a door with no key on exactly the accounts that most\nneeded it (`cygnus-api` #36 measured it: 400 \"Incorrect current password\").\n\nThere is a link under the password field now — \"Não tenho senha — receber um\ncódigo por e-mail\" — which asks the API to mail a code and swaps the field.\n\n**The app cannot detect which accounts have a password**, and does not try: the\nrandom hash is indistinguishable from a real one, so the person says. That is\nalso why the password path is untouched for everybody else.\n\nSubmitting in code mode does not go through `handleSubmit`: the resolver still\nrequires the password, and validating it there would make the submit never reach\nthe handler — silently, which is the worst way for a delete button to fail.\n\n263 unit tests, 91 stories, lint, tsc -b green.","tree":{"sha":"9a468eccb3336749510f00b546bc7cb5dee9300d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/9a468eccb3336749510f00b546bc7cb5dee9300d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/f2d46af8d9b1a1e78bd784c1aa28e5e3ea3c8deb","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a468eccb3336749510f00b546bc7cb5dee9300d\nparent 90b46875bf3ef7e2ab8f5752171009615f030bd8\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788813387 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788813387 -0300\n\nfeat(profile): offer the mailed code when there is no password to type (#93)\n\nThe delete dialog asked for a password, which an account created by signing in\nwithout one does not have — its hash is random bytes, so no password is ever\ncorrect and the dialog was a door with no key on exactly the accounts that most\nneeded it (`cygnus-api` #36 measured it: 400 \"Incorrect current password\").\n\nThere is a link under the password field now — \"Não tenho senha — receber um\ncódigo por e-mail\" — which asks the API to mail a code and swaps the field.\n\n**The app cannot detect which accounts have a password**, and does not try: the\nrandom hash is indistinguishable from a real one, so the person says. That is\nalso why the password path is untouched for everybody else.\n\nSubmitting in code mode does not go through `handleSubmit`: the resolver still\nrequires the password, and validating it there would make the submit never reach\nthe handler — silently, which is the worst way for a delete button to fail.\n\n263 unit tests, 91 stories, lint, tsc -b green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnyBLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArqcQAGYjZ7SZQsllX19bzpcew/Y0\nqpXHp7Tl3Irq1XIvbYgKSa44egH79Up3rdCJEfjFww1cNtUcl+n7qB5vxCZ6bi6V\n9chPaFrHOIcEZF5tzVNBb3IwxuivUwvhKA4AfFpS9PoHHy3oQ7NLfFTqZ2WEXVcS\nR6yhd+iAluaamVxDheY4V0joCw7/oEmctODcbHLD/2Oc6wxlhzsXXRYaECnx7mK2\nkbqq1fhY0C5/dvCCLhfrrGdvESZlu/3r7fSt0JpSJD+rCyoKIN2xwj1FI9/xkFIZ\nyxGYlhlaacqyqDzcqP46wbZ0wOfXR0j0OJWx/xl7RlvC2iScr7v02eYNgrXPosSy\nKGnbDGoW96P8aokWzCRG+C1ijYNFzUzZhr8TDHsy4vQMqdHAUJh