tting the padding\nback to `p-2` at seven items reports 43.43. Both were tried and reverted.\n\n`md:hidden` moves to the shell, and that is not incidental. On the\ncomponent the bar is `display: none` in the story canvas, which has no\nboxes to measure — the same class that makes it a phone-only bar would\nhave made the test measure nothing and pass. Where it applies belongs to\nthe shell anyway, beside the two headers it already switches at the same\nbreakpoint.\n\n* feat(nav): a tab for the care team, and a bar re-measured to hold it\n\n`/profissionais` has been reachable only from the profile page since it\ngot a page of its own (#83). A professional is looked up as often as an\nappointment is, and one screen away from the profile is not where that\nlookup starts. It becomes the seventh tab; `/plano-de-saude` does not,\nand the asymmetry is the difference between something looked up daily\nand a card number looked up at a clinic desk.\n\nThe seventh item does not fit for free. Targets are `flex-1`, so each is\n`(bar width − padding) / items`, and seven under the bar''s `p-2` measure\n43.4px at 320px — below the 44px floor (WCAG 2.5.5, AAA) that six\ncleared at 50.7px. Two paddings answer for two different things:\n\n- the **bar''s**, halved to `px-1`, decides the target: 44.6 / 50.3 /\n  54.6px at 320 / 360 / 390. Halving rather than removing keeps the\n  active pill off the screen edge.\n- the **item''s**, given up entirely, decides only how much of that\n  target the label may use — it cannot change the target at all. With it\n  at `px-1`, \"Consultas\" and \"Remédios\" truncate at every width; without\n  it, nothing truncates at 360 or 390, which is better than what the\n  six-item bar shipped.\n\nSo the bar carries one more destination and cuts fewer words than\nbefore. 320px still truncates those two, and that is the one width where\nseven items cost something.\n\nMeasured on the container build, signed in, at all three widths — and\nagain as five variants against the built CSS, which is how the item''s\npadding turned out to be the lever that mattered. A `px-0.5` variant\nmeasured identical to no padding at all, because Tailwind never\ngenerated that class: a variant that invents a class silently measures\nsomething else.\n\nUsersIcon, not the stethoscope the page itself uses — the bar would\ncarry the same glyph twice, side by side, and at 320px the icon is what\nstill means something after the label truncates.\n\n* test(e2e): follow the bar to its new label and its new tab\n\nThe a11y sweep walks the app by clicking nav links by name, so renaming\nthe notifications label to \"Avisos\" broke it: `waiting for\ngetByRole(''link'', { name: ''Notificações'' })`, then a timeout. It failed\non the first local run after the rename and would not have failed in CI,\nwhich does not run this suite — the label was three commits old by then.\n\nThe sweep also now follows the new tab. `/profissionais` is a main page\nof the app as of this branch, and a page nothing scans is a page whose\nviolations nobody finds; it reports clean, empty state included.\n\nRun against the local stack: 7 passed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnM+LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa3cQAHNoLSIPJ5YKluySI8tSRdBB\nMkr29PXp/hK+9jvHfrqfhigQkS9eZKkV6umZJtzfVi9cGV0uUjJT8IbvXc4zoTSj\nNw2knbX9YlyF+CMvzniY8XVHI796TLi+g/tRuntSgngg3/qCLr0MO0IMwhKj9uHH\nz73qDnPNw49FWP1AF9xt4UtO+2F1jUMjw5Hau4jmRj/INRa32cbDsdyrI9iMcwIn\nEeC8FdEA2MVtjNHP/aRjmJL/M+Jx8+tj7A5NbJSlzk93XUuAn2gfyz3kWOjdHVcJ\n80tZtg2PWe8BLKuVJuNjCtTKFgTCYMNQphDoDIrcneBLqHmOo6PLTKigVxUi8dBg\nAF52mcOdWWkLaTTdkUuxhj80GKmHmJI4rzhO75z4tF8moW5cGC2QsJ+M+H2IY/dS\nNDfDs78QCjOpS3NrOqLRiSnNeVPg33euUUqEAZk2KP6nb/5qkzC6kKl24BQ0tiE/\nb6JqPTcgJTWOdRAa4FI/pgT8bK6zNpK9S1Fus9WxnaPkDK4dhZcshczhJCRBHAqz\nkVhOu09hEJfC7mtmFHYHoH1QkPhvCCfVA/s7wErDztcGsJSE20w+hlvrTv8rrmt6\nzwbojbAj7bgHtucp3PPyNbWQesMkE8QbnraWc0jYZKsF29Ydd+o/8wJyVB1tY5Y5\nK+WVF4yLY1ht+IPFNVXp\n=cYHT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T02:27:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/b25a447c58488994aac312de4e698d5eb9b2b378","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGIyNWE0NDdjNTg0ODg5OTRhYWMzMTJkZTRlNjk4ZDVlYjliMmIzNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/0626a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d","sha":"0626a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/0626a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d"}],"sha":"b25a447c58488994aac312de4e698d5eb9b2b378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b25a447c58488994aac312de4e698d5eb9b2b378"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/0626a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:46:46Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:46:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(specialists): a page of their own, and the health plan beside it (#83)\n\nTwo records that belong to the account stopped living inside one child''s\nedit dialog.\n\n**Profissionais** is now `/profissionais`. It had to move: the entry\nbelongs to the account, and a form for account data nested inside a\nspecific child''s profile is the wrong place to edit it — you would open\nElis to change the paediatrician that also sees Miguel. The page carries\nwhat the new model needs and the old section could not express: which\nchildren a professional sees (none is a valid answer), and which guardians\nit was shared with.\n\nEach card says which of those it is, because the difference between \"I\nsaved a phone number\" and \"I saved it and the other parent sees it\" is\ninvisible in a list and is exactly the decision the person just made.\nEditing and removing only appear on entries you own: the API answers 404\nto anyone else, and a button that always fails is worse than no button.\n\n**Plano de Saúde** is now `/plano-de-saude`, every child on one screen.\nIt left the profile form for the opposite reason — it is what gets looked\nup at a clinic desk, alone and in a hurry, and it was sitting between the\nphoto, the birth date and the allergies, behind an edit button inside a\ndialog. The question arrives as \"what is Miguel''s card number?\", so the\nanswer is a screen where the children are side by side.\n\nBoth hang off the profile page rather than the bottom bar. Measured\nearlier today: six items give each target 51px at 320px, and an eighth\nwould drop them to ~38px, under the 44px floor. `/profile` is where the\naccount settings and the list of children already live.\n\nThe appointment form now reads the account-level list filtered to the\nchild, from the same cache — no extra request. Saving a professional from\ninside that form still links it to the child of the appointment, which is\nthe context the person is in; the other children and the sharing are left\nto the page, because a trigger that asks three questions is no longer\ninline and ignorable.","tree":{"sha":"68f0a9ba04e3498e6a0ab8fa7799e57614eef896","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/68f0a9ba04e3498e6a0ab8fa7799e57614eef896"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/0626a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d","verification":{"payload":"tree 68f0a9ba04e3498e6a0ab8fa7799e57614eef896\nparent 83051d8b8475ae428f53f1599738fc58f0de2d3c\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788569206 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788569206 -0300\n\nfeat(specialists): a page of their own, and the health plan beside it (#83)\n\nTwo records that belong to the account stopped living inside one child''s\nedit dialog.\n\n**Profissionais** is now `/profissionais`. It had to move: the entry\nbelongs to the account, and a form for account data nested inside a\nspecific child''s profile is the wrong place to edit it — you would open\nElis to change the paediatrician that also sees Miguel. The page carries\nwhat the new model needs and the old section could not express: which\nchildren a professional sees (none is a valid answer), and which guardians\nit was shared with.\n\nEach card says which of those it is, because the difference between \"I\nsaved a phone number\" and \"I saved it and the other parent sees it\" is\ninvisible in a list and is exactly the decision the person just made.\nEditing and removing only appear on entries you own: the API answers 404\nto anyone else, and a button that always fails is worse than no button.\n\n**Plano de Saúde** is now `/plano-de-saude`, every child on one screen.\nIt left the profile form for the opposite reason — it is what gets looked\nup at a clinic desk, alone and in a hurry, and it was sitting between the\nphoto, the birth date and the allergies, behind an edit button inside a\ndialog. The question arrives as \"what is Miguel''s card number?\", so the\nanswer is a screen where the children are side by side.\n\nBoth hang off the profile page rather than the bottom bar. Measured\nearlier today: six items give each target 51px at 320px, and an eighth\nwould drop them to ~38px, under the 44px floor. `/profile` is where the\naccount settings and the list of children already live.\n\nThe appointment form now reads the account-level list filtered to the\nchild, from the same cache — no extra request. Saving a professional from\ninside that form still links it to the child of the appointment, which is\nthe context the person is in; the other children and the sharing are left\nto the page, because a trigger that asks three questions is no longer\ninline and ignorable.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm2Z2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlskQADbV9dxUbzfKRDzeabuM68DE\nJPXXSMrOgg/h4LI+1KR8Wh/YjXe3j9x6zi4bSjaHwrtv+YHzmfMg7KKdqKSyZz/q\nExhMN+2PfVSzqayVFdpmqd5+H5WeE+57CcKQ3zYQKPcvE2/jgiA/WvSzEZWLVkVu\nMTSWzGQSXEFgGJEVhf+tmseuC7ifKaW8Wi+scczJZs5prKkXDR1O21+