26a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/0626a5c755380569d30baa188c43379c8b34552d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/83051d8b8475ae428f53f1599738fc58f0de2d3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T20:25:25Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T20:25:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(babies): sex at birth is optional, and named for what it is (#82)\n\nThree vocabularies described one column: `gender` in code, \"Sexo\" on\nscreen, \"Menino/Menina\" in the labels. In a child''s health record the\nuseful variable is **sex at birth** — what the Caderneta da Criança prints\nand what DATASUS registers — and gender identity is a different datum with\na different purpose. The field now says which one it is.\n\n**It is also optional now, and that is the part that mattered.** It was\nrequired at sign-up and read by nothing: not by the PNI calendar, not by\nany screen. The same one-way street `bloodType` and `allergies` were on\nbefore #69, except this one was mandatory and is sensitive data about a\nchild. Demanding it with no use is exactly the collection a privacy policy\nhas to justify and cannot.\n\n\"Prefiro não informar\" writes **absence**, not a third enum value. Two\nways to say the same thing in one field is how a query starts returning\nthe wrong rows.\n\nThe three cards are stacked rather than side by side, and that is\nmeasured, not taste: three across the dialog''s left column give each card\n104px, where \"Masculino\" needs 71px of text in the 48px it gets and spills\nover its neighbour. Two fitted; three do not.\n\nDepends on cygnus-api#32, which ships the rename with a deprecated\n`gender` bridge so the currently deployed frontend keeps working between\nthe two deploys.\n\nOne E2E fixture needed fixing on the way: typing the birth date leaves the\ncalendar open, and the click that followed was landing on the popover\nrather than the field below it. It went unnoticed while the sex field had\ntwo options and the target sat clear of the overlay; with three it does\nnot. The helper now closes the calendar, which is what a person does\nwithout thinking.","tree":{"sha":"a40bab6080ce611b99a7463df51e8fd6f8df80f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/a40bab6080ce611b99a7463df51e8fd6f8df80f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/83051d8b8475ae428f53f1599738fc58f0de2d3c","verification":{"payload":"tree a40bab6080ce611b99a7463df51e8fd6f8df80f7\nparent 067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788553525 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788553525 -0300\n\nfeat(babies): sex at birth is optional, and named for what it is (#82)\n\nThree vocabularies described one column: `gender` in code, \"Sexo\" on\nscreen, \"Menino/Menina\" in the labels. In a child''s health record the\nuseful variable is **sex at birth** — what the Caderneta da Criança prints\nand what DATASUS registers — and gender identity is a different datum with\na different purpose. The field now says which one it is.\n\n**It is also optional now, and that is the part that mattered.** It was\nrequired at sign-up and read by nothing: not by the PNI calendar, not by\nany screen. The same one-way street `bloodType` and `allergies` were on\nbefore #69, except this one was mandatory and is sensitive data about a\nchild. Demanding it with no use is exactly the collection a privacy policy\nhas to justify and cannot.\n\n\"Prefiro não informar\" writes **absence**, not a third enum value. Two\nways to say the same thing in one field is how a query starts returning\nthe wrong rows.\n\nThe three cards are stacked rather than side by side, and that is\nmeasured, not taste: three across the dialog''s left column give each card\n104px, where \"Masculino\" needs 71px of text in the 48px it gets and spills\nover its neighbour. Two fitted; three do not.\n\nDepends on cygnus-api#32, which ships the rename with a deprecated\n`gender` bridge so the currently deployed frontend keeps working between\nthe two deploys.\n\nOne E2E fixture needed fixing on the way: typing the birth date leaves the\ncalendar open, and the click that followed was landing on the popover\nrather than the field below it. It went unnoticed while the sex field had\ntwo options and the target sat clear of the overlay; with three it does\nnot. The helper now closes the calendar, which is what a person does\nwithout thinking.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmyk1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAndAQAHbpaCzRDSghpXDL1w8+nMVb\nlvX+cLMTBDnCcX/fex2ohwgrEtKOIQPskeEEB5QxKRMiNOKtimBO9gCr3QoC7nJH\nxt3VjV1OF61XqS5NNDqguuv8lKZOtXIq4cOm0ppOEwiPbwgM+I8DZZrEr3+TlF6P\njRLTsr7At5uxwiTFBywAsXpdJvovpKs9jJNOo+lylwaEO1lpisjK09qGIKoFDNSI\n7UAPfDryfrguudRWfOWdahuqo5HJBXUS+FgURzJHpKftZKHC44W9Un0QXH6AGb5d\nLSQLXm+1N6OF+2q+PpQcsocI9gO0alrudXDIYx4UH95hppOgdsHjdVjxW3dfFBbj\nOa2TTfs/P9uQncLoQPNoz2A7NLvDgF8SOq9/kQGmm8Bm2JNGUiJpJ9Yso7w+v+EI\nL+Rk6y46V/8i083uyn4BlNUqFEN9X03JTYfGPjiJ+6t+JXgEjofHvnRUqsrVPJoZ\ntZQJaMXtHVg3owmZMJdfRM5bcU81eY42T8DXKzNlZ8g6DJfjHFcSeZn6rprSnYUh\naWKTk1ORDWijBNuOWhnrKWqBiP4zeellWuYYqTsZtqOusVKyt3a7ns12ueq4D4Q9\n2PV/bClquOJ6wZVSGvFb/I8qccjGftw+mNYekCy/YQyGEk8ENA4ywghKITV2gO+1\nHqxZfgfJzd+oFTnjkzu9\n=DC0A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T20:25:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/83051d8b8475ae428f53f1599738fc58f0de2d3c","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDgzMDUxZDhiODQ3NWFlNDI4ZjUzZjE1OTk3MzhmYzU4ZjBkZTJkM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85","sha":"067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85"}],"sha":"83051d8b8475ae428f53f1599738fc58f0de2d3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/83051d8b8475ae428f53f1599738fc58f0de2d3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T20:21:30Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T20:21:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(profile): stop asking for a password nobody needed to type (#80)\n\n* fix(dialogs): keep the coloured header in place while the body scrolls\n\nEvery dialog with a coloured header put `overflow-y-auto` on the dialog\nitself, so the header scrolled away with the content. In the child''s edit\ndialog that is 1209px of content in an 810px box on desktop, and 1601 in\n760 on a phone: the title, the child''s name and the close button all leave\nthe screen on the first swipe, and the way back to them is scrolling up.\n\nThe content box is now a flex column that clips, the header does not\nshrink, and the body is what scrolls. Measured after: the dialog itself no\nlonger scrolls at all (`scrollHeight === clientHeight`) and the body does.\n\nSix dialogs share the defect and the fix, because they share the shape:\nadd and edit a child, add an appointment, add and edit a medication, add a\nmilestone. Fixing one and leaving five identical ones is how a pattern\nturns into an exception nobody can explain later.\n\n* refactor(babies): one way to set a photo, and cards that get the full width\n\nTwo things were wrong with the child''s form, and both were about blocks\nsitting where fields belong.\n\n**The cards were inside a column.** Guardians, professionals and the\ndanger zone rendered in the right-hand column, under the health fields.\nThat produced a tall void below the left column — which ends at \"Sexo\" —\nand squeezed every card into half the width, where the header of each one\n(icon, title, description and button) wrapped into four lines. A card is a\nblock, not a field; it does not share a column with a form. The grid now\nholds only the fields, and the cards run full width beneath it.\n\n**The photo had two ways in and one of them was theatre.** The paste-a-URL\ninput took the whole width of the block and asked the person to have the\nimage hosted somewhere, which almost nobody does. What people actually do\nis pick a file, which the camera button already did. The input is gone and\nremoving the photo is now a labelled action rather than an \"x\" attached to\na field that no longer exists.\n\nAn `avatarUrl` already stored as an http address still renders: the schema\ndid not change, only the way to fill it.\n\nThe dialog''s test used to set the avatar by typing in that URL field —\ncovering the real path by proxy. It now drives the file input for real,\nwith `createImageBitmap` and canvas stubbed, since jsdom implements\nneither. That is more mocking than before and it buys the path that\nactually ships.\n\n* fix(profile): stop asking for a password nobody needed to type\n\nOpening this page to change the language showed **four password fields**:\n\"senha atual\" in the account form, plus current, new and confirm in the\npassword section. None of them was needed to be there.\n\nThe one in the account form is only required when the e-mail changes —\nthat is the backend''s rule and the schema already mirrored it — so it now\nappears exactly when it becomes required, and never for someone editing\ntheir own name.\n\nThe password section is a button. The three fields render after somebody\nasks to change the password, and collapse again once it is changed, with\nthe values cleared. Cancelling does the same.\n\nThe reason is not tidiness. Changing a password is a deliberate, rare\ntask; a password field standing open on a settings page trains people to\ntype a password without asking what for, and that is the last habit to\nteach in an app holding a child''s health record.\n\nThree tests lock the behaviour: no password field exists until asked, the\nsection returns to the button after a successful change with nothing left\nin the inputs, and the account form only asks for the current password\nonce the e-mail actually differs.","tree":{"sha":"5ca9c8d8e2d3ab30818a6492c516e3231c66371c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/5ca9c8d8e2d3ab30818a6492c516e3231c66371c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ca9c8d8e2d3ab30818a6492c516e3231c66371c\nparent 537cc60c2bd3f11c4188dbf93080f183d4fb2656\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788553290 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788553290 -0300\n\nfix(profile): stop asking for a password nobody needed to type (#80)\n\n* fix(dialogs): keep the coloured header in place while the body scrolls\n\nEvery dialog with a coloured header put `overflow-y-auto` on the dialog\nitself, so the header scrolled away with the content. In the child''s edit\ndialog that is 1209px of content in an 810px box on desktop, and 1601 in\n760 on a phone: the title, the child''s name and the close button all leave\nthe screen on the first swipe, and the way back to them is scrolling up.\n\nThe content box is now a flex column that clips, the header does not\nshrink, and the body is what scrolls. Measured after: the dialog itself no\nlonger scrolls at all (`scrollHeight === clientHeight`) and the body does.\n\nSix dialogs share the defect and the fix, because they share the shape:\nadd and edit a child, add an appointment, add and edit a medication, add a\nmilestone. Fixing one and leaving five identical ones is how a pattern\nturns into an exception nobody can explain later.\n\n* refactor(babies): one way to set a photo, and cards that get the full width\n\nTwo things were wrong with the child''s form, and both were about blocks\nsitting where fields belong.\n\n**The cards were inside a column.** Guardians, professionals and the\ndanger zone rendered in the right-hand column, under the health fields.\nThat produced a tall void below the left column — which ends at \"Sexo\" —\nand squeezed every card into half the width, where the header of each one\n(icon, title, description and button) wrapped into four lines. A card is a\nblock, not a field; it does not share a column with a form. The grid now\nholds only the fields, and the cards run full width beneath it.\n\n**The photo had two ways in and one of them was theatre.** The paste-a-URL\ninput took the whole width of the block and asked the person to have the\nimage hosted somewhere, which almost nobody does. What people actually do\nis pick a file, which the camera button already did. The input is gone and\nremoving the photo is now a labelled action rather than an \"x\" attached to\na field that no longer exists.\n\nAn `avatarUrl` already stored as an http address still renders: the schema\ndid not change, only the way to fill it.\n\nThe dialog''s test used to set the avatar by typing in that URL field —\ncovering the real path by proxy. It now drives the file input for real,\nwith `createImageBitmap` and canvas stubbed, since jsdom implements\nneither. That is more mocking than before and it buys the path that\nactually ships.\n\n* fix(profile): stop asking for a password nobody needed to type\n\nOpening this page to change the language showed **four password fields**:\n\"senha atual\" in the account form, plus current, new and confirm in the\npassword section. None of them was needed to be there.\n\nThe one in the account form is only required when the e-mail changes —\nthat is the backend''s rule and the schema already mirrored it — so it now\nappears exactly when it becomes required, and never for someone editing\ntheir own name.\n\nThe password section is a button. The three fields render after somebody\nasks to change the password, and collapse again once it is changed, with\nthe values cleared. Cancelling does the same.\n\nThe reason is not tidiness. Changing a password is a deliberate, rare\ntask; a password field standing open on a settings page trains people to\ntype a password without asking what for, and that is the last habit to\nteach in an app holding a child''s health record.\n\nThree tests lock the behaviour: no password field exists until asked, the\nsection returns to the button after a successful change with nothing left\nin the inputs, and the account form only asks for the current password\nonce the e-mail actually differs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmyhKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJvAQAHGKPpR04w7jpp4oyXm0CP4J\nAnzOXXlHQtyx1MoCPqnI2wUMQYUAbVY35+SPvd8ukKpqvtay+sj/NKGIbaieiuoS\nRsbu3Ei/IoFCIni7TjSfPSzGBobJ0IDYtxfVgdWWgSHI9Mgd4sWSTyjP04Z76aXu\nVrUdEFt/eaGxwucn+prZwQEiUvhUNvZ1jfEU7bk7DfOqBP/pIjGIwQyY3GtEf2qy\npr24agAoDojyWjbZVfzWaN5+f5H1e5HsEIQ6StiZzuCn4ZBAiOTv9Qz0zLMSpqy3\n3Vv4lvmQHtvtPfv+QRkomlG753i2tEnWdDx8Odo05K95EKnpv3Zy8OZZ9LPDDdKt\nLiY7O/LCW++6xqUYilAN5MnKzYmwGee9/89WKDtCs8+iB4OaEZQRTk92D56OQ52P\npvYEW5fOdcG7m9WM4nhBVf/wUfW9JVE2BOpQKzeEYT73xGfJTcTZGSt4886rv3ET\nR6qx/1xJ+5LqpjxKGX+hV8nAmw/gcEP5LWdEIHWr65cGySYvD/ZO0nKneGSgEzU9\nJDRxxFU+W79t+7Jy4rT0HLTVKpCBjJ1W6jO3bEo65ytx7gq6d8iFLr6U0mYF69R0\nByAl2cdU36qnRkQiZy9hyAUVZos+zxPBPOYs6ctK/qJiuTuPhl21U/RMjnFqjGod\ndP7IfrozjjnSwYa+DXcs\n=rpCx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T20:21:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDA2N2JhOThlMTlmNzk3ZThmNjU5ZWI5OGY5YWRjYWUyMThlOTljODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/537cc60c2bd3f11c4188dbf93080f183d4fb2656","sha":"537cc60c2bd3f11c4188dbf93080f183d4fb2656","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/537cc60c2bd3f11c4188dbf93080f183d4fb2656"}],"sha":"067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/067ba98e19f797e8f659eb98f9adcae218e99c85"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/537cc60c2bd3f11c4188dbf93080f183d4fb2656/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:39:29Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:39:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(brand): a mark for Ninho, drawn from the display face (#79)\n\n* fix(pwa): the installed app still called itself Meu Neném\n\nThe rename in #78 changed twelve strings and missed two, both in\n`public/manifest.webmanifest`: `name` and `short_name`. They are what\nAndroid and iOS print under the icon once somebody installs the app, so\nthe one place the old name would have survived is the home screen — the\nmost visible surface there is.\n\nThe miss has a cause worth naming: the search that drove that change\ncovered `src/`, `index.html`, `README.md` and `e2e/`, and `public/` was\nnot in it. Static assets carry user-facing copy too.\n\n* feat(brand): a mark for Ninho, drawn from the display face\n\nThe logo was a heart — generic on its own, and since medications took a\nslot in the bottom bar, also the exact silhouette of the \"Remédios\" tab.\nThe brand and one of six tabs were the same shape.\n\nIt is now the lowercase \"n\" of Fraunces, the serif the app already uses\nfor display type. Four rounds of exploration got here, and the three\ndiscarded ones are the reason this one is a letter:\n\n  · a nest bowl with one egg reads as a person meditating;\n  · with two eggs it reads as a smiling face — two dots over an upward\n    curve is the canonical smiley, and no amount of adjusting the curve\n    escapes it;\n  · the nest as a ring with the egg inside reads as an eye, which is the\n    last thing a health record for a child should look like;\n  · seen from above, as woven circles, it reads as a wifi symbol — and\n    means the opposite of what the app does.\n\nThat is not four unlucky drafts. A nest reduced to a monochrome 24px\nglyph converges on faces and eyes because \"curve plus dots\" is their\nvocabulary. A letter has no such neighbours, and the \"n\" of Fraunces is\nalready an arch resting on two stems: the shape of shelter, without\ndrawing shelter.\n\n**The glyph is a path, not text.** A monogram written as `<text>` only\nexists once the font has loaded, and this repository spent months\nrendering in `system-ui` because a family name differed by one space\n(#73). A mark that sometimes is not there is not a mark. The outline is\nthe real glyph, extracted from the `@fontsource-variable/fraunces` this\napp already ships, instantiated at `wght 900, opsz 72, SOFT 0, WONK 0`\nand fitted to the 24×24 box — the same curve, not a lookalike.\n\n`favicon.svg` and the three PWA icons were regenerated from that outline.\nThe maskable one keeps the glyph at 1.15 rather than 1.55: an adaptive\nicon''s safe zone is a circle of 80% of the side, and anything outside it\nis the system''s to crop.","tree":{"sha":"93ffbe137ff22aeeccb117dfa8777b02427d6bca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/93ffbe137ff22aeeccb117dfa8777b02427d6bca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/537cc60c2bd3f11c4188dbf93080f183d4fb2656","verification":{"payload":"tree 93ffbe137ff22aeeccb117dfa8777b02427d6bca\nparent 4674a6fe60731f163fb04efb1a62230e3ffd86c6\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788550769 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788550769 -0300\n\nfeat(brand): a mark for Ninho, drawn from the display face (#79)\n\n* fix(pwa): the installed app still called itself Meu Neném\n\nThe rename in #78 changed twelve strings and missed two, both in\n`public/manifest.webmanifest`: `name` and `short_name`. They are what\nAndroid and iOS print under the icon once somebody installs the app, so\nthe one place the old name would have survived is the home screen — the\nmost visible surface there is.\n\nThe miss has a cause worth naming: the search that drove that change\ncovered `src/`, `index.html`, `README.md` and `e2e/`, and `public/` was\nnot in it. Static assets carry user-facing copy too.\n\n* feat(brand): a mark for Ninho, drawn from the display face\n\nThe logo was a heart — generic on its own, and since medications took a\nslot in the bottom bar, also the exact silhouette of the \"Remédios\" tab.\nThe brand and one of six tabs were the same shape.\n\nIt is now the lowercase \"n\" of Fraunces, the serif the app already uses\nfor display type. Four rounds of exploration got here, and the three\ndiscarded ones are the reason this one is a letter:\n\n  · a nest bowl with one egg reads as a person meditating;\n  · with two eggs it reads as a smiling face — two dots over an upward\n    curve is the canonical smiley, and no amount of adjusting the curve\n    escapes it;\n  · the nest as a ring with the egg inside reads as an eye, which is the\n    last thing a health record for a child should look like;\n  · seen from above, as woven circles, it reads as a wifi symbol — and\n    means the opposite of what the app does.\n\nThat is not four unlucky drafts. A nest reduced to a monochrome 24px\nglyph converges on faces and eyes because \"curve plus dots\" is their\nvocabulary. A letter has no such neighbours, and the \"n\" of Fraunces is\nalready an arch resting on two stems: the shape of shelter, without\ndrawing shelter.\n\n**The glyph is a path, not text.** A monogram written as `<text>` only\nexists once the font has loaded, and this repository spent months\nrendering in `system-ui` because a family name differed by one space\n(#73). A mark that sometimes is not there is not a mark. The outline is\nthe real glyph, extracted from the `@fontsource-variable/fraunces` this\napp already ships, instantiated at `wght 900, opsz 72, SOFT 0, WONK 0`\nand fitted to the 24×24 box — the same curve, not a lookalike.\n\n`favicon.svg` and the three PWA icons were regenerated from that outline.\nThe maskable one keeps the glyph at 1.15 rather than 1.55: an adaptive\nicon''s safe zone is a circle of 80% of the side, and anything outside it\nis the system''s to crop.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmx5xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJuEQACz4sR8azOEZ1FI5W4TbkkEi\novwsdmYL6SIsRsBay/b8SCgyJW0wCGIcvw+gRrYV04iClAa9CQZK+9BzSLBc4brc\nm15qyJWLO++sD8IePukrLpMgyeh5UlSJ+T/eMYL22/1qpyCDKzCm+aAasJ+llB32\nZodwZy+p+8T0plUDzLkviaoO7fe5b8jIAhwgAsuBFpb6iFDH/gapO0vvWa0+gVhY\nYGKdLLyv7MxJWRDUw+KWfq6rboOj2B/igVVgHSI/FEcjxP6xIW6iD+8LC3H6H0WQ\n00LYO2Pt/+KZCjU1v48zEy20jy8xDA6QVfYNxHT7+75m5QVfbZKs2KhJDBi9HNkH\nTxAntekXpIDGJBPseQMFIvSpbkjYzIY0XDgq3UdEQUU1B6M7C1bPUkPYGYTH4go6\nIqYEaf1CTWttz3KOgtFwIi21KrCnzfWfjc3HV+Yphh5M84sSwt3aUCo6WR9F+5uS\nY/xwKfe7Og1/78jOCnMbcbRneHM0koNzE5wP4A8fhU4ujb29G7tttye8rt8ObYjk\nuAJSFIJz9tGklplu8MDFp/xgyUChfLFY4i4LcOt87IiH2QUb24YfaCB+WYYfjivp\nxnOEhxWV1CZJ3apziJ