f0fd9a9ffd415","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/644b20fcb73fa94b340ed90e9d1f0fd9a9ffd415"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3d24b9a7d6c1a3fe4ff2d44ab21fd099f5e01c38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:47:05Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:47:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(design): give factual data its own typographic voice (#68)\n\nDates, times, counts and percentages now render in DM Mono, a third family\nbeside Nunito (display) and Inter (body). Taken from the LoginAndDashboardDesign\nreference, where it is the cheapest decision in the whole prototype: a\nmonospaced date reads as a record, a proportional one reads as prose.\n\nThe payoff is not only tonal. In the vaccination card the date column is a stack\nof dd/mm/yyyy values, and fixed glyph width aligns day, month and year down the\npage on their own — the em dash standing in for \"no date\" now occupies the same\nbox instead of shifting its neighbours. On the dashboard the four stat values\nline up with each other for the same reason.\n\nCost, measured on 03/09/2026:\n\n- DM Mono latin, weight 400: 14.820 bytes of woff2. The latin-ext face beside it\n  (9.552) practically never downloads in pt-BR — ã, ç and é all sit below U+00FF.\n- The static package is deliberate. @fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono ships\n  40.404 bytes for the same latin subset, 2.7x, and buys a weight axis this use\n  has no use for: factual data has no emphasis hierarchy, it has one register.\n  For scale, Inter latin costs 48.256 and Nunito 39.128.\n- CSS 128.29 -> 129.18 kB, gzip 20.16 -> 20.30, so +143 bytes gzip. Entry JS\n  unchanged at 149.77 kB gzip; the class strings are the only delta.\n\nOnly weight 400 is loaded, so where the voice landed on text that was bold the\nweight was removed rather than lowered. Both alternatives fail quietly:\nfont-bold/font-extrabold make the browser synthesise the bold, which smears a\nmonospace face, while font-medium does not synthesise but falls back to 400\nthrough CSS font matching — rendering correctly while the class claims a weight\nthe family does not have.\n\nThe voice stops at the sentence boundary. \"Aplicada em 12/03/2024\" keeps its\nproportional face because the number is part of a phrase there, and swapping\nfamily mid-line would make the sentence jump instead of highlighting the data.\nLabel-and-value is a different shape and does take it, which is why the\nvaccination card''s \"Nascimento: 03/07/2026\" is split.\n\nVerified: lint, tsc, 146 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build (app + embed +\nMF remote). audit-surface.mjs over /dashboard, /vaccines and /appointments —\n3 viewports x 2 themes, no overflow, no clipped text, no new sub-44px target.\npages-a11y.mjs 12/12 on the six authenticated pages in both themes. Looked at by\neye at 360px, where the stat card dates run closest to the edge, and in dark.","tree":{"sha":"be82e136cb37dbae3c38e0630ddaa54166fbd68b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/be82e136cb37dbae3c38e0630ddaa54166fbd68b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/3d24b9a7d6c1a3fe4ff2d44ab21fd099f5e01c38","verification":{"payload":"tree be82e136cb37dbae3c38e0630ddaa54166fbd68b\nparent a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788468425 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788468425 -0300\n\nfeat(design): give factual data its own typographic voice (#68)\n\nDates, times, counts and percentages now render in DM Mono, a third family\nbeside Nunito (display) and Inter (body). Taken from the LoginAndDashboardDesign\nreference, where it is the cheapest decision in the whole prototype: a\nmonospaced date reads as a record, a proportional one reads as prose.\n\nThe payoff is not only tonal. In the vaccination card the date column is a stack\nof dd/mm/yyyy values, and fixed glyph width aligns day, month and year down the\npage on their own — the em dash standing in for \"no date\" now occupies the same\nbox instead of shifting its neighbours. On the dashboard the four stat values\nline up with each other for the same reason.\n\nCost, measured on 03/09/2026:\n\n- DM Mono latin, weight 400: 14.820 bytes of woff2. The latin-ext face beside it\n  (9.552) practically never downloads in pt-BR — ã, ç and é all sit below U+00FF.\n- The static package is deliberate. @fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono ships\n  40.404 bytes for the same latin subset, 2.7x, and buys a weight axis this use\n  has no use for: factual data has no emphasis hierarchy, it has one register.\n  For scale, Inter latin costs 48.256 and Nunito 39.128.\n- CSS 128.29 -> 129.18 kB, gzip 20.16 -> 20.30, so +143 bytes gzip. Entry JS\n  unchanged at 149.77 kB gzip; the class strings are the only delta.\n\nOnly weight 400 is loaded, so where the voice landed on text that was bold the\nweight was removed rather than lowered. Both alternatives fail quietly:\nfont-bold/font-extrabold make the browser synthesise the bold, which smears a\nmonospace face, while font-medium does not synthesise but falls back to 400\nthrough CSS font matching — rendering correctly while the class claims a weight\nthe family does not have.\n\nThe voice stops at the sentence boundary. \"Aplicada em 12/03/2024\" keeps its\nproportional face because the number is part of a phrase there, and swapping\nfamily mid-line would make the sentence jump instead of highlighting the data.\nLabel-and-value is a different shape and does take it, which is why the\nvaccination card''s \"Nascimento: 03/07/2026\" is split.\n\nVerified: lint, tsc, 146 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build (app + embed +\nMF remote). audit-surface.mjs over /dashboard, /vaccines and /appointments —\n3 viewports x 2 themes, no overflow, no clipped text, no new sub-44px target.\npages-a11y.mjs 12/12 on the six authenticated pages in both themes. Looked at by\neye at 360px, where the stat card dates run closest to the edge, and in dark.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmdzJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOmYQAClXFJhQfnTfFkKVlUp096E+\nfKuAOBjyIPj6lIsraIgFZ0ZKSSn2HmSxUPmP+wGXs7oUqsBh7CEw5KJCFukeXJ0w\n1np0HbWXwXDMEEkhysrfCA4MNimvO8vkDMrvUj7SI5hyuMJLKQbjX4Zx1XrOfniA\njWgZ2ULPwg0F+/Duw2AXPxxl30JvR49TvSLl/9Q/jaaB/bTGVMV5OCVMfBxFrP24\n5ymUToKvNt3ezr/ZkC5gp/Lk9VoMP/n4D/mygkS5WRuzSVqYZPKIYrL71TYS4dpB\n5FX/D+Kce2z7gULV+JDR9jU/EL42J6/6zvv/ms0EovvY+tiwyLtyE7ZgZgn/lgJj\n//639un3Mk3ENGpLVi1eiss/O2tqWrMSdjSSO1uzfFTl4xJ5rnF4AbY98qJVwLRb\nYP0PWWTkXtqFpu/1aVFgq43hWlMTpCkbQFEPNZMbAk0K2cNXdDfZXrCC9nICedVu\n+odvD1y7MNNhGvd40HU65boCVbRL/GnqxlnBwisbtxPEgggq5XVUvllqzLkV6Qn6\nSbajEQsRTKu2M5xYRKj2HAWvFhmUE1YI4MJu8Ugaep+OtAvs1IvQy6Waw28BB4T3\nbWzFIGh3JexC6/3V2d9MrHuL/U+rMM04dzANILgBdnQ3OUt58n5YNs6VawT1R06l\nBGJt9skAFIF4t+32ytSX\n=tHQ2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T20:47:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/3d24b9a7d6c1a3fe4ff2d44ab21fd099f5e01c38","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDNkMjRiOWE3ZDZjMWEzZmU0ZmYyZDQ0YWIyMWZkMDk5ZjVlMDFjMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87","sha":"a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87"}],"sha":"3d24b9a7d6c1a3fe4ff2d44ab21fd099f5e01c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3d24b9a7d6c1a3fe4ff2d44ab21fd099f5e01c38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:36:09Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:36:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(appointments): let a mistyped appointment be deleted (#67)\n\nAn appointment was the only thing a user creates in this app and cannot remove.\nA milestone can be deleted, an ad-hoc vaccine can, a child can, a guardian can,\nthe account itself can — an appointment could only be cancelled.\n\nCancelling is a different act. It is PATCH status=CANCELLED and keeps the row,\nbecause a visit that was called off belongs in the history. That is right for\n\"it was called off\" and wrong for \"I typed it wrong\", and there was nothing for\nthe second case. Recording a past consultation (#60) made the gap sharper:\ncancelling something that already happened says nothing at all.\n\nThe action sits outside the SCHEDULED branch on purpose. Cancelling only makes\nsense for a booked visit; a typo happens in any status, and a completed one had\nno way out before this.\n\nThe confirmation copy points back at the other act — \"if it was merely called\noff, cancel it instead, that keeps it in the history\" — because the two are easy\nto confuse and only one is reversible in the sense that matters.\n\nNeeds cygnus-api #23, which adds DELETE /babies/{babyId}/appointments/{id}. Two\nthings worth saying plainly about that:\n\n- Verified end to end against the real stack with that branch built into the\n  local API container: DELETE answers 204, the following GET answers 404, and\n  the list comes back empty. Not inferred from the tests.\n- **contract-drift.mjs would not have caught this dependency.** Its map covers\n  GET response shapes only — ten entries, no DELETE — so a front calling an\n  endpoint the API does not expose passes the gate. Worth extending; noted\n  rather than done here, since it is a change to the gate and not to this\n  feature.\n\nTwo tests, and the one that matters is the failure path: closing the dialog on a\nfailed delete would look exactly like success while leaving the row on screen\nwith no explanation. Both were confirmed to fail without the mutation call.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 146 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity.","tree":{"sha":"6245161a17d2034c0864771b8452499737acbfd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/6245161a17d2034c0864771b8452499737acbfd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87","verification":{"payload":"tree 6245161a17d2034c0864771b8452499737acbfd4\nparent bcd8f3d2e6316588e05dff3f67b437dc9e890bfc\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788298569 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788298569 -0300\n\nfeat(appointments): let a mistyped appointment be deleted (#67)\n\nAn appointment was the only thing a user creates in this app and cannot remove.\nA milestone can be deleted, an ad-hoc vaccine can, a child can, a guardian can,\nthe account itself can — an appointment could only be cancelled.\n\nCancelling is a different act. It is PATCH status=CANCELLED and keeps the row,\nbecause a visit that was called off belongs in the history. That is right for\n\"it was called off\" and wrong for \"I typed it wrong\", and there was nothing for\nthe second case. Recording a past consultation (#60) made the gap sharper:\ncancelling something that already happened says nothing at all.\n\nThe action sits outside the SCHEDULED branch on purpose. Cancelling only makes\nsense for a booked visit; a typo happens in any status, and a completed one had\nno way out before this.\n\nThe confirmation copy points back at the other act — \"if it was merely called\noff, cancel it instead, that keeps it in the history\" — because the two are easy\nto confuse and only one is reversible in the sense that matters.\n\nNeeds cygnus-api #23, which adds DELETE /babies/{babyId}/appointments/{id}. Two\nthings worth saying plainly about that:\n\n- Verified end to end against the real stack with that branch built into the\n  local API container: DELETE answers 204, the following GET answers 404, and\n  the list comes back empty. Not inferred from the tests.\n- **contract-drift.mjs would not have caught this dependency.** Its map covers\n  GET response shapes only — ten entries, no DELETE — so a front calling an\n  endpoint the API does not expose passes the gate. Worth extending; noted\n  rather than done here, since it is a change to the gate and not to this\n  feature.\n\nTwo tests, and the one that matters is the failure path: closing the dialog on a\nfailed delete would look exactly like success while leaving the row on screen\nwith no explanation. Both were confirmed to fail without the mutation call.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 146 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql0VJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtJUQADmcX4ydUcK2mscmmW6c9C+T\n554zV+QsXDXCwesLdBlqsbEizNi2srEx7mbHA0OlrgAkHj9EygFsjaqRDNggt4Lt\n3PXVD2SaJB1qPfvs7uqWAZb8k5gcbo9TZI7tRu664P4GHh8Kg/MAxZhCB6oBb6ti\nDBbS3BjMcYhTkkqHNV9hu9evDOWS9xm6aHDh