890bfc"}],"sha":"a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a5d6e621512e20e2a46d1e84ce099f03eba76a87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bcd8f3d2e6316588e05dff3f67b437dc9e890bfc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:12:48Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T21:12:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dashboard): make the empty states invite instead of reporting nothing (#66)\n\nRegister a child and the dashboard answers with six blanks. Measured on a real\naccount with one child and nothing else recorded:\n\n  VACINAS TOMADAS      0    34 pendentes\n  PRÓXIMA CONSULTA     —    Sem consulta agendada\n  MARCOS REGISTRADOS   0    marcos do desenvolvimento\n  ÚLTIMA CONSULTA      —    —\n\nplus \"Sem consultas agendadas\" and \"Nenhum marco registrado ainda\". The worst\nwas the last stat card, whose value *and* subtitle were both em-dashes: it\noccupied a quarter of the grid and said nothing at all.\n\nEvery one of those states now points somewhere:\n\n- The milestones card lists three examples of what families record, with the\n  category emoji, and links to the screen where they can be acted on.\n- The appointments card says an appointment that already happened can be\n  recorded too — true since #60, and the empty state was still written as if\n  booking were the only option — and links to both.\n- The two dead subtitles say what is missing rather than printing a dash.\n- On /milestones, the empty state''s examples are buttons: tapping one opens the\n  form with the title filled and the category already chosen. AddMilestoneDialog\n  takes an optional `suggestion` for that, and everything stays editable.\n\n**The examples are deliberately not anchored to an age, and that is the design.**\nThe obvious version — \"at 2 months babies usually smile, hold their head up,\nfollow objects\" — turns the screen into a checklist a parent measures their\nchild against, and a child not doing those things by that month makes the app\nthe bearer of a worry it is not qualified to raise. This app states plainly that\nit gives no clinical guidance; a developmental timetable would be exactly that,\nin the friendliest possible voice. So the copy is \"what other families record\",\nand the four examples exist to make the four categories legible through\ninstances rather than through an abstract label.\n\nThe category comes selected with the title, because a suggestion that filled\nonly the title would leave the person deciding the one part of the form that is\nnot obvious.\n\nVerified against the container build on a freshly created account: the\nmilestones card renders the three examples, /milestones shows all four as\nbuttons, and tapping \"Primeira palavra\" opens the dialog with that title and\nLANGUAGE already `aria-checked`. Two tests cover the filled and the blank case.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 144 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity,\npages-a11y 12/12.","tree":{"sha":"afda602efa5ac73c66b40cf0734ea983ba430e2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/afda602efa5ac73c66b40cf0734ea983ba430e2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/bcd8f3d2e6316588e05dff3f67b437dc9e890bfc","verification":{"payload":"tree afda602efa5ac73c66b40cf0734ea983ba430e2b\nparent a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788297168 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788297168 -0300\n\nfeat(dashboard): make the empty states invite instead of reporting nothing (#66)\n\nRegister a child and the dashboard answers with six blanks. Measured on a real\naccount with one child and nothing else recorded:\n\n  VACINAS TOMADAS      0    34 pendentes\n  PRÓXIMA CONSULTA     —    Sem consulta agendada\n  MARCOS REGISTRADOS   0    marcos do desenvolvimento\n  ÚLTIMA CONSULTA      —    —\n\nplus \"Sem consultas agendadas\" and \"Nenhum marco registrado ainda\". The worst\nwas the last stat card, whose value *and* subtitle were both em-dashes: it\noccupied a quarter of the grid and said nothing at all.\n\nEvery one of those states now points somewhere:\n\n- The milestones card lists three examples of what families record, with the\n  category emoji, and links to the screen where they can be acted on.\n- The appointments card says an appointment that already happened can be\n  recorded too — true since #60, and the empty state was still written as if\n  booking were the only option — and links to both.\n- The two dead subtitles say what is missing rather than printing a dash.\n- On /milestones, the empty state''s examples are buttons: tapping one opens the\n  form with the title filled and the category already chosen. AddMilestoneDialog\n  takes an optional `suggestion` for that, and everything stays editable.\n\n**The examples are deliberately not anchored to an age, and that is the design.**\nThe obvious version — \"at 2 months babies usually smile, hold their head up,\nfollow objects\" — turns the screen into a checklist a parent measures their\nchild against, and a child not doing those things by that month makes the app\nthe bearer of a worry it is not qualified to raise. This app states plainly that\nit gives no clinical guidance; a developmental timetable would be exactly that,\nin the friendliest possible voice. So the copy is \"what other families record\",\nand the four examples exist to make the four categories legible through\ninstances rather than through an abstract label.\n\nThe category comes selected with the title, because a suggestion that filled\nonly the title would leave the person deciding the one part of the form that is\nnot obvious.\n\nVerified against the container build on a freshly created account: the\nmilestones card renders the three examples, /milestones shows all four as\nbuttons, and tapping \"Primeira palavra\" opens the dialog with that title and\nLANGUAGE already `aria-checked`. Two tests cover the filled and the blank case.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 144 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity,\npages-a11y 12/12.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlz/QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsQAQAIPoThBL6aYqJErimllna4sh\n3Fg1rTgLyxhSF5RHOh/HSblzuc6vYhLFbJPFtz325PqSgkxfwT6YS70Itu6eJ+nJ\nQayZHCHyqUWIe/o5CjXoPNbAoPtyh/pPdwgw0ohKtXlGImIJB3wAS8HB15RwIf5L\noIM15bH/V3csokh0OZf9Lgl+s2jd4Rh2bm8yjPb6/ZonQYtWt+jr9c48zU7VK7Bt\nTh80LUCUoQ6+A08dNaHcVU63hmuc9YesRophT37rTV70tnzBifuuSel9KV99K0xS\nJJ/Pqz0aTennHtJ6G8t4FGAKYjZwXWs+59Y+B2hhLEY62VgVXkGiARX6KyUtLZOS\n4WDwsSXODlrvqexFBvlZwmtsO6muI+QgWEUXBHrhJgOLGnGU9UXmq54ChyJ/Dq/p\nqg6kbI7CezVRAM3BgBzm6967LQljskyoNPTC1RQv8ayd3Uq1CvK5cI+r6Dwjbqfk\nD8iuZwfLSYE7jjR9Jnvyg/UaEjpYjlxiHKAIqMKgcr8AoEc34zGGUoncQdbwYzmS\nYSBBapTkQAj3WqIbYKUQWegVlvGasCE1HWzyMr3claMNqav8/H0AJlMjzgDFUHPO\nvfQ1/Xb9PxBEwgk0AS0XEd0zqB5/dsNknbFwP/9xB1HvvfrVuKV4CttcJz3quA+L\neJRpgLKHxb4RxaUPQcm3\n=nFun\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T21:12:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bcd8f3d2e6316588e05dff3f67b437dc9e890bfc","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGJjZDhmM2QyZTYzMTY1ODhlMDVkZmYzZjY3YjQzN2RjOWU4OTBiZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1","sha":"a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1"}],"sha":"bcd8f3d2e6316588e05dff3f67b437dc9e890bfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bcd8f3d2e6316588e05dff3f67b437dc9e890bfc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:58:43Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:58:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(legal): ask for consent, and stay inert until there is a text worth accepting (#65)\n\nThe documents and the API contract have both existed since 27/08; nothing asked\nanybody anything. This closes that, and it closes it in the only order that\nmakes sense: the gate ships now and does nothing, because there is nothing\nhonest to ask yet.\n\nBoth documents are drafts, so `documentsInForce()` is empty, the query is\ndisabled, no request goes out and children render untouched. The day a reviewed\ntext lands and `status` flips to `''in-force''` in shared/legal.ts, the gate starts\nasking on its own. No other file changes. That is what \"ready to be swapped\" has\nto mean to be worth saying.\n\nA gate rather than a checkbox at sign-up, because a version bump has to re-ask,\nand it has to re-ask people who already have accounts. A checkbox on the\nregistration form only ever catches new users and would leave every existing\naccount agreeing to a text they never saw.\n\nVersion-aware, matching the API''s unique key of (user, document, version): an\nacceptance of 0.9.0 does not satisfy 1.0.0. Without that, changing the words\nwould silently inherit an agreement to words nobody read.\n\nTwo behaviours are deliberate and easy to get wrong in the other direction:\n\n- **A failed query lets the app through.** The gate collects consent; it does not\n  hold a health record hostage to a network hiccup. Locking someone out of their\n  child''s vaccine history because /legal/acceptances returned 500 would be a\n  worse outcome than a late acceptance.\n- **There is no \"later\" button.** The app handles a child''s health data, and\n  continuing without consent would be processing it with no basis. The way out\n  is signing out, and the copy says so.\n\nAcceptances are recorded one request at a time, sequentially, so a failure\nhalfway through leaves the accepted ones accepted — each is a fact about the\npast on its own.\n\n`/legal/acceptances` was added to the contract gate''s map. The script says an\nendpoint with no entry there shows up as a gap rather than as silence, and this\nis the first endpoint added since that became CI.\n\nFive tests, and the one that matters most is the inert case: a component that\ndoes nothing is indistinguishable from a component that is broken, so the draft\npath asserts that zero requests were made, not merely that no gate appeared.\nLEGAL_DOCUMENTS is mocked per test because the real module has both documents as\ndrafts — without that there would be no way to exercise the half that only\nmatters on the day a text is published. Verified by neutralising the gate, which\nturns exactly the two blocking tests red.\n\nVerified on the container build that the inert path is real: pages-a11y.mjs\nstill passes 12/12 with the gate mounted inside ProtectedLayout.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 142 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity,\ncontract drift.","tree":{"sha":"fe057d67850b8026c19858f8a5561cec0988411b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/fe057d67850b8026c19858f8a5561cec0988411b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1","verification":{"payload":"tree fe057d67850b8026c19858f8a5561cec0988411b\nparent c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788296323 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788296323 -0300\n\nfeat(legal): ask for consent, and stay inert until there is a text worth accepting (#65)\n\nThe documents and the API contract have both existed since 27/08; nothing asked\nanybody anything. This closes that, and it closes it in the only order that\nmakes sense: the gate ships now and does nothing, because there is nothing\nhonest to ask yet.\n\nBoth documents are drafts, so `documentsInForce()` is empty, the query is\ndisabled, no request goes out and children render untouched. The day a reviewed\ntext lands and `status` flips to `''in-force''` in shared/legal.ts, the gate starts\nasking on its own. No other file changes. That is what \"ready to be swapped\" has\nto mean to be worth saying.\n\nA gate rather than a checkbox at sign-up, because a version bump has to re-ask,\nand it has to re-ask people who already have accounts. A checkbox on the\nregistration form only ever catches new users and would leave every existing\naccount agreeing to a text they never saw.\n\nVersion-aware, matching the API''s unique key of (user, document, version): an\nacceptance of 0.9.0 does not satisfy 1.0.0. Without that, changing the words\nwould silently inherit an agreement to words nobody read.\n\nTwo behaviours are deliberate and easy to get wrong in the other direction:\n\n- **A failed query lets the app through.** The gate collects consent; it does not\n  hold a health record hostage to a network hiccup. Locking someone out of their\n  child''s vaccine history because /legal/acceptances returned 500 would be a\n  worse outcome than a late acceptance.\n- **There is no \"later\" button.** The app handles a child''s health data, and\n  continuing without consent would be processing it with no basis. The way out\n  is signing out, and the copy says so.\n\nAcceptances are recorded one request at a time, sequentially, so a failure\nhalfway through leaves the accepted ones accepted — each is a fact about the\npast on its own.\n\n`/legal/acceptances` was added to the contract gate''s map. The script says an\nendpoint with no entry there shows up as a gap rather than as silence, and this\nis the first endpoint added since that became CI.\n\nFive tests, and the one that matters most is the inert case: a component that\ndoes nothing is indistinguishable from a component that is broken, so the draft\npath asserts that zero requests were made, not merely that no gate appeared.\nLEGAL_DOCUMENTS is mocked per test because the real module has both documents as\ndrafts — without that there would be no way to exercise the half that only\nmatters on the day a text is published. Verified by neutralising the gate, which\nturns exactly the two blocking tests red.\n\nVerified on the container build that the inert path is real: pages-a11y.mjs\nstill passes 12/12 with the gate mounted inside ProtectedLayout.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 142 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity,\ncontract drift.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlzyDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmpUQACo5tc8LDX/eaMa00BqP/9/f\nNgEA8FRsJUihjjRqOOphPah+RYVPwsq0zCqStmqrH5ziPL3sDBseqObXnAbdQDGn\nZ2tgW7boA7esReV14mtBm5ovZ2gusl+qQ0Wu6TKlHOqvl+7ZtEOCiycmIwLZOUDd\njO5ACJ8NrsRNox5VkbjOApRsFCMaw56jkGhHvhWesHLO+j+UtRQygYXfPzsG8UYS\n990nGLdRraZwrINChLjhnoyt0i+HJ7+qpVlRTBgt0/V5iMygloNGYMWT7SA0Y4v1\ndZx1kWPL0m3JVRpuxrXG4TV5W5OpCM0MIt8vdFnwR8SYhVZZzmIrhXsIVpTUsYFn\nmCYp43XquMCcr/H4D0YiQK1g+7vKDdNNNbY2nveijEOkS08qMbfFuWVOfwUWdNs3\n5QsisauZjEWcOG92a4OQUGY6WfZGY931NVXKPU6/uCQz9YX0oYkzH3NZyiNz3srp\nCLLhWPq/7FXfJWGlgoI2f8FQS46XPcM+VZmN08scWrK2QkOd7UiMu1KAtpHyy30C\n3Wf/ThJgpZUqpy3IREsDZWwS+n4gki1wUeT/NCEDX9bR69CvjVPZpStRwYgnC+qm\n67vMAsRfRunbx0MQTmWWu7zsOIN6QweUVmwjA4kJjBnDLAiXnxfsShP0KjKz8Hm1\nkQR/KDBeONkEMnifuymg\n=aJww\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:58:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGEyN2ZjMzdlNzQ4Nzk5Nzg5OWY2Mjg0NjU4MmIyN2U1NTgwM2U0YjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635","sha":"c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635"}],"sha":"a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a27fc37e7487997899f62846582b27e55803e4b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:25:43Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:25:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(legal): write the policy and terms as drafts, ready to be swapped (#64)\n\nBoth pages listed section *headings* and had no body. They now carry the full\ntext, and the arrangement is built so that publishing the reviewed version is\none substitution rather than a project.\n\nThe prose lives in `features/legal/content/`, one file per document, not in\n`src/locales/*.json`. Three reasons, in order of weight: substitution has to be\na single file rather than a merge across three 700-line locale files; a policy\nis a versioned artefact whose exact wording is the thing being agreed to, not UI\ncopy; and three \"equivalent\" translations of a binding document would be a lie.\nThe app serves Brazil and the document is governed by Brazilian law, so the\nPortuguese text binds and the other locales render it with a notice saying so.\n\nThe line this draws is the whole point, and it is drawn per section:\n\n- What describes **what the software does** — which fields exist, who can see\n  them, which providers process them, what account deletion actually cascades —\n  was read off this repository''s Zod schemas and deploy configuration. It is\n  verifiable and needed no lawyer to be true.\n- What is a **legal commitment** — retention periods, the controller''s identity\n  and contact, the lawful basis claimed under LGPD art. 14 for a child''s\n  sensitive data, the limits of liability, the governing forum — is marked\n  `needsReview`, carries no invented figures, and renders with a visible warning\n  on the section itself. A fabricated retention period is worse than an absent\n  one: it reads as a promise nobody made.\n\nThe warning is per section rather than only at the top, because an anchor link\nlands someone in the middle of the document and the top notice never reaches\nthem.\n\nA test keeps the failure this exists to prevent from ever shipping: a document\ncannot be `in-force` while any section still awaits review. Nothing else would\ncatch it — the page renders, the types check, and placeholder prose looks like\nprose. Verified by flipping both documents to `in-force`, which turns three\ntests red, and back.\n\nTwenty dead locale lines went with it: `pendingSections`, `sectionsTitle` and\nthe two `sections` arrays existed only to render the list of headings this\nreplaces.\n\nAlso gives both pages a `<main>`. They are the only screens that draw their own\npage without going through a layout, and they had no main landmark at all —\nsomebody navigating by landmarks could not jump to the document, which is the\nonly thing on the page. It surfaced because `audit-surface.mjs` now refuses a\ncell whose `main` never rendered, which yesterday it would have passed.\n\nMeasured on the container build: privacy renders 10 sections and 7606\ncharacters, terms 9 sections and 4822, axe clean in both themes, and\naudit-surface.mjs passes both routes across three viewports and two themes.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 137 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity.","tree":{"sha":"067d7c9a83657777c1fea87f24c93c2bb05b5fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/067d7c9a83657777c1fea87f24c93c2bb05b5fd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635","verification":{"payload":"tree 067d7c9a83657777c1fea87f24c93c2bb05b5fd5\nparent 3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788294343 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788294343 -0300\n\nfeat(legal): write the policy and terms as drafts, ready to be swapped (#64)\n\nBoth pages listed section *headings* and had no body. They now carry the full\ntext, and the arrangement is built so that publishing the reviewed version is\none substitution rather than a project.\n\nThe prose lives in `features/legal/content/`, one file per document, not in\n`src/locales/*.json`. Three reasons, in order of weight: substitution has to be\na single file rather than a merge across three 700-line locale files; a policy\nis a versioned artefact whose exact wording is the thing being agreed to, not UI\ncopy; and three \"equivalent\" translations of a binding document would be a lie.\nThe app serves Brazil and the document is governed by Brazilian law, so the\nPortuguese text binds and the other locales render it with a notice saying so.\n\nThe line this draws is the whole point, and it is drawn per section:\n\n- What describes **what the software does** — which fields exist, who can see\n  them, which providers process them, what account deletion actually cascades —\n  was read off this repository''s Zod schemas and deploy configuration. It is\n  verifiable and needed no lawyer to be true.\n- What is a **legal commitment** — retention periods, the controller''s identity\n  and contact, the lawful basis claimed under LGPD art. 14 for a child''s\n  sensitive data, the limits of liability, the governing forum — is marked\n  `needsReview`, carries no invented figures, and renders with a visible warning\n  on the section itself. A fabricated retention period is worse than an absent\n  one: it reads as a promise nobody made.\n\nThe warning is per section rather than only at the top, because an anchor link\nlands someone in the middle of the document and the top notice never reaches\nthem.\n\nA test keeps the failure this exists to prevent from ever shipping: a document\ncannot be `in-force` while any section still awaits review. Nothing else would\ncatch it — the page renders, the types check, and placeholder prose looks like\nprose. Verified by flipping both documents to `in-force`, which turns three\ntests red, and back.\n\nTwenty dead locale lines went with it: `pendingSections`, `sectionsTitle` and\nthe two `sections` arrays existed only to render the list of headings this\nreplaces.\n\nAlso gives both pages a `<main>`. They are the only screens that draw their own\npage without going through a layout, and they had no main landmark at all —\nsomebody navigating by landmarks could not jump to the document, which is the\nonly thing on the page. It surfaced because `audit-surface.mjs` now refuses a\ncell whose `main` never rendered, which yesterday it would have passed.\n\nMeasured on the container build: privacy renders 10 sections and 7606\ncharacters, terms 9 sections and 4822, axe clean in both themes, and\naudit-surface.mjs passes both routes across three viewports and two themes.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 137 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build, locale parity.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlzTHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiD8QAAwXGcAnm0Pvbor4TUKlOytw\nglNSZiEW5a8/nMLx+pMWIhxsIHcDvZiQLsuogrSrdd4TrCJXVCyvTgCwm/Vr7EHo\niYRAUoH5eCKCJ22wDapVSvZpdOvhpWKZMrWoHSO39sxrwfYMSNfdTUSkh7QCNdUu\nM5tSZCFLX2TxEgVyOHLOnEU81flSwlfD489X/DAio93Vi0Q00pfZPnosfQ8CTHxE\nPnfz+lgeLIfhmYmCOoGwcZXGud+PoZ7NzLlQni4kzw0RIZaPetK5Zu7MzmNTirll\nr0VGj4NTCbkMXP26CplogY6SPX3lkwu/WCcKna1pyLr0LxyzieriPWln4+4tW14x\nm/4vwLE2jCRpN/1h5Yghvu0cNf8FvEPaoVl/DElVU/RdLe5N/0GC63THDfp1ezpV\nI5xNRucVQ8sCy/ibh2oyldfB3lEoKXk4mHzg8LhMZE50JTsimm0Lt1fn/4B8kv2Y\n1a4H54vxXwAmsGzhYL1wnQ7PxUxSA4TuOcTlK0suaUWPJm/joblwn986J7x89MMp\npsM1TG2/8xNidIDtkwFVYH3uFytAzOkcnP+7cu7inm+tacCcDLQGGt8YeZlLBDZ4\n8V5Kvxgqeap3YmDXW2XM+wZoznFWZO8CQEQ/KlLVqpTHeEqXHlAGyMQPt3UvT8tG\naQqUjFCzhka2zSA6Ekpd\n=8thr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:25:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGM5YjczMDcyODk4MGUwOWE4NGYxZTMyZmFiOTQ3NDIxMDkwNmU2MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea","sha":"3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea"}],"sha":"c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c9b730728980e09a84f1e32fab9474210906e635"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:10:09Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:10:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): put the ad-hoc delete trigger on the button, not on a span (#63)\n\nAlertDialogTrigger asChild wrapped a <span>, and Radix puts\n`aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"` and `aria-expanded` on whatever element it is handed.\nA bare <span> has no role that may carry either, so axe reported\n`aria-allowed-attr` once per ad-hoc vaccine row on /vaccines.\n\nThe span existed only for `relative inline-flex flex-shrink-0`. Those classes\nmoved onto the button, which is where the trigger belonged: the layout wrapper\nwas never the interactive element.\n\nSecond time this exact shape has been paid for here — PR #29 fixed the same\nthing with `aria-expanded` on a <span> used as an AlertDialogTrigger. The rule\nthat survives is short: the trigger goes on the interactive element, and layout\nearns classes rather than a wrapper.\n\nIt stayed invisible until today for a reason worth recording. The defect is old,\nbut seed-family.mjs created no ad-hoc vaccine, so this list never rendered a row,\nthe trigger never existed, and every axe sweep over /vaccines scanned a page\nwhere the offending node was absent. Seeding the two rows — done yesterday to\nreach the 13th dialog at all — is what made it appear. An audit only sees the\nstates its fixture can reach.\n\npages-a11y.mjs goes from 2 failing nodes to 12/12 pages clean across both\nthemes, and audit-dialog.mjs passes 6/6 on the dialog this trigger opens.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 128 unit tests, 83 story tests.","tree":{"sha":"d15b3226e865d2ba4f8b1610d1e7ef7da3858f72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/d15b3226e865d2ba4f8b1610d1e7ef7da3858f72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea","verification":{"payload":"tree d15b3226e865d2ba4f8b1610d1e7ef7da3858f72\nparent 86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788293409 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788293409 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): put the ad-hoc delete trigger on the button, not on a span (#63)\n\nAlertDialogTrigger asChild wrapped a <span>, and Radix puts\n`aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"` and `aria-expanded` on whatever element it is handed.\nA bare <span> has no role that may carry either, so axe reported\n`aria-allowed-attr` once per ad-hoc vaccine row on /vaccines.\n\nThe span existed only for `relative inline-flex flex-shrink-0`. Those classes\nmoved onto the button, which is where the trigger belonged: the layout wrapper\nwas never the interactive element.\n\nSecond time this exact shape has been paid for here — PR #29 fixed the same\nthing with `aria-expanded` on a <span> used as an AlertDialogTrigger. The rule\nthat survives is short: the trigger goes on the interactive element, and layout\nearns classes rather than a wrapper.\n\nIt stayed invisible until today for a reason worth recording. The defect is old,\nbut seed-family.mjs created no ad-hoc vaccine, so this list never rendered a row,\nthe trigger never existed, and every axe sweep over /vaccines scanned a page\nwhere the offending node was absent. Seeding the two rows — done yesterday to\nreach the 13th dialog at all — is what made it appear. An audit only sees the\nstates its fixture can reach.\n\npages-a11y.mjs goes from 2 failing nodes to 12/12 pages clean across both\nthemes, and audit-dialog.mjs passes 6/6 on the dialog this trigger opens.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 128 unit tests, 83 story tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlzEiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATMwQAFPuRkAhb6KaeGaryQVmH8g5\nthiSvY2Ds4afzogfVBWihQvmlFGTruGsfhmb3+UYulLKhictnhjo71A+vkuc3etM\n9pmpiLVGZsitmLzXVIP0l2Q2vQCExJmis5mgpyzc/4QAEJYYaGl4Bybhmde8rwKr\nMRem9IEZYXEuQXoZkl5fx5a8mpctFsaKQIjJUWqEbNXwSP/7E8QujDRK5ePUqVWu\nZgtViiLZ41rw8NXGR/hxumvTlO3yzDxp25B+5u6b2XqHOjrAxsygvl89cC9WhuIm\naQUDqlT11d89V7i5+uFryJ5UhGNlDFZWNsRuwP2C8jECRuRbzJZ64YyDLB6lQhcB\nLVoi1K6AwAeGN/xFcg3xidZrDFU/KmIjE/8HjZKkTbeve1m463R2zVVQyr7T+XH2\n0sX4ox8AXHTGngAw68KjDJmfbpQu7L+NfTmcgvl+ogmUzsowjMcAtGUIgBqVe/zs\nULo2DFdhFte0dGTvriEh0O71P5KK2rUO5ZZnd87If8ETrbni+22q1ZajhEdR/JS4\n01Ent1iQ7FCGcHGEL7LIUutBB5YMZ+UtZhEuySo0ZvLsluFUwX7zSbUw+9qxBFtj\nFpn5LY3Z8EzQ0aWiJ7aRbmc1lyNzFpuTm5rsrXoCz1zdvD2IsM3d1hR1HrhrtRGF\ni0OPNL1FfDL0jSGqXzt+\n=9Ukt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:10:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDNiZmEyMGE4OWU3YTk3MzY0NzZlNTU0YzU5ZmQ4MDViYTcwYTBlZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815","sha":"86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815"}],"sha":"3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3bfa20a89e7a9736476e554c59fd805ba70a0eea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:10:03Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:10:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(ui): give the primary action one named scale (#62)\n\nEvery routed screen had already reached 48px by hand — `px-6 py-3` retyped as a\nraw <button> in six files — while the dashboard hero landed on ~52px. That 52\nwas never chosen: it is `py-3.5` plus the line-height of `text-base`, so it\nmoves on its own if the type changes. A height is a decision; a computed height\nis a side effect.\n\n48px wins on four counts: it is what six of the seven primary actions already\nmeasured, it is a scale step where 52 is off-scale, it clears the 44px floor of\nWCAG 2.5.5 that the rest of the app still owes in places, and it can be stated\nas a height instead of inferred from padding.\n\nIt is now a Button size (`cta`), so the scale has one definition and a name\nrather than being retyped per screen.\n\nThis also finishes what #57 left half-done, and that is worth saying plainly:\nthat change made the primary action emerald everywhere, but only for buttons\nthat were <Button> to begin with. These six were raw <button> elements with the\ndomain hue hardcoded — bg-violet-600 on appointments, bg-amber-700 on\nmilestones, bg-amber-500 on the dashboard''s bottom CTA — so the rule recorded in\nDESIGN.md was true of the components and false of the screens. Routing them\nthrough Button fixes both at once, which is why this is one change and not two.\n\nThe dashboard hero keeps its white fill: it sits on the emerald panel, which is\nthe same colour in both themes, and DESIGN.md already documents why nothing\npainted there may flip. Only its scale changed. Contrast was checked before\ntouching any of it — white on emerald-700 5.48:1, emerald-700 on white 5.48:1,\nand the amber-950-on-amber-500 that went away was 5.60:1, so none of this was\nforced by contrast; consistency was the reason.\n\nMeasured on the container build rather than read off the classes, because\nreading classes is what hid the 52 in the first place: all four primary actions\nnow render at exactly 48px, including the hero in the zero-children state, which\nis the one that changed. The probe that says so is\nverification/primary-action-scale.mjs.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 128 unit tests, 83 story tests.","tree":{"sha":"5f38c6168863f06b8e0ffbc9fc959fd8c6a8a5bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/5f38c6168863f06b8e0ffbc9fc959fd8c6a8a5bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f38c6168863f06b8e0ffbc9fc959fd8c6a8a5bf\nparent af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788293403 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788293403 -0300\n\nrefactor(ui): give the primary action one named scale (#62)\n\nEvery routed screen had already reached 48px by hand — `px-6 py-3` retyped as a\nraw <button> in six files — while the dashboard hero landed on ~52px. That 52\nwas never chosen: it is `py-3.5` plus the line-height of `text-base`, so it\nmoves on its own if the type changes. A height is a decision; a computed height\nis a side effect.\n\n48px wins on four counts: it is what six of the seven primary actions already\nmeasured, it is a scale step where 52 is off-scale, it clears the 44px floor of\nWCAG 2.5.5 that the rest of the app still owes in places, and it can be stated\nas a height instead of inferred from padding.\n\nIt is now a Button size (`cta`), so the scale has one definition and a name\nrather than being retyped per screen.\n\nThis also finishes what #57 left half-done, and that is worth saying plainly:\nthat change made the primary action emerald everywhere, but only for buttons\nthat were <Button> to begin with. These six were raw <button> elements with the\ndomain hue hardcoded — bg-violet-600 on appointments, bg-amber-700 on\nmilestones, bg-amber-500 on the dashboard''s bottom CTA — so the rule recorded in\nDESIGN.md was true of the components and false of the screens. Routing them\nthrough Button fixes both at once, which is why this is one change and not two.\n\nThe dashboard hero keeps its white fill: it sits on the emerald panel, which is\nthe same colour in both themes, and DESIGN.md already documents why nothing\npainted there may flip. Only its scale changed. Contrast was checked before\ntouching any of it — white on emerald-700 5.48:1, emerald-700 on white 5.48:1,\nand the amber-950-on-amber-500 that went away was 5.60:1, so none of this was\nforced by contrast; consistency was the reason.\n\nMeasured on the container build rather than read off the classes, because\nreading classes is what hid the 52 in the first place: all four primary actions\nnow render at exactly 48px, including the hero in the zero-children state, which\nis the one that changed. The probe that says so is\nverification/primary-action-scale.mjs.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 128 unit tests, 83 story tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlzEbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApKMQAJc2oIJJs/M3rdM8pBkyqXnd\n/GI7o94zbDxXxbEG2UyOTj38KonRwB7T/lfdMk9r1MtJYVQsxhDY+AIQNg6ySo9Q\nqEdP4X+FvI9vWVpaRbzhKdJ1EO4v42FF28q+mJFlGirVfiGclsAnwjAvaHt/DTrW\nUB8ZpkyrsUihnLu4d5fFLL6Kuym92qMl3gQzCwida3AmuDzyKeUAhHlhXCKMFU3R\nbau6hACRZzi5BxtV+GPcD/EUh1PRLhTtVdlem165DLA/22gwmDjfrHjcdeM3T/d1\naC5ViVdcYtHsl3VcXLOuS4kYWxyy5ylNtd0T/lJ+Y0PNoKzDF2vuLb4PuSQF8mC1\npZbJ4jyUi2ZHZNLTUBaB7l14OTSCcZTIXmXjRMZwaqtpe3VJSttRmjR0rpNZyLwb\niCUDUZGlHkdZl469iuxsmXELjxAOeRIT2Z21BxFgVjlY+23Dk8Qm3iA84TUlLu4e\nNTBOBRd4qXz8DKNkJDq52YfmCCjPOZvzc2HoDUpPtFVDRGfYHERMMbwXfKFY2Mg7\n18KXt2ohf5erUZoBRgCX8nzN+67xRWKgEjWDmxszFm38NkQ3p+1/+EtLl4Y7RAZ0\n0h+V6z2LBJfQQDvBHye8oBrlcyB5qBkNyrDkMcW4j7/O11yOH8JjUTC5SPq8UT0v\nWeRv1tbDXI7qIE+cMQOf\n=r3x5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T20:10:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDg2YmI0YmIzMmY1M2M0N2M1YzA2YjY0YzA3YWNiZGQ5YWE1M2E4MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1","sha":"af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1"}],"sha":"86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/86bb4bb32f53c47c5c06b64c07acbdd9aa53a815"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:49:04Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:49:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(contract): gate every PR on drift against the published API contract (#61)\n\nFrom 13/08 to 27/08/2026 the vaccine calendar did not load, because the front\nrequired `guidance` and `recommendationKind` and the API did not send them. The\nresponse was 200, so there was no error in the log, none in Sentry and none in\nany test — the screen said \"could not load\" and nobody noticed for thirteen\ndays. Nothing in this pipeline catches that class of defect.\n\ncontract-drift.mjs has caught it since 26/08 and has been passing since the\ncontract was fixed, but it only ran when somebody remembered to type the\ncommand, because it lived in docs/ — which is gitignored, and a pipeline cannot\nrun what git does not have. Promoting it to a gate is therefore also what makes\nit public, and that is the trade Samuel accepted.\n\nIt fetches the contract over the network on every run. A committed copy would\ndrop the dependency but would go stale, and a gate comparing against an old\ncontract stays green while production drifts — the same silence it exists to\nbreak. The accepted cost is that a raw.githubusercontent outage turns a PR red\nfor an unrelated reason, and CONTRACT= is the way around it.\n\nThree things changed on the way out of docs/:\n\n- It no longer imports the probes'' lib.mjs, which loads Playwright and axe at\n  the top level. A contract checker has no business dragging a browser into the\n  pipeline, so reportRow/summarise are inlined — twelve lines, no third-party\n  dependency at all.\n- Comments and identifiers are in English. It is tracked and public now, and\n  the repo rule for code on disk applies to it as it does to src/.\n- The alias hook came along, since importing `*.schemas.ts` directly is the\n  whole reason this can compare the real schemas rather than a copy of them.\n  Copying them here would reintroduce the duplication the script exists to find.\n\nVerified in both directions, which is the only way to know a gate is not\ndecorative: green against the live spec, and red with exit 1 against a spec\nwhere `metadata` was deleted from the vaccine response — it names the missing\nfield and says the response will still arrive 200. Also run after `npm ci` from\na clean install, which is what the runner does.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b.","tree":{"sha":"baba02f768b93a4cb261e94fa64f6e1d7c315192","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/baba02f768b93a4cb261e94fa64f6e1d7c315192"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1","verification":{"payload":"tree baba02f768b93a4cb261e94fa64f6e1d7c315192\nparent bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788292144 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788292144 -0300\n\nci(contract): gate every PR on drift against the published API contract (#61)\n\nFrom 13/08 to 27/08/2026 the vaccine calendar did not load, because the front\nrequired `guidance` and `recommendationKind` and the API did not send them. The\nresponse was 200, so there was no error in the log, none in Sentry and none in\nany test — the screen said \"could not load\" and nobody noticed for thirteen\ndays. Nothing in this pipeline catches that class of defect.\n\ncontract-drift.mjs has caught it since 26/08 and has been passing since the\ncontract was fixed, but it only ran when somebody remembered to type the\ncommand, because it lived in docs/ — which is gitignored, and a pipeline cannot\nrun what git does not have. Promoting it to a gate is therefore also what makes\nit public, and that is the trade Samuel accepted.\n\nIt fetches the contract over the network on every run. A committed copy would\ndrop the dependency but would go stale, and a gate comparing against an old\ncontract stays green while production drifts — the same silence it exists to\nbreak. The accepted cost is that a raw.githubusercontent outage turns a PR red\nfor an unrelated reason, and CONTRACT= is the way around it.\n\nThree things changed on the way out of docs/:\n\n- It no longer imports the probes'' lib.mjs, which loads Playwright and axe at\n  the top level. A contract checker has no business dragging a browser into the\n  pipeline, so reportRow/summarise are inlined — twelve lines, no third-party\n  dependency at all.\n- Comments and identifiers are in English. It is tracked and public now, and\n  the repo rule for code on disk applies to it as it does to src/.\n- The alias hook came along, since importing `*.schemas.ts` directly is the\n  whole reason this can compare the real schemas rather than a copy of them.\n  Copying them here would reintroduce the duplication the script exists to find.\n\nVerified in both directions, which is the only way to know a gate is not\ndecorative: green against the live spec, and red with exit 1 against a spec\nwhere `metadata` was deleted from the vaccine response — it names the missing\nfield and says the response will still arrive 200. Also run after `npm ci` from\na clean install, which is what the runner does.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlywwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAExcQADVCyXfrcFrAh6os5Rqu5vzQ\n1d4+OkuNIvcjqhXiPPV79p/aqlXS9tarUxc3MCUWr+uGpWEM6zaYrKOjG2yo/gyd\nP3PixvNZHAV5kgLPoTDOUM5w9ex5ZlPvNLHnkSa+3LTK4fv7EHmD5zlUs5TCPbdb\n026PIyod+ht2nmSSkwnpCc8buwvNdwvPCrsKBdLy5X2F/Hh9QKKfS9Xl2Wv4oVqu\nBGRhbjGlVQiBK971JAl4K8KZ6R/7vIgkjUH6D5Eyzjap8a04crWgyYyfY1fYZkNy\n1Hh7cAfkcXnik8QAdfArmUBv64JociAmEz3+JTve+vJZjbPSa6e64Lk+giCJFrHc\ni0RO4xO4dAKxf9lzYGWQZ4o1He3ADuvKZXCLluBrHxq7wsj9pAFIJkivOJ6558lM\nfxc/yzo12UPUe2T+bqA5wX3QP9KaMo2UlB+5LsDT9JvuScTOX9NSDYg6JF/BR7F9\nW/AfD+Wpnf6o3CyH1V4YKV4Cg0X0lkkHKP4WGETt9VUsMOHxHQCxaIK5K14234md\nKQSYEQCbawp9WD15Bv5HXoXPD1ekewsIzyj5lt71I4qUcp6I00Ty4f5Vp2bGN4E1\nkZ7F9kVOlLQZEo8KffyB+0WDe8MCZzysux8frj8gFjKRJ1O62YH94BZprW0R9Fmj\n0fNbdokdCa99ZZ2bpOaf\n=f/sQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T19:49:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGFmM2EzYWI3ZjE2NjdiNTE5ZTliYjk4YjIzYjUyYjgwN2UyZTE4ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e","sha":"bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e"}],"sha":"af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/af3a3ab7f1667b519e9bb98b23b52b807e2e18f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:35:01Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T19:35:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(appointments): let the app record a consultation that already happened (#60)\n\ncygnus-api #21 closed on 27/08/2026 and there was no UI for it. A vaccine has\nan applicationDate, a milestone has a date; an appointment was the only part of\nthe history that could only be written forward. A health record exists to keep\nwhat already happened.\n\nThe invariant is not loosened, it is mirrored. `appointmentFormSchema` used one\nrefine that refused any past date/time. It now takes the intent as a field and\nchecks the matching direction: booking still refuses the past, and recording\nrefuses the future. Booking for last Tuesday remains a typo, and the rule that\ncatches it is intact.\n\nThe intent is asked, not inferred. Reading a past date as \"they must have meant\nto record it\" would silently reinterpret exactly the typo the scheduling rule\nexists to catch, so the schedule step now opens with two cards — book, or record\nsomething that already happened — and the validation flips with the answer.\n\nEach direction gets its own i18n key rather than one generic message. The issue\nis `custom` on purpose: zod-error.ts maps a custom issue''s message straight to a\nkey, while a built-in code would collapse both directions into one string and\ntell the person the opposite of what they got wrong. Three locales, six lines\neach, inserted next to the message they pair with.\n\n`status` is required on the schema with no `.default()`, and that is deliberate\nafter trying the other way: a default makes the schema''s input type differ from\nits output type, and zodResolver cannot reconcile `status?` going in with\n`status` coming out — it fails across every Control and Resolver in the feature.\nThe default belongs in `defaultValues`, which is also the only place that knows\nthe field starts on \"book it\". `reset()` had to become `reset({ status:\n''SCHEDULED'' })` for the same reason: a bare reset cleared a field the schema\nrequires, and the second open would have submitted without one.\n\nThe request stays additive: status is sent only when recording, so booking is\nbyte-identical to what this app sent before COMPLETED existed.\n\nBoth directions are tested, at the schema and through the screen, because\neither one passing alone is the state that existed before. The screen-level test\nwas confirmed to fail without the wiring — dropping the status line from the\nrequest body turns it red, and nothing else.\n\nVerified against the container build: audit-dialog-states.mjs green on all five\nstates of this dialog, audit-dialog.mjs 6/6 across both themes and three\nviewports, pages-a11y.mjs 12/12, contract-drift.mjs clean against the published\nopenapi.json, and audit-locale-parity.mjs with no gaps across the three locales.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 128 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build.","tree":{"sha":"54f25c52cbba7c282cd95743deed38ed82a84712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/54f25c52cbba7c282cd95743deed38ed82a84712"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e","verification":{"payload":"tree 54f25c52cbba7c282cd95743deed38ed82a84712\nparent a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788291301 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788291301 -0300\n\nfeat(appointments): let the app record a consultation that already happened (#60)\n\ncygnus-api #21 closed on 27/08/2026 and there was no UI for it. A vaccine has\nan applicationDate, a milestone has a date; an appointment was the only part of\nthe history that could only be written forward. A health record exists to keep\nwhat already happened.\n\nThe invariant is not loosened, it is mirrored. `appointmentFormSchema` used one\nrefine that refused any past date/time. It now takes the intent as a field and\nchecks the matching direction: booking still refuses the past, and recording\nrefuses the future. Booking for last Tuesday remains a typo, and the rule that\ncatches it is intact.\n\nThe intent is asked, not inferred. Reading a past date as \"they must have meant\nto record it\" would silently reinterpret exactly the typo the scheduling rule\nexists to catch, so the schedule step now opens with two cards — book, or record\nsomething that already happened — and the validation flips with the answer.\n\nEach direction gets its own i18n key rather than one generic message. The issue\nis `custom` on purpose: zod-error.ts maps a custom issue''s message straight to a\nkey, while a built-in code would collapse both directions into one string and\ntell the person the opposite of what they got wrong. Three locales, six lines\neach, inserted next to the message they pair with.\n\n`status` is required on the schema with no `.default()`, and that is deliberate\nafter trying the other way: a default makes the schema''s input type differ from\nits output type, and zodResolver cannot reconcile `status?` going in with\n`status` coming out — it fails across every Control and Resolver in the feature.\nThe default belongs in `defaultValues`, which is also the only place that knows\nthe field starts on \"book it\". `reset()` had to become `reset({ status:\n''SCHEDULED'' })` for the same reason: a bare reset cleared a field the schema\nrequires, and the second open would have submitted without one.\n\nThe request stays additive: status is sent only when recording, so booking is\nbyte-identical to what this app sent before COMPLETED existed.\n\nBoth directions are tested, at the schema and through the screen, because\neither one passing alone is the state that existed before. The screen-level test\nwas confirmed to fail without the wiring — dropping the status line from the\nrequest body turns it red, and nothing else.\n\nVerified against the container build: audit-dialog-states.mjs green on all five\nstates of this dialog, audit-dialog.mjs 6/6 across both themes and three\nviewports, pages-a11y.mjs 12/12, contract-drift.mjs clean against the published\nopenapi.json, and audit-locale-parity.mjs with no gaps across the three locales.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 128 unit tests, 83 story tests, full build.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlyjlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK4MQAHRbL2IR+hs+pCZdmYL9DcTe\nc+pbeJ12jvZzsqTpAxBfCJ2MZs1GEHy+TFXF/t3FVSkXro5k+GM6D7KDejWyaOxK\nyG2Rbk73nEkflpC1pS0ivNJ0keLRsarTv4c+VOrVwMqO8hv0APrrCiFJaIztsbQe\nX3WXmb3NinrI7IrFwaT2Z3a5EAt8w9U00trjOsEZs9e0bndbU9gRFqPmSQzfLMoO\nxRmti9HYTBsMENPZeZBRPe0U5BnGdRPqP7Fbg2eKXOPDR9LHzpYf2U8ITp8JFBvY\nHKx+de+slbG9VPGaqfLqcA875GgK5fmdxzIcQu43eccJTHKd9e2qtImF3uNy8bgF\n7MYgWN85h9ANdBDxJD+fI9s4jzXVYWwRBgx5e4kWGEtXts+09MMWSrMww/dp2hDo\nXQLmeDxvczeG661kl2udWNhZCymQwDkAlmw4y1mddgpWiKFjLOVZmk4/t3O0bMB3\nsdcmm8xKtILcb/L/EaRe4CViDTAaLqjWlq0aVG1w4Yp4zMAiRWniNNj+yGvCIbm5\n3pge9kqZNC9M3+Vw901HQZxEkW9Nj8nQn52xgw3abVQnV4g53bTJCmbjo59a2f11\n94mzOYx5k1qLrZr/sJ1Qojx9fTDT1nusJVE+qvqrUsX12xBP7GjWBLnugAfQdo+Y\nM6MPV0g+aIq6Ft/qQ0cX\n=Fded\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T19:35:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGJmYjljMTMyMDBjYzU4ZGQ5ZTAxNDQ1MWFlZjdiNmRjYzZkMWVjM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e","sha":"a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e"}],"sha":"bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bfb9c13200cc58dd9e014451aef7b6dcc6d1ec3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:08:50Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:08:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): bring the hero photograph to phone and tablet (#59)\n\nThe brand panel is `lg:flex`, so the photograph — half the identity of these\nscreens — did not exist below the desktop breakpoint. Mobile is most of the\ntraffic for an app like this one.\n\nIt is now the page background under `lg`, with the card floating on it. Above\n`lg` nothing changes: the panel already carries the photograph, and painting it\nin both places would be the same image twice on one screen.\n\nThe card is now opaque and bordered at every width, which reverses the earlier\n\"no card chrome below sm\". The arithmetic is what changed, not the taste: with\nthe form sitting straight on the wash, every label, input and tab would have\nbeen composited over photograph pixels — the one contrast case no gate in this\nrepo can see, since axe reads the nearest opaque ancestor and sees neither the\n<img> nor a sibling gradient. A box inside a box costs a little air; text over a\nphotograph costs legibility that nothing measures.\n\nThree things stay outside the card and are painted straight on the photograph:\nthe theme toggle, the language switcher and the footer. So the scrim is a\nvertical gradient whose bottom stop lands at 88%, leaving the last 12% solid\nsurface — the same technique the brand panel already uses for its own bottom\nthird. Measured, that band matters: with the gradient still interpolating under\nthe footer the composite read rgb(225,227,224) and 12px ink-faint fell to\n4.03:1, under the floor. Solid surface there restores rgb(244,246,243) and\n4.79:1, which is what that token is measured at.\n\n                          light    dark\n  language switcher 13px  5.95:1   8.06:1\n  copyright/note    12px  4.79:1   6.19:1\n  legal links       12px  4.83:1   6.14:1\n\nTwelve combinations — three public routes by two viewports by two themes — with\nno failure. Photograph actually visible, counting pixels away from the surface\ncolour: 18% on phone, 40% on tablet.\n\nThe `< sm` height floor was re-measured and moved from 47rem to 50.5rem. The\npadding the card needed to sit on the photograph took /login from 752 to 761,\npast a 752 floor, and the segmented control started drifting 4px again —\nlayout.mjs caught it, nothing else would have. Re-swept 360 to 1920: the band is\nflat at 786 from 380 to 620 and jumps to 807 at 360 alone, where a line wraps,\nso the floor is set by the narrowest phone rather than the typical one. The\nother two bands are unchanged.\n\nNone of this is gate-covered, so it ships with its own probe:\nverification/auth-chrome-contrast.mjs, which measures the text outside the card\nagainst the composited pixels. contrast.mjs measures the desktop panel; this\nmeasures the other half. Its own trap is written at the top — the screenshot has\nto be fullPage, because the target coordinates are document-space and a viewport\ncapture makes getImageData clamp and sample a different part of the image, which\nreported 3.48:1 where the real figure was 4.03:1.\n\nVerified on the container build: layout.mjs back to 0px variation and 0px\nsegmented drift across twelve widths with the four shell nodes surviving a tab\nswitch; contrast.mjs unchanged on the desktop panel; a11y.mjs clean;\naudit-surface.mjs clean on all three public routes in both themes and three\nviewports. Recorded in AUTH.md §3.1 and §5.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 122 unit tests, 83 story tests.","tree":{"sha":"fbafc23360ab7f2b2a224f06cae393b90a1a40ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/fbafc23360ab7f2b2a224f06cae393b90a1a40ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e","verification":{"payload":"tree fbafc23360ab7f2b2a224f06cae393b90a1a40ce\nparent b38949ed0e9f7956f5723c1476d474eed3139359\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788282530 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788282530 -0300\n\nfeat(auth): bring the hero photograph to phone and tablet (#59)\n\nThe brand panel is `lg:flex`, so the photograph — half the identity of these\nscreens — did not exist below the desktop breakpoint. Mobile is most of the\ntraffic for an app like this one.\n\nIt is now the page background under `lg`, with the card floating on it. Above\n`lg` nothing changes: the panel already carries the photograph, and painting it\nin both places would be the same image twice on one screen.\n\nThe card is now opaque and bordered at every width, which reverses the earlier\n\"no card chrome below sm\". The arithmetic is what changed, not the taste: with\nthe form sitting straight on the wash, every label, input and tab would have\nbeen composited over photograph pixels — the one contrast case no gate in this\nrepo can see, since axe reads the nearest opaque ancestor and sees neither the\n<img> nor a sibling gradient. A box inside a box costs a little air; text over a\nphotograph costs legibility that nothing measures.\n\nThree things stay outside the card and are painted straight on the photograph:\nthe theme toggle, the language switcher and the footer. So the scrim is a\nvertical gradient whose bottom stop lands at 88%, leaving the last 12% solid\nsurface — the same technique the brand panel already uses for its own bottom\nthird. Measured, that band matters: with the gradient still interpolating under\nthe footer the composite read rgb(225,227,224) and 12px ink-faint fell to\n4.03:1, under the floor. Solid surface there restores rgb(244,246,243) and\n4.79:1, which is what that token is measured at.\n\n                          light    dark\n  language switcher 13px  5.95:1   8.06:1\n  copyright/note    12px  4.79:1   6.19:1\n  legal links       12px  4.83:1   6.14:1\n\nTwelve combinations — three public routes by two viewports by two themes — with\nno failure. Photograph actually visible, counting pixels away from the surface\ncolour: 18% on phone, 40% on tablet.\n\nThe `< sm` height floor was re-measured and moved from 47rem to 50.5rem. The\npadding the card needed to sit on the photograph took /login from 752 to 761,\npast a 752 floor, and the segmented control started drifting 4px again —\nlayout.mjs caught it, nothing else would have. Re-swept 360 to 1920: the band is\nflat at 786 from 380 to 620 and jumps to 807 at 360 alone, where a line wraps,\nso the floor is set by the narrowest phone rather than the typical one. The\nother two bands are unchanged.\n\nNone of this is gate-covered, so it ships with its own probe:\nverification/auth-chrome-contrast.mjs, which measures the text outside the card\nagainst the composited pixels. contrast.mjs measures the desktop panel; this\nmeasures the other half. Its own trap is written at the top — the screenshot has\nto be fullPage, because the target coordinates are document-space and a viewport\ncapture makes getImageData clamp and sample a different part of the image, which\nreported 3.48:1 where the real figure was 4.03:1.\n\nVerified on the container build: layout.mjs back to 0px variation and 0px\nsegmented drift across twelve widths with the four shell nodes surviving a tab\nswitch; contrast.mjs unchanged on the desktop panel; a11y.mjs clean;\naudit-surface.mjs clean on all three public routes in both themes and three\nviewports. Recorded in AUTH.md §3.1 and §5.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 122 unit tests, 83 story tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlwaiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOPoQABUjupAc/1KSCpseT+x5XrMW\nQ14LIjVCXZTObpYcxBcEUmj0hG4PNf5rA4aSKXLEmhEjnwLQEhCa574qAudGt6II\nbfoD76OrEFsx5+IO7lqO2CwJVApRIJgyLB9C9PPiOCyIIRGXC2VbNQLTH2x86x3N\nNwd8ap5PapSUahpdafwoVgfsj6sRz9RjUI3csnE3yYzGg7UAqqCQAt6fVCrbMBXl\nuKfDKU5RvArqwkAuQhBzG1BlqMF06UK3f0Pbl/daF79O/7HcYt47Ypzu8JwQBF27\nDL226OGPVO1KIy1kGILCdtQx+NwVBGrCjY3vwf9YqnGbGnoLVPmrV9QZmokDFW1q\nJO/JEiJcD5SodMPVW7+XdXz6h9iHNd+2WSGYaNn4VY8X+GuQTKV2yiKMv18QiT4Y\nipaKQrxudMMpEsET5Lr7jRyDTav2tFI7LRKN/Z51Y+RgCAasuYHcwpyHgrELG5jf\nqwHhe49YRBn4Tjgzx0kLiAu23c7GN+jzQKcYS0oZ0BAGfLJImc5vVhe0p1tkh764\nh40ijEF69WOtjoa4o2v76r2FpUJgBI1T/uwH5CXUuBkGFm2kQ5UIu26qyYvZAAq7\nbV3Wlw5XD/YGi2o1TYB3V8JkrWvoZZGwEaUMIFyD5Jxl4yTE/5afLsWWmRiqgJht\nmY1e1cu6OU2P5OcISXnT\n=F9lT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T17:08:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGExODcwNjFjM2MwYTJjOGU3NGQzNDIxNmExYzQyNjlkOTA4NGJhOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/b38949ed0e9f7956f5723c1476d474eed3139359","sha":"b38949ed0e9f7956f5723c1476d474eed3139359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b38949ed0e9f7956f5723c1476d474eed3139359"}],"sha":"a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a187061c3c0a2c8e74d34216a1c4269d9084ba8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b38949ed0e9f7956f5723c1476d474eed3139359/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:29:29Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:29:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): render the invite screen inside the auth shell (#58)\n\n/invites/:code was the third public screen and the only one left out of the\nredesign. It drew a whole page of its own — a min-h-screen wrapper, its own\nlogo, its own centring — with no brand panel, no theme or language control and\nno legal footer.\n\nThe duplication was not the expensive part. The seam was: an invite sends a\nlogged-out visitor to /login and brings them back, and the screen changed\nidentity in the middle of the one flow that crosses both.\n\nIt is now a child of AuthLayout and owns only the column''s content. What it\ndoes not inherit is the segmented control and the card''s height floor, and that\ndistinction is the whole design decision here.\n\nThe floors exist so the card does not resize when the segmented control swaps\nroutes. An invite is not reached by the segmented control — it is its own\ndestination — so there is no jump to prevent, and applying the floor would draw\na 712px card a little over half full. Measured with the floor off, in both\nstates the screen has:\n\n  viewport   invite open   already used   pair''s floor\n  390        428px         260px          752px\n  768        494px         326px          820px\n  1440       561px         561px          712px\n\nDesktop lands on the same number in both states because the brand panel is the\ntallest cell in the grid and sets the row height. The shell already does what\nthe floor would have done, without the dead space.\n\nImplemented as a route handle (`authTabs`) read through useMatches rather than\na pathname check inside the layout: the shell should not have to know which URLs\nexist, and a fourth public screen added later gets the right behaviour by saying\nnothing. One flag drives both the tabs and the floor because it answers one\nquestion — is this route part of the pair?\n\nVerified against the container build, logged out, which is the screen''s real\naudience: audit-surface.mjs passes 3 viewports x 2 themes in both invite states,\nwith zero axe violations in each of the six cuts. The sub-44px warnings that\nremain are the shell''s own controls (theme, language, footer links), already\ninventoried as an open decision — inherited, not new.\n\nNo regression on the pair: layout.mjs reports 0px height variation and 0px\nsegmented-control drift across all twelve widths, and the four shell nodes still\nsurvive a tab switch. a11y.mjs clean. Recorded in docs/AUTH.md §5 and §6.1.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 122 unit tests, 83 story tests.","tree":{"sha":"3431c993eaa8710c6d17a6a8c63299ab6cb87986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/3431c993eaa8710c6d17a6a8c63299ab6cb87986"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/b38949ed0e9f7956f5723c1476d474eed3139359","verification":{"payload":"tree 3431c993eaa8710c6d17a6a8c63299ab6cb87986\nparent 8e17c135dc9343e57b1fed1f6c0a8b59858f53fb\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788280169 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788280169 -0300\n\nfeat(auth): render the invite screen inside the auth shell (#58)\n\n/invites/:code was the third public screen and the only one left out of the\nredesign. It drew a whole page of its own — a min-h-screen wrapper, its own\nlogo, its own centring — with no brand panel, no theme or language control and\nno legal footer.\n\nThe duplication was not the expensive part. The seam was: an invite sends a\nlogged-out visitor to /login and brings them back, and the screen changed\nidentity in the middle of the one flow that crosses both.\n\nIt is now a child of AuthLayout and owns only the column''s content. What it\ndoes not inherit is the segmented control and the card''s height floor, and that\ndistinction is the whole design decision here.\n\nThe floors exist so the card does not resize when the segmented control swaps\nroutes. An invite is not reached by the segmented control — it is its own\ndestination — so there is no jump to prevent, and applying the floor would draw\na 712px card a little over half full. Measured with the floor off, in both\nstates the screen has:\n\n  viewport   invite open   already used   pair''s floor\n  390        428px         260px          752px\n  768        494px         326px          820px\n  1440       561px         561px          712px\n\nDesktop lands on the same number in both states because the brand panel is the\ntallest cell in the grid and sets the row height. The shell already does what\nthe floor would have done, without the dead space.\n\nImplemented as a route handle (`authTabs`) read through useMatches rather than\na pathname check inside the layout: the shell should not have to know which URLs\nexist, and a fourth public screen added later gets the right behaviour by saying\nnothing. One flag drives both the tabs and the floor because it answers one\nquestion — is this route part of the pair?\n\nVerified against the container build, logged out, which is the screen''s real\naudience: audit-surface.mjs passes 3 viewports x 2 themes in both invite states,\nwith zero axe violations in each of the six cuts. The sub-44px warnings that\nremain are the shell''s own controls (theme, language, footer links), already\ninventoried as an open decision — inherited, not new.\n\nNo regression on the pair: layout.mjs reports 0px height variation and 0px\nsegmented-control drift across all twelve widths, and the four shell nodes still\nsurvive a tab switch. a11y.mjs clean. Recorded in docs/AUTH.md §5 and §6.1.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 122 unit tests, 83 story tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlv1pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApc0QAE0VlKSOfSpInXoayyEFyUEc\n3eIFzGmfZTibdsHhSmBjgnLXa1V0JTJzemuXvht6fFz7Q3eWjEyADV2lcATn0gQJ\nvrCGAfYDx62u8BhKdVD0tRlnsjsSabw+tMLqtTTP55UxMdCxwxKEIxaVA0Wxo5tx\n61UmHfq1K3MorcBrY/MoB/wVWhA9yhTk8SrpaiEO1O1TFI5jl91wzcqH9/7NgOgz\n6i9eFfrO+dpetJkZan3PAvVPjS5yOYjKNqe6T8kW7gFR54UgodFFn+FTQt75MXHz\n67+bZ5XokkeneTzWjYd6VdW3JZFHo4zhXUli63MCPaFuGHJDZnAeKsHijUFzvKDz\nawPmmI6vFtBYYIm8uee7dJTlrznRVgi1y+e4b4N3jJ2cUDMysZDKh6LiMbZzXkm