t.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/8e17c135dc9343e57b1fed1f6c0a8b59858f53fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:08:48Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:08:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(ui): make the primary action emerald everywhere (#57)\n\nNine primary buttons were painted by hand, in three treatments no rule could\nderive: appointments used bg-violet-600 on two wizard \"Continuar\", one submit\nand the \"mark as completed\" action; milestones used bg-amber-700 on two\n\"Continuar\" and bg-foreground — near black — on its two submits; everything\nelse already fell through to the Button default, bg-primary.\n\nThe symptom that settles it lived inside a single dialog. In AddMilestoneDialog\n\"Continuar\" was amber and \"Salvar Marco\" was black: two primary actions, two\ncolours, one screen.\n\nEmerald rather than the domain hue, measured with white text on the fill:\nemerald-700 5.48:1, violet-600 5.70:1, amber-700 5.02:1 — but amber-500, which\nis the milestone hue defined in the @theme block, is 2.68:1, and stock amber-600\nis 3.19:1. Both fail the 4.5:1 floor. The brand amber cannot be a filled primary\nbutton with white text at all, which is why those submits ended up black in the\nfirst place: someone hit that wall and worked around it on that screen, and the\nreason was never written down. A rule keyed on the domain hue is born with an\nexception, and every new hue owes its own measurement in both themes. One hue\nmeans one measurement for the whole app.\n\nThe per-domain colours are untouched and keep doing what they are for —\nidentity in badges, chips, icons and decorative fills, where they carry no white\ntext and owe no contrast. Identity is one thing; \"press this to continue\" is\nanother, and an app should only have one of those.\n\nRemoving the overrides also removes their hover pairs, so hover now comes from\nthe variant too instead of nine separate declarations.\n\nDecided by Samuel on 01/09/2026 against two stated alternatives (domain hue with\na written exception; dark neutral everywhere). Recorded in docs/DESIGN.md.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 122 unit tests, 83 story tests.","tree":{"sha":"3280f74ab248c2333a69d796eeb3983bd9cc1a7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/3280f74ab248c2333a69d796eeb3983bd9cc1a7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/8e17c135dc9343e57b1fed1f6c0a8b59858f53fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 3280f74ab248c2333a69d796eeb3983bd9cc1a7d\nparent bbe646740e4ae3edd8e288da94ac51d38fab1caf\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788278928 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788278928 -0300\n\nrefactor(ui): make the primary action emerald everywhere (#57)\n\nNine primary buttons were painted by hand, in three treatments no rule could\nderive: appointments used bg-violet-600 on two wizard \"Continuar\", one submit\nand the \"mark as completed\" action; milestones used bg-amber-700 on two\n\"Continuar\" and bg-foreground — near black — on its two submits; everything\nelse already fell through to the Button default, bg-primary.\n\nThe symptom that settles it lived inside a single dialog. In AddMilestoneDialog\n\"Continuar\" was amber and \"Salvar Marco\" was black: two primary actions, two\ncolours, one screen.\n\nEmerald rather than the domain hue, measured with white text on the fill:\nemerald-700 5.48:1, violet-600 5.70:1, amber-700 5.02:1 — but amber-500, which\nis the milestone hue defined in the @theme block, is 2.68:1, and stock amber-600\nis 3.19:1. Both fail the 4.5:1 floor. The brand amber cannot be a filled primary\nbutton with white text at all, which is why those submits ended up black in the\nfirst place: someone hit that wall and worked around it on that screen, and the\nreason was never written down. A rule keyed on the domain hue is born with an\nexception, and every new hue owes its own measurement in both themes. One hue\nmeans one measurement for the whole app.\n\nThe per-domain colours are untouched and keep doing what they are for —\nidentity in badges, chips, icons and decorative fills, where they carry no white\ntext and owe no contrast. Identity is one thing; \"press this to continue\" is\nanother, and an app should only have one of those.\n\nRemoving the overrides also removes their hover pairs, so hover now comes from\nthe variant too instead of nine separate declarations.\n\nDecided by Samuel on 01/09/2026 against two stated alternatives (domain hue with\na written exception; dark neutral everywhere). Recorded in docs/DESIGN.md.\n\nGates: lint, tsc -b, 122 unit tests, 83 story tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlviQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtgUQAGfk4pQJDfJRG8EdztCvULWM\nqrlYDUy9VwJ7q09FFqoJJok71TXE1ZwfKVM/UOf4Hkje2zJm2SDXpeJAZFCgqfo9\nhAnMv/OheEZC9A6BK1kQoUVcx7jTDyiLm7/K1DarcmJjvpvC28pnavFhEnbS