ana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d9bf8f455900c374b355f7db78635668f328c4a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:42:55Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:42:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): give the vaccine catalog notice a dark theme (#55)\n\nVaccineCatalogNotice carried no `dark:` variant at all. In the dark theme its\n`bg-sky-50/70` composited to #adb4b8 and `text-sky-800` stayed #00598a, which\naxe measured at 3.57:1 against a 4.5:1 floor — three nodes failing on\n/vaccines: the source line, the \"open official calendar\" link and the\ndisclaimer.\n\nIt went unseen because it was unreachable. The notice only renders once the\nvaccine calendar loads, and GET /babies/{babyId}/vaccines answered a shape the\nfrontend rejected from 13/08 to 27/08/2026 — /vaccines never left its error\nstate, so every axe sweep over the page scanned an error screen and passed.\nThe contract fix in cygnus-api #17 is what made this measurable, not a change\nin the component.\n\nThe fix is the pattern the rest of the app already uses for a tinted panel —\n`bg-<hue>-50 dark:bg-<hue>-950/40` with `text-<hue>-700 dark:text-<hue>-300`,\nas in AppointmentCard, WelcomeDashboard and GuardiansSection. The border gets\na dark variant too: `border-sky-100` alone drew a near-white line around a\ndark panel, which is the same oversight one property over.\n\nVerified against the container build, not the dev server: `pages-a11y.mjs`\nwent from 1 failure to 12/12 pages clean across both themes, and\n`dark-conflicts.mjs` reports no duplicate variant-and-property pairs across\n222 files. Storybook suite green, 25 files, 83 tests.","tree":{"sha":"723c4c37c8e6d5400fc971bc422aba1c0bec3f11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/723c4c37c8e6d5400fc971bc422aba1c0bec3f11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/d9bf8f455900c374b355f7db78635668f328c4a5","verification":{"payload":"tree 723c4c37c8e6d5400fc971bc422aba1c0bec3f11\nparent ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788273775 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788273775 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): give the vaccine catalog notice a dark theme (#55)\n\nVaccineCatalogNotice carried no `dark:` variant at all. In the dark theme its\n`bg-sky-50/70` composited to #adb4b8 and `text-sky-800` stayed #00598a, which\naxe measured at 3.57:1 against a 4.5:1 floor — three nodes failing on\n/vaccines: the source line, the \"open official calendar\" link and the\ndisclaimer.\n\nIt went unseen because it was unreachable. The notice only renders once the\nvaccine calendar loads, and GET /babies/{babyId}/vaccines answered a shape the\nfrontend rejected from 13/08 to 27/08/2026 — /vaccines never left its error\nstate, so every axe sweep over the page scanned an error screen and passed.\nThe contract fix in cygnus-api #17 is what made this measurable, not a change\nin the component.\n\nThe fix is the pattern the rest of the app already uses for a tinted panel —\n`bg-<hue>-50 dark:bg-<hue>-950/40` with `text-<hue>-700 dark:text-<hue>-300`,\nas in AppointmentCard, WelcomeDashboard and GuardiansSection. The border gets\na dark variant too: `border-sky-100` alone drew a near-white line around a\ndark panel, which is the same oversight one property over.\n\nVerified against the container build, not the dev server: `pages-a11y.mjs`\nwent from 1 failure to 12/12 pages clean across both themes, and\n`dark-conflicts.mjs` reports no duplicate variant-and-property pairs across\n222 files. Storybook suite green, 25 files, 83 tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqluRvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEEkQABl44S9hU+tfcZYAKNIfN93r\nT7MbQ79woguh5IT4rtEnQpPY8TiiDF0QLlHb5KB7KNE/0j7hdPk/OPMxtzDk0CvG\n/CgNxfuRBW5Hzuf+N6p34sTuS0PNv9xWCyEc0uz+fFmx6s/yAFPDrvg8edPqGq6u\nrJqrjIM36M0/za9NmY2btKX0F0n3Cq0HUUMGFDaeOOt52qPtif1pkVz638zHUBQu\n+R6JsLHGNraT2jUqf53Seee4l/5xuhnAVjaYEq3+0gBiLExpNkX56VVT9o5rOjvY\nyy9jwd3rwUvmiiNY6eW7gZtR3nsIFY1v0r49dGHK5XYwc+3+zdDut/KSlb1bdCbk\nRd29qUsBSKsJWHhmiTb9SNtnYdXub2Q5M8hIEFHn3Gh4gGz0kCynxfwDHB8P/FXn\nOkQLy5WC7A1X2J/G+g7rvD9bive8M/ZHPRvVA/MhwyK4NnIXGcGDiW383CpoiY7D\nI16zH7sQZNnk2SfaMGOrIjTfD0xOF8fc9IUt4syx9iWYrlCXY2CtfAuDifFecSuY\nU9wM0ewibk+/KJDdXhAM8qot6Q9J3a3seN2+6fleUQMGaJ9NVSMQLc/ynxQdVkAQ\ncY2bbrK2gkhrcRGKjjfBHbTrm5siQHD0rbfvchmGeIXfJq9IlwWge7+kJXgLsWk+\nPMGjl19RkleYWOJAGDpG\n=fgew\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:42:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/d9bf8f455900c374b355f7db78635668f328c4a5","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGQ5YmY4ZjQ1NTkwMGMzNzRiMzU1ZjdkYjc4NjM1NjY4ZjMyOGM0YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db","sha":"ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db"}],"sha":"d9bf8f455900c374b355f7db78635668f328c4a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d9bf8f455900c374b355f7db78635668f328c4a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:28:53Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:28:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(babies): stop asserting a bare digit that the calendar could steal (#54)\n\nFamilyStrip''s delayed-count test asserted `getByText(/3/)`. It passed from\n27/08 to 31/08/2026 and failed on 01/09 with nobody touching the code: the\nchip prints the child''s age next to the vaccine status, the fixture is born\non 01/06/2026, and on 01/09 that child turned exactly 3 months old. Two\nelements then matched `/3/` — \"3 meses\" and \"3 vacinas atrasadas\" — and\ntesting-library fails a multiple match regardless of which one is right.\n\nThis broke `main`, not a branch: #53 touched only e2e/ and its own CI was\ngreen on 27/08, so the failure arrived with the calendar rather than with a\nchange. Any run of the suite between 01/09 and the day the fixture stops\ncontaining a 3 would have reproduced it.\n\nThe digit alone was never what the test wanted to prove. Matching the whole\nsentence makes the assertion independent of the date and strictly stronger:\nit now fails if the i18n pluralization breaks, which `/3/` accepted silently\nin either form.\n\nChecked for the same shape elsewhere: this was the only assertion in the\nsuite matching a bare number. Full suite green — 29 files, 122 tests.","tree":{"sha":"d5a4bc7c50faf9da166fcbb8e14fe184a0ae7429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/d5a4bc7c50faf9da166fcbb8e14fe184a0ae7429"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db","verification":{"payload":"tree d5a4bc7c50faf9da166fcbb8e14fe184a0ae7429\nparent f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788272933 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788272933 -0300\n\ntest(babies): stop asserting a bare digit that the calendar could steal (#54)\n\nFamilyStrip''s delayed-count test asserted `getByText(/3/)`. It passed from\n27/08 to 31/08/2026 and failed on 01/09 with nobody touching the code: the\nchip prints the child''s age next to the vaccine status, the fixture is born\non 01/06/2026, and on 01/09 that child turned exactly 3 months old. Two\nelements then matched `/3/` — \"3 meses\" and \"3 vacinas atrasadas\" — and\ntesting-library fails a multiple match regardless of which one is right.\n\nThis broke `main`, not a branch: #53 touched only e2e/ and its own CI was\ngreen on 27/08, so the failure arrived with the calendar rather than with a\nchange. Any run of the suite between 01/09 and the day the fixture stops\ncontaining a 3 would have reproduced it.\n\nThe digit alone was never what the test wanted to prove. Matching the whole\nsentence makes the assertion independent of the date and strictly stronger:\nit now fails if the i18n pluralization breaks, which `/3/` accepted silently\nin either form.\n\nChecked for the same shape elsewhere: this was the only assertion in the\nsuite matching a bare number. Full suite green — 29 files, 122 tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqluElCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApbQQAKMsEmu4Rr1IGmQukfj5hXGM\nKJmW0bSxydFbXXMm3hOapeCIdXuVAo7YYOOs1awoNnYu4nnjmAeIgzA1GV69iJfk\nPASq5knkOKjJXrje+W1E3sXIuR4Teknl1D2F8MrIbQwNVg9gap+LCXJTJDQS7L0x\nOEoVJM75AEhn9Boi0O15mkJU4zu6vLWBHK89t1B9oOF5Ydti1SFpCQgF0MIk7htI\nMIq1UMhsfzq+JeKPzqWR9AbmsvqSYCQwmcVYCpTRlJfueqcCcAlWN0VYP4n6NWGM\npe5pIra4P0DLau14r+WHAlYmxU5CYkrazx92e2PIckQ3Z/h93GeNgoH43qxRUT4s\nNIVnBUoGXp7m2YFpAhML5Py2CyrynB1f0vA6cVNBF1x6fzecriIMjKYdKd7CfiHS\nZPTQh2mc3+dA7UgwNXPuGU0WpYMPp1/QR2DhFNY/Ki54Y/y68dJ1ekC7xgQNUnHh\nDTUGCTWqZzirb9EfYRZOQCfipFvMmB4FfeItqGpg//u4ajwuAUHF+WytIprd+ae9\nbVSpLWxsr2+gjMIh0akMDqLPhZd0lg4TequBFToVrqOBSd4ZzNPMXlufSw2JT7x9\ndizVd3iP0OaYwRhtNdic2E2qCf5XKRrqbmFpQ6WAnT0FaCocmomMSGYiJFmC8/7x\nGdVVM/mwJVP2RaXRmY/t\n=evit\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:28:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGVlNjE5YzVkNTA3MDMzMTg1ZTg2NTE5M2I0ZWQwYzJmNDhiOTYzZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c","sha":"f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c"}],"sha":"ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/ee619c5d507033185e865193b4ed0c2f48b963db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:09:03Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:09:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): un-skip logging a vaccine, and fix what the working contract exposed (#53)\n\nlog-vaccine has been `fixme` since 13/08/2026, when GET /babies/{babyId}/vaccines\nstarted answering a shape the frontend''s Zod rejects and /vacinas could only reach\nits error state. Its own comment said removing the `fixme` would be the first test\nthat the contract was fixed. cygnus-api #17 fixed it; this removes it.\n\nTwo assumptions in the spec turned out to have expired, and neither is a defect in\nthe app.\n\nThe date of birth now decides whether there is anything to apply. The 2026 catalog\ntook effect on 29/07/2026, and the API never marks a dose whose due date falls\nbefore that as pending or overdue — it reports GUIDANCE, and the screen says\n\"Orientação\". \"BCG at 0 months, so a freshly-added baby always has it pending\" was\ntrue of the previous catalog and is false of this one: measured against a real\nstack, a child born three years ago gets 29 guidance rows, 5 pending and zero\noverdue. The birth date is now computed from today rather than fixed, so the early\ndoses land inside the catalog''s validity.\n\nThe applied row leaves the first page. The list paginates and sorts taken doses to\nthe end, so looking for \"Aplicada em\" in the row that was just clicked finds\nnothing. The assertion moved to the \"Tomadas\" filter, which is where a person would\nlook.\n\n`getByRole(''dialog'')` also had to become the dialog *by name*: the date picker\ninside it is a Radix popover that carries role=\"dialog\" too and stays in the DOM\nafter closing. Two matches is a strict-mode violation, which fails regardless of\nvisibility — that assertion could never have passed.\n\nadd-baby needed `exact` for the same underlying reason. With the calendar loading\nagain, the dashboard also lists doses as \"Alice E2E · 1ª dose\", so the loose text\nmatched six elements where it used to match one.\n\nThe journey itself was verified independently before any of these edits: the apply\nPATCH goes out and comes back 200, and the dialog closes on its own.\n\n7 of 7 e2e specs pass against a real stack, including the WCAG 2 A/AA scan over\n/vaccines with real content — which had never been scanned with any. Note this\nsuite is not in CI (it needs a second repository plus Postgres and Redis), so CI\nwill not confirm it.","tree":{"sha":"8555ad820b21d6bff13a312ba911334f91add3f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/8555ad820b21d6bff13a312ba911334f91add3f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c","verification":{"payload":"tree 8555ad820b21d6bff13a312ba911334f91add3f2\nparent bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788271743 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788271743 -0300\n\ntest(e2e): un-skip logging a vaccine, and fix what the working contract exposed (#53)\n\nlog-vaccine has been `fixme` since 13/08/2026, when GET /babies/{babyId}/vaccines\nstarted answering a shape the frontend''s Zod rejects and /vacinas could only reach\nits error state. Its own comment said removing the `fixme` would be the first test\nthat the contract was fixed. cygnus-api #17 fixed it; this removes it.\n\nTwo assumptions in the spec turned out to have expired, and neither is a defect in\nthe app.\n\nThe date of birth now decides whether there is anything to apply. The 2026 catalog\ntook effect on 29/07/2026, and the API never marks a dose whose due date falls\nbefore that as pending or overdue — it reports GUIDANCE, and the screen says\n\"Orientação\". \"BCG at 0 months, so a freshly-added baby always has it pending\" was\ntrue of the previous catalog and is false of this one: measured against a real\nstack, a child born three years ago gets 29 guidance rows, 5 pending and zero\noverdue. The birth date is now computed from today rather than fixed, so the early\ndoses land inside the catalog''s validity.\n\nThe applied row leaves the first page. The list paginates and sorts taken doses to\nthe end, so looking for \"Aplicada em\" in the row that was just clicked finds\nnothing. The assertion moved to the \"Tomadas\" filter, which is where a person would\nlook.\n\n`getByRole(''dialog'')` also had to become the dialog *by name*: the date picker\ninside it is a Radix popover that carries role=\"dialog\" too and stays in the DOM\nafter closing. Two matches is a strict-mode violation, which fails regardless of\nvisibility — that assertion could never have passed.\n\nadd-baby needed `exact` for the same underlying reason. With the calendar loading\nagain, the dashboard also lists doses as \"Alice E2E · 1ª dose\", so the loose text\nmatched six elements where it used to match one.\n\nThe journey itself was verified independently before any of these edits: the apply\nPATCH goes out and comes back 200, and the dialog closes on its own.\n\n7 of 7 e2e specs pass against a real stack, including the WCAG 2 A/AA scan over\n/vaccines with real content — which had never been scanned with any. Note this\nsuite is not in CI (it needs a second repository plus Postgres and Redis), so CI\nwill not confirm it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqltx/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw2wQAJo8ohOLqRHwBetEuVcoBQ+i\ng8azPPmS74xei24Bpno/yJVj8yqK30FpIuqDNbs3AjXUEHCa9h8ejhlQWsh8x63Z\nIiGeMo3wJZ5PLHArU6ym3I0ArJLkRgNK/KDCIenaF5wIHtKF2IqUt6U8TpbdxJT8\nT1F7zQRQNom2o+nOqrMMqYHNaRU+3eZPkhjBLKHibrEaOWGCZVfMe3VmmwLTna4V\nFfZnwMzeYNHJcjImRcQIUz+LXhoXnRXpf8OwIGWMLruoPr3uSif4mAi87PYKPtZ2\nK6lfSFWFZOZ8u0A6k93upXf9wXCyvEC5wgWnTDKB1cN1ltW9we9WDnsUFFCblp1P\nXIHSp+97+5ybXMumitqx3xqaLplUFPXMkjspw5E3RLmCnyPBBs7/vOAD0lfwQbXJ\no0jTIOs7G3ZTCe5Nv/ZyaCeDgG5hxjTVFw0uVTX5KTUpJjTBLC2+OU+9+FtEWig2\nEA8s283JkhFqipZ25Ko4MlIL1y40JVX46UNwcJd91SOPIJoB4atGKy+rph0LT8Dw\nwCWa9XLeienHm+i7qQyAhqnDuVklDGYTR9vxslAqjF+vuyQmIxqtFACjRDjknzxZ\nuVxFCLY+2vUEdNIR27ZUHSUMFqhxrqrrMR11q7DcYAQ+wevpk9bOyFvSlKvkTfQh\nRBXRQbJrl4VLkKCtZTzp\n=AOu+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:09:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGY1NTJiZjU0YmFlZTBmNDdhN2RlZWVhNzY0ZWU3YzJjMzlmN2ExN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f","sha":"bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f"}],"sha":"f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f552bf54baee0f47a7deeea764ee7c2c39f7a17c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T03:30:30Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T03:30:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): let the desktop header wrap when the text is enlarged (#52)\n\nThe header is a flex row with three children — logo, nav, actions — and only\nthe middle one wrapped. The other two are flex-shrink-0, so when the text grew\nthe row had nowhere to go and simply overflowed.\n\nMeasured with root font-size at 200% in a fixed 1280 viewport, which is what\nWCAG 1.4.4 asks for (text resized, viewport unchanged):\n\n  /dashboard      rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n  /appointments   rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n  /milestones     rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n  /notifications  rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n\nThat is loss of function, not of polish: the account and the logout leave the\nviewport and cannot be reached.\n\n`flex-wrap` on the header itself fixes all four. Nothing moves at 100%: the\nrow fits on one line and the wrap never triggers.\n\nAlso measured in the same sweep and already correct: reflow at 320px CSS\n(WCAG 1.4.10) across all seven routes, and text at 200% on the two public\nscreens. Fourteen of fourteen now pass.","tree":{"sha":"724c710be15282b27e0cc098b3cfc6a0c8bd8ca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/724c710be15282b27e0cc098b3cfc6a0c8bd8ca2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f","verification":{"payload":"tree 724c710be15282b27e0cc098b3cfc6a0c8bd8ca2\nparent 56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787801430 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787801430 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): let the desktop header wrap when the text is enlarged (#52)\n\nThe header is a flex row with three children — logo, nav, actions — and only\nthe middle one wrapped. The other two are flex-shrink-0, so when the text grew\nthe row had nowhere to go and simply overflowed.\n\nMeasured with root font-size at 200% in a fixed 1280 viewport, which is what\nWCAG 1.4.4 asks for (text resized, viewport unchanged):\n\n  /dashboard      rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n  /appointments   rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n  /milestones     rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n  /notifications  rolagem-h=true   fora da tela: Família Teste, Sair da conta\n\nThat is loss of function, not of polish: the account and the logout leave the\nviewport and cannot be reached.\n\n`flex-wrap` on the header itself fixes all four. Nothing moves at 100%: the\nrow fits on one line and the wrap never triggers.\n\nAlso measured in the same sweep and already correct: reflow at 320px CSS\n(WCAG 1.4.10) across all seven routes, and text at 200% on the two public\nscreens. Fourteen of fourteen now pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj69WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe4AQAB3EAkOH4LHMF0zS0iVtgTpx\n8BwMItswB72RbSI+YEzDuK41uAFZoVGssw14mdWoi8+1gxLtJeGPfpKckBNz6qAg\nlJxqRC9ciQK8mtUErQeZiFryLWMzfpteeAl5CBxt/89pfFqZMwxna2G/xiPmuspJ\nAMYpkPJVbPWxdkJk8Gfrfu8yr9BLp8KH6NQpc0DDXXYy+ceM/wT6CqmczoifnpKZ\nmyJS2/aztmV0a0h6/BxuefwDXuEx0GAPr9EY+FPfCVOEawkna+F+RBazTCs9Bt9Y\ncKdr31W9mE1VD9YxYKxFVycSTVzHum3ajwpxcfMjGD+NeCIin/SaBdam7wQM9j2t\njkxgNN253a0leh8elG3dQBP0u3fRu5APOMQvu1uCIqGRczm8Bs5Z5O8DNF3DdwtM\nt5WsmCkA78tgld/XjPVQrdUJhcouHVc4kxakZuUVn0mHToqwnIbcUTPGM5XGSw/s\nMI8DnlRS1G//3/8W9/2Gd/G/M+MGGFFmauYZ1fG7NSGKMpgT818lIDwoP1Vglx6+\nEE6du8hr6giu2JeKPPvh9O6IQtT+qN1CQgHzlj+WGyK9s3ICRyFyYV3OLPuMjqsj\n37AnbeAG6wJxQ4VJSX6Ma0AMBJrGfmtbCo4UmiyWUC0BpXOt4G8VgVSfLFQgYOLE\nbih/0O07AXnBSjY7p3uJ\n=OWsk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T03:30:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGJiZThkYmY2YWY4YmU5MWUzZDM0MDY0NjJhOTRjYTFiZTQ1ZTIxNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002","sha":"56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002"}],"sha":"bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bbe8dbf6af8be91e3d3406462a94ca1be45e215f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T02:57:01Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T02:57:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(i18n): remove three keys nothing reads (#51)\n\ncomingSoonMessage, appointments.dateLabel and notifications.bellAria are\ndefined in all three locales and referenced nowhere in src. Twelve lines of\ncopy a translator would maintain and no one would ever see.\n\nappointments.dateLabel is not the one the appointment form uses — that is\nappointments.form.dateLabel, a different key, and it stays. So does\nvaccines.applicationDetails.dateLabel. Both were checked explicitly, because\nremoving a key by its leaf name is exactly how you delete the wrong one.\n\nFound by a new checker, docs/verification/audit-locale-parity.mjs, which\nanswers three questions: is a key present in one locale and missing from\nanother, is a key used in src and undefined, is a key defined and never used.\nAll three now report zero.\n\nThe checker was wrong twice before it was right, and both corrections are\nwritten into it:\n\n  Plural suffixes cannot be compared key by key. en and es send 0 to `other`,\n  pt-BR sends it to `one`, which is why *_zero exists only in pt-BR — measured\n  in an earlier iteration. Literal parity reported five failures where there\n  were five correct decisions. It now compares each locale against its own\n  Intl.PluralRules categories.\n\n  Reading only the first argument of t() called 30 keys dead. A ternary inside\n  the call — t(canLeave ? ''a'' : ''b'') — hides both branches from that. Matching\n  any dotted literal that exactly equals a defined key brought it to 3, and\n  those 3 were real.","tree":{"sha":"3d36b873efb37e96a7ebfa4187c76208113c72e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/3d36b873efb37e96a7ebfa4187c76208113c72e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d36b873efb37e96a7ebfa4187c76208113c72e1\nparent 14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787799421 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787799421 -0300\n\nchore(i18n): remove three keys nothing reads (#51)\n\ncomingSoonMessage, appointments.dateLabel and notifications.bellAria are\ndefined in all three locales and referenced nowhere in src. Twelve lines of\ncopy a translator would maintain and no one would ever see.\n\nappointments.dateLabel is not the one the appointment form uses — that is\nappointments.form.dateLabel, a different key, and it stays. So does\nvaccines.applicationDetails.dateLabel. Both were checked explicitly, because\nremoving a key by its leaf name is exactly how you delete the wrong one.\n\nFound by a new checker, docs/verification/audit-locale-parity.mjs, which\nanswers three questions: is a key present in one locale and missing from\nanother, is a key used in src and undefined, is a key defined and never used.\nAll three now report zero.\n\nThe checker was wrong twice before it was right, and both corrections are\nwritten into it:\n\n  Plural suffixes cannot be compared key by key. en and es send 0 to `other`,\n  pt-BR sends it to `one`, which is why *_zero exists only in pt-BR — measured\n  in an earlier iteration. Literal parity reported five failures where there\n  were five correct decisions. It now compares each locale against its own\n  Intl.PluralRules categories.\n\n  Reading only the first argument of t() called 30 keys dead. A ternary inside\n  the call — t(canLeave ? ''a'' : ''b'') — hides both branches from that. Matching\n  any dotted literal that exactly equals a defined key brought it to 3, and\n  those 3 were real.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj6d9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdzAQAAJVxlozARgleGaBhAMF9484\n4DFY4YXqXSG1lxQNV/Bc+Ty4m1mllJpqL9cU8boFFv9yozORaM1lsnZNgXcu9CdB\nmkzFd5muljLQZ6qYZXgakBx+rPpW9rfDEqrsc24oHAY9rHsRNP2geLK/TKm31dkv\nel0ztp9Ehl3rSZu4Jn0OslPbqzLKqtRsLToli/Nfu0Z4w5wUaWdBCb1RlSrttcN9\nWqioMPFRCRALI7Eaw2ROETtNEsAzwYKjsV4+QpREkfLLvA2dkgPK7/h6rcKHRIZq\nQo0efVFKf5IQS+XqjFKym5bWd/wDCi28kXs4n1QjKpyHiDWw0A6sTrZCpevnCZ5r\nqixkYY+lSToBsjhWXqniKCbwZcz1v3KRak75LhXCDk7lbmlYj2K1tL6qjPnMlh9D\n2kH9Y0RI/JS+roKdy0Jx2N4oOyXyxI32RFKi5ZnGeoxIYEkdxnBkT/I2HaTaFC6Y\nJSHIwKRQXO1LCbBwULp3RU9PsTGpXxCmGEbWvf+Q99PxSpbTAGf7xlYHQFXWY8/j\nm4HtyPEuefLBRXQ5SUmLBvSn/si7qNRby9z2VWW4PwAlKBVmNTa/f16Vk+GXucjW\nWv+fgB2dj4oEseBz7LQApmMGV5n63otjzldJmIQ4iUnTqnWaB9++WsmiFerP7eEX\n9OPr6nmLzc3cHPuEy7D8\n=p2HX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T02:57:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDU2ZTBjYzY1YWYyMWE0MzcwMjU2OTg1YmY4ODJlMjQxYzcxZWUwMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6","sha":"14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6"}],"sha":"56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/56e0cc65af21a4370256985bf882e241c71ee002"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T01:56:37Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T01:56:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): add a skip link so the keyboard can bypass the nav (#50)\n\nThere was none. Measured on the rebuilt container, signed in: the first Tab\nlanded on the logo, and reaching the main content took eleven presses —\nthrough the logo, five nav items, \"Adicionar Filho\", the theme control, the\naccount and \"Sair da conta\". On every page. WCAG 2.4.1, Level A.\n\nThe link is the first focusable element, hidden until focused\n(sr-only focus:not-sr-only), so it costs nothing visually and appears for\nwhoever is looking and tabbing.\n\n`tabIndex={-1}` on <main> is what makes it work rather than merely exist. A\nskip link pointing at an element that cannot hold focus only moves the\nscroll: focus stays in the header, and the next Tab goes right back into the\nnav. Verified by activating it, not by its presence:\n\n  primeiro Tab   \"Pular para o conteúdo\"\n  Enter          focus lands on \"Boa noite, Família Teste! 👋\", inside <main>\n\nAlso checked in the same sweep and already correct: focus is visible at every\nstop. Eighteen files carry `outline-none`, but each pairs it with\n`focus-visible:ring`, so the computed style at focus always shows an\nindicator — measured as computed style, not by grepping class names.","tree":{"sha":"d6173238eb1b7bd4fbac4295122f300fdc50957e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/d6173238eb1b7bd4fbac4295122f300fdc50957e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6","verification":{"payload":"tree d6173238eb1b7bd4fbac4295122f300fdc50957e\nparent 72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787795797 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787795797 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): add a skip link so the keyboard can bypass the nav (#50)\n\nThere was none. Measured on the rebuilt container, signed in: the first Tab\nlanded on the logo, and reaching the main content took eleven presses —\nthrough the logo, five nav items, \"Adicionar Filho\", the theme control, the\naccount and \"Sair da conta\". On every page. WCAG 2.4.1, Level A.\n\nThe link is the first focusable element, hidden until focused\n(sr-only focus:not-sr-only), so it costs nothing visually and appears for\nwhoever is looking and tabbing.\n\n`tabIndex={-1}` on <main> is what makes it work rather than merely exist. A\nskip link pointing at an element that cannot hold focus only moves the\nscroll: focus stays in the header, and the next Tab goes right back into the\nnav. Verified by activating it, not by its presence:\n\n  primeiro Tab   \"Pular para o conteúdo\"\n  Enter          focus lands on \"Boa noite, Família Teste! 👋\", inside <main>\n\nAlso checked in the same sweep and already correct: focus is visible at every\nstop. Eighteen files carry `outline-none`, but each pairs it with\n`focus-visible:ring`, so the computed style at focus always shows an\nindicator — measured as computed style, not by grepping class names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj5lVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANCUQAAds8Wu1N9tV8rWNPAfxxASE\nN/zqge+iijrsHEnQpa7oNnxWwYTggMxkSR88zRSpF3thYvYjuD3N0gaszQOxc2nW\n2RU1lTu51k5dHLJQoAqmUcr/I17R1dDdK+G0jPnZyhWPTQbvsMjqwpPkC3pjHgtb\nsQyFdIvMW0nyPisRW2nljAx55UCjdXUcGtZmHF8irRawTgGtQhlK5Cvy8miEVSGn\nCJhXUFXA+JM3FDDUJ1d3OmHU3bUe6/Y9qAeUauW5Di3mbYdpx/2KRnsnJ/XAmNJX\na+xn1DjRxfS40KvT2X3Z1TQrd5ThIfTvHy4cQL+HZtNC++NdyHNbuy2aMVw9tJB9\nStAvuTU1PM3fmevfJQMYfpOzPf+DfmXLiOK+OO97dv5BOy5lGl5z6aYOQoBuZtI1\nq1tGRJBc4mI9EOnCJ2x/EXTH+NR6iXtBrbic9bT4VYWM+VkT9IsRz/TxkTUKVJ+B\nU7Hev7r0ikqsxF5NmzHs/5bQS+0hqlYO/0AyK7Tw2nET89RkQ77Baaj9U7olof0N\nCuDSYCPep6gcqMn2oX6n+94J0FjvKWbOhqB94c01o3pkYLTE3inFt/1/VUo3QdfN\ncMiZC02jp4D5KrHyIM2txpLyvnsTj06gLiNHj0HycvX32IIDUuzZZ2XHOOZN752a\nh8erNDlxjUMVIsUcWh1d\n=hOhm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T01:56:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDE0ZTdmNDc3N2EyZDIxNDM0ZGZjOTJlY2FjNzk4OTJkYjA4NDFmYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524","sha":"72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524"}],"sha":"14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/14e7f4777a2d21434dfc92ecac79892db0841fa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T00:25:34Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T00:25:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): return focus to the trigger when a dialog closes (#49)\n\nRadix restores focus to the trigger on close — but it only knows a trigger if\none is a <DialogTrigger>. In this app eight of the nine dialogs are driven by\nstate (open={!!baby}, open={isAddBabyDialogOpen}), so there is nothing for it\nto restore to.\n\nMeasured by closing each with Escape and reading document.activeElement for\nthree seconds:\n\n  DeleteAccountDialog  (has <DialogTrigger>)  -> \"Excluir minha conta\"\n  AddBabyDialog                               -> body\n  EditBabyDialog                              -> body\n  AddMilestoneDialog                          -> body\n  AppointmentDetailDialog                     -> body\n\nLanding on body sends whoever opened the dialog from the keyboard back to the\nstart of the document, to tab through everything again — WCAG 2.4.3.\n\nThe capture lives in the Dialog root, not in DialogContent, and two earlier\nattempts failed for exactly that reason. Content mounts *after* Radix has\nalready moved focus inside, so reading document.activeElement there captures\nan element of the dialog itself; restoring that later sends focus nowhere. An\nonCloseAutoFocus interceptor built on the same wrong reference broke the one\ndialog that had been working. The root stays mounted and sees `open` flip.\n\nIt only restores when focus was left orphaned on body: if the person moved\nfocus somewhere else meanwhile, taking it back is worse than the defect.\n\nVerified on the rebuilt container, all five dialogs now return to their own\ntrigger, and the other three keyboard properties hold: focus enters on open,\nand Tab and Shift+Tab both stay trapped over 30 and 15 presses.\n\nThis edits a file the shadcn CLI generates, which the repo''s rules discourage.\nThe reason is written at the edit: the defect is in the primitive and affects\nevery dialog, so fixing it at nine call sites would be nine places to forget.","tree":{"sha":"8b1ba41ac1a244fce3fba8f457dc501f465b2be5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/8b1ba41ac1a244fce3fba8f457dc501f465b2be5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b1ba41ac1a244fce3fba8f457dc501f465b2be5\nparent 544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787790334 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787790334 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): return focus to the trigger when a dialog closes (#49)\n\nRadix restores focus to the trigger on close — but it only knows a trigger if\none is a <DialogTrigger>. In this app eight of the nine dialogs are driven by\nstate (open={!!baby}, open={isAddBabyDialogOpen}), so there is nothing for it\nto restore to.\n\nMeasured by closing each with Escape and reading document.activeElement for\nthree seconds:\n\n  DeleteAccountDialog  (has <DialogTrigger>)  -> \"Excluir minha conta\"\n  AddBabyDialog                               -> body\n  EditBabyDialog                              -> body\n  AddMilestoneDialog                          -> body\n  AppointmentDetailDialog                     -> body\n\nLanding on body sends whoever opened the dialog from the keyboard back to the\nstart of the document, to tab through everything again — WCAG 2.4.3.\n\nThe capture lives in the Dialog root, not in DialogContent, and two earlier\nattempts failed for exactly that reason. Content mounts *after* Radix has\nalready moved focus inside, so reading document.activeElement there captures\nan element of the dialog itself; restoring that later sends focus nowhere. An\nonCloseAutoFocus interceptor built on the same wrong reference broke the one\ndialog that had been working. The root stays mounted and sees `open` flip.\n\nIt only restores when focus was left orphaned on body: if the person moved\nfocus somewhere else meanwhile, taking it back is worse than the defect.\n\nVerified on the rebuilt container, all five dialogs now return to their own\ntrigger, and the other three keyboard properties hold: focus enters on open,\nand Tab and Shift+Tab both stay trapped over 30 and 15 presses.\n\nThis edits a file the shadcn CLI generates, which the repo''s rules discourage.\nThe reason is written at the edit: the defect is in the primitive and affects\nevery dialog, so fixing it at nine call sites would be nine places to forget.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj4P+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcSgQAEoP56NfDwEtSsALaHQuur3T\nC7tvVzWF+kJ5pwYKrcQNVxcyQB8xU6blfZ4TaUDVhlU4Z5GvhWwN0NZnqmJeVjq3\n0Jlre4eRgjvUxxviSoEhylUpttjl4EiM7dJSJrRpomHCrFtvwlA08jjABTx6LVUa\nAh+0t1Zd/SXEncPq52o1O9VXxWplOus535pDYfyAz9LWaecpSXGZm00n/wJKOLM+\nIxn8dorNmTwySD1iw3LTKTPgYtImXoae3hVKhorrVYZ7Zp3WOJTcLATNdx7dsp0o\nQkmYT68RuyOb1m5IC4q7gzWrRcBFZOQQW6MHs6b+NVu2gpvKWqudHp09rXNUbX6S\n0bnneWcEMdq9cQi0vH8jHiYVFWJOg53xEG5O/O+vJkTKNyjEq+yiqzL7bAelgX1O\nT+qB0V37qtifLjkQ6NW1+bT02pJNcNAx/JEriwNC+iDJKXL0Tv7nFgBBhHPr6SYF\niWY45AXOAyJQlX0x+6RhtH+jsF/VH5o3iL/gxViCtHvHVcmoYniObse+CQ04vZLo\nm1KcIH8gxtOUud/1FNZECnX/r4GNkjc4O+AyqLDGG4NEB79OwaNFty9EO7NQ1CZa\nX45r3nHr6ZAz7MfaGbGjHzOiK9QXBduZ9UuG41WzOlcqEBiodeKp49+7MWhg1frB\njg2R7z5VHfet65fJS9jn\n=fflr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T00:25:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDcyNDI3MDIzZmRkZmRmMzkyOWJjZDEzNmY2YWE0YjBiNzBlODU1MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213","sha":"544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213"}],"sha":"72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/72427023fddfdf3929bcd136f6aa4b0b70e85524"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T23:19:18Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T23:19:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(profile): give the delete-account dialog a way out that says so (#48)\n\nThis was the only dialog in the app with no labelled exit. Its controls were\n\"Excluir conta permanentemente\" and the X in the corner — nothing else. The\none dialog without a Cancel was the irreversible one.\n\nMeasured across the sweep:\n\n  EditBabyDialog       …, Cancelar, Salvar Alterações\n  RescheduleDialog     …, Cancelar, Salvar Alterações, Fechar\n  DeleteAccountDialog  Excluir conta permanentemente, Fechar\n\nEscape and the X did work, so nobody was trapped. What was wrong is that the\nonly prominent, named affordance was the destructive one — the opposite of\nwhat a destructive confirmation should do, where the safe choice ought to be\nat least as easy to reach as the dangerous one.\n\nCancel comes first, uses the existing common.cancel key, and is disabled while\nthe request is in flight like every other control here. No new copy.\n\nVerified on the rebuilt container: controls are now\n[\"Cancelar\", \"Excluir conta permanentemente\", \"Fechar\"], Cancel closes the\ndialog, and the account survives — navigating to /dashboard afterwards still\nlands there.\n\nThe other five states were already correct, including the wrong-password path\n(\"Senha atual incorreta.\") and the success path landing on /login.","tree":{"sha":"8bc7f70eed01e7eba206e7a41ef0154f5f3d005f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/8bc7f70eed01e7eba206e7a41ef0154f5f3d005f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213","verification":{"payload":"tree 8bc7f70eed01e7eba206e7a41ef0154f5f3d005f\nparent b75de8a7911f6b7eb96b83533981c2f7420f0924\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787786358 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787786358 -0300\n\nfix(profile): give the delete-account dialog a way out that says so (#48)\n\nThis was the only dialog in the app with no labelled exit. Its controls were\n\"Excluir conta permanentemente\" and the X in the corner — nothing else. The\none dialog without a Cancel was the irreversible one.\n\nMeasured across the sweep:\n\n  EditBabyDialog       …, Cancelar, Salvar Alterações\n  RescheduleDialog     …, Cancelar, Salvar Alterações, Fechar\n  DeleteAccountDialog  Excluir conta permanentemente, Fechar\n\nEscape and the X did work, so nobody was trapped. What was wrong is that the\nonly prominent, named affordance was the destructive one — the opposite of\nwhat a destructive confirmation should do, where the safe choice ought to be\nat least as easy to reach as the dangerous one.\n\nCancel comes first, uses the existing common.cancel key, and is disabled while\nthe request is in flight like every other control here. No new copy.\n\nVerified on the rebuilt container: controls are now\n[\"Cancelar\", \"Excluir conta permanentemente\", \"Fechar\"], Cancel closes the\ndialog, and the account survives — navigating to /dashboard afterwards still\nlands there.\n\nThe other five states were already correct, including the wrong-password path\n(\"Senha atual incorreta.\") and the success path landing on /login.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj3R2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADKsQAKmcxrBncAmasVU4Kt8T3xRG\nKBeWA8VjTIjxZyN4AEfyPTw/UDAE5BebJpNFggxbS0LtF1M9eG3Wm3g213w4gx2l\n0BGqPGkVI+Vw7IW974/XLMUQdflPeeKaKk7jhIyA2ZRSOcPPCSWRT4iFSaoK5Ebg\nJTDwPn+sh1Dl8vuY+Gelw+kStsL3bWm1t1elDcRXSE2SRpWkX+mnfpPzCIwzajdI\nzF/7B9aCYbPASedboh8a8tMdTn8kNhvmDh29nMe8d43wwu/e/vRpoDt4GoD5rVJ4\nLAGxODkHDQ5AitWsQSws4nZwg7eZEBxXWUboqg/z+9riwr3ZjBA5TLrH+PIlP60M\n/bD0dtq3aQ+9zH9LIF1X8Gb04iOuxJF9BnF4jXJGo27boBkJzC9yuJTVrwP0bbo9\nqLZUcCw6OwaTzqTlH6H6ziRWiWevw2Cak+lpU/WRNwNLXz6TJRaqAwW/sKcxw6KH\n/FcFF/DUM1j/jBIYvro1T2yl5gD1pd6aYm0PVyd9eqbk2FBC9Z1EDylOXXXgntky\nztyVH82f1DGDz2QiWTJ0hytZtiJxOkHh7I3pOjaMG355ToxS99Rai3lZASajvjCy\nURoTJPrlZynu7TZ054lhxY18snUKkBN2UW9fEk60u05DP2CHVm4p6bA+A6vyrapy\nr29txxHY219QdQ93frmK\n=RUgJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T23:19:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDU0NGJmNTQwZGZiMWVkNmIwNmJkMjk4MmViYzc4MDQ3YmYyNDcyMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/b75de8a7911f6b7eb96b83533981c2f7420f0924","sha":"b75de8a7911f6b7eb96b83533981c2f7420f0924","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b75de8a7911f6b7eb96b83533981c2f7420f0924"}],"sha":"544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/544bf540dfb1ed6b06bd2982ebc78047bf247213"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b75de8a7911f6b7eb96b83533981c2f7420f0924/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T22:37:44Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T22:37:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(guardians): say which action failed when removing a guardian (#47)\n\nThe success toast branches between leaving a profile and removing someone\nelse; the failure toast did not, and paid for it with the only message in the\napp that does not name what failed: \"Não foi possível concluir a ação.\"\n\nEvery other error in this codebase names the thing — criar o convite, salvar o\nmarco, excluir o perfil, carregar os responsáveis. This one asked the person\nto guess.\n\nIt matters more here than elsewhere. Radix''s AlertDialogAction closes the\nalert dialog on click, before the async handler settles, so a failure cannot\nbe shown inline — the toast is all the person sees.\n\nNow it branches like the success path, with the two actions the UI already\nnames (\"Sair como responsável\" and \"Remover {{name}}\"). No new concept: the\nwording follows the app''s existing convention.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, guardian present, DELETE stubbed 500:\n\n  before  \"Não foi possível concluir a ação. Tente novamente.\"\n  after   \"Não foi possível remover o responsável. Tente novamente.\"\n\nThe guardian stays listed either way, which was already correct.\n\nFound while sweeping GuardiansSection''s states — invite pending, invite\nerror, invite success with the link and copy button, removal error and\nremoval success all behave correctly.","tree":{"sha":"291390697d81e53c2a811aa028d03f7bc6ce14ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/291390697d81e53c2a811aa028d03f7bc6ce14ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/b75de8a7911f6b7eb96b83533981c2f7420f0924","verification":{"payload":"tree 291390697d81e53c2a811aa028d03f7bc6ce14ea\nparent d0ef7c92dabaf309f6869fdef335281a4a590c05\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787783864 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787783864 -0300\n\nfix(guardians): say which action failed when removing a guardian (#47)\n\nThe success toast branches between leaving a profile and removing someone\nelse; the failure toast did not, and paid for it with the only message in the\napp that does not name what failed: \"Não foi possível concluir a ação.\"\n\nEvery other error in this codebase names the thing — criar o convite, salvar o\nmarco, excluir o perfil, carregar os responsáveis. This one asked the person\nto guess.\n\nIt matters more here than elsewhere. Radix''s AlertDialogAction closes the\nalert dialog on click, before the async handler settles, so a failure cannot\nbe shown inline — the toast is all the person sees.\n\nNow it branches like the success path, with the two actions the UI already\nnames (\"Sair como responsável\" and \"Remover {{name}}\"). No new concept: the\nwording follows the app''s existing convention.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, guardian present, DELETE stubbed 500:\n\n  before  \"Não foi possível concluir a ação. Tente novamente.\"\n  after   \"Não foi possível remover o responsável. Tente novamente.\"\n\nThe guardian stays listed either way, which was already correct.\n\nFound while sweeping GuardiansSection''s states — invite pending, invite\nerror, invite success with the link and copy button, removal error and\nremoval success all behave correctly.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj2q4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdcIQACWreclSJIbe61Q0z1O6PpoR\njBaNo/wFS6UEy4fcsF+kEnnh4EAK8LnldKOTqJ4GKJPtRSL//b1ZBuCpMqNxqQFa\nYFikwTN/gYRjbL+3cCZFlwm/i3BSrWIobHz0QTieTdgW65WETzrzbcaynjK3eFJi\nNTME384ezUyC/ORahx1P7nYYGiXIUpBA/a6eZfy/p8CF6fu0kt56T0tpbflPKCi/\n4A74ru0pWoh7FC2r0JogzMSpchWlNWqMpZXwVKZfmxalVyC2fMMQatvbNz/JaxmN\njFYdP3DGyeaBBZuwMAo/RF+yG+xXAr4WCzAGm1y2DkfAdJK6bNvetIHA1FTx2frQ\nHMSpAEHTme8emvXmc28GpWT0GCEikFu7++b/x3AfgX7k25UOSxiJiWQw5Rt0Wb4g\nzlmh+zdjqOJL/Hl7WoyJIEyDptDwwkdBrQkXc6S9e6WzkA6fsdBWYRUaBcouGOwy\nndAq+O