tana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d0ef7c92dabaf309f6869fdef335281a4a590c05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T21:31:15Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T21:31:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(babies): tie the avatar palette back to the theme tokens (#46)\n\nAVATAR_BORDER_COLORS is four bare hexes in a component, and CLAUDE.md §4 says\nthe @theme block in index.css is the single source of truth for colour.\n\nChecked against it rather than assumed. Three of the four are exact copies of\nlive tokens:\n\n  #E8853A = --color-amber-500\n  #D95560 = --color-rose-500\n  #6C63FF = --color-violet-500\n\nThe fourth, #2A9D8F, matches nothing. It is teal — from the hand-tuned ramp\nthe emerald migration deleted on 25/08, whose removal is documented at the top\nof the same @theme block. Its three siblings are live tokens; it is a fossil,\nand it is still offered as a choice.\n\nThe hexes stay literal on purpose: the chosen value is persisted as\navatarColor and comes back from the database as a string, so it cannot be a\nvar(--color-…) resolved at render time. What could not stay implicit is where\nthey came from — without the note, a token changing would leave this palette\ndiverging in silence.\n\nNo behaviour change. Replacing the orphan teal is a brand choice, not an\nimplementation one, and it is recorded in the queue rather than taken here.\nChanging the palette would not alter avatars already saved anyway: it changes\nwhat is offered, not what is stored.\n\nFound while sweeping EditBabyDialog''s states, which all pass.","tree":{"sha":"f76f908a4428bd7b9ce2642acd8c1f1b9b9ce88b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/f76f908a4428bd7b9ce2642acd8c1f1b9b9ce88b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/d0ef7c92dabaf309f6869fdef335281a4a590c05","verification":{"payload":"tree f76f908a4428bd7b9ce2642acd8c1f1b9b9ce88b\nparent bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787779875 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787779875 -0300\n\ndocs(babies): tie the avatar palette back to the theme tokens (#46)\n\nAVATAR_BORDER_COLORS is four bare hexes in a component, and CLAUDE.md §4 says\nthe @theme block in index.css is the single source of truth for colour.\n\nChecked against it rather than assumed. Three of the four are exact copies of\nlive tokens:\n\n  #E8853A = --color-amber-500\n  #D95560 = --color-rose-500\n  #6C63FF = --color-violet-500\n\nThe fourth, #2A9D8F, matches nothing. It is teal — from the hand-tuned ramp\nthe emerald migration deleted on 25/08, whose removal is documented at the top\nof the same @theme block. Its three siblings are live tokens; it is a fossil,\nand it is still offered as a choice.\n\nThe hexes stay literal on purpose: the chosen value is persisted as\navatarColor and comes back from the database as a string, so it cannot be a\nvar(--color-…) resolved at render time. What could not stay implicit is where\nthey came from — without the note, a token changing would leave this palette\ndiverging in silence.\n\nNo behaviour change. Replacing the orphan teal is a brand choice, not an\nimplementation one, and it is recorded in the queue rather than taken here.\nChanging the palette would not alter avatars already saved anyway: it changes\nwhat is offered, not what is stored.\n\nFound while sweeping EditBabyDialog''s states, which all pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj1sjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMmAQAGhj1vuAjo0Ko48RK2xGuq1N\n7Mb7sfeHZ1YWNk6z4N4jYfUk8KXw8rimgl9LbfVv6KDcpxRQJBzXUG+6aVuLSstC\nd+tHzv/U/4odrCME2yZ2s88ToPxIi5NFiV3l25CurlmbeJO0Gq+gvpLRQobtouyl\nSMC8YILYPeNKvtu2jFv0jqWUhRNSqtScAKwtLJe7mk2pG3ggjA2dD0/2wZGWGxJu\ntl8boWXHkNlGPEUUsGeNjqcbvqA7/gOwpZoSlIeGl5Z6pOaymEp5Sa2RYZHFnaMd\nR2tMz7mLYdtd/jNw/MuVZTguqxT6/jux/GFH4dB1tKl4D453787TRidCpkWSQLhK\narrf3ZSPsqM280M/QQ3rxMtfq8u1S5oigN+4AH+LyIdigwrKSamV/pNEzu66kwHs\nC3sUEVC79fGoBpTiLodDyjzMLdnD2L0TldMvp+o2wyGtvVk6gw0nmuUizqkom7dw\n7EpH7QBNvUzmISkyw7/Q+6dLvX12O/cLaDjrlZcAQgqTSs+ej2g/7oGIUZve8zZm\nIMAg7Q1XxspUrjUzmJaQVNAg9/11/qAlvYmr8HkLq6QbcsrsHDuMC/qxVzkyH+Hy\ncNSl4BW+Q2bjgQfRnfX7hilg0o1XMXN5LKoU3kENIxL1lqSNXsYUlRJ0TzO1SZhH\neDDMXP1GxDqf1CDOV1y8\n=ha0Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T21:31:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/d0ef7c92dabaf309f6869fdef335281a4a590c05","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGQwZWY3YzkyZGFiYWYzMDlmNjg2OWZkZWYzMzUyODFhNGE1OTBjMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c","sha":"bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c"}],"sha":"d0ef7c92dabaf309f6869fdef335281a4a590c05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d0ef7c92dabaf309f6869fdef335281a4a590c05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T20:02:38Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T20:02:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): point the appointment fields at their own error messages (#45)\n\nThree inputs in the appointment feature set aria-invalid and rendered an\nerror paragraph, but never connected the two. A screen reader on doctorName,\ndate or time announced \"invalid\" and stopped — the reason was on screen and\nunreachable.\n\nEvery other form in the app already does this: AuthField, BabyProfileFields,\nMilestoneCoreFields, ChangePasswordForm, DeleteAccountDialog, ProfileForm and\nVaccineApplicationDetailsFields all pair aria-invalid with aria-describedby\nand an id on the message. Appointments was the one place the pattern was\nmissed.\n\nFound by the dialog-state sweep, which reports how many elements inside the\nopen dialog carry aria-describedby. AddMilestoneDialog answered 3 and\nAddAppointmentDialog answered 0 for the same kind of failure — the gap showed\nup as a difference between two cells, not as a rule anyone remembered.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, validation-failing state:\n\n  before  aria-invalid=1  describedby=0\n  after   aria-invalid=1  describedby=1\n\nNote on scope: a repo-wide grep also flags badge, button, input, radio-group,\nselect and textarea. Those are false positives — there aria-invalid appears\ninside a class string as a Tailwind variant selector, not as an attribute the\ncomponent sets.","tree":{"sha":"62f16588b1c4a47b221d4f35ef62a6dbdb511bb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/62f16588b1c4a47b221d4f35ef62a6dbdb511bb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c","verification":{"payload":"tree 62f16588b1c4a47b221d4f35ef62a6dbdb511bb4\nparent 4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787774558 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787774558 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): point the appointment fields at their own error messages (#45)\n\nThree inputs in the appointment feature set aria-invalid and rendered an\nerror paragraph, but never connected the two. A screen reader on doctorName,\ndate or time announced \"invalid\" and stopped — the reason was on screen and\nunreachable.\n\nEvery other form in the app already does this: AuthField, BabyProfileFields,\nMilestoneCoreFields, ChangePasswordForm, DeleteAccountDialog, ProfileForm and\nVaccineApplicationDetailsFields all pair aria-invalid with aria-describedby\nand an id on the message. Appointments was the one place the pattern was\nmissed.\n\nFound by the dialog-state sweep, which reports how many elements inside the\nopen dialog carry aria-describedby. AddMilestoneDialog answered 3 and\nAddAppointmentDialog answered 0 for the same kind of failure — the gap showed\nup as a difference between two cells, not as a rule anyone remembered.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, validation-failing state:\n\n  before  aria-invalid=1  describedby=0\n  after   aria-invalid=1  describedby=1\n\nNote on scope: a repo-wide grep also flags badge, button, input, radio-group,\nselect and textarea. Those are false positives — there aria-invalid appears\ninside a class string as a Tailwind variant selector, not as an attribute the\ncomponent sets.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj0ZeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6oMQAKb5b/nNYmTPqg5wc85e+ERY\nJR3y4muTbFFJXj56ZFjnP+PavyGScpRFzivi9Gu3/uVGE8HK3ZLIZIW9rOLAWW0o\npyjuvFp2tq1OXMvztMpkmy5/HDpKabakR78FqYwVFTQIIwIeXh1Hvm2oBQ3x+QfU\nKBaRfhWsBZBtdWdMokA4XcWzZWTtix6OdYizTnb4NtEvR7kzt8TGnS/L+a9bf/R4\njCWYg8rRTvsQbAnxr6Rem3Xt2xNpKWecI2oduuKsz5GL0+DMpsm3HK3Y8kkDutTg\nDpx6mrYZwAzoW7BKR3KHpM42vw58So31B9fqmNPyCQdehVJTe4ALBMBb2IQ0dHLj\nSUWvZiCt6HsyAVrbQED5giYtcW5sm84HyL+fKMb26LsNj7AHfayiVvwVgTF0Z3TH\ntCZim7PRwnwPVIkjLMqY1GoP+p/KDeVX1UgBHfIORqYyrEo3+qeO0XkuAD5yl+UP\niWlVynQC/c1l3ARrF7EKXa4AHe1Mffc6O8ejmb4qdire6nQr/GwmUywZzAouFVLe\nK0dQvzvirCm7jAIh6QuzyJRPp/gjcvHEYI4b8B4MvZXjLd3NawWkmhmQSnfKmgUv\nPoTuwkMtXFm+4d7TdvhVx+xm9JB1QtRTsvOV423vopHmd8YWuiL9pFxzN3v7ONXv\nX5jM5g+aLwZelc7ffT7C\n=eEg1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T20:02:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGJlYThkNzc2MmE5OTgxZWMwM2U1MjQ0NDUwNDMzMDJhNjI2MTg4MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d","sha":"4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d"}],"sha":"bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/bea8d7762a9981ec03e524445043302a6261881c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:03:04Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:03:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): say so when signing out fails (#44)\n\nhandleLogout awaited the mutation and then navigated. On failure the\nrejection was unhandled, the navigate never ran, and nothing was said: the\nperson pressed \"Sair\", stayed on the dashboard, and had no way to know they\nwere still signed in.\n\nFailing here is ordinary, not exotic — the API sleeps on Render''s free plan\nand takes about a minute to wake.\n\nThe tempting fix is to clear the identity and navigate anyway, since leaving\nis what the person asked for. That is wrong. The session cookie is HttpOnly,\nso the client cannot delete it, and if the server never confirmed the logout\nit is still valid: navigating would leave someone *looking* signed out\nwithout being, and going back to /dashboard would restore the session through\nthe silent refresh. In a child-health app on a possibly shared device, that\nlie is worse than the error.\n\nSo it stays put, reports, and stays retryable. A toast rather than an inline\nalert because the control is an icon in the header with no form to attach to\n— same surface GuardiansSection and InviteRedeemRoute already use for this.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, both paths:\n\n  logout OK     -> /login,     no toast,        no rejection\n  logout falha  -> /dashboard, error toast,     no rejection\n\nSame class as #43, outside a dialog.","tree":{"sha":"140049e22512d7e1e564f1313f39a623ee17e88f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/140049e22512d7e1e564f1313f39a623ee17e88f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d","verification":{"payload":"tree 140049e22512d7e1e564f1313f39a623ee17e88f\nparent 8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787770984 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787770984 -0300\n\nfix(auth): say so when signing out fails (#44)\n\nhandleLogout awaited the mutation and then navigated. On failure the\nrejection was unhandled, the navigate never ran, and nothing was said: the\nperson pressed \"Sair\", stayed on the dashboard, and had no way to know they\nwere still signed in.\n\nFailing here is ordinary, not exotic — the API sleeps on Render''s free plan\nand takes about a minute to wake.\n\nThe tempting fix is to clear the identity and navigate anyway, since leaving\nis what the person asked for. That is wrong. The session cookie is HttpOnly,\nso the client cannot delete it, and if the server never confirmed the logout\nit is still valid: navigating would leave someone *looking* signed out\nwithout being, and going back to /dashboard would restore the session through\nthe silent refresh. In a child-health app on a possibly shared device, that\nlie is worse than the error.\n\nSo it stays put, reports, and stays retryable. A toast rather than an inline\nalert because the control is an icon in the header with no form to attach to\n— same surface GuardiansSection and InviteRedeemRoute already use for this.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, both paths:\n\n  logout OK     -> /login,     no toast,        no rejection\n  logout falha  -> /dashboard, error toast,     no rejection\n\nSame class as #43, outside a dialog.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzhoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAriUQAJbHRWlbnkZYhQXAj0rG505S\nvauQdnmiN/GsTI6QWwZeJQ6qFYbF+4MSUJfV0GnwG+mHDj9crqW8u8c4m77l7Kz5\nwY9sGfypPP3dS+7zllAjYM+uyQhIPnF/AqbxuCJi93cfxvIq1VI2nFAsFUuXKmWL\n5emuf42SI09jll9lxbL8PxUkjLbH92AU8Pm4vD7KJJuAqOMFUzAYgHsqvvlsJpFK\nprsINVVrCQZOwcCLdFbHVtXf4CalJ/6Hq/2oCbkDr++jcWOS8RmHnT1smVMUQrF0\n2TpAvhqRFgWi0E9/+BhozYtAs0JEq1loQGHmfCaGKawaHnGrrjnY9bQ9Np6PMgrV\n9cGPto4Kvfaxnc5/oTvOPm34nVKy0C7IvotVNTkODBO9Kwa4oXniPBa/NIwAHTMR\nwsuB4hE/vZhrDianXTN0eW5IlkQqLvoAqI8B83TWalvPxY4kYSPBSFlav6aDeoWl\ntsWz6Lz8JaTuuzYNsy6bCtmRyJK/p5NJbOoCdvh3kAYDtgDcgwA8bLWk6FhUBo4Y\nJLkG2gHHyiltCFjTocIF43gtby71JFSRbEXel+BNrNavnLFZyD2uLAZl84uPEyIJ\n5e3wtNoGhUuKsfiv+indrotXpzvH99/nVyremy5rWqFTel46aBjg4jbu47zWJcna\n/ii/P8hXh4SnhXZBp8cr\n=cJ0u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T19:03:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDQ1Nzk0ODkxMjRkMmRhMDkyODg4MzQ1YWJlZWYxN2ZkNjk4MDVkMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389","sha":"8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389"}],"sha":"4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/4579489124d2da092888345abeef17fd69805d2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:32:54Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T18:32:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dialogs): tell the user when a submission fails (#43)\n\nWalking AddBabyDialog through its states found the API-error one silent. The\ndialog stayed open, the button went back to \"Criar Perfil\", and nothing was\nsaid. The only trace was an uncaught ApiError in the console. Someone clicks\nsave, sees the button flicker, and clicks again — and if the failure was\npartial, that is how duplicates get created.\n\nThe copy for this already existed and was never wired: babies.form\n.genericError, milestones.form.genericError and appointments.form\n.genericError have been in all three locales the whole time.\n\nThe shared forms — BabyForm, MilestoneForm, AppointmentForm — already catch\nthe rejection from their onSubmit prop and render role=\"alert\". So\nEditBabyDialog, EditMilestoneDialog and RescheduleDialog were fine. What was\nmissing is the three \"add\" wizards, which carry their own useForm instead of\ndelegating, plus the catch in AppointmentDetailDialog, whose alert was\nalready rendered but whose rejection still escaped as an unhandled rejection\nand therefore as a Sentry crash event for a failure the screen was handling.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, AddBabyDialog across five states:\n\n  validação reprovando  dialog open, still on step 1, 2 aria-invalid, 3 messages\n  enviando              button \"Salvando...\", disabled\n  erro da API   before  no alert, no toast, ApiError uncaught\n                after   \"Não foi possível salvar. Tente novamente.\", no rejection\n  fechar no meio        reopening starts clean on step 1\n\nA note on how the scope was found, because the first two attempts were wrong.\nGrepping each dialog file for catch/onError reported seven files as having\nnone — but three of those delegate to a shared form that handles it, and the\ngrep could not see across the component boundary. Then grepping for `<BabyForm`\nmatched `useForm<BabyFormInput>` in files that never render it. Only matching\nreal JSX usage gave the true list.","tree":{"sha":"a092f2d1328035a740fecf091d48c09be2b73473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/a092f2d1328035a740fecf091d48c09be2b73473"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389","verification":{"payload":"tree a092f2d1328035a740fecf091d48c09be2b73473\nparent 1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787769174 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787769174 -0300\n\nfix(dialogs): tell the user when a submission fails (#43)\n\nWalking AddBabyDialog through its states found the API-error one silent. The\ndialog stayed open, the button went back to \"Criar Perfil\", and nothing was\nsaid. The only trace was an uncaught ApiError in the console. Someone clicks\nsave, sees the button flicker, and clicks again — and if the failure was\npartial, that is how duplicates get created.\n\nThe copy for this already existed and was never wired: babies.form\n.genericError, milestones.form.genericError and appointments.form\n.genericError have been in all three locales the whole time.\n\nThe shared forms — BabyForm, MilestoneForm, AppointmentForm — already catch\nthe rejection from their onSubmit prop and render role=\"alert\". So\nEditBabyDialog, EditMilestoneDialog and RescheduleDialog were fine. What was\nmissing is the three \"add\" wizards, which carry their own useForm instead of\ndelegating, plus the catch in AppointmentDetailDialog, whose alert was\nalready rendered but whose rejection still escaped as an unhandled rejection\nand therefore as a Sentry crash event for a failure the screen was handling.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, AddBabyDialog across five states:\n\n  validação reprovando  dialog open, still on step 1, 2 aria-invalid, 3 messages\n  enviando              button \"Salvando...\", disabled\n  erro da API   before  no alert, no toast, ApiError uncaught\n                after   \"Não foi possível salvar. Tente novamente.\", no rejection\n  fechar no meio        reopening starts clean on step 1\n\nA note on how the scope was found, because the first two attempts were wrong.\nGrepping each dialog file for catch/onError reported seven files as having\nnone — but three of those delegate to a shared form that handles it, and the\ngrep could not see across the component boundary. Then grepping for `<BabyForm`\nmatched `useForm<BabyFormInput>` in files that never render it. Only matching\nreal JSX usage gave the true list.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjzFWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuUcQAIc1pvZ23pLS22L6XozytO+k\nuCbxeXCgDCDxihaUh8ysNordx+whAofmpX6J3Z8yl4Rz+aDI6hZn3+pyd164fSsA\nanzQYB01XSE+l5aVO2DJYuHZZVKYqqELogNpo+LalLYDoM8LdLsh7IF1/wTWZf+x\nkqml1QevGeJm3K1clI1JkTQdsXP1HNnaTsMZOyxhOWWGg6u4YfGUuaqABle0QToq\nOLnyUggu3t0GjcoZgKvDDFUK6Mrtl17fFK54ZCASYBFyD70H8o1KMFT6J7EHQ9T0\neyThrQU4aNAGeNC2S3uaa9nBhROULBjZtM4p5Ne/KbtTFSSr57NG9NIX5Vlq5y2e\nsF5lrIBrqmj+WbRZyIuM7vzI15YYim7YtXzkuDyETh3zCdQeU1zHGzhHJEtEckbu\npthQhC50rVG8eaCx4xewTg8/4+LOBtm7kDKzD3KQ/7Xgt2uCJQmfXSfxKimrd0/v\nCT3W6xGshueSfIIL7JaJ27Wpc9ZUBYE5eO/KX92WhsBYn+K2Ik9sGK++S+w0ozJ7\ns5tTxaHsOvbdOfAMnDVyvrg4xEOeTjDH8Mwt5YRREzIQ2sjzqDOej12oBenLHrw7\n0DbtWDihwDk6McTTxtk/a0DrEc3OZhlEGTFoy9Btvr5vrREh2mkW61KYmMb39e0y\nuvPyRINVaRQaFga7428r\n=l6y+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T18:32:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDg5MzgzNzkxNDBkYmM4NTQxYWIwODRmOWUzOWI3MGI2NDIyZjYzODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464","sha":"1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464"}],"sha":"8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/8938379140dbc8541ab084f9e39b70b6422f6389"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T17:52:22Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T17:52:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(router): stop showing React Router''s developer error screen to users (#42)\n\nEvery route in this app is lazy and main auto-deploys, so a deploy renames\nthe chunks. Anyone with the tab open who navigates afterwards requests a file\nthat no longer exists — and with no errorElement, React Router renders its\nown development screen: \"Unexpected Application Error!\" plus the stack.\n\nThe ErrorBoundary in App.tsx never sees this. A route error is handled by the\nrouter before it can reach a React boundary, which is why wrapping the app\nwas not enough.\n\nThe same browser error has two causes with opposite remedies, so the screen\ndistinguishes them. A deploy replaced the chunks: reloading is exactly right,\nbecause it fetches the new index.html pointing at the new chunks. There is no\nnetwork: reloading does nothing, and telling someone to try would be sending\nthem to do something useless. useOnlineStatus already existed for\nOfflineBanner.\n\n  chunk missing + online   \"Este app foi atualizado\"\n  chunk missing + offline  \"Sem conexão\"\n  anything else            the existing generic message\n\nDetection is a loose text match because browsers disagree on the wording —\nChrome \"Failed to fetch dynamically imported module\", Firefox \"error loading\ndynamically imported module\", Safari \"Importing a module script failed\". A\nfalse positive only swaps one error copy for another; a false negative falls\nback to the generic screen, which is what existed before. Neither makes\nanything worse.\n\nVerified twice, and the test was proven to fail without the fix: sabotaging\nthe detection to return false turns 2 of the 4 unit tests red. In the browser,\nsigning in and then navigating offline to a route never opened in that session\nnow renders \"Sem conexão\" instead of the raw error screen.\n\nFound while verifying the PWA, but it is not a PWA problem — it is a deploy\nproblem that offline merely made easy to reproduce.","tree":{"sha":"ebaf7007990298e4f0a35ff511a805ecf8661e27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/ebaf7007990298e4f0a35ff511a805ecf8661e27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464","verification":{"payload":"tree ebaf7007990298e4f0a35ff511a805ecf8661e27\nparent 5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787766742 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787766742 -0300\n\nfix(router): stop showing React Router''s developer error screen to users (#42)\n\nEvery route in this app is lazy and main auto-deploys, so a deploy renames\nthe chunks. Anyone with the tab open who navigates afterwards requests a file\nthat no longer exists — and with no errorElement, React Router renders its\nown development screen: \"Unexpected Application Error!\" plus the stack.\n\nThe ErrorBoundary in App.tsx never sees this. A route error is handled by the\nrouter before it can reach a React boundary, which is why wrapping the app\nwas not enough.\n\nThe same browser error has two causes with opposite remedies, so the screen\ndistinguishes them. A deploy replaced the chunks: reloading is exactly right,\nbecause it fetches the new index.html pointing at the new chunks. There is no\nnetwork: reloading does nothing, and telling someone to try would be sending\nthem to do something useless. useOnlineStatus already existed for\nOfflineBanner.\n\n  chunk missing + online   \"Este app foi atualizado\"\n  chunk missing + offline  \"Sem conexão\"\n  anything else            the existing generic message\n\nDetection is a loose text match because browsers disagree on the wording —\nChrome \"Failed to fetch dynamically imported module\", Firefox \"error loading\ndynamically imported module\", Safari \"Importing a module script failed\". A\nfalse positive only swaps one error copy for another; a false negative falls\nback to the generic screen, which is what existed before. Neither makes\nanything worse.\n\nVerified twice, and the test was proven to fail without the fix: sabotaging\nthe detection to return false turns 2 of the 4 unit tests red. In the browser,\nsigning in and then navigating offline to a route never opened in that session\nnow renders \"Sem conexão\" instead of the raw error screen.\n\nFound while verifying the PWA, but it is not a PWA problem — it is a deploy\nproblem that offline merely made easy to reproduce.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjyfWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzncQAFszM6NxSuhAjGUzL9eak3Y3\njHrFOdjMeXrmiy9zWADftEVz4oaVO9xpYs9W+N+gWLrx4uwTC/iDLsORXgOFttxM\nJim/ptFuiFCCuEKwU7bD3orqexrS1bFshFn0X5J18iXlD9FIl2XbViC2NNMZ/kzN\nfVzVRuUqbRgc+qd040OPtFnvdG9xD4OgoeGdtzUy8gEYqtPnjRQBRFa8SSwBinEI\n3CXrQNqzHeUfwJbAvkl4VEyg+r9VTV3B/UAhT0DYOnuJQncGWWIE0QN8qzmW0T0T\nmbLcZz5FYTeb7m1kdWJJ+GXOkVet7LrAfVbkvS9Bt1Te6SOhgGopEPjLQZ2eBkpx\n8YNLSFpgISJZkEWg0LXANdn9mxABXccvFsxHEsZQI/eajw4x+n2V16c9c7VxTWQK\nbxtnBXvUIoTDVXjZYjCmQ5UKklqebnDSVekHOn/XlQizNF6XI1JD/Ir6Yas243X1\nhNjeEGWDVM3luqBY4xo3VlRYGUkkeZpOL5WqUo0Fdzd3NTm78IfChD6adLAj3ZkM\nlnx/5LaD1o3jcZpWxlKDI3armuyyzr+Z5qVjWwDw9b1ob0ZZRmabNRFy0dG7hmp2\nq6OR6N67RMUPEqK6AqwK0PHvzzXrdOeC0tbzIMh/BuE4l3LMAE72WgqlNv3uAdII\n9sxFlWq9QxXKSOfYaO4T\n=mx8m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T17:52:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDFkMjQzNWM2M2Q5MGViYmIyYTMyMGY0NTNmYzYzNzA1YTdhMmE0NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1","sha":"5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1"}],"sha":"1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/1d2435c63d90ebbb2a320f453fc63705a7a2a464"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T17:03:26Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T17:03:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(legal): add versioned privacy and terms pages, marked as drafts (#41)\n\nThe only red blocker left in the queue. The app handles child health data —\nallergies, vaccines, appointments — and had no privacy page at all.\n\nWhat this delivers: the two public routes, the versioned document registry,\nand the footer links. What it deliberately does not deliver is the legal\ntext. Legal content cannot be generated, so the page says so at the top,\nbefore anything else, and `status: ''draft''` in the registry is what makes it\nsay that.\n\nThe split is the point:\n\n  the data inventory   factual, and derived from this repo''s Zod schemas —\n                       six categories describing what the app actually stores\n  the legal sections   listed by heading only, so it is visible what still has\n                       to be written, with no invented commitments about\n                       retention, legal basis or jurisdiction\n\n`shared/legal.ts` carries the version and is dependency-free, because the\nversion is what an acceptance record has to reference. A document changing\ncontent bumps its version, and everyone who accepted the previous one has to\naccept again — that is what makes consent auditable instead of a boolean with\nno meaning.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, both routes x both themes x 390/1440:\ndraft notice present in all eight, 6 inventory categories, 7 and 6 sections,\nno horizontal scroll, axe (wcag2a, wcag2aa, wcag22aa) clean. The footer of\n/login carries both links.\n\nNot delivered, and it needs the API: storing the acceptance. It is personal\ndata and has to survive a cache flush, so it belongs in Postgres, not Redis,\nand that is cygnus-api. The contract the front needs is recorded in the\nqueue. Nothing here pretends an acceptance was stored.","tree":{"sha":"fd3fc34295e1402269d7433c54efb3b433613200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/fd3fc34295e1402269d7433c54efb3b433613200"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1","verification":{"payload":"tree fd3fc34295e1402269d7433c54efb3b433613200\nparent d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787763806 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787763806 -0300\n\nfeat(legal): add versioned privacy and terms pages, marked as drafts (#41)\n\nThe only red blocker left in the queue. The app handles child health data —\nallergies, vaccines, appointments — and had no privacy page at all.\n\nWhat this delivers: the two public routes, the versioned document registry,\nand the footer links. What it deliberately does not deliver is the legal\ntext. Legal content cannot be generated, so the page says so at the top,\nbefore anything else, and `status: ''draft''` in the registry is what makes it\nsay that.\n\nThe split is the point:\n\n  the data inventory   factual, and derived from this repo''s Zod schemas —\n                       six categories describing what the app actually stores\n  the legal sections   listed by heading only, so it is visible what still has\n                       to be written, with no invented commitments about\n                       retention, legal basis or jurisdiction\n\n`shared/legal.ts` carries the version and is dependency-free, because the\nversion is what an acceptance record has to reference. A document changing\ncontent bumps its version, and everyone who accepted the previous one has to\naccept again — that is what makes consent auditable instead of a boolean with\nno meaning.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, both routes x both themes x 390/1440:\ndraft notice present in all eight, 6 inventory categories, 7 and 6 sections,\nno horizontal scroll, axe (wcag2a, wcag2aa, wcag22aa) clean. The footer of\n/login carries both links.\n\nNot delivered, and it needs the API: storing the acceptance. It is personal\ndata and has to survive a cache flush, so it belongs in Postgres, not Redis,\nand that is cygnus-api. The contract the front needs is recorded in the\nqueue. Nothing here pretends an acceptance was stored.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjxxeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApXYQAFL1CwqdbW/CAxPBKiUiw+lU\nZygySR5WCEupa3j0+6MvlGAPfVV6WCZ/1TGdughZ0lG6/uDtCvt+uYyu1YwrHDob\n62RHGw4EF19JtED+jhni0azzp0n+5V2pW7iPzC2cvNNUcHMgH4IHAS9R6K7B9pNO\nfQC4cHfw7QmEdAUHU/EzMPMjWhyRoKx1Q4XVOlWLFUBCN2Xj2RvlbRphMoOBW26v\nQlV34Q71SARgLki71KOJiZjoe9u2DEoz24aCUHufKmUBErlnDi+3E/vK2xuVkOL2\n/zxbRKlsX7UITsMpnwlctN56dJ3kGPM32HFalWiybpijesDs9uc8H6PR1Bu7mE8x\nyGjbZgDHYbtqcA80B/yvStW7tRHHiX7o0UGGFfCCKXC6RyH7+ShHau29NQZzwqVZ\n8EIzPv1JcUfeInYrxWD7nJXvqWI+PNxgsr5cusaoF+k2B78yHfURTw+nbiuwrZlH\nSZyqcj7GANkQirRxoehvdYhQVhZ3rirtb81puZj+ExhMxrh5wkkdn3lV5smW0tLy\nG1MQy7I4m9g4JD6mq3L8wGNvCEfML2SNCNfF2/e6KjxxEQ3ZN/hXvm60Yl1LbcCx\n1g4H8eEmOKHeSr0vOLqSsJhjfFk0ouGUKM6ywjPGqSuuARdZiE8iCN2a++APtWez\nnFcAaAcgt0e4ej8sjPZt\n=pWFh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T17:03:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDU0NjU2NDY3NzZkZDA1MTYyZjM2MzkzM2JjOTA1MTg0ZWMwOTllYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545","sha":"d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545"}],"sha":"5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/5465646776dd05162f363933bc905184ec099ec1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T15:20:06Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T15:20:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pwa): make the app installable and usable offline (#40)\n\nA child-health app is consulted on a phone, in a clinic, often on a bad\nconnection. `useOnlineStatus` and `OfflineBanner` already existed — the app\nknew it was offline and did nothing about it.\n\n**The service worker is hand-written, no Workbox**, and the reason is the deny\nlist. `embed/` and `mf/` are published contracts whose consumers live in other\npeople''s deployments, with stable unhashed filenames and `max-age=600` on\npurpose. Caching them there is not a local bug: it is a frozen version the\nconsumer has no way to invalidate. Sixty explicit lines beat a generator whose\nscope I would have had to audit anyway.\n\nStrategies, each for a stated reason:\n\n  navigation  network first, cache as a safety net. index.html is served\n              `no-cache` because it points at hashed assets; cache-first would\n              serve a stale index pointing at assets that no longer exist.\n  /assets/    cache first — safe only because the names carry a hash and\n              Vercel serves them `immutable`.\n  everything  passes through untouched. /api/ and /uploads/ are excluded on\n  else        top of embed/mf: child health data behind a session does not\n              belong in Cache Storage, which any same-origin script can read\n              and which survives logout.\n\nIcons are generated from the app''s own LogoIcon on the --primary emerald.\nThe favicon they replace was a purple bolt from the initial scaffold commit,\nunrelated to this app''s brand — the tab and the installed icon now agree.\n\nRegistration is production-only: an active SW intercepts Vite''s HMR and\nserves stale modules, which is the same \"my edit did not take\" symptom the\ncontainer already produces on :4205. One way to be fooled is enough.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container:\n\n  /sw.js                 200 application/javascript  (not swallowed by the\n                                                      SPA rewrite)\n  registration           registered, controlling, scope /\n  manifest               standalone, 3 icons, maskable present\n  embed/ mf/ api/        0 entries in Cache Storage after fetching all three\n  /assets/ under SW      cached\n  offline, visited route login renders fully\n\nKnown limit, measured not assumed: a route never visited fails offline,\nbecause its lazy chunk was never fetched. It fails with React Router''s raw\nerror screen rather than anything friendly — recorded in the queue, since\nthat same screen appears online whenever a deploy removes a chunk a client\nstill references.","tree":{"sha":"92843cb7688c852cdf183415b1cd74d02f32d56c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/92843cb7688c852cdf183415b1cd74d02f32d56c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545","verification":{"payload":"tree 92843cb7688c852cdf183415b1cd74d02f32d56c\nparent ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787757606 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787757606 -0300\n\nfeat(pwa): make the app installable and usable offline (#40)\n\nA child-health app is consulted on a phone, in a clinic, often on a bad\nconnection. `useOnlineStatus` and `OfflineBanner` already existed — the app\nknew it was offline and did nothing about it.\n\n**The service worker is hand-written, no Workbox**, and the reason is the deny\nlist. `embed/` and `mf/` are published contracts whose consumers live in other\npeople''s deployments, with stable unhashed filenames and `max-age=600` on\npurpose. Caching them there is not a local bug: it is a frozen version the\nconsumer has no way to invalidate. Sixty explicit lines beat a generator whose\nscope I would have had to audit anyway.\n\nStrategies, each for a stated reason:\n\n  navigation  network first, cache as a safety net. index.html is served\n              `no-cache` because it points at hashed assets; cache-first would\n              serve a stale index pointing at assets that no longer exist.\n  /assets/    cache first — safe only because the names carry a hash and\n              Vercel serves them `immutable`.\n  everything  passes through untouched. /api/ and /uploads/ are excluded on\n  else        top of embed/mf: child health data behind a session does not\n              belong in Cache Storage, which any same-origin script can read\n              and which survives logout.\n\nIcons are generated from the app''s own LogoIcon on the --primary emerald.\nThe favicon they replace was a purple bolt from the initial scaffold commit,\nunrelated to this app''s brand — the tab and the installed icon now agree.\n\nRegistration is production-only: an active SW intercepts Vite''s HMR and\nserves stale modules, which is the same \"my edit did not take\" symptom the\ncontainer already produces on :4205. One way to be fooled is enough.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container:\n\n  /sw.js                 200 application/javascript  (not swallowed by the\n                                                      SPA rewrite)\n  registration           registered, controlling, scope /\n  manifest               standalone, 3 icons, maskable present\n  embed/ mf/ api/        0 entries in Cache Storage after fetching all three\n  /assets/ under SW      cached\n  offline, visited route login renders fully\n\nKnown limit, measured not assumed: a route never visited fails offline,\nbecause its lazy chunk was never fetched. It fails with React Router''s raw\nerror screen rather than anything friendly — recorded in the queue, since\nthat same screen appears online whenever a deploy removes a chunk a client\nstill references.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjwQmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/SsQAKTUSntJCfiH3ugSMjR+jIOE\nJH+5ZLfs1DMSPQJzC1TAlbE9EwFelH3MMZoq6bSzJpnyM/5sHCxhEbQV/V0TAj8v\nNrdbVPBE9d+eLFEKjF5Wu0vI6zNFBNJpbWZoc5rPWrWXHXAwdtyWzmBEEtRGmjdb\nywwiOeVTmiOMuswBU63lt4IFarVsOIg624hvi/sNBawM60BGI/nGp4PJGLsizc+r\ntagmJsPNf3Zoj761/PWOW8ccchNQTFhFigfngvIus7qLsHFsEYPVscgWP8USwPrU\nlfgLJ4mUXBUGRSuY6LtXvOq9eV8qHWNd6JTJNJ9qYZxlrZGFWYp7cgKvGytCewMD\n8Mb04uB/UsOyZGyfsC9rHWEaE8DJa4cEqgQMjErbpIswfjLnM1VAZXO/wMM+cu54\nPy/+7QAVNO+B1Agrdr7OqNmuIA294Pj3pdqg+6n63rod+TBOwM6DyqhYLngRMSt7\nv0Cq3w+1gIbp6NUmE4UyagUZBrrCfGqZ9k/BD34tiQ/gDL9lDdjIT1vJHQK/ZxFK\n/qtHB3kktOkhq6+FWOb8UHXk8Ibty5W5L7bck4r9VqaQ6GDR21sruKAIEsfWr+DH\nXvnqB7GxoaVch+bX1VNh/LZVh3IEX4K1++k3TZCjsMlZD+6yerkgLgQug7a/PyzA\nINJfZny2/EFUkhFb+oJV\n=rxly\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T15:20:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGQ3NDBlNmUwMGZjNmQ3YmFiN2QwMDRiYTdjM2U2ZTAxMzQ0YTc1NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e","sha":"ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e"}],"sha":"d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/d740e6e00fc6d7bab7d004ba7c3e6e01344a7545"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:45:00Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:45:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(404): size the way out like a primary action (#39)\n\nThe catch-all route sits outside ProtectedLayout and outside AppShellLayout,\nso a 404 renders with no nav and no header in either auth state. That makes\n\"Voltar ao início\" the only way off the page — and it was drawn at 117x32,\nthe raw Button default.\n\nThat is the exact measurement the invite CTA carried before it was fixed, for\nthe same reason: a screen whose whole purpose is one action was presenting\nthat action smaller than any form submit in the app. Here it matters more,\nbecause there is no shell to fall back on.\n\nNow h-12, full width up to max-w-xs. Measured on the rebuilt container across\nboth auth states and both viewports:\n\n  deslogado  390 / 1440   117x32 -> 320x48   escape lands on /login\n  logado     390 / 1440   117x32 -> 320x48   escape lands on /dashboard\n\naxe (wcag2a, wcag2aa, wcag22aa) clean in all four, before and after.\n\nNot changed, deliberately: the missing app shell. Nesting the catch-all under\nProtectedLayout would send a logged-out visitor to /login instead of showing\nthem a 404, which is worse than the inconsistency — the same trap the invite\nroute''s comment already records. Whether a signed-in 404 should carry the\nshell is a routing decision, and it is recorded in the queue rather than\ntaken here.","tree":{"sha":"54f1826534ae4b85416de33219e500e0eda2df58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/54f1826534ae4b85416de33219e500e0eda2df58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e","verification":{"payload":"tree 54f1826534ae4b85416de33219e500e0eda2df58\nparent 097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787755500 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787755500 -0300\n\nfix(404): size the way out like a primary action (#39)\n\nThe catch-all route sits outside ProtectedLayout and outside AppShellLayout,\nso a 404 renders with no nav and no header in either auth state. That makes\n\"Voltar ao início\" the only way off the page — and it was drawn at 117x32,\nthe raw Button default.\n\nThat is the exact measurement the invite CTA carried before it was fixed, for\nthe same reason: a screen whose whole purpose is one action was presenting\nthat action smaller than any form submit in the app. Here it matters more,\nbecause there is no shell to fall back on.\n\nNow h-12, full width up to max-w-xs. Measured on the rebuilt container across\nboth auth states and both viewports:\n\n  deslogado  390 / 1440   117x32 -> 320x48   escape lands on /login\n  logado     390 / 1440   117x32 -> 320x48   escape lands on /dashboard\n\naxe (wcag2a, wcag2aa, wcag22aa) clean in all four, before and after.\n\nNot changed, deliberately: the missing app shell. Nesting the catch-all under\nProtectedLayout would send a logged-out visitor to /login instead of showing\nthem a 404, which is worse than the inconsistency — the same trap the invite\nroute''s comment already records. Whether a signed-in 404 should carry the\nshell is a routing decision, and it is recorded in the queue rather than\ntaken here.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjvvsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7AIQAH5Vj4tJkgyVyGODH54cMn8a\nJL8gjEKWtIZ+LYcn55SWo2Co2WM8Dh3kQYaVl/JJovuz35sHqfHJlGgYdcPaG1Vo\njE4BG2a5+52g