ps://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59"}],"sha":"ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/ad5a2bdf4a1aff61d9dc33c9cbe7ba72f83d596e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:08:31Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:08:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(i18n): stop rendering zero with singular grammar in pt-BR (#38)\n\nCLDR puts 0 in the `one` category for Portuguese, so every count of zero\npicked the singular string: \"0 mês\", \"0 não lida\", \"0 momento especial\nregistrado\". English and Spanish put 0 in `other` and were already correct,\nwhich is why this only ever showed in the default locale.\n\nA sweep of pt-BR found ten `_one` keys carrying {{count}}. Five of them can\nactually receive zero; the other five are behind a `> 0` guard at the call\nsite, and one (`notifications.bellAria`) is not referenced anywhere in src.\nOnly the five reachable ones get a `_zero` variant:\n\n    babies.monthsOld                        \"0 mês\"    -> \"0 meses\"\n    babies.dashboard.statVaccinesAppliedSub \"0 pendente\"\n    vaccines.ageGroupLabel                  \"0 mês\"\n    milestones.summary                      \"0 momento especial registrado\"\n    notifications.unreadCount               \"0 não lida\" -> \"0 não lidas\"\n\ni18next honours a `_zero` suffix for count === 0 even in a language whose\nCLDR rules have no zero category — verified against the installed version\nbefore relying on it, not assumed from the docs.\n\nen.json and es.json are deliberately untouched: adding `_zero` there would\nduplicate `_other` and put noise in the diff for no behaviour change.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container: /profile with a newborn reads \"0 meses\",\n/notifications reads \"0 não lidas\".","tree":{"sha":"60791771bb9ea9afd5be6e6546625fb9d9d27a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/60791771bb9ea9afd5be6e6546625fb9d9d27a4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59","verification":{"payload":"tree 60791771bb9ea9afd5be6e6546625fb9d9d27a4a\nparent 50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787753311 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787753311 -0300\n\nfix(i18n): stop rendering zero with singular grammar in pt-BR (#38)\n\nCLDR puts 0 in the `one` category for Portuguese, so every count of zero\npicked the singular string: \"0 mês\", \"0 não lida\", \"0 momento especial\nregistrado\". English and Spanish put 0 in `other` and were already correct,\nwhich is why this only ever showed in the default locale.\n\nA sweep of pt-BR found ten `_one` keys carrying {{count}}. Five of them can\nactually receive zero; the other five are behind a `> 0` guard at the call\nsite, and one (`notifications.bellAria`) is not referenced anywhere in src.\nOnly the five reachable ones get a `_zero` variant:\n\n    babies.monthsOld                        \"0 mês\"    -> \"0 meses\"\n    babies.dashboard.statVaccinesAppliedSub \"0 pendente\"\n    vaccines.ageGroupLabel                  \"0 mês\"\n    milestones.summary                      \"0 momento especial registrado\"\n    notifications.unreadCount               \"0 não lida\" -> \"0 não lidas\"\n\ni18next honours a `_zero` suffix for count === 0 even in a language whose\nCLDR rules have no zero category — verified against the installed version\nbefore relying on it, not assumed from the docs.\n\nen.json and es.json are deliberately untouched: adding `_zero` there would\nduplicate `_other` and put noise in the diff for no behaviour change.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container: /profile with a newborn reads \"0 meses\",\n/notifications reads \"0 não lidas\".","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjvNfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhJcQAA/rZfngtHty1hLpRwfl60RK\naXHFfmZ+1T9yA7Hk9PBLk/OTV1kyd6g+NFv7p/ytHk5EvQ0G/11YJDvY2pV4N3Pi\nalb/DG3eTjbP46KuXKJ2dXCDxD9Ng+9wBrlW8oWre/c7wdfG0NHB9uaVIbG4yopf\nHWMXgYlfbmUDmfBucTlYr1aIR+AiaSp1Uh5ggJ3d3ghR3XTYX/bCaEf17TSdjQV5\nDXhkqb4JKGkaKActpsbCX7lM/UC4+z50vCPR8JCUOygdkdpyBG+LAIc8HalTp5Xh\n0ArbmEN4c/kjdJqItOrkhMvePqnV3m2PiULQl5oLACQEkQymWs9pmNKzrHCvH8Hy\nmv9y1Ncqa6qlnqXClxVUBO71SykierPMRUlxOeEe98djlnhUjDSwAkA85t5T4cKr\n59F9BKrOVyIwvfpDosXZvOL5x9wfR3GOdMByQgxF02rw2wvh7V93saztpbtPW8H5\nFFcma3O8GqiU2OqTbf0czz2oTk3XbY+AQ0Nn0D9m//F0biLctLDtysKpJ7CsqdrN\nNFLXtglO3xifnLz4N8L7U0CUGp7NG87nczQG6ELCjQA6Nh6BbmHdKecbgfbfsvPz\nQO+AP7xOWK72mkLI7Gndt2ZRv6Tq+w/PDRGZf2YSn3KGTKEWu/QijHmnnUbk1ZJ1\nMp8N9wU5fdTLjnZmgzPL\n=RdXR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T14:08:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDA5N2NlMjg1MzFmNzJiOGY3M2ZmYmIzN2IzNThmZDNmYmUyYTZmNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd","sha":"50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd"}],"sha":"097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/097ce28531f72b8f73ffbb37b358fd3fbe2a6f59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T13:30:00Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T13:30:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: stop presenting an unfetched list as a fact (notifications, dashboard) (#37)\n\n* fix(notifications): stop reporting an unread count that was never fetched\n\nunreadItems comes from `data ?? []`, so it is empty while the query is\npending and while it failed — and \"0 não lida\" is a reassuring sentence to\nread when the truth is that nothing was fetched. On failure it sat directly\nabove \"Não foi possível carregar as notificações.\"\n\nMeasured against the running stack, by delaying and by failing the request:\n\n  before  loading  \"Notificações 🔔  0 não lida\"\n          error    \"0 não lida\"  above the error\n  after   loading  \"Notificações 🔔  Carregando as notificações…\"\n          error    no subtitle, error alone\n          data     \"0 não lida\"   (unchanged — the API really returns [])\n\nThis is the fifth screen with this shape, after the dashboard, /vaccines,\n/appointments and /milestones. The sweep that declared the class closed was\na one-line grep for `.filter(...).length`, and here the list and its `.length`\nlive on different lines, so it saw nothing. That claim was wrong; the\nreplacement sweep lives in docs/verification and matches names across the\nfile.\n\n* fix(dashboard): do not show the onboarding screen while the family loads\n\n`babies.data ?? []` is empty for three different reasons and only one of them\nis \"this family has no children\". Falling straight through to the length\ncheck meant that while GET /babies was in flight — or after it failed — a\nparent of six saw the onboarding screen: \"Bem-vindo(a) ao Meu Neném!\nAcompanhe vacinas, consultas e os marcos mais especiais…\", followed by their\nreal dashboard once the data arrived.\n\nThis is the same class as the four false counts already fixed, but a degree\nworse: not a wrong number inside the right screen, the wrong screen.\n\nMeasured by delaying GET /babies by 5s and by failing it, with three children\nseeded:\n\n  before  loading  \"Bem-vindo(a) ao Meu Neném! Acompanhe vacinas…\"\n          error    same onboarding screen\n  after   loading  skeleton, no copy\n          error    \"Não foi possível carregar os dados da família.\"\n          data     \"Bom dia, Família Teste! 👋  Acompanhando 3 crianças\"\n\nThe other widgets on this page already branch on their own pending/error.\nThis query is different in kind because it decides which screen exists at\nall, which is why the guard belongs before the length check rather than\ninside a card.","tree":{"sha":"a9fb8572ef42f63c38cd7e6e68e441c7856749c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/a9fb8572ef42f63c38cd7e6e68e441c7856749c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd","verification":{"payload":"tree a9fb8572ef42f63c38cd7e6e68e441c7856749c1\nparent 5535cc3ff50c43c0efa3936b6fc7ad91806a071b\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787751000 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787751000 -0300\n\nfix: stop presenting an unfetched list as a fact (notifications, dashboard) (#37)\n\n* fix(notifications): stop reporting an unread count that was never fetched\n\nunreadItems comes from `data ?? []`, so it is empty while the query is\npending and while it failed — and \"0 não lida\" is a reassuring sentence to\nread when the truth is that nothing was fetched. On failure it sat directly\nabove \"Não foi possível carregar as notificações.\"\n\nMeasured against the running stack, by delaying and by failing the request:\n\n  before  loading  \"Notificações 🔔  0 não lida\"\n          error    \"0 não lida\"  above the error\n  after   loading  \"Notificações 🔔  Carregando as notificações…\"\n          error    no subtitle, error alone\n          data     \"0 não lida\"   (unchanged — the API really returns [])\n\nThis is the fifth screen with this shape, after the dashboard, /vaccines,\n/appointments and /milestones. The sweep that declared the class closed was\na one-line grep for `.filter(...).length`, and here the list and its `.length`\nlive on different lines, so it saw nothing. That claim was wrong; the\nreplacement sweep lives in docs/verification and matches names across the\nfile.\n\n* fix(dashboard): do not show the onboarding screen while the family loads\n\n`babies.data ?? []` is empty for three different reasons and only one of them\nis \"this family has no children\". Falling straight through to the length\ncheck meant that while GET /babies was in flight — or after it failed — a\nparent of six saw the onboarding screen: \"Bem-vindo(a) ao Meu Neném!\nAcompanhe vacinas, consultas e os marcos mais especiais…\", followed by their\nreal dashboard once the data arrived.\n\nThis is the same class as the four false counts already fixed, but a degree\nworse: not a wrong number inside the right screen, the wrong screen.\n\nMeasured by delaying GET /babies by 5s and by failing it, with three children\nseeded:\n\n  before  loading  \"Bem-vindo(a) ao Meu Neném! Acompanhe vacinas…\"\n          error    same onboarding screen\n  after   loading  skeleton, no copy\n          error    \"Não foi possível carregar os dados da família.\"\n          data     \"Bom dia, Família Teste! 👋  Acompanhando 3 crianças\"\n\nThe other widgets on this page already branch on their own pending/error.\nThis query is different in kind because it decides which screen exists at\nall, which is why the guard belongs before the length check rather than\ninside a card.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjupYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnvYQAG4kCyNCspZ94BZvIctRCyai\nwUFDTUS7XCH29wCW4eVTvumj62VY7JtkTUEkIMmWPX/S5QxH6XUtDvmYWvfdPiWy\n8W1hde+jGqK2pG94cC5RtdH5uJJnfBYEDSBlediN2imJYUf4dUdH7dx/QC+iq3Gh\nQmAR1M4kIT/eZaROAKev5G1PZPR8qRc2cDwrWGOJW7f6W/QqQSRXbJMmnr1WHcQA\nZRFH1EE96wHrS9B5q86rEpZVzb5HBCXNYlAlMkxmrcxr4rAa3S17BStyYsAWfale\nVuKCxRg7ylcUjOaywa3fEy99Pul+Agggfl7Ec7QtEHQ0HtaL5D+AqNclcjweS9ee\nMF5LzU3Yamk5HQYJWy+toEXzqgPOjRWJWF/xwOK93ZAspQU2Qzf2ssm1eylizNtB\nzvWqRv1Kek3Vz6h5Ue3F7RP9TnUO2U1ODjRJWwzmW4RD4Odji9rPRJonhcJtt/ht\nic4ZKOmPQeSAhXKsZ9DR/06aimDs1fUXVGHF7jZFXk5j8/Sp5UHJh/i3pfYcUoXK\nCuAdA1jqfj9/fi30b2gqiH7sFsG8m4uKv9BcHCnGwIX1nXaX8Q87ELsFcmEtL267\nh4rAdRhWoF3KvLnanEJ8IbCF0mc0RAU8efOTDSgGxE8yzIJ3zh0WxrWDSx2YbEBO\nbSz1cwic4IFCcaClC1A/\n=zrDy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T13:30:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDUwZTFmYjkwY2Y1NDViZWY5YzBkZjZiMDljMGNkM2YzYmE3NzUzYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/5535cc3ff50c43c0efa3936b6fc7ad91806a071b","sha":"5535cc3ff50c43c0efa3936b6fc7ad91806a071b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/5535cc3ff50c43c0efa3936b6fc7ad91806a071b"}],"sha":"50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/50e1fb90cf545bef9c0df6b09c0cd3f3ba7753bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/5535cc3ff50c43c0efa3936b6fc7ad91806a071b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:45:21Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:45:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): name the filter chip groups and expose their pressed state (#36)\n\nThe baby filter (shared/components/BabyFilterChips) carries role=\"group\",\nan aria-label and aria-pressed on every chip. The two filter rows written\ninline — milestone categories and vaccine status — carried none of it.\n\nOn /milestones that produced a concrete failure: the category row''s first\nchip is also labelled \"Todos\", so the screen announced \"Todos, button\" twice\nwith nothing to tell the two filters apart, and which category was selected\nwas conveyed by fill colour alone.\n\nBoth rows now match the shared component: the group has a name, each chip\nreports aria-pressed.\n\nVerified on the rebuilt container, signed in as a seeded family:\n\n  /milestones  grupo \"Filtrar por criança\":   Todos=true  Ana=false  Maria=false\n               grupo \"Filtrar por categoria\": Todos=true  Motor=false  …\n               chips in a group with no aria-pressed: 0\n\nThe vaccine half could not be exercised in the browser: the calendar contract\nis broken, so /vaccines renders its error state and the filter row never\nmounts. The change there is source-only and mirrors the verified one; it will\nbe observable once the API delivers the contract.\n\nLocale keys written with LF, one line per file.","tree":{"sha":"7612025772d62c48274b0cef0b1656678d215c5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/7612025772d62c48274b0cef0b1656678d215c5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/5535cc3ff50c43c0efa3936b6fc7ad91806a071b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7612025772d62c48274b0cef0b1656678d215c5c\nparent 36d484eebec4b0f984ec093d28e09d1d565f28a3\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748321 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748321 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): name the filter chip groups and expose their pressed state (#36)\n\nThe baby filter (shared/components/BabyFilterChips) carries role=\"group\",\nan aria-label and aria-pressed on every chip. The two filter rows written\ninline — milestone categories and vaccine status — carried none of it.\n\nOn /milestones that produced a concrete failure: the category row''s first\nchip is also labelled \"Todos\", so the screen announced \"Todos, button\" twice\nwith nothing to tell the two filters apart, and which category was selected\nwas conveyed by fill colour alone.\n\nBoth rows now match the shared component: the group has a name, each chip\nreports aria-pressed.\n\nVerified on the rebuilt container, signed in as a seeded family:\n\n  /milestones  grupo \"Filtrar por criança\":   Todos=true  Ana=false  Maria=false\n               grupo \"Filtrar por categoria\": Todos=true  Motor=false  …\n               chips in a group with no aria-pressed: 0\n\nThe vaccine half could not be exercised in the browser: the calendar contract\nis broken, so /vaccines renders its error state and the filter row never\nmounts. The change there is source-only and mirrors the verified one; it will\nbe observable once the API delivers the contract.\n\nLocale keys written with LF, one line per file.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt/hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZcgQAIqufWM3u9FXWnEyuxbLyYm4\ng0bdNhOslly9Quyaqo1K/ArtBD5AasUV9WNeLmlBKtx+mYFsUkD1sxmK/FVWoyT5\n0ab5lJD4Z2Ov8FHuqv2yG0BiPrAb5rPFYuqWHxv2PlslsZfmIN6OFdmSSLHTnXTg\nXdesJUDC1zPIDhnMykQY6wPYnsmiSXuTBYlHGgWEuDcmWX2mnHnr0B1V9dtL1aR2\nUuW501PalCi9lN6nUitLPa1KBYq/O0AqFq9Q95JIxPUm3v/2lAxO+ka7Fz+jJYzg\ni8UFYNB41wXhZndjgAqUZHFdx+VsHupTHV+m0p+KdsT3XdLDPXoRLrIq++9OBFs5\nSitkq07JxW7pnxq8Z6vqTlm+j5OYHU/YLhGeFmVdrzHi85KpVM86j6KWE8IQljA7\ns2eohIe26XuvO65wjYhfVc/ZdkjmCTThv/dUcgYT4s/JVcL4RXLdTP2KhsDXIn5a\nM3+7HTOomc0xVRjS01xx5m7UM4m/bbbP2tpmsQXwW51mYwA