095d46419d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/33ab887ed3aef3c389a0728926ac2095d46419d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/61690e3bcbd56292479a87500e6df95a9812581c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:44:47Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:44:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): hold AA on the destructive tint in every state (#30)\n\nThe destructive Button and Badge paint text-destructive on a tint of\n--destructive itself. Both sides of the pairing come from one token, so\nmoving the token moves both and the ratio saturates — and whatever surface\nsits under the tint decides the outcome, which the component cannot know.\n\nSix of eight measured pairings were below the 4.5:1 floor for normal text:\n\n  light  /10 on white              4.55  pass\n  light  /10 on the danger zone    4.36  FAIL\n  light  /20 hover on white        3.78  FAIL\n  light  /20 hover in danger zone  3.62  FAIL\n  dark   /20 on the card           4.64  pass\n  dark   /20 in the danger zone    4.46  FAIL\n  dark   /30 hover on the card     3.83  FAIL\n  dark   /30 hover in danger zone  3.69  FAIL\n\nOnly the two resting-on-a-clean-surface cases held. axe reported one of the\neight, because axe does not hover.\n\nTwo changes, and neither works alone.\n\nThe token moves to 0.49 (light) and 0.74 (dark): at those values the resting\ntint clears 4.5 on every surface the app actually paints it on, with margin\ninstead of the 0.05 it had. A lightness sweep from 0.44 to 0.53 also proves\nthe token cannot fix hover on its own — in dark mode the /30 pairing never\nreaches 4.5 at any lightness, because brightening the text brightens the tint\nunderneath it by the same amount.\n\nSo hover stops deepening the fill and deepens the border instead. The state\nstays legible, the affordance stays, and the label''s background no longer\ndepends on how many times a tint has been stacked beneath it.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, in the danger zone, which is the most\nhostile surface in the app:\n\n  light   rest 4.36 -> 4.81   hover 3.62 -> 4.81\n  dark    rest 4.46 -> 4.63   hover 3.69 -> 4.63\n\nKnown bound, written at the token: on a dark --muted surface the pairing tops\nout at 4.29:1 and no lightness fixes it. No destructive control sits there\ntoday; one that did would need an opaque fill rather than a tint of its own\ntext colour.\n\nAlso corrects a stale claim: the comment asserted 4.77:1 for 0.529 on the\ntint. Re-measuring gives 4.55.","tree":{"sha":"c05f908decb7932919983101ae1006cbbdedfd56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/c05f908decb7932919983101ae1006cbbdedfd56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/61690e3bcbd56292479a87500e6df95a9812581c","verification":{"payload":"tree c05f908decb7932919983101ae1006cbbdedfd56\nparent 2ce01a71364bfc001495fa678b1f7af4e75e7b6a\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748287 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748287 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): hold AA on the destructive tint in every state (#30)\n\nThe destructive Button and Badge paint text-destructive on a tint of\n--destructive itself. Both sides of the pairing come from one token, so\nmoving the token moves both and the ratio saturates — and whatever surface\nsits under the tint decides the outcome, which the component cannot know.\n\nSix of eight measured pairings were below the 4.5:1 floor for normal text:\n\n  light  /10 on white              4.55  pass\n  light  /10 on the danger zone    4.36  FAIL\n  light  /20 hover on white        3.78  FAIL\n  light  /20 hover in danger zone  3.62  FAIL\n  dark   /20 on the card           4.64  pass\n  dark   /20 in the danger zone    4.46  FAIL\n  dark   /30 hover on the card     3.83  FAIL\n  dark   /30 hover in danger zone  3.69  FAIL\n\nOnly the two resting-on-a-clean-surface cases held. axe reported one of the\neight, because axe does not hover.\n\nTwo changes, and neither works alone.\n\nThe token moves to 0.49 (light) and 0.74 (dark): at those values the resting\ntint clears 4.5 on every surface the app actually paints it on, with margin\ninstead of the 0.05 it had. A lightness sweep from 0.44 to 0.53 also proves\nthe token cannot fix hover on its own — in dark mode the /30 pairing never\nreaches 4.5 at any lightness, because brightening the text brightens the tint\nunderneath it by the same amount.\n\nSo hover stops deepening the fill and deepens the border instead. The state\nstays legible, the affordance stays, and the label''s background no longer\ndepends on how many times a tint has been stacked beneath it.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, in the danger zone, which is the most\nhostile surface in the app:\n\n  light   rest 4.36 -> 4.81   hover 3.62 -> 4.81\n  dark    rest 4.46 -> 4.63   hover 3.69 -> 4.63\n\nKnown bound, written at the token: on a dark --muted surface the pairing tops\nout at 4.29:1 and no lightness fixes it. No destructive control sits there\ntoday; one that did would need an opaque fill rather than a tint of its own\ntext colour.\n\nAlso corrects a stale claim: the comment asserted 4.77:1 for 0.529 on the\ntint. Re-measuring gives 4.55.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt+/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+FkQAJvUFLiuiCSXeTeBcVce9CHf\nhJZ6Ne29V8KSeGK2rbggB4Qh6LVx4oYx9jNtGgLApp3LOreyZDX/527t5dXC5K33\n9rrvpVxlIpPobQTcAj6zciSlUvaBXFXguNGa0xNPcnvYwGlxSwqIyXXF+toEBlK6\nqnb1lFBA16JUbFt36RVDygmmFlZ6pfESWYmyMaNfvw79ReuF2JeLAOqvrkDvzMHA\nhsnrH3RtP9vprv0AHZPq1YzipG/InQukb3kOo4TU71K64xrqX4lvzOHdijiUdBGX\nTqIOdfoXjTkqyKVvQ83N1Kf060M7BX+D42koy1z5JNod9NuMbD4Iil1ImpS8tEmO\nH61hb/Tg+5GkwGAAYoljbAvKD63RJAnBKg3KJGtmgWaodn6bx19vw/3+6D/zmXjW\n1ZzkQ2377gmDn27CBbgalCfVq0nrbqFLIvIucFs1qG+kkxKGvcAcASR21BZ+XfJp\n/1KoOyMrgtrBovnzBt93D9hfjmJ9B3NbI05jCzAtrnGHK+aqfjjAoQCUzYU2fNDI\n50FmTLZHAOSTrYG1hLINTSVEg79SKVEnWXVO1NY40O+FbYzbNsR65mAF0RYa4Naz\nqwjJESyj5Y8nA1N0oTMp+zKHH3nfY5lmNNHW0qJeB0nbwotYOCdSq1mvgZqEtPtI\ngBan836uGlGyrI8ps+OR\n=kzQB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:44:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/61690e3bcbd56292479a87500e6df95a9812581c","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDYxNjkwZTNiY2JkNTYyOTI0NzlhODc1MDBlNmRmOTVhOTgxMjU4MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/2ce01a71364bfc001495fa678b1f7af4e75e7b6a","sha":"2ce01a71364bfc001495fa678b1f7af4e75e7b6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/2ce01a71364bfc001495fa678b1f7af4e75e7b6a"}],"sha":"61690e3bcbd56292479a87500e6df95a9812581c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/61690e3bcbd56292479a87500e6df95a9812581c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/2ce01a71364bfc001495fa678b1f7af4e75e7b6a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:44:42Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:44:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): put the alert dialog trigger on the button itself (#29)\n\nAlertDialogTrigger asChild wrapped a <span> in GuardiansSection and in\nMilestoneTimeline. asChild forwards Radix''s trigger props to that child —\ntype, aria-haspopup=\"dialog\", aria-expanded — and a span''s implicit role\naccepts none of them. axe reports aria-allowed-attr: critical, wcag2a,\nwcag412. One node per list row, so a timeline of twelve milestones carried\ntwelve violations.\n\nThe wrapper bought nothing. The -inset expander that widens the hit area is\npositioned against the button, which already carries `relative`; the span''s\nown `inline-flex` and `flex-shrink-0` move onto the button unchanged. No\npixel moves.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, /milestones signed in as a seeded family:\nspan[aria-expanded] went from 12 to 0, and button[data-slot=\n\"alert-dialog-trigger\"] from 0 to 6 — the triggers are still there, they are\njust legal now.\n\nWorth recording why this survived: the a11y sweep that covers these pages\nregistered a fresh account and never created data, so every list page was\nscanned empty and the rows that carry the defect never rendered. The sweep\nnow signs in as a seeded family. A gate pointed at the empty state is\npointed at the easiest case.","tree":{"sha":"5ecb5ee0219efd5a425584cbcca7967443af43e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/5ecb5ee0219efd5a425584cbcca7967443af43e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/2ce01a71364bfc001495fa678b1f7af4e75e7b6a","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ecb5ee0219efd5a425584cbcca7967443af43e4\nparent 4290c0a06ae817ae7eeda5358ac70e05f22b7ee6\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748282 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748282 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): put the alert dialog trigger on the button itself (#29)\n\nAlertDialogTrigger asChild wrapped a <span> in GuardiansSection and in\nMilestoneTimeline. asChild forwards Radix''s trigger props to that child —\ntype, aria-haspopup=\"dialog\", aria-expanded — and a span''s implicit role\naccepts none of them. axe reports aria-allowed-attr: critical, wcag2a,\nwcag412. One node per list row, so a timeline of twelve milestones carried\ntwelve violations.\n\nThe wrapper bought nothing. The -inset expander that widens the hit area is\npositioned against the button, which already carries `relative`; the span''s\nown `inline-flex` and `flex-shrink-0` move onto the button unchanged. No\npixel moves.\n\nMeasured on the rebuilt container, /milestones signed in as a seeded family:\nspan[aria-expanded] went from 12 to 0, and button[data-slot=\n\"alert-dialog-trigger\"] from 0 to 6 — the triggers are still there, they are\njust legal now.\n\nWorth recording why this survived: the a11y sweep that covers these pages\nregistered a fresh account and never created data, so every list page was\nscanned empty and the rows that carry the defect never rendered. The sweep\nnow signs in as a seeded family. A gate pointed at the empty state is\npointed at the easiest case.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt+6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA27sQAIJZeYvIr70jq0idVpBE91vp\nyMDDT1vW38KhQ2CuSnTRgtZP32ZkoHnpg8UTF9jyuD9BmibUEB4JgxatVkFE+Tmy\n15h7IBy7HiiN3Kakh3l79pv3DlOX9aTYuk3wckCg8OSF0XKG2Frmztv9V49+kEHa\npO1jmCoDw17e1TWVSjQPl5K39uloO/8PM1KmWmjY1wH3spT5ODoRjW1fl4eLQuIq\nkIyE+6Le2lmR6R6HEeaWx/o4iEmUUTqe8wrby+aACilVf74HvXEuVV34Nr8zye2S\nWFNheTYZsNBm5jICBIq3muZq0po+WEj8DIauKKkMZ+iA9oVXcU7yLU4wh48ajGz4\n+mQW3OpW9+Y8B8Kwnr8Dwb6lfGf13+o1+ZOiJ2SkWphzzEFvKcsN5TLnvVuHDzMk\nDTgTB3OTayqOTLo+fQSDg6qHdyAswgSEP9ckgTXEnT5H82KxnQcG+3Y8QNo/53ja\nWSegkXzs/5PwIBEmzhGxBgIbC2hIJYZnGtpxOT0w4S2IK/OpI51UByezyIsrZaIB\nhxLzRaSmR65MTuYPP3oMhxA6bRJUJ7gx9D7rjJDNU5Me8ujYm1RVittC0G