//api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/4290c0a06ae817ae7eeda5358ac70e05f22b7ee6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:44:37Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:44:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dashboard): wrap the family strip instead of clipping the last child (#28)\n\nAt 1440px with six children the last chip was cut mid-word at the container''s\nedge. The strip is `overflow-x-auto`, so the content was reachable — but\nnothing said so, and a name sliced in half reads as a layout defect rather than\nan invitation to scroll.\n\nHorizontal scroll is the right pattern for a row of chips on a phone, where\nvertical space is the scarce thing. On a desktop it is not: there is room\nbelow, and wrapping hides nothing.\n\n`lg:flex-wrap lg:overflow-x-visible` — measured with six children:\n\n    desktop 1440   rola=false   cortados=0   altura=161 (duas linhas)\n    mobile   390   rola=true    o padrão certo ali\n\nThe alternative was measuring overflow in JS and painting a fade on the edge.\nThat is a scrollbar reinvented to signal something the desktop does not need to\nsignal.\n\nFound in the /dashboard cell of the surface audit, in the six-children state.","tree":{"sha":"d8f5c8b44f6160a53458e6dffd566de03ad5f801","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/d8f5c8b44f6160a53458e6dffd566de03ad5f801"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/4290c0a06ae817ae7eeda5358ac70e05f22b7ee6","verification":{"payload":"tree d8f5c8b44f6160a53458e6dffd566de03ad5f801\nparent 44be587f15eb00e16ed446670cba56f3ef6eb04a\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748277 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748277 -0300\n\nfix(dashboard): wrap the family strip instead of clipping the last child (#28)\n\nAt 1440px with six children the last chip was cut mid-word at the container''s\nedge. The strip is `overflow-x-auto`, so the content was reachable — but\nnothing said so, and a name sliced in half reads as a layout defect rather than\nan invitation to scroll.\n\nHorizontal scroll is the right pattern for a row of chips on a phone, where\nvertical space is the scarce thing. On a desktop it is not: there is room\nbelow, and wrapping hides nothing.\n\n`lg:flex-wrap lg:overflow-x-visible` — measured with six children:\n\n    desktop 1440   rola=false   cortados=0   altura=161 (duas linhas)\n    mobile   390   rola=true    o padrão certo ali\n\nThe alternative was measuring overflow in JS and painting a fade on the edge.\nThat is a scrollbar reinvented to signal something the desktop does not need to\nsignal.\n\nFound in the /dashboard cell of the surface audit, in the six-children state.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt+1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKgAQAIqvO9sXBgLoR8qdpehGiyWd\nPxZXeAbkFyB6DBoiuI/tLKayRDiMTZ+8sXaydRPIn0zLVnhLXmWCCqF6AoBeP28H\nwqG9ko5PeqpP2m6dObxNNJb9p8kezLNhVeADlSCndzi6cwBuhyCYURn4c09FFdxh\nIhlO/RfMig87p1YtZi+R8Hw8s3rKyz7M3cDypZL/OzAYpP0Z3l/tRiZlx+jVWem3\ny/U5cCNnEOZNKdQdLDxamme8hhNxSTuT4NxlscPhTzxVPD1V0dkqCYr+UlJP6lL+\nj7I