16ed446670cba56f3ef6eb04a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c92a6df6e3e2b240ee214295762d0160aa15edb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:42:10Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:42:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): keep the step indicator from widening dialogs on a phone (#26)\n\nTwo of the wizard dialogs scrolled horizontally at 390px, in both themes. The\npanel is 358 wide; its content measured 420.\n\nThe cause is a grid version of the trap already paid for in the milestone\ntimeline. DialogContent is `display: grid` with `max-width: calc(100% - 32px)`,\nso the box is 358 — but the column is `auto`, and a grid item does not shrink\nbelow its content''s minimum while `min-width` is `auto`:\n\n    diálogo   w=358  grid-template-columns: 420.453px\n      header  w=420  min-width: auto\n      corpo   w=420  min-width: auto   <- \"1 Criança 2 Profissional 3 Agendamento\"\n\nThe header looked guilty at first because it was the first element reported as\noverflowing, and its `h2` measured 364. Both were consequences: a block child\ninherits its parent''s width, and the parent was 420 because the *body* set the\ncolumn. The widest leaf inside the header was 364, which is exactly\n420 minus `px-7` on both sides — nothing in the header forced anything.\n\n`StepIndicator` is the real width: three circles, two connectors and three\nlabels come to ~420px of min-content, and the wizard dialogs are the only place\nit renders. Below `sm` the labels are now `sr-only` — hidden visually, still\nread aloud, and still present for the step count. The current step is named in\nthe dialog body anyway (\"Para qual criança é isso?\"), so nothing is lost on\nscreen; above `sm` the labels come back with `not-sr-only`.","tree":{"sha":"4f958f452f66799eea926a8e7c3fbca2304f8982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/4f958f452f66799eea926a8e7c3fbca2304f8982"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/c92a6df6e3e2b240ee214295762d0160aa15edb6","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f958f452f66799eea926a8e7c3fbca2304f8982\nparent 90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748130 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748130 -0300\n\nfix(ui): keep the step indicator from widening dialogs on a phone (#26)\n\nTwo of the wizard dialogs scrolled horizontally at 390px, in both themes. The\npanel is 358 wide; its content measured 420.\n\nThe cause is a grid version of the trap already paid for in the milestone\ntimeline. DialogContent is `display: grid` with `max-width: calc(100% - 32px)`,\nso the box is 358 — but the column is `auto`, and a grid item does not shrink\nbelow its content''s minimum while `min-width` is `auto`:\n\n    diálogo   w=358  grid-template-columns: 420.453px\n      header  w=420  min-width: auto\n      corpo   w=420  min-width: auto   <- \"1 Criança 2 Profissional 3 Agendamento\"\n\nThe header looked guilty at first because it was the first element reported as\noverflowing, and its `h2` measured 364. Both were consequences: a block child\ninherits its parent''s width, and the parent was 420 because the *body* set the\ncolumn. The widest leaf inside the header was 364, which is exactly\n420 minus `px-7` on both sides — nothing in the header forced anything.\n\n`StepIndicator` is the real width: three circles, two connectors and three\nlabels come to ~420px of min-content, and the wizard dialogs are the only place\nit renders. Below `sm` the labels are now `sr-only` — hidden visually, still\nread aloud, and still present for the step count. The current step is named in\nthe dialog body anyway (\"Para qual criança é isso?\"), so nothing is lost on\nscreen; above `sm` the labels come back with `not-sr-only`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt8iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS3IQAC/QK6Dc8BAgDftM96k2vFiu\nin/kBsfyKWu9v65cSg6eshkUMH/rRDJ51ioHLLO6PfquFCqRkGkU4IVO8OedW/sp\nFCzYiQAu9vnLHbpyCgHw+NKLp6kY1UiHADrWopg5HdYXqikXtlsbaiujUPhQIThF\nkGF5wbVSUGF+s6qmilo5S8A9gTj0TokXFLuONrfJGdhcWNZAzXi/MBL6HMkw5zYv\nckwTtEVqnFwec1PdGA6J4paXj2RsdxBR145hr4+IIDLiSPZxQPXM0xtf82Bv5RO+\nb20zvHJXyWjFqXSK1706/JBgZYbHeocf2HZBdA79XpgCido88lcCIg6Dj5izyRYu\nlDDsV9W43PTM92cuFBkXeNY0IwF8x/z92DBMlS5/k/guSpyhp1tkWd9qaJYVLs/e\nr9n0u1B04fB+NUsGycAp7iEaY7ympnE2EanLFdc3AuOx0LiBjjl6ZxJEx/k6JEqt\nrxrdv6jeEBUwbYyXvAqSrJk9S2ddwS6YQW4ld91YZncDvHGDC6en+9p0Sgov7sm7\nA1nm70flxyPtcl5wpRSZ53GHqPL3Tgv9KBEQd6WNNkk4xYYlD/7hUrI4WSma52vT\n1Za0rxIumx8c9WPnBf8Ro8u8mqU8xM1neC90CsgRlNBsIp7qeIvXgVWgo1pDonVK\nKOttfNQgiug8RUjjOhhX\n=bDiF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:42:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/c92a6df6e3e2b240ee214295762d0160aa15edb6","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGM5MmE2ZGY2ZTNlMmIyNDBlZTIxNDI5NTc2MmQwMTYwYWExNWVkYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1","sha":"90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1"}],"sha":"c92a6df6e3e2b240ee214295762d0160aa15edb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c92a6df6e3e2b240ee214295762d0160aa15edb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:42:00Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:42:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): give the three \"add\" dialogs an accessible name (#25)\n\n* fix(a11y): give the three \"add\" dialogs an accessible name\n\n`AddBabyDialog`, `AddAppointmentDialog` and `AddMilestoneDialog` rendered their\nheading as a plain `<h2>` inside a custom gradient header, so Radix never wired\n`aria-labelledby` and the dialogs had no accessible name at all:\n\n    aria-labelledby: null   aria-label: null   aria-describedby: null\n\nA screen reader announced \"dialog\" and nothing else — the person had no idea\nwhat had just opened. The other ten dialogs in the app use `DialogTitle` and\nwere fine; these three share one template and the same omission.\n\nSwapping to `DialogTitle`/`DialogDescription` with the same classes restores\nthe wiring without touching the visual:\n\n    aria-labelledby -> \"Novo Perfil\"   aria-describedby -> set\n\n**Why no gate caught it:** axe files `aria-dialog-name` under `best-practice`,\nnot `wcag2a`/`wcag2aa`, and both `pages-a11y.mjs` and the story suite filter to\nWCAG tags. The rule fires as soon as `best-practice` is included — it was\nnever that axe could not see this, only that it was not asked.\n\nFound in the first cell of the dialog phase of the surface audit.\n\n* fix(a11y): EditBabyDialog was the fourth nameless dialog, not the third\n\nThe sweep that found the other three missed this one, and the reason is worth\nrecording: it grepped for `DialogTitle`, which matches as a substring inside\n`AlertDialogTitle`. EditBabyDialog contains an AlertDialog for the destructive\naction, so it counted as \"has a title\" while its own DialogContent had none.\n\nRe-swept with `<DialogTitle` against `<DialogContent`, which separates the two\ncomponents, and checked the AlertDialogs on their own — all five of those\ncarry `AlertDialogTitle` and are fine.\n\nSame fix as the other three: `DialogTitle`/`DialogDescription` with the same\nclasses, so Radix wires `aria-labelledby` and the visual does not move.","tree":{"sha":"ffbd3d8d1ca8057516900aa8a8d4adda56ae1662","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/ffbd3d8d1ca8057516900aa8a8d4adda56ae1662"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1","verification":{"payload":"tree ffbd3d8d1ca8057516900aa8a8d4adda56ae1662\nparent 17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748120 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748120 -0300\n\nfix(a11y): give the three \"add\" dialogs an accessible name (#25)\n\n* fix(a11y): give the three \"add\" dialogs an accessible name\n\n`AddBabyDialog`, `AddAppointmentDialog` and `AddMilestoneDialog` rendered their\nheading as a plain `<h2>` inside a custom gradient header, so Radix never wired\n`aria-labelledby` and the dialogs had no accessible name at all:\n\n    aria-labelledby: null   aria-label: null   aria-describedby: null\n\nA screen reader announced \"dialog\" and nothing else — the person had no idea\nwhat had just opened. The other ten dialogs in the app use `DialogTitle` and\nwere fine; these three share one template and the same omission.\n\nSwapping to `DialogTitle`/`DialogDescription` with the same classes restores\nthe wiring without touching the visual:\n\n    aria-labelledby -> \"Novo Perfil\"   aria-describedby -> set\n\n**Why no gate caught it:** axe files `aria-dialog-name` under `best-practice`,\nnot `wcag2a`/`wcag2aa`, and both `pages-a11y.mjs` and the story suite filter to\nWCAG tags. The rule fires as soon as `best-practice` is included — it was\nnever that axe could not see this, only that it was not asked.\n\nFound in the first cell of the dialog phase of the surface audit.\n\n* fix(a11y): EditBabyDialog was the fourth nameless dialog, not the third\n\nThe sweep that found the other three missed this one, and the reason is worth\nrecording: it grepped for `DialogTitle`, which matches as a substring inside\n`AlertDialogTitle`. EditBabyDialog contains an AlertDialog for the destructive\naction, so it counted as \"has a title\" while its own DialogContent had none.\n\nRe-swept with `<DialogTitle` against `<DialogContent`, which separates the two\ncomponents, and checked the AlertDialogs on their own — all five of those\ncarry `AlertDialogTitle` and are fine.\n\nSame fix as the other three: `DialogTitle`/`DialogDescription` with the same\nclasses, so Radix wires `aria-labelledby` and the visual does not move.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt8YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm88QADvLx5CdNcdYjD9hiPHbcU+p\n7xZLDtxiL2WPDTtXkljmjVouyPZZeArZPN4cLxTiXeqN/q1dc6ahJKXSq044p9X+\nEK3Yjfh939K+pReNDV9ymUXRaL60Vb5bW8t8bKipd/UBLiYt4n+gdBNE1lhgsxqh\niolFeFf/1NzJztx+FkJBzYsqeiKgDPX3IqAXC09EYeEN6qiCMu5u0za/mpRU+l8Z\n9dJ/G24VeVq35UcziWgkErn2FnnzeGnG/YoFHXTCpj+09ZKRGUYZZ4NL75IZaJY/\noIr6jJ1cTFIYgce6WFF3MJTHqyEj9APiBj7N8wRcovEVYP+M8IMVD38t+ITqsaQP\nfWlW5zmrFRo92Hhx8A2//hUB6/bixKTGhcuB80n6i5K1PoLHp7fG9+feLmRP5aML\nuzq6INTEFqsIerVagPLmkbPAwbx5LliHSNJgH/zbKV23PQclm7PlgUmf6sk21Adc\n6tmQ/94G/UVzos8n+v70vgDJurEJuIrAhMCIbSnEmYqlDKuGlPaUx+0HOGNw5szb\nxlZ/lT63G5sEDTEOmvH7+l55ybB7Z+jVosfliQoAipDePdotwQcg34qko6FGFOrI\nk/8JT2KPAFY9OjUOWn6fgDY8fs3Kf9QQimhW2/Nn+6KWMusW6guBcvV+rsgvyF5I\nGT001Ggfy5jWvX6zVXqW\n=nDGz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:42:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDkwNzA1NTg4YmY2ZTM5NmI0YTYzZDFmODIzZTU1ZjkyZjRlZDJmZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202","sha":"17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202"}],"sha":"90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/90705588bf6e396b4a63d1f823e55f92f4ed2fd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:55Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(profile): give the theme control a settings-shaped variant (#24)\n\nOn the profile page, \"Idioma\" was a 44px labelled select and \"Tema\" was the\nheader''s 36px icon button — two settings, stacked, with completely different\naffordances. Cycling is fine in a header, where the control is an afterthought\nand one tap gets you somewhere. It is the wrong shape on a settings page: the\nperson came specifically to set this, and an icon that cycles neither shows\nwhat the options are nor what the current one means without decoding a glyph.\n\nLanguageSwitcher already carries exactly this split, and the reasoning in its\n`variant` comment applies here word for word. The pattern was half-applied —\nthe language control got its settings variant and the theme control never did.\n\n`field` mirrors that variant deliberately: same height, same radius, same tinted\nfill, so the two line up on the page and with the form fields below them. It\nalso inherits the `position=\"popper\"` fix — this trigger has no SelectValue\neither, and item-aligned positioning measures that node.\n\nNo new copy: `common.theme.light/dark/system` already existed for the aria\nlabel and the tooltip, and now they are what the control shows.","tree":{"sha":"a0af2f31c43917339e38687015fbdbbd809037f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/a0af2f31c43917339e38687015fbdbbd809037f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202","verification":{"payload":"tree a0af2f31c43917339e38687015fbdbbd809037f7\nparent 2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748115 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748115 -0300\n\nfeat(profile): give the theme control a settings-shaped variant (#24)\n\nOn the profile page, \"Idioma\" was a 44px labelled select and \"Tema\" was the\nheader''s 36px icon button — two settings, stacked, with completely different\naffordances. Cycling is fine in a header, where the control is an afterthought\nand one tap gets you somewhere. It is the wrong shape on a settings page: the\nperson came specifically to set this, and an icon that cycles neither shows\nwhat the options are nor what the current one means without decoding a glyph.\n\nLanguageSwitcher already carries exactly this split, and the reasoning in its\n`variant` comment applies here word for word. The pattern was half-applied —\nthe language control got its settings variant and the theme control never did.\n\n`field` mirrors that variant deliberately: same height, same radius, same tinted\nfill, so the two line up on the page and with the form fields below them. It\nalso inherits the `position=\"popper\"` fix — this trigger has no SelectValue\neither, and item-aligned positioning measures that node.\n\nNo new copy: `common.theme.light/dark/system` already existed for the aria\nlabel and the tooltip, and now they are what the control shows.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt8TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYHQQAAkJbMo04DbdLJojbpGGToWv\nksAteCRuVqsG04WaPX9K4We5T+aUrdNMXq0ypVOzW7JgrKH9IA8n9jpvK1+z28Ri\npf/u2dNzn+09GtErpJ+bKFl6lyUhjtjqNlLmeVl6KQq3SjfrJzqFGHOqSy8VaKMz\nP30+g4kC898xw7PerTBwnT/4JJ3QOKY6TUSVkCGc32M+zP9sGHsD8mPMfussEszY\nGPUS9wAVT1GRbiH8HFQVltdlXXkTj3jfWp1PABeiS6LuFvwRqUd4mVag18jMS8jF\nweI9S+ZZqCDdi0N+yQiS/YEOuktSAX/mwRN5UZlZWQZpgFdqjqqoqNFZFgsfzhTN\npbG9YioetbheubLqYAhRGn0m0TMUS6Q3TIKrq6D/V9flFTX0oxg0sgRPtqOMlLz5\nVKOR5g0XhfNH5Vp9XNxV911mlT9UwSATaQBLFe7oBiCeJ2P0CKN1ebYAVkclHXpn\nPxYwuxpi6APAcYZXgrZOFUFg1tCjibhL4RRy+JFG1MwtxPvdGlpZyxF04DAnDMRs\ngMQUbEP5RKcf7urTAZja6Zut+LqM7soxOSR1bFtWraqJNuCELKmiB4QCHG0dUjUi\niD9fZn6/s4OCk+tpEUqbpgsqnlu7snW1LDzRikaMHTsg3tOH1R8zNtBsb2oBYJqd\nhhR1Tw7qrJC0K3on0R8N\n=iRzt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDE3ZmM4MDc4MTA3ZDI3NTQ0YmY1Yjc3ZjUyM2Q2NTUxZDM0YTcyMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf","sha":"2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf"}],"sha":"17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/17fc8078107d27544bf5b77f523d6551d34a7202"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:49Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(milestones): stop the timeline card from scrolling the page sideways (#23)\n\nAt 390px the milestones page scrolled horizontally, in both themes. Two causes\nstacked, and fixing either alone left the other:\n\n**The card could not shrink.** `flex-1` is `flex: 1 1 0%`, but a flex item will\nnot go below its content''s intrinsic minimum while `min-width` is `auto`. The\nrow already carried `min-w-0`; the card did not, so it measured 296px inside a\n330px row that also holds a 40px node and a 20px gap — 26px past its own\nparent.\n\n**The header row could not wrap.** With the card correctly sized at 270px, the\nheader has 238px, and the right-hand group (category, date, edit, delete) is\n`flex-shrink-0` at 193px. Title plus group exceeds the space, so the group\noverflowed instead. Measured after the first fix:\n\n    cartão        100..370  (w=270)  correct\n    cabeçalho     116..354  (w=238)\n    grupo direita 187..380  (w=193)  26px past the header\n\nTruncating the title would drop the milestone''s name, which is the content.\nLetting the group wrap to its own line costs nothing.\n\nFound by the mechanical check in the /milestones cell of the surface audit —\nthe invisible -inset-3 touch expander was the first thing to poke out, which\nmade the card look innocent until the geometry was read.","tree":{"sha":"9e942e9dcaa0a789c0365afa602619cf47e5d292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/9e942e9dcaa0a789c0365afa602619cf47e5d292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e942e9dcaa0a789c0365afa602619cf47e5d292\nparent 3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748109 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748109 -0300\n\nfix(milestones): stop the timeline card from scrolling the page sideways (#23)\n\nAt 390px the milestones page scrolled horizontally, in both themes. Two causes\nstacked, and fixing either alone left the other:\n\n**The card could not shrink.** `flex-1` is `flex: 1 1 0%`, but a flex item will\nnot go below its content''s intrinsic minimum while `min-width` is `auto`. The\nrow already carried `min-w-0`; the card did not, so it measured 296px inside a\n330px row that also holds a 40px node and a 20px gap — 26px past its own\nparent.\n\n**The header row could not wrap.** With the card correctly sized at 270px, the\nheader has 238px, and the right-hand group (category, date, edit, delete) is\n`flex-shrink-0` at 193px. Title plus group exceeds the space, so the group\noverflowed instead. Measured after the first fix:\n\n    cartão        100..370  (w=270)  correct\n    cabeçalho     116..354  (w=238)\n    grupo direita 187..380  (w=193)  26px past the header\n\nTruncating the title would drop the milestone''s name, which is the content.\nLetting the group wrap to its own line costs nothing.\n\nFound by the mechanical check in the /milestones cell of the surface audit —\nthe invisible -inset-3 touch expander was the first thing to poke out, which\nmade the card look innocent until the geometry was read.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt8NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwzoQADYx1dmaeKtVXSG+ZHmV/LPv\ngeiKf1+AXHQzB8ftgCyI22K74M3eFaKg5aGj7cN7R+CDwILmyu3ueaEM8mYp58mp\nPmMY7GeRJsThY4TClp2XAUryBUX8SB80ot9LikYu4ZjcgUHp6UCb+a/Yk9iwbqm1\nP3jxU6ShAXDh+QVPJhTae6vnbFZsp/V5IJLDJD2UBHXAKQOGECWgjhmhUXc0xw/4\nd82lGfSjDKEy6O0Kz1ZtD03MsE9MDB5FW6h8Ms9xBC4TQjzJUjEvBqD+7+xglnNN\nKuoSsqn0uXPn7uRNQznMqjuOvDBYmemuT4NnmHBt4Bjv5rEK8h9MgqFtdovP9cTG\np7E3InvPjSEPTAcipMe87F0PWmN8eCjfpjcsXks5yEUnyxut+LCuuBEpecQcUUVN\nycNPwqlccQ0UBJb9b+tm90n+Rz81FjSr5B1/Qqidiht5bzxUHlflICoKhvXWaI8k\nWqjoSK2lOLhLfCzyid76ex0RQBH39y6WsXlSIb6TJAUu7dwiqNYMfDe5QLAZ8k6j\nfA0wR399DnLLcnWpCQtd/TyLZMPaeYDanGamh81UOAuWcPz+oukB/V8T1piYaHaE\ncAOjVR9zz/oj80+GKKFKLxshmCwtkIktzK5ZYeJlnbWl9JWJ4W3pk2j69zLI8I9h\nZs1Ql8O88IwEz5toVuWS\n=W/B1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDJiN2Y5OTk0YTdkZTc3OTliOGUwMGNhNGY2MjBmM2VmNWY5M2FiY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24","sha":"3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24"}],"sha":"2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/2b7f9994a7de7799b8e00ca4f620f3ef5f93abcf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:42Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(appointments): stop painting a cancelled appointment green (#22)\n\nThe card''s action button branched on `isScheduled`, which is a two-way split\nover three states — so CANCELLED fell into the same bucket as COMPLETED and got\nthe emerald treatment. A cancelled appointment with a green button reads as\nthough nothing is wrong with it.\n\nDESIGN.md already assigns `Appointment CANCELLED` to a neutral slate, and the\nstatus badge at the top of the same card follows that. Only this button did\nnot, so the card contradicted itself: a grey \"Cancelada\" badge above a green\naction.\n\nVerified in the rebuilt container — the three states now resolve to three\ntones:\n\n    Agendada   rgb(240, 238, 255)          violet tint\n    Cancelada  oklch(0.97 0 0)             neutral, was emerald\n    Concluída  oklch(0.979 0.021 166.113)  emerald tint\n\nFound in the /appointments cell of the surface audit.","tree":{"sha":"a90d9763addfde7ab98a19d352b51f86eec4bbcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/a90d9763addfde7ab98a19d352b51f86eec4bbcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24","verification":{"payload":"tree a90d9763addfde7ab98a19d352b51f86eec4bbcb\nparent b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748102 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748102 -0300\n\nfix(appointments): stop painting a cancelled appointment green (#22)\n\nThe card''s action button branched on `isScheduled`, which is a two-way split\nover three states — so CANCELLED fell into the same bucket as COMPLETED and got\nthe emerald treatment. A cancelled appointment with a green button reads as\nthough nothing is wrong with it.\n\nDESIGN.md already assigns `Appointment CANCELLED` to a neutral slate, and the\nstatus badge at the top of the same card follows that. Only this button did\nnot, so the card contradicted itself: a grey \"Cancelada\" badge above a green\naction.\n\nVerified in the rebuilt container — the three states now resolve to three\ntones:\n\n    Agendada   rgb(240, 238, 255)          violet tint\n    Cancelada  oklch(0.97 0 0)             neutral, was emerald\n    Concluída  oklch(0.979 0.021 166.113)  emerald tint\n\nFound in the /appointments cell of the surface audit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt8GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApcYQAHAXDOmqvDx6q2SBdspKYrEz\nXmS39fvLRPgpnxEw3w/XPEFzpOHUOwWroBN6N8h5775BIzdXSLcuZXtlkw1la+rr\n+a72R0xpcVexXs+TevqpnyA314v9HuoDsPQD4JCdq+U593A5OWjuyyL83bzen7nt\nfiqWWtvmRYvBI13/0NyAlpmj/hA2rNgsoEmgqe3jBoHDE+LuXpHnQgBChthkctWb\na+Vsc30ZZvqVyt0GNd/edpP4kK0x1L5lR3gHwWlGjTjKwQPribyAckEavkEXXtqi\ngGI4ZFMpOsrb32CaiiYjgYQS8fcaTZbDbJ/im121AdzkDQIg3TDznGsKgKulZpbz\nX1jMDDCT/Xl2s+HcE4852ljS8TsZ4g3gB0dMW+oH6oCr2mIhXwbVaYUSN79Axu+5\nB/nIT9ecD4IWE3j+hJvZ/VJVtzhV0sFX2o8b+lNEPvxlIinTXroeEOe17BqIyDLD\nZ2QyPSC9cbrkZ1FjwCqZNRP/DMiPczel5LI2qgeWjIAWwVQcYcd8Gsi1umdUTtGv\nWsnThWQHMY+JOq/ApZeEb8KSFQwvOSdnaG2xBnpTXdtxm//MxPow/k59dw/grWe6\nWiFPEy23hmKlQW6tZkA8GueLafwEPWM4Exz7DYwi0kfw9TsjIhs0yXE7NiqAeddp\nddwgcp5fgDwrRQo7vDtT\n=Xbif\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDNmNDgxNGJkODcwNTRlMGE3ZjhmYTNiNDY0MDljOTM2MmFhY2ZjMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693","sha":"b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693"}],"sha":"3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/3f4814bd87054e0a7f8fa3b46409c9362aacfc24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:35Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dashboard): never claim vaccines are up to date without the data (#21)\n\n* fix(i18n): drop the duplicate dark styles on the language menu''s checked row\n\nThe emerald migration (#17) left two backgrounds and two text colours on the\nsame element, under the same variant chain:\n\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-950/40   <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-500/10   <- already there\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-300    <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-400    <- already there\n\nWhich one applies is decided by the order in the generated CSS, not by the\norder in the class list, so the result was correct only by accident.\n\nThe migration script skipped lines that already contained `dark:bg-`, and what\nwas here read `dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-` — a variant sitting between the\n`dark:` and the property, so the guard never matched. Same shape as the\n`hover:` prefix bug already fixed in #17, in a spot that sweep could not see.\n\nThe pre-existing pair is kept, not the migration''s: emerald-500/10 with\nemerald-400 was written deliberately to match how links read on the auth\nscreens in dark. Verified in the rebuilt container — the checked row now\nresolves to exactly that pair, from a single rule.\n\nSwept the whole of src/ for siblings and there are none. Seven other files look\nlike duplicates when grouped by line, and all seven are ternaries\n(`cond ? violet : emerald`) whose branches never coexist on an element.\n\n* fix(dashboard): never claim vaccines are up to date without the data\n\nThe family chip and the vaccine stat both read a count and rendered a\nconclusion. When the vaccine calendar fails to load, `items` is an empty array,\nso the count is zero — the same zero that means \"nothing overdue\". The screen\nanswered \"Vacinas em dia\" and \"0 tomadas\" for a child whose record it had not\nmanaged to read.\n\nIn an app whose reason to exist is tracking the PNI schedule, that is the worst\navailable failure: the parent sees no error, concludes there is nothing to do,\nand the app has silently asserted the child is protected.\n\nFound running the dashboard against a seeded family of six. The calendar query\nis failing for an unrelated reason — a contract drift filed separately — and\nwhat surfaced was not an error state but a confident, wrong summary.\n\nThe chip now takes `vaccineStatusKnown` and shows \"não foi possível verificar\"\ninstead. Required rather than optional on purpose: `tsc` immediately found a\nsecond call site in VaccinesRoute with the same flaw, which is exactly the\nprotection an optional field would not have given. The state is read per baby\nfrom `perBaby`, not from the aggregate — one failed request must not mark the\nother five unknown.\n\nA known delay is still reported, because that information is true whenever it\nexists. Only the absence of a delay is ambiguous.\n\n* fix(vaccines): stop summarising a calendar that failed to load\n\nSame defect as the family chip, in the page header. `counts` is derived from\n`items`, which is an empty array when the calendar query fails, so the subtitle\nread \"0 tomadas · 0 atrasadas · 0 pendentes\" — three stated facts, sitting\ndirectly above the message admitting nothing could be read.\n\nNow the subtitle carries the loading text while pending and is omitted on\nerror, where the message below already says what happened. Repeating it in a\nsubtitle only competes with it for attention.\n\nFound in the /vaccines cell of the surface audit, which is the screen where the\ncontract drift is most visible today.","tree":{"sha":"67fe83ee3ca4a506330ada47cb12329037ed9057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/67fe83ee3ca4a506330ada47cb12329037ed9057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693","verification":{"payload":"tree 67fe83ee3ca4a506330ada47cb12329037ed9057\nparent 0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748095 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748095 -0300\n\nfix(dashboard): never claim vaccines are up to date without the data (#21)\n\n* fix(i18n): drop the duplicate dark styles on the language menu''s checked row\n\nThe emerald migration (#17) left two backgrounds and two text colours on the\nsame element, under the same variant chain:\n\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-950/40   <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-500/10   <- already there\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-300    <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-400    <- already there\n\nWhich one applies is decided by the order in the generated CSS, not by the\norder in the class list, so the result was correct only by accident.\n\nThe migration script skipped lines that already contained `dark:bg-`, and what\nwas here read `dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-` — a variant sitting between the\n`dark:` and the property, so the guard never matched. Same shape as the\n`hover:` prefix bug already fixed in #17, in a spot that sweep could not see.\n\nThe pre-existing pair is kept, not the migration''s: emerald-500/10 with\nemerald-400 was written deliberately to match how links read on the auth\nscreens in dark. Verified in the rebuilt container — the checked row now\nresolves to exactly that pair, from a single rule.\n\nSwept the whole of src/ for siblings and there are none. Seven other files look\nlike duplicates when grouped by line, and all seven are ternaries\n(`cond ? violet : emerald`) whose branches never coexist on an element.\n\n* fix(dashboard): never claim vaccines are up to date without the data\n\nThe family chip and the vaccine stat both read a count and rendered a\nconclusion. When the vaccine calendar fails to load, `items` is an empty array,\nso the count is zero — the same zero that means \"nothing overdue\". The screen\nanswered \"Vacinas em dia\" and \"0 tomadas\" for a child whose record it had not\nmanaged to read.\n\nIn an app whose reason to exist is tracking the PNI schedule, that is the worst\navailable failure: the parent sees no error, concludes there is nothing to do,\nand the app has silently asserted the child is protected.\n\nFound running the dashboard against a seeded family of six. The calendar query\nis failing for an unrelated reason — a contract drift filed separately — and\nwhat surfaced was not an error state but a confident, wrong summary.\n\nThe chip now takes `vaccineStatusKnown` and shows \"não foi possível verificar\"\ninstead. Required rather than optional on purpose: `tsc` immediately found a\nsecond call site in VaccinesRoute with the same flaw, which is exactly the\nprotection an optional field would not have given. The state is read per baby\nfrom `perBaby`, not from the aggregate — one failed request must not mark the\nother five unknown.\n\nA known delay is still reported, because that information is true whenever it\nexists. Only the absence of a delay is ambiguous.\n\n* fix(vaccines): stop summarising a calendar that failed to load\n\nSame defect as the family chip, in the page header. `counts` is derived from\n`items`, which is an empty array when the calendar query fails, so the subtitle\nread \"0 tomadas · 0 atrasadas · 0 pendentes\" — three stated facts, sitting\ndirectly above the message admitting nothing could be read.\n\nNow the subtitle carries the loading text while pending and is omitted on\nerror, where the message below already says what happened. Repeating it in a\nsubtitle only competes with it for attention.\n\nFound in the /vaccines cell of the surface audit, which is the screen where the\ncontract drift is most visible today.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt7/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANboQAIRC5D3S3GLw/Nfh/uPzC4gM\n5K0Zfw/gv81CESpbJod95y1kMKm15FcyLIzy3G/vZBxdfnqOcKMFy016spMHFRfz\nAgUfz4IzHUP8h4iKriwU0ArLZQ1VYj4NslJQLJtJhbgLmqneRHWpo3oZ5ucUqPKD\nmVNPwJvYdry4puUuNa0hIZqrXaAL+Rc5jomNX0OFC/WCOx5oZ3EMzOMUpLJZWEtS\nxcPyn5RYMrmwM6Tdr7QDvFWA6Yl9+wxvS5DgbKcEE0RwPQvepsuiH84BW/E8U2nx\no0dr0w9DlO6XGlW5fucrESRzwh7GsN5rf6ke0m7ym2b55EYxd+1WB40KsKEcc3I6\n7FNpCA0suKcF70f9VCxbjeB7fRprNtjLWVrloPZx5cW/0ff1tohmBfPka3pXFBNn\n9bDTABcBmpQKCRyFSrQJSKhTtvg0LLhrh+YhR9mwf1CqkxGiofKItY6pmxOSF0+e\nq2tlbfhS6W4VfOcK9mJf+r4VyIW8k+2IMJc8MoSVQNi4oz1+DsgryuEDP+zoQgXW\nb2BiJHEZ2wcUzp4rcAiukJZtRYc8GqOFy0kp4J1mos6p2RA1lbK+QEgYdVS/csct\nSLXmHcZfRKUFLljLeAIgiQcp9q9IE+Ip/Juc/u9PYdTViAtDr3/obtolqcPDieRL\nwZCHjDUNdAgAPvwy0Yop\n=d8Yr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGIxNjdkODg4MDMxYmVlOTkyZThkMzk2NDFmZDhiOWJlNjI5OTU2OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4","sha":"0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4"}],"sha":"b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b167d888031bee992e8d39641fd8b9be62995693"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:21Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(i18n): drop the duplicate dark styles on the language menu''s checked row (#20)\n\nThe emerald migration (#17) left two backgrounds and two text colours on the\nsame element, under the same variant chain:\n\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-950/40   <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-500/10   <- already there\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-300    <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-400    <- already there\n\nWhich one applies is decided by the order in the generated CSS, not by the\norder in the class list, so the result was correct only by accident.\n\nThe migration script skipped lines that already contained `dark:bg-`, and what\nwas here read `dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-` — a variant sitting between the\n`dark:` and the property, so the guard never matched. Same shape as the\n`hover:` prefix bug already fixed in #17, in a spot that sweep could not see.\n\nThe pre-existing pair is kept, not the migration''s: emerald-500/10 with\nemerald-400 was written deliberately to match how links read on the auth\nscreens in dark. Verified in the rebuilt container — the checked row now\nresolves to exactly that pair, from a single rule.\n\nSwept the whole of src/ for siblings and there are none. Seven other files look\nlike duplicates when grouped by line, and all seven are ternaries\n(`cond ? violet : emerald`) whose branches never coexist on an element.","tree":{"sha":"c92f724209f9af288fdeca0120e1ded3814b0920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/c92f724209f9af288fdeca0120e1ded3814b0920"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4","verification":{"payload":"tree c92f724209f9af288fdeca0120e1ded3814b0920\nparent f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748081 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748081 -0300\n\nfix(i18n): drop the duplicate dark styles on the language menu''s checked row (#20)\n\nThe emerald migration (#17) left two backgrounds and two text colours on the\nsame element, under the same variant chain:\n\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-950/40   <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-emerald-500/10   <- already there\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-300    <- added by the migration\n    dark:data-[state=checked]:text-emerald-400    <- already there\n\nWhich one applies is decided by the order in the generated CSS, not by the\norder in the class list, so the result was correct only by accident.\n\nThe migration script skipped lines that already contained `dark:bg-`, and what\nwas here read `dark:data-[state=checked]:bg-` — a variant sitting between the\n`dark:` and the property, so the guard never matched. Same shape as the\n`hover:` prefix bug already fixed in #17, in a spot that sweep could not see.\n\nThe pre-existing pair is kept, not the migration''s: emerald-500/10 with\nemerald-400 was written deliberately to match how links read on the auth\nscreens in dark. Verified in the rebuilt container — the checked row now\nresolves to exactly that pair, from a single rule.\n\nSwept the whole of src/ for siblings and there are none. Seven other files look\nlike duplicates when grouped by line, and all seven are ternaries\n(`cond ? violet : emerald`) whose branches never coexist on an element.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt7xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7eAQAIaYC9TSGp/FrUNhUTMGNJEq\nMo3/D8gTGUfR9SWUr2wo88QnDkqxKKRmiArpb4iulBg0t480AYZI7yyFY0FhmFlC\nT7Jq/ydQjGt2LtK8T1Mt5b284Ry8PnN6K0P/G8DqgSCj6HYOJXFe3wj4VH1nXUoW\njULeAQ0PXBhSRqblRlFFhkMRhnMTPxMeuqcjbVU6DVJOei0HM0rTdzxCDiQu1EE0\n3axAVO5gHJBQlXfJMIdBOcVjQzCvSsuYAd3Dae1ELTBuTo6K2cU3qEE4YCl7mmv1\nqAzX0Rr+ymsyRorzA8qQ50WywKaDEDySbq/FkNBF5/8t6eoAtfSvl+t/XOWlHPf0\nsM/YMtYboLXHeeIfWEtDXs9kYM2ZcUr66ID0/eIrS2sJvoH0mHGyxQYHxgX9q0jS\nQuq56KZ8N+dC8i9ojeQwHChSTAavSQ6t7dtk1FKvPm88AznWYtIuY1zAI3jBMCuf\nTz0PHIp8R/2KUm6cyhvLLOZMpTS8zPXFOROujMyidW/5iIHIZAm6vuCmej1IubC1\npJgBaIzCjzt0IVDMx/vUqKy0PjA3OS/AOYCvr2vuRq0jMDRte2l8RZTMHuhucKas\nwiYeEoXArm93+Ovmz2GaGY3bkByp4u2L4Sjdf+YIuRO2x0Bva2pZecc2JL2g9jhn\nvnOm5nsEoa6RQhHhFd6p\n=zWum\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDBkNzAzMGUyN2I5ZjJiNDdmNTE2ZTFjZjliMjgyMGVmZTlhZjQ0ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250","sha":"f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250"}],"sha":"0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/0d7030e27b9f2b47f516e1cf9b2820efe9af44f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:17Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(invites): keep the invite readable for a logged-out visitor (#19)\n\n* feat(query): let a query declare that a 401 is an expected answer\n\nGroundwork, landed before the fix that needs it. Purely additive: the cache\nerror handlers now receive the query (or mutation) that failed and read\n`meta.expectsAnonymous` off it before reporting a session expiry.\n\nEvery 401 was previously treated the same way — \"your session died, go to\n/login\" — which is correct for the protected shell and wrong for a public route\nthat merely *asks* whether anyone is signed in. `useCurrentUser` is shared\nbetween both, so the opt-out has to be per call site rather than a global\nswitch, which is why it rides on `meta` instead of a module-level flag.\n\nThe handler signature difference is worth noting: QueryCache passes the query\nsecond, MutationCache passes the mutation fourth. Both are narrowed to the one\nfield this reads.\n\n* fix(invites): keep the invite readable for a logged-out visitor\n\n`/invites/:code` sits outside ProtectedLayout on purpose, so that someone who\nfollowed an invite link can read who invited them before signing in. It did not\nwork: the route calls `useCurrentUser()` on mount, that 401s for a logged-out\nvisitor, and the global unauthorized handler answers with\n`window.location.assign(''/login'')` — a hard navigation, before the preview ever\npaints.\n\nTraced on a real invite code against the running stack:\n\n    /invites/<code>  ->  /invites/<code>  ->  /login\n\nThe screen was unreachable for the only audience it has, and nothing reported\nit: from the outside a redirect to /login looks like ordinary behaviour for a\nlogged-out visitor. The guardian-invite feature is complete on the backend —\nBabyGuardian, BabyInvite, invite mail through Resend — and could not be entered\nfrom the link it sends.\n\n`expectsAnonymous` marks the 401 as \"nobody is signed in\" rather than \"the\nsession expired\", so the handler stays out of it. After the fix, a valid code\nrenders \"Você foi convidado(a) para ajudar a cuidar de Ana\" and an unknown one\nrenders \"Convite não encontrado\", both without a session.\n\nThe test renders with the **app''s** queryClient rather than\n`renderWithProviders`, and that is the whole point of it: the gating lives in\nthe real client''s `queryCache.onError`, so a test using the per-test client\npasses with and without the fix. The first version of this file did exactly\nthat and was worthless. Verified the current one fails when the flag is\nremoved.\n\nFound by the surface audit, which could not scan the screen at all while it\nredirected away.","tree":{"sha":"063becda27f11d0658664845d9cfdb94f1872e64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/063becda27f11d0658664845d9cfdb94f1872e64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250","verification":{"payload":"tree 063becda27f11d0658664845d9cfdb94f1872e64\nparent a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748077 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748077 -0300\n\nfix(invites): keep the invite readable for a logged-out visitor (#19)\n\n* feat(query): let a query declare that a 401 is an expected answer\n\nGroundwork, landed before the fix that needs it. Purely additive: the cache\nerror handlers now receive the query (or mutation) that failed and read\n`meta.expectsAnonymous` off it before reporting a session expiry.\n\nEvery 401 was previously treated the same way — \"your session died, go to\n/login\" — which is correct for the protected shell and wrong for a public route\nthat merely *asks* whether anyone is signed in. `useCurrentUser` is shared\nbetween both, so the opt-out has to be per call site rather than a global\nswitch, which is why it rides on `meta` instead of a module-level flag.\n\nThe handler signature difference is worth noting: QueryCache passes the query\nsecond, MutationCache passes the mutation fourth. Both are narrowed to the one\nfield this reads.\n\n* fix(invites): keep the invite readable for a logged-out visitor\n\n`/invites/:code` sits outside ProtectedLayout on purpose, so that someone who\nfollowed an invite link can read who invited them before signing in. It did not\nwork: the route calls `useCurrentUser()` on mount, that 401s for a logged-out\nvisitor, and the global unauthorized handler answers with\n`window.location.assign(''/login'')` — a hard navigation, before the preview ever\npaints.\n\nTraced on a real invite code against the running stack:\n\n    /invites/<code>  ->  /invites/<code>  ->  /login\n\nThe screen was unreachable for the only audience it has, and nothing reported\nit: from the outside a redirect to /login looks like ordinary behaviour for a\nlogged-out visitor. The guardian-invite feature is complete on the backend —\nBabyGuardian, BabyInvite, invite mail through Resend — and could not be entered\nfrom the link it sends.\n\n`expectsAnonymous` marks the 401 as \"nobody is signed in\" rather than \"the\nsession expired\", so the handler stays out of it. After the fix, a valid code\nrenders \"Você foi convidado(a) para ajudar a cuidar de Ana\" and an unknown one\nrenders \"Convite não encontrado\", both without a session.\n\nThe test renders with the **app''s** queryClient rather than\n`renderWithProviders`, and that is the whole point of it: the gating lives in\nthe real client''s `queryCache.onError`, so a test using the per-test client\npasses with and without the fix. The first version of this file did exactly\nthat and was worthless. Verified the current one fails when the flag is\nremoved.\n\nFound by the surface audit, which could not scan the screen at all while it\nredirected away.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt7tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqJkQAGjPYWVpZyfz06hI6TU0coeB\nPIOVPfvWb7Ko7yUu6Z3nsD1TZJpnxgboz+bcmc8e9Lx1duFyNrxvJlV6WAj39LhW\nglml6k+GEtgF94xZpHNFithdwEBjtDlrpp+hq0EFANBDZk4s/M4RLMLYd+1birrI\neWK3OZglyCcMwPr5yy6vmEZFiW3HT5GiCEWTyvOw4wq2Pv55Gb63JJ00jV2F45Tf\ntz5P6sxst+xF6l7gr7z3E32u9vSPLDABGb6d/dmxplrsU5DatiC2MSphCUxxnJP1\nKDETWccZLqWvjYLS39Di+l8GWrE0gZvl90bufR98pYhUYUJx2k3X24L7rWChZESD\nqSVNTQeKZSH1tWTXb3uA6q6kIdG1lT9ShMPhV6Vf6Wvps4krU7L2tMiT28lVM6ax\nUwLS+txTP3NDhkmkwx49IShkq2kUHyp8HzCPuR2dRSDljdlQOIFABScTeXD68lVC\nM+xzxtmF/dXjWaaShd5wJzUlmViqFdB+mfGJjslr/dTgV1p0/CsA9EUV3KbqP3P5\nPJJIEDaDTeIq7LkXC00yG2IIaMQ5n/0gYH4V8LLhkLXWY2YZ6qbsJ5Em9x9UjRFV\nZWdUfL2fxGBwAYnamQd5ZFnHyH/0CfwFMLzrP8rcplTb1SnnojggM48Yp3rIWb8V\nYXhYBtveWfUNGJiTUj+U\n=L8Xl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGY2NDgzOGE0YjBlYjBiMDE3MTJhOGM2MGRlNmUzOTY3ZjRlNDIyNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19","sha":"a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19"}],"sha":"f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/f64838a4b0eb0b01712a8c60de6e3967f4e42250"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:13Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(i18n): keep the compact language switcher ghost in dark mode (#18)\n\nThe header pairs LanguageSwitcher with ThemeToggle, and the pairing broke the\nmoment the theme flipped: SelectTrigger carries `dark:bg-input/30` and\n`dark:hover:bg-input/50`, which the compact variant never undid. Measured on\n/login at 390px — ThemeToggle `rgba(0,0,0,0)` in both themes, this one\n`oklab(1 0 0 / 0.045)` in dark. One control gained a visible box, the other\nstayed ghost, side by side.\n\n`dark:bg-transparent` is not redundant with the primitive''s own\n`bg-transparent`: the dark variant wins over the base in the cascade, so the\noverride has to be at the same specificity to land.\n\nFound by the first cell of the surface audit — the light screenshot showed\nnothing, and only the dark one made the mismatch visible.","tree":{"sha":"c10bbe8ce3cc75d42e73b92373f89fcf3631b37b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/c10bbe8ce3cc75d42e73b92373f89fcf3631b37b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19","verification":{"payload":"tree c10bbe8ce3cc75d42e73b92373f89fcf3631b37b\nparent e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787748073 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787748073 -0300\n\nfix(i18n): keep the compact language switcher ghost in dark mode (#18)\n\nThe header pairs LanguageSwitcher with ThemeToggle, and the pairing broke the\nmoment the theme flipped: SelectTrigger carries `dark:bg-input/30` and\n`dark:hover:bg-input/50`, which the compact variant never undid. Measured on\n/login at 390px — ThemeToggle `rgba(0,0,0,0)` in both themes, this one\n`oklab(1 0 0 / 0.045)` in dark. One control gained a visible box, the other\nstayed ghost, side by side.\n\n`dark:bg-transparent` is not redundant with the primitive''s own\n`bg-transparent`: the dark variant wins over the base in the cascade, so the\noverride has to be at the same specificity to land.\n\nFound by the first cell of the surface audit — the light screenshot showed\nnothing, and only the dark one made the mismatch visible.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjt7pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoagQAH/0q5P9g4EaiPlDjE+7gVa4\nhfY+XPC+pKBXbdpkiA7OvVl1C++Zg2eRrON3UCG6Upu80/Ln0jEXeaiXw4fhY4td\n/Q5vUvMNHUPiV8dOzydhwuEFUNGYyA2yg88dT+iyqhOwHZ+S0RL98IrfvfpgpdWG\no6TKudFeuPWGr3SFUzP9qqCLFjGx6IReyyvNzGWjP3L/F80lJcN3Bj9Ua01axG72\nJRTL4ViGum+IzXINHbKMWXseTIE9ElFo+2+KXtEi3Vy3PRd2T/7PcgOrN4Qht4w3\nX8nnHAR5UasTHNcPnwOEWbobxBRM4JnVIJm93AUotGbJbNm/ZHhakZggG/peJ6Wl\nkYsm8WFGCLYtwLu+MJNskro8Fv7pNjfqybjaZhkKVUJ3gC945RrAqhpLkxatG3pK\nc7vkTCvWL9LK+8ZzmAEF5ZZVyP7AJPkfM1Wya3nBqyLrjBJT0je8x4M8WSJH7FNt\nXfWjv0AZUyMGpz7opxB9ye+JxM+l+EOSBMnVatd1G00BiphCuA92cgnpqolKCHJl\nNWR3u4bJsq1+bhH0pH7gELT0Y9j9e3/6PXoX8WU3h5ny1eo8yw7n3xFWm0kv7Z2o\nkflZ9FSVmJGMwzoQwOj3dYhGuR4WeVaoM56qIVQyoYZm58CerPH2XXIGtjpgBfzH\nOCw7culjOeRmG1h2q5dj\n=5YhQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T12:41:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGEwNGQwYWRkZTMzZTMzMjNmZWJiMTA1MzcxMDhlZDMxZDA1M2VmMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1","sha":"e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1"}],"sha":"a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/a04d0adde33e3323febb10537108ed31d053ef19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:26:22Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:26:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(theme): make dark mode legible and move the app to emerald (#17)\n\nfix(theme): paint app surfaces with tokens so dark mode is legible\n\nThe authenticated app was light-only by construction: 197 stock colour\nutilities across 48 files against 8 `dark:` variants in total. Since the ink\nscale and the shadcn tokens *do* flip, the result was not \"unstyled in dark\",\nit was unreadable — a `bg-white` card carrying `text-ink`, which resolves to\nnear-white on dark. The profile page was the worst case: every label, field\nvalue and section heading was white on white, and the form could not be used\nat all.\n\nMechanical, and only where the meaning is unambiguous:\n\n    bg-white            -> bg-card\n    bg-slate-50/100/200 -> bg-muted\n    border-slate-*      -> border-border\n    divide-slate-100    -> divide-border\n    text-slate-400      -> text-ink-faint\n\nTwo categories are deliberately left alone, because they are not surfaces:\n`text-white` and `bg-white/<alpha>` sit on the coloured hero panels and icon\nchips, which are the same colour in both themes — flipping those would break\nexactly what the tokens are meant to protect. The dashboard hero''s CTA is the\none opaque `bg-white` that stays literal for the same reason, and now says so\nin a comment; converting it turned a white button on teal into a near-black\nbutton whose teal label was unreadable.\n\nThe two milestone submit buttons overrode the primary with `bg-slate-900`, an\nintentional high-emphasis neutral that vanishes against a dark card. They are\nnow `bg-foreground text-background`, which keeps the intent and inverts with\nthe theme.\n\nVerified by rebuilding the container and re-shooting the two worst screens in\ndark, plus the full story suite, whose axe gate runs in both themes with no\nstanding exceptions.\n\n---\nfix(a11y): clear the contrast failures on the assembled pages\n\nAn axe sweep over the six authenticated pages, in both themes, found ten\nfailures that the story suite cannot see: it scans components in isolation,\nagainst the default background, so a pairing that only exists once a component\nis painted on a particular surface never gets measured. Light mode is now\nclean on all six pages; two of the failures predate this branch entirely.\n\n`text-teal-600` on `bg-teal-50` measured **4.09:1** at 10-11px — under AA, and\nfailing in *light* mode, where it has been shipping. teal-700 on the same tint\nis 6.12:1 and 6.84:1 on white, so all 18 text usages move up one step. Sampled\nbefore choosing: the whole brand ramp was measured against every surface it is\nactually painted on rather than assuming the shade numbers carry meaning.\n\nWhite on `bg-amber-500` was **2.68:1** — below even the 3:1 floor for large\ntext — on the dashboard CTA and the offline banner. Darkening the fill until\nwhite passes needs amber-700 (5.02:1), which turns the warm accent muddy;\nkeeping the brand fill and darkening the label to amber-950 gives 5.60:1, so\nthat is what both now do.\n\nThe app shell''s header and bottom nav were `bg-white/90`. That is chrome, not\ndecoration on a coloured panel, and the earlier pass wrongly grouped it with\nthe latter: in dark it composited to #e7e7e7 while the ink inside had already\nflipped to near-white — 1.13:1, the worst ratio in the app. Now `bg-card/90`.\n\n`docs/verification/pages-a11y.mjs` is the sweep itself, kept because every\nviolation it found was of a kind the existing gate is structurally unable to\ncatch. It needs a real stack, like the e2e specs, so it is a tool rather than\na test.\n\nTwo dark-mode patterns remain and are deliberately left for the next commit:\nbrand text on a dark card, and the tinted badges. Both are the same missing\npiece — the brand ramp has no dark mode — and 22 of the call sites are the\nsame ones the emerald migration has to touch, so splitting them means editing\nthose files twice.\n\n---\nfeat(theme): move the app to emerald and give the brand ramp a dark mode\n\nTwo changes that had to land together, because 22 of the call sites are the\nsame ones: promoting emerald app-wide, and giving the brand tints a dark\ncounterpart. Doing them apart means editing those files twice.\n\n**The shades are measured, not renumbered.** The old ramp was a hand-tuned\nteal where the numbers carried no relation to Tailwind''s, so a same-number\nswap breaks in two places and both were caught before shipping:\n\n    bg-teal-500 + white icon   3.32:1  ->  emerald-500 would be 2.54:1, under\n                                           the 3:1 floor for a graphical object\n    bg-teal-600 + white text   4.57:1  ->  emerald-600 would be 3.77:1, under AA\n\nAnything carrying white content moves to `bg-primary`/`text-primary-foreground`\nso the fill and its content flip together, or up a step where it must stay\nfixed. `--primary` is emerald-700 (5.48:1 on white, 5.10:1 on emerald-50) —\nemerald-600 is the intuitive pick, is what the auth screens use for focus\nrings, and does not clear AA for text.\n\nThe custom `--color-teal-*` block is deleted rather than recoloured. It also\ncarried a trap: `text-teal-800` was in use while only 50–700 were defined, so\nthat one class silently resolved to stock Tailwind teal, a different hue from\nits six siblings. Stock emerald has every step.\n\n**The dark counterparts have to be added at the call site**, because stock\nshades do not flip while the tokens around them do. Tints go to `950/40` and\n`900/40`, and the text that rides on them comes up to the 300 step. Two traps\npaid for here:\n\n- The first pass appended the dark class without the variant prefix of the one\n  that produced it, so `hover:bg-emerald-50` gained a resting `dark:bg-...`\n  and inactive nav items sat permanently tinted. 15 tokens, now `dark:hover:`.\n- The pastel card headers are **gradients**, and axe cannot evaluate text over\n  a gradient — it reads the nearest opaque ancestor. The sweep passed while\n  the four headers had pale text on a pale tint, and only a screenshot showed\n  it. Same blind spot the auth panel is documented against.\n\nThe hero CTA stays literal white with a literal emerald label, and now says\nwhy: it sits on a panel that is the same colour in both themes, so nothing\npainted on it may flip.\n\nNames and comments were corrected rather than left: `EmptyStateTone` had a\n`''teal''` member that painted emerald, and three comments described a hue the\ncode no longer uses.\n\nVerified: axe clean on all six pages in both themes; the auth panel re-measured\n(ten lines, worst 5.25:1) since --primary and --ring moved; layout and the\nassisted-flow scans unchanged; 113 unit, 83 story, full build.\n\n---","tree":{"sha":"acd395f4fba20ed3a1bf995343ef33e01ee90e2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/acd395f4fba20ed3a1bf995343ef33e01ee90e2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1","verification":{"payload":"tree acd395f4fba20ed3a1bf995343ef33e01ee90e2e\nparent 9dc4a69dc4b798b44d8f487f1f929325d6cd8764\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787703982 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787703982 -0300\n\nfeat(theme): make dark mode legible and move the app to emerald (#17)\n\nfix(theme): paint app surfaces with tokens so dark mode is legible\n\nThe authenticated app was light-only by construction: 197 stock colour\nutilities across 48 files against 8 `dark:` variants in total. Since the ink\nscale and the shadcn tokens *do* flip, the result was not \"unstyled in dark\",\nit was unreadable — a `bg-white` card carrying `text-ink`, which resolves to\nnear-white on dark. The profile page was the worst case: every label, field\nvalue and section heading was white on white, and the form could not be used\nat all.\n\nMechanical, and only where the meaning is unambiguous:\n\n    bg-white            -> bg-card\n    bg-slate-50/100/200 -> bg-muted\n    border-slate-*      -> border-border\n    divide-slate-100    -> divide-border\n    text-slate-400      -> text-ink-faint\n\nTwo categories are deliberately left alone, because they are not surfaces:\n`text-white` and `bg-white/<alpha>` sit on the coloured hero panels and icon\nchips, which are the same colour in both themes — flipping those would break\nexactly what the tokens are meant to protect. The dashboard hero''s CTA is the\none opaque `bg-white` that stays literal for the same reason, and now says so\nin a comment; converting it turned a white button on teal into a near-black\nbutton whose teal label was unreadable.\n\nThe two milestone submit buttons overrode the primary with `bg-slate-900`, an\nintentional high-emphasis neutral that vanishes against a dark card. They are\nnow `bg-foreground text-background`, which keeps the intent and inverts with\nthe theme.\n\nVerified by rebuilding the container and re-shooting the two worst screens in\ndark, plus the full story suite, whose axe gate runs in both themes with no\nstanding exceptions.\n\n---\nfix(a11y): clear the contrast failures on the assembled pages\n\nAn axe sweep over the six authenticated pages, in both themes, found ten\nfailures that the story suite cannot see: it scans components in isolation,\nagainst the default background, so a pairing that only exists once a component\nis painted on a particular surface never gets measured. Light mode is now\nclean on all six pages; two of the failures predate this branch entirely.\n\n`text-teal-600` on `bg-teal-50` measured **4.09:1** at 10-11px — under AA, and\nfailing in *light* mode, where it has been shipping. teal-700 on the same tint\nis 6.12:1 and 6.84:1 on white, so all 18 text usages move up one step. Sampled\nbefore choosing: the whole brand ramp was measured against every surface it is\nactually painted on rather than assuming the shade numbers carry meaning.\n\nWhite on `bg-amber-500` was **2.68:1** — below even the 3:1 floor for large\ntext — on the dashboard CTA and the offline banner. Darkening the fill until\nwhite passes needs amber-700 (5.02:1), which turns the warm accent muddy;\nkeeping the brand fill and darkening the label to amber-950 gives 5.60:1, so\nthat is what both now do.\n\nThe app shell''s header and bottom nav were `bg-white/90`. That is chrome, not\ndecoration on a coloured panel, and the earlier pass wrongly grouped it with\nthe latter: in dark it composited to #e7e7e7 while the ink inside had already\nflipped to near-white — 1.13:1, the worst ratio in the app. Now `bg-card/90`.\n\n`docs/verification/pages-a11y.mjs` is the sweep itself, kept because every\nviolation it found was of a kind the existing gate is structurally unable to\ncatch. It needs a real stack, like the e2e specs, so it is a tool rather than\na test.\n\nTwo dark-mode patterns remain and are deliberately left for the next commit:\nbrand text on a dark card, and the tinted badges. Both are the same missing\npiece — the brand ramp has no dark mode — and 22 of the call sites are the\nsame ones the emerald migration has to touch, so splitting them means editing\nthose files twice.\n\n---\nfeat(theme): move the app to emerald and give the brand ramp a dark mode\n\nTwo changes that had to land together, because 22 of the call sites are the\nsame ones: promoting emerald app-wide, and giving the brand tints a dark\ncounterpart. Doing them apart means editing those files twice.\n\n**The shades are measured, not renumbered.** The old ramp was a hand-tuned\nteal where the numbers carried no relation to Tailwind''s, so a same-number\nswap breaks in two places and both were caught before shipping:\n\n    bg-teal-500 + white icon   3.32:1  ->  emerald-500 would be 2.54:1, under\n                                           the 3:1 floor for a graphical object\n    bg-teal-600 + white text   4.57:1  ->  emerald-600 would be 3.77:1, under AA\n\nAnything carrying white content moves to `bg-primary`/`text-primary-foreground`\nso the fill and its content flip together, or up a step where it must stay\nfixed. `--primary` is emerald-700 (5.48:1 on white, 5.10:1 on emerald-50) —\nemerald-600 is the intuitive pick, is what the auth screens use for focus\nrings, and does not clear AA for text.\n\nThe custom `--color-teal-*` block is deleted rather than recoloured. It also\ncarried a trap: `text-teal-800` was in use while only 50–700 were defined, so\nthat one class silently resolved to stock Tailwind teal, a different hue from\nits six siblings. Stock emerald has every step.\n\n**The dark counterparts have to be added at the call site**, because stock\nshades do not flip while the tokens around them do. Tints go to `950/40` and\n`900/40`, and the text that rides on them comes up to the 300 step. Two traps\npaid for here:\n\n- The first pass appended the dark class without the variant prefix of the one\n  that produced it, so `hover:bg-emerald-50` gained a resting `dark:bg-...`\n  and inactive nav items sat permanently tinted. 15 tokens, now `dark:hover:`.\n- The pastel card headers are **gradients**, and axe cannot evaluate text over\n  a gradient — it reads the nearest opaque ancestor. The sweep passed while\n  the four headers had pale text on a pale tint, and only a screenshot showed\n  it. Same blind spot the auth panel is documented against.\n\nThe hero CTA stays literal white with a literal emerald label, and now says\nwhy: it sits on a panel that is the same colour in both themes, so nothing\npainted on it may flip.\n\nNames and comments were corrected rather than left: `EmptyStateTone` had a\n`''teal''` member that painted emerald, and three comments described a hue the\ncode no longer uses.\n\nVerified: axe clean on all six pages in both themes; the auth panel re-measured\n(ten lines, worst 5.25:1) since --primary and --ring moved; layout and the\nassisted-flow scans unchanged; 113 unit, 83 story, full build.\n\n---","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjjKuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaOoQAITh7qMNdV/tsXtPTVKTsani\ngAo5EoIgd0Q8KTOISbQfy+44O8cU1cSMoYcgPxMmTav+TT8OALodQ3R7Ui/e+rkq\n7ftM7v3v7SzEDSmSu6kYEtqD6Rg2/CXzLyCsqlIgcrxis63LEPyAOSB3MVN9XYmO\nI9/6pCuo+K2xp+rsft6wuFU0W5aSU/X9Lh9FGTpMZycSPtWjE7H6AkSRuUEWfa6w\nSvrT7MbQPlL/l1z/fCUtuYNyhn+0T1cGwWOBP8NdMawjnN4QUf4R02JMIpi5S5X6\nqK35wJROzX30E4X8A/sVkAnZJLkDoOzip+O8Rqelk24Gw4m1cxocY8e/QKHv1sQk\nxhoF4rQQirYV+WDUU1gG8cgaY+tnrN6rzw0kxpFYU8adqQ7bvYLrT+vLskUBaMdK\nJ3DNdPNQ5NLtNW+l8apj122Q1elHVAeDJsaSa8XAGrJrc0e74WGOwi2MLkICRWZr\nyqbyPs4LZsLMYAzAgpZFKbFc5+pyT0BYPshsQhC9eNbUefNOjLiCOOwwUaZVylOU\n60+u4aAkZf6CJS1ogwaMciLiWhm/ov5fPgA6yaUjrTZgTWnl1ViPhJZ1pjbxmOjG\ncDUs359IsoDhmPkytZgsw+KmEwtSMv93Cuc4otVgpqgrOBsyMq5yh6+U97g/pji0\njjqEytib1XVUFyijI0kT\n=8S6y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T00:26:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGUzOWEyMjZmYzEwZTVhYTRiODgxY2YyYWZiNzQ5MDY4YzRiMTVlZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/9dc4a69dc4b798b44d8f487f1f929325d6cd8764","sha":"9dc4a69dc4b798b44d8f487f1f929325d6cd8764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/9dc4a69dc4b798b44d8f487f1f929325d6cd8764"}],"sha":"e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/e39a226fc10e5aa4b881cf2afb749068c4b15ef1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/9dc4a69dc4b798b44d8f487f1f929325d6cd8764/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T23:38:26Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T23:38:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): redesign the sign-in and sign-up screens (#16)\n\nfix(theme): use the muted token for the theme toggle hover\n\n`hover:bg-slate-100` is a stock Tailwind class, so it resolves to the same\nnear-white in both themes — on dark it painted a light block behind the\nicon on hover, the one state where the control should recede.\n\n`bg-muted` is defined in the `@theme` block in index.css and flips with the\ntheme, which is the whole reason the token exists. This is the rule in §4 of\nthe repo''s conventions applied to a control that predates it.\n\n---\nfeat(icons): add the icons the auth screens need\n\nFive additions on the existing `icon-base` pattern: eye/eye-off for the\npassword reveal toggle, mail for the assisted flow, google for the social\nbutton, spinner for the pending state.\n\n`google-icon` is the only one that departs from the pattern: it carries the\nfour brand colours as literal hex fills instead of `currentColor`, because\nGoogle''s brand terms do not allow recolouring the mark. It is deliberately\nexempt from the \"no hardcoded colour\" rule, and the reason is in the file.\n\n---\nfeat(hooks): keep the submit spinner from flashing on fast responses\n\nTwo timers, because a naive spinner has two separate failure modes and\nfixing only one moves the flash rather than removing it:\n\n- a response in 80ms would light the spinner and kill it inside a frame, so\n  nothing renders for the first 400ms;\n- a response in 420ms would clear the first guard and then show the spinner\n  for 20ms — the same flash, one step later — so once it is lit it stays lit\n  for 400ms.\n\nOnly the visual is smoothed. `disabled` and `aria-busy` follow the real\nmutation state, so the button refuses a second click from the first\nmillisecond; delaying those would turn a cosmetic fix into a double-submit.\n\n---\nfeat(i18n): give LanguageSwitcher a field variant for the profile page\n\nThe header and the profile page were using one component for two\nincompatible jobs. `compact` (the default) is a 36px ghost control paired\nwith ThemeToggle, falling back to the two-letter code below `sm`; `field` is\n44px and matches the height of the surrounding form inputs.\n\nFixes a positioning bug introduced while showing \"PT\" in the trigger and\n\"Português\" in the menu: dropping SelectValue broke the menu placement,\nbecause Radix''s `item-aligned` mode positions itself by measuring that very\nnode. Measured — with SelectValue the menu opened at 1144,36; without it, at\n0,797, i.e. off screen. `position=\"popper\"` anchors to the trigger instead\nand does not depend on the trigger''s contents.\n\nThe story covers both variants, the pairing with ThemeToggle, and an\ninteraction. It waits for the listbox to disappear rather than only clicking\naway: an open Radix portal marks the rest of the page `aria-hidden` while\nleaving the trigger focusable, which the a11y gate reports as a violation,\nand the exit animation keeps the portal mounted after the close.\n\n---\nfeat(auth): add the assisted sign-in calls to the data layer\n\nGroundwork for the passwordless and password-reset flows, landed before the\nscreen that uses it so the UI commit stays about the UI. Purely additive:\nfour endpoint functions, their schemas, and two hooks.\n\nBoth request endpoints answer identically for an address with no account, so\nneither the api function nor the hook returns anything a caller could branch\non — the screen must not be able to report whether an e-mail is registered.\nThe comments say so at both layers, because a later `return response.status`\nwould look harmless.\n\n`codeField` is a `.refine` rather than `.length(6).regex(...)` so the message\ncollapses into a single i18n key: zod-error.ts maps a `custom` issue''s\nmessage straight to a key, while the built-in codes would report \"too short\"\nand \"not digits\" as the same generic format error.\n\nuseVerifyAssistedCode mirrors useLogin: both endpoints end in a session and\nneither returns a user payload, so only the submitted e-mail is known and\nauthIdentity holds `name: null` until GET /auth/me confirms it.\n\n---\nfeat(auth): rebuild the sign-in and sign-up screens\n\nReplaces the two standalone auth pages with one shell: a brand panel over a\nphotograph beside a card holding a segmented control, and the passwordless\nand password-reset flows inline on the login screen rather than on routes of\ntheir own.\n\nAuthLayout becomes a parent route with an Outlet, in the same shape as\nProtectedLayout -> AppShellLayout. /login and /register were siblings, each\nrendering its own <AuthLayout>, which React treats as different components in\nthat position — every tab switch remounted the whole card. Marking the DOM\nnodes before a switch and reading them after showed tabs, panel, photo and\ncard all coming back as new nodes; the photo was served from cache but the\nnew <img> still forced a decode and a repaint. The sliding pill on the\nsegmented control is only possible because of this: a transition has nowhere\nto animate from on a freshly created node. Kept lazy, so the shared shell\ndoes not land in the entry chunk of someone who is already signed in.\n\nThe segmented control used to drop 13px on the way to \"Sign in\". Two causes\nthat had to be fixed together: register is one field taller, and the card is\ncentred on the page, so the top edge fell by half the difference; and the\ncolumn is centred too, so the shorter content floated down inside it even\nwith the height pinned. Adding \"sign in without a password\" to login brought\nthe jump from 85px to 25px on its own; three measured min-heights plus\ntop-anchoring took it to 0. Heights were swept across every width from 360 to\n1920, and the floors sit at the top of each flat band: 47rem below sm,\n51.25rem from sm to lg, 44.5rem above. If either form gains or loses a row,\nthese have to be re-measured — a floor the taller route has outgrown brings\nthe jump back silently, and nothing in the suite catches it.\n\nThe brand panel''s contrast is arithmetic, not a gate: axe reads the nearest\nopaque ancestor and cannot see a sibling gradient or an <img>, so none of the\npanel is covered by the a11y gate. Each line was measured by making the text\ntransparent, screenshotting the panel, taking the lightest pixel inside each\nline''s box and compositing the text colour over it — ten lines pass, the\nworst at 4.96:1. The photo is darkened with `multiply` rather than a veil\nbecause a veil strong enough pulls the light and dark parts of the image to\nthe same value and flattens it to texture; `isolate` on the panel is\nload-bearing, since blend modes compose against whatever shares their\nstacking context and neither `relative` nor `overflow-hidden` opens one.\n\nThe e2e fixture follows the renamed submit buttons, and its password lookups\ngain `exact: true` — getByLabel matches substrings, and both forms now carry\na reveal toggle whose label contains the word.\n\nGoogle sign-in has no backend, so that button says so instead of failing\nsilently. Nothing is faked. The four assisted endpoints it needs do exist —\nPOST /auth/{passwordless,password-reset}/{request,verify} — so the flow is\nwired to the real API, and the failure branches map 401/410 to \"wrong or\nexpired code\" and 429 to \"wait\" rather than collapsing both into a generic\nretry, which would tell someone who is rate-limited to do the one thing that\ncannot work.\n\n---","tree":{"sha":"ffb14ecc275f0b05a4d8dbae81c5b95c72c72cee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/ffb14ecc275f0b05a4d8dbae81c5b95c72c72cee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/9dc4a69dc4b798b44d8f487f1f929325d6cd8764","verification":{"payload":"tree ffb14ecc275f0b05a4d8dbae81c5b95c72c72cee\nparent 28befc7913107b86f6e48b621813c4f45ebedfa7\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787701106 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787701106 -0300\n\nfeat(auth): redesign the sign-in and sign-up screens (#16)\n\nfix(theme): use the muted token for the theme toggle hover\n\n`hover:bg-slate-100` is a stock Tailwind class, so it resolves to the same\nnear-white in both themes — on dark it painted a light block behind the\nicon on hover, the one state where the control should recede.\n\n`bg-muted` is defined in the `@theme` block in index.css and flips with the\ntheme, which is the whole reason the token exists. This is the rule in §4 of\nthe repo''s conventions applied to a control that predates it.\n\n---\nfeat(icons): add the icons the auth screens need\n\nFive additions on the existing `icon-base` pattern: eye/eye-off for the\npassword reveal toggle, mail for the assisted flow, google for the social\nbutton, spinner for the pending state.\n\n`google-icon` is the only one that departs from the pattern: it carries the\nfour brand colours as literal hex fills instead of `currentColor`, because\nGoogle''s brand terms do not allow recolouring the mark. It is deliberately\nexempt from the \"no hardcoded colour\" rule, and the reason is in the file.\n\n---\nfeat(hooks): keep the submit spinner from flashing on fast responses\n\nTwo timers, because a naive spinner has two separate failure modes and\nfixing only one moves the flash rather than removing it:\n\n- a response in 80ms would light the spinner and kill it inside a frame, so\n  nothing renders for the first 400ms;\n- a response in 420ms would clear the first guard and then show the spinner\n  for 20ms — the same flash, one step later — so once it is lit it stays lit\n  for 400ms.\n\nOnly the visual is smoothed. `disabled` and `aria-busy` follow the real\nmutation state, so the button refuses a second click from the first\nmillisecond; delaying those would turn a cosmetic fix into a double-submit.\n\n---\nfeat(i18n): give LanguageSwitcher a field variant for the profile page\n\nThe header and the profile page were using one component for two\nincompatible jobs. `compact` (the default) is a 36px ghost control paired\nwith ThemeToggle, falling back to the two-letter code below `sm`; `field` is\n44px and matches the height of the surrounding form inputs.\n\nFixes a positioning bug introduced while showing \"PT\" in the trigger and\n\"Português\" in the menu: dropping SelectValue broke the menu placement,\nbecause Radix''s `item-aligned` mode positions itself by measuring that very\nnode. Measured — with SelectValue the menu opened at 1144,36; without it, at\n0,797, i.e. off screen. `position=\"popper\"` anchors to the trigger instead\nand does not depend on the trigger''s contents.\n\nThe story covers both variants, the pairing with ThemeToggle, and an\ninteraction. It waits for the listbox to disappear rather than only clicking\naway: an open Radix portal marks the rest of the page `aria-hidden` while\nleaving the trigger focusable, which the a11y gate reports as a violation,\nand the exit animation keeps the portal mounted after the close.\n\n---\nfeat(auth): add the assisted sign-in calls to the data layer\n\nGroundwork for the passwordless and password-reset flows, landed before the\nscreen that uses it so the UI commit stays about the UI. Purely additive:\nfour endpoint functions, their schemas, and two hooks.\n\nBoth request endpoints answer identically for an address with no account, so\nneither the api function nor the hook returns anything a caller could branch\non — the screen must not be able to report whether an e-mail is registered.\nThe comments say so at both layers, because a later `return response.status`\nwould look harmless.\n\n`codeField` is a `.refine` rather than `.length(6).regex(...)` so the message\ncollapses into a single i18n key: zod-error.ts maps a `custom` issue''s\nmessage straight to a key, while the built-in codes would report \"too short\"\nand \"not digits\" as the same generic format error.\n\nuseVerifyAssistedCode mirrors useLogin: both endpoints end in a session and\nneither returns a user payload, so only the submitted e-mail is known and\nauthIdentity holds `name: null` until GET /auth/me confirms it.\n\n---\nfeat(auth): rebuild the sign-in and sign-up screens\n\nReplaces the two standalone auth pages with one shell: a brand panel over a\nphotograph beside a card holding a segmented control, and the passwordless\nand password-reset flows inline on the login screen rather than on routes of\ntheir own.\n\nAuthLayout becomes a parent route with an Outlet, in the same shape as\nProtectedLayout -> AppShellLayout. /login and /register were siblings, each\nrendering its own <AuthLayout>, which React treats as different components in\nthat position — every tab switch remounted the whole card. Marking the DOM\nnodes before a switch and reading them after showed tabs, panel, photo and\ncard all coming back as new nodes; the photo was served from cache but the\nnew <img> still forced a decode and a repaint. The sliding pill on the\nsegmented control is only possible because of this: a transition has nowhere\nto animate from on a freshly created node. Kept lazy, so the shared shell\ndoes not land in the entry chunk of someone who is already signed in.\n\nThe segmented control used to drop 13px on the way to \"Sign in\". Two causes\nthat had to be fixed together: register is one field taller, and the card is\ncentred on the page, so the top edge fell by half the difference; and the\ncolumn is centred too, so the shorter content floated down inside it even\nwith the height pinned. Adding \"sign in without a password\" to login brought\nthe jump from 85px to 25px on its own; three measured min-heights plus\ntop-anchoring took it to 0. Heights were swept across every width from 360 to\n1920, and the floors sit at the top of each flat band: 47rem below sm,\n51.25rem from sm to lg, 44.5rem above. If either form gains or loses a row,\nthese have to be re-measured — a floor the taller route has outgrown brings\nthe jump back silently, and nothing in the suite catches it.\n\nThe brand panel''s contrast is arithmetic, not a gate: axe reads the nearest\nopaque ancestor and cannot see a sibling gradient or an <img>, so none of the\npanel is covered by the a11y gate. Each line was measured by making the text\ntransparent, screenshotting the panel, taking the lightest pixel inside each\nline''s box and compositing the text colour over it — ten lines pass, the\nworst at 4.96:1. The photo is darkened with `multiply` rather than a veil\nbecause a veil strong enough pulls the light and dark parts of the image to\nthe same value and flattens it to texture; `isolate` on the panel is\nload-bearing, since blend modes compose against whatever shares their\nstacking context and neither `relative` nor `overflow-hidden` opens one.\n\nThe e2e fixture follows the renamed submit buttons, and its password lookups\ngain `exact: true` — getByLabel matches substrings, and both forms now carry\na reveal toggle whose label contains the word.\n\nGoogle sign-in has no backend, so that button says so instead of failing\nsilently. Nothing is faked. The four assisted endpoints it needs do exist —\nPOST /auth/{passwordless,password-reset}/{request,verify} — so the flow is\nwired to the real API, and the failure branches map 401/410 to \"wrong or\nexpired code\" and 429 to \"wait\" rather than collapsing both into a generic\nretry, which would tell someone who is rate-limited to do the one thing that\ncannot work.\n\n---","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjidyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjaYQACtVznWWfCutw5GVX3Q63Plm\nyZS4f87CJZNYm3Ajc+YgviR50c2nJCuOhHsoWjHX7OA5M0Dm+YR0wRHuHbe/NeMY\nI7xy5XQ/o014ozp8dkF/rJnGaaorqsvImTVgEX+iOPvWHVkipsz0jcQDTZC/DvZH\nKLE5oyJAqQowD/BiZUV5D9E0KAegdgSD0fsNblCriyScas4JRYgo6hkd2y13sw5Q\nxVjbKf3G2B0zw0hXwsLgExJraeBYQ971gBt/d7B+fYk+Hqg9hy/+JFlH4tp/i4tf\nDlJj5LDpyi2BhxvQbCUxo942cbY2GR4i17yRKK8eO4T9HjJl2WJ8GXOyiGQPZbS/\nRJP6i9UEzRiBmJP/xHH6Ag5guePQepQa78QjS6aYC7uihXt8e4inlqaKrrvKr8uq\nz0DQW1zO+ekXLQuAap2kVi7FlmUsRGYszguyBxnE/8c6MJOrwvHrnHCIpyhSnfuR\ncMZPl0KjHHwHlBQv70SicD6zVaCzcA2h9gKaOU4xPEwUohs+kf9Q9y10uTc/j25f\ndBwoW68m1RyztOMnkAxAZYyo6b9fciUmthxCJE1LfPRDe181ij9LtbLkz4DP1B/6\nj5OhXHwN/54E6jGBrm8xPT17qSm4Lr8CBFdXqyPx4neqcHZwvUnAIJWodA+Y5Gq7\ng6cNBxWctedbUtx7IhTA\n=8rCH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T23:38:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gis