thub.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/28befc7913107b86f6e48b621813c4f45ebedfa7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T14:12:02Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T14:12:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: correct the README''s account of the accessibility gate (#15)\n\nThe README pointed readers at `src/test/a11y-known-issues.ts` for the list of\nknown axe exceptions. That file does not exist, and neither does the concept:\nno story disables the a11y check, and `parameters.a11y.test = ''error''` in\n.storybook/preview.tsx turns any violation into a failed build.\n\nThe claim also undersold what happened. The tokens that were below AA were not\ngranted an exception — they were darkened. `--primary`, `--color-ink-faint`,\n`--destructive` and `--muted-foreground` each carry the measured ratio and the\nreason at their point of definition in src/index.css, which is where a reader\ncan actually check them.\n\nThis mattered more than an ordinary typo: the pointer was in the public README,\nso it sent anyone reading the repository on GitHub to a path that resolves to\nnothing, to learn about a mechanism that does not exist.","tree":{"sha":"4e05730f250850d3e44aa08247785521949610db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/4e05730f250850d3e44aa08247785521949610db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/28befc7913107b86f6e48b621813c4f45ebedfa7","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e05730f250850d3e44aa08247785521949610db\nparent c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787407922 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787407922 -0300\n\ndocs: correct the README''s account of the accessibility gate (#15)\n\nThe README pointed readers at `src/test/a11y-known-issues.ts` for the list of\nknown axe exceptions. That file does not exist, and neither does the concept:\nno story disables the a11y check, and `parameters.a11y.test = ''error''` in\n.storybook/preview.tsx turns any violation into a failed build.\n\nThe claim also undersold what happened. The tokens that were below AA were not\ngranted an exception — they were darkened. `--primary`, `--color-ink-faint`,\n`--destructive` and `--muted-foreground` each carry the measured ratio and the\nreason at their point of definition in src/index.css, which is where a reader\ncan actually check them.\n\nThis mattered more than an ordinary typo: the pointer was in the public README,\nso it sent anyone reading the repository on GitHub to a path that resolves to\nnothing, to learn about a mechanism that does not exist.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqia4yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABMwQACLauCB7VSOHIsKBXKJqp2/B\niW/+vPlot0O+TlIVDZx8DkfjsBFZQ+SzJizNgqwCES1WTqQPjpoMHcT1r9IPx3xo\nVQX43lWF6jdVMfwamMD4hFPnt4GTPXUgLFkZ5vhwYk7e5xD9z0R7lAJSDVadIq54\nPLALZPHm7uttiW1yvaUnYzRc5Ye5gYKT48cihhoP/MFARSqQ198My6MDeBiqFvVW\ndrI0fwFmFYsVKppK+id54PHGFFQOoda8o9Pea3E6NYw5r7LukX8XKjguCCb27ulE\n9MulIW67+eQcfio9cKoIJmXaS9b/luNPdabyPFgEhLByS5dpBhvrV3WPR/NThYnC\njWybadzyaMgBbJ5WjSAOW/tXcyo2J7FZiL106hewub1DVaaDiFHpaReVfyIjOgbg\nm2qNTFBGU97+NNWocv+GjzW5RuoWJDs/AqumtMRIXg3svZ+APRJPVHOQHugvphY1\nVbKuzEssKa3kzMZXb6wqxsrKOthXOZOh0qi/ZBJrNMT+S+EJmcdMP14IeyGsOfXG\nWQEJgJUXdI8rpxt2D/CmqpjYMuILwyTx/vKM/cUtiHc+MkLwsD3fWij0N6YMdqvg\nyUkKnv/yUQbXfmyDqXWD1xLuor3V/QGJKtysleSdvKDG8hDDI0p/M27pgIq4930Q\nGA2VIitItnwNdsxCTEXf\n=Cw7D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T14:12:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/28befc7913107b86f6e48b621813c4f45ebedfa7","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDI4YmVmYzc5MTMxMDdiODZmNmU0OGI2MjE4MTNjNGY0NWViZWRmYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27","sha":"c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27"}],"sha":"28befc7913107b86f6e48b621813c4f45ebedfa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/28befc7913107b86f6e48b621813c4f45ebedfa7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:22:23Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:22:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mf): expose the vaccine schedule as a Module Federation remote (#14)\n\n* refactor(embed): extract the public schedule contract into a shared module\n\n`GET /public/vaccine-schedule` is about to have a second consumer — a Module\nFederation remote — and its type, its fetch and its age formatting lived inside\nthe embed. Duplicating them would have put the wire contract in two places at\nonce, which is the one kind of drift nothing catches at build time.\n\nThe new module holds the no-dependencies line the embed depends on: no Zod, no\nhttpClient. That is also why the response guard is hand-written. It costs 130\nbytes gzip (2.52 -> 2.65 kB, measured on both variants) and buys validation the\nembed did not have — it used to cast the body and trust it, so a shape change on\nthe API side would have surfaced as an unreadable render rather than an error.\n\nMalformed rows are dropped, a missing `schedule` list throws. One bad row is not\na reason to deny a visitor the other twenty-seven; a missing envelope is, because\nan empty schedule is indistinguishable from a real answer.\n\n* feat(mf): expose the vaccine schedule as a Module Federation remote\n\nPublishes `/mf/remoteEntry.js` — a federated container exposing the PNI\nschedule as a React component a host mounts inside its own React tree, plus a\nprobe module a host uses to verify the React negotiation actually happened.\n\nThe schedule is the only screen here that can be federated to an anonymous\nvisitor: the other six features are scoped to a signed-in guardian and a\nspecific baby, while the PNI calendar is published policy behind the single\nunauthenticated endpoint the API exposes.\n\n`react` and `react-dom` are shared as singletons with `requiredVersion`.\nWithout `singleton` the container may satisfy the remote from its own copy and\nwill, silently — the widget still renders, and nothing fails until it touches\nhost-owned context or state, several layers from the cause. `runtimeProbe`\nreturns `useState` and `createElement` by reference rather than a version\nstring, because both sides report 19.2.x either way; reference equality is the\nonly assertion that can fail when sharing fails.\n\nThree build details are the way they are because the first run got them wrong:\n\n- `rollupOptions.input` names the container entry. Vite treats a root\n  index.html as the default entry, so the first build emitted the whole\n  application next to the remote — 139 chunks, 7 MB. Naming it: 23 files.\n- `dts.tsConfigPath` points at a new tsconfig.mf.json. The generator otherwise\n  extends the root tsconfig, which is solution-style and has no `jsx`, failing\n  TS17004 on every JSX line while the bundle built fine.\n- `disableRemote` drops remote-resolution from the runtime, since this\n  container only exposes. Measured: 18.86 -> 12.74 kB gzip.\n\nType generation cannot gate this build and the config says so rather than\nimplying otherwise. With a type error planted in an exposed module the build\nexits 0, prints nothing, and writes a declaration asserting `number` for a\nstring — the generator is a detached child process that reports after Vite has\nfinished, and emitDeclarationOnly emits regardless of diagnostics. `tsc -b`\nis the real gate, and now covers mf/.\n\nStyles are prefixed and injected once rather than shadow-scoped like the embed:\na shadow root would sever the component from the host''s React tree, which is\nthe reason to federate instead of embed. A test asserts the prefix discipline,\nsince restyling somebody else''s page fails silently and remotely.\n\nNot yet verified against a real host — that lands with the host page.\n\n* docs(mf): correct the version claim with what the live host actually reports\n\nThe probe''s rationale said both sides would report 19.2.x either way, so the\nversion proves nothing. Half right, and the wrong half was written before\nanything had been measured.\n\nVerified against the Next 16 host at samuelsantana.dev/micro-frontends: this\ncontainer is compiled against React 19.2.8 and reports 19.3.0-canary-*, the\nbuild Next vendors for its App Router. A remote announcing a version it does\nnot ship can only have been handed one — so here the version corroborates\nrather than proving nothing.\n\nThe underlying argument stands and is now stated properly: a *matching*\nversion is not evidence, because two copies of one version are still two\nobjects. Reference equality remains the assertion.\n\nAlso records what this implies about requiredVersion. Under strict semver a\nprerelease does not satisfy `^19.0.0`; the runtime accepted it. Had it\nrefused, the remote would have fallen back to its own React, rendered\ncorrectly, and failed only on contact with host-owned state — which is why the\nprobe runs on every load instead of once, by hand, at integration time.\n\n* fix(mf): let the immutable cache rule survive the general one\n\nVercel applies every matching `headers` rule and the last one wins, so the\ngeneral `/mf/(.*)` rule listed after `/mf/assets/(.*)` overwrote `immutable`\nwith `max-age=600`. Content-hashed chunks were being revalidated every ten\nminutes on a URL that can never change.\n\nCaught on the preview deployment, not by reading the config back — the config\nlooked correct, and nothing reports a cache header that is merely wrong.\nGeneral first, specific after.","tree":{"sha":"1de21408d69311acf72ec1eb0fa4f504e924bd8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/1de21408d69311acf72ec1eb0fa4f504e924bd8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27","verification":{"payload":"tree 1de21408d69311acf72ec1eb0fa4f504e924bd8a\nparent 1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787264543 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787264543 -0300\n\nfeat(mf): expose the vaccine schedule as a Module Federation remote (#14)\n\n* refactor(embed): extract the public schedule contract into a shared module\n\n`GET /public/vaccine-schedule` is about to have a second consumer — a Module\nFederation remote — and its type, its fetch and its age formatting lived inside\nthe embed. Duplicating them would have put the wire contract in two places at\nonce, which is the one kind of drift nothing catches at build time.\n\nThe new module holds the no-dependencies line the embed depends on: no Zod, no\nhttpClient. That is also why the response guard is hand-written. It costs 130\nbytes gzip (2.52 -> 2.65 kB, measured on both variants) and buys validation the\nembed did not have — it used to cast the body and trust it, so a shape change on\nthe API side would have surfaced as an unreadable render rather than an error.\n\nMalformed rows are dropped, a missing `schedule` list throws. One bad row is not\na reason to deny a visitor the other twenty-seven; a missing envelope is, because\nan empty schedule is indistinguishable from a real answer.\n\n* feat(mf): expose the vaccine schedule as a Module Federation remote\n\nPublishes `/mf/remoteEntry.js` — a federated container exposing the PNI\nschedule as a React component a host mounts inside its own React tree, plus a\nprobe module a host uses to verify the React negotiation actually happened.\n\nThe schedule is the only screen here that can be federated to an anonymous\nvisitor: the other six features are scoped to a signed-in guardian and a\nspecific baby, while the PNI calendar is published policy behind the single\nunauthenticated endpoint the API exposes.\n\n`react` and `react-dom` are shared as singletons with `requiredVersion`.\nWithout `singleton` the container may satisfy the remote from its own copy and\nwill, silently — the widget still renders, and nothing fails until it touches\nhost-owned context or state, several layers from the cause. `runtimeProbe`\nreturns `useState` and `createElement` by reference rather than a version\nstring, because both sides report 19.2.x either way; reference equality is the\nonly assertion that can fail when sharing fails.\n\nThree build details are the way they are because the first run got them wrong:\n\n- `rollupOptions.input` names the container entry. Vite treats a root\n  index.html as the default entry, so the first build emitted the whole\n  application next to the remote — 139 chunks, 7 MB. Naming it: 23 files.\n- `dts.tsConfigPath` points at a new tsconfig.mf.json. The generator otherwise\n  extends the root tsconfig, which is solution-style and has no `jsx`, failing\n  TS17004 on every JSX line while the bundle built fine.\n- `disableRemote` drops remote-resolution from the runtime, since this\n  container only exposes. Measured: 18.86 -> 12.74 kB gzip.\n\nType generation cannot gate this build and the config says so rather than\nimplying otherwise. With a type error planted in an exposed module the build\nexits 0, prints nothing, and writes a declaration asserting `number` for a\nstring — the generator is a detached child process that reports after Vite has\nfinished, and emitDeclarationOnly emits regardless of diagnostics. `tsc -b`\nis the real gate, and now covers mf/.\n\nStyles are prefixed and injected once rather than shadow-scoped like the embed:\na shadow root would sever the component from the host''s React tree, which is\nthe reason to federate instead of embed. A test asserts the prefix discipline,\nsince restyling somebody else''s page fails silently and remotely.\n\nNot yet verified against a real host — that lands with the host page.\n\n* docs(mf): correct the version claim with what the live host actually reports\n\nThe probe''s rationale said both sides would report 19.2.x either way, so the\nversion proves nothing. Half right, and the wrong half was written before\nanything had been measured.\n\nVerified against the Next 16 host at samuelsantana.dev/micro-frontends: this\ncontainer is compiled against React 19.2.8 and reports 19.3.0-canary-*, the\nbuild Next vendors for its App Router. A remote announcing a version it does\nnot ship can only have been handed one — so here the version corroborates\nrather than proving nothing.\n\nThe underlying argument stands and is now stated properly: a *matching*\nversion is not evidence, because two copies of one version are still two\nobjects. Reference equality remains the assertion.\n\nAlso records what this implies about requiredVersion. Under strict semver a\nprerelease does not satisfy `^19.0.0`; the runtime accepted it. Had it\nrefused, the remote would have fallen back to its own React, rendered\ncorrectly, and failed only on contact with host-owned state — which is why the\nprobe runs on every load instead of once, by hand, at integration time.\n\n* fix(mf): let the immutable cache rule survive the general one\n\nVercel applies every matching `headers` rule and the last one wins, so the\ngeneral `/mf/(.*)` rule listed after `/mf/assets/(.*)` overwrote `immutable`\nwith `max-age=600`. Content-hashed chunks were being revalidated every ten\nminutes on a URL that can never change.\n\nCaught on the preview deployment, not by reading the config back — the config\nlooked correct, and nothing reports a cache header that is merely wrong.\nGeneral first, specific after.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh34fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKvgQACtneY7I+q4fdg3YEM7HDO1Q\najNjMPwmJb4zaXGDiuXce2NSXP2WsVMYF1AoOhjAnem78ARZ1G0G+RIyYQ9OtwyG\nukEZjD+O/1GhAA7XrwtA6gTTFZdSvBbeeu0uEfFB0lS09GrapJbMlgYimRDbdHdD\nB0iv1Sv9LxquTl0G3IRbaMu4E57PQcSA1GQfojLHOkL/r6gP8aZ01ETiqTFEIsQj\nM0SvGc/CMUykNJzasagGGQJBx7ZeblmFyE47cgxTE+DYLXOlLHabA7jLPrfTBE07\ngZtmdXOsLZQoOP9rMxoLIVk90BIGZUtc6EobsvvTz7+yMt3c95kKip6+/VfvSp66\n8/mb1zVd7oojHJuzeqly3tT8i8Ch4h9stl4DC0MxhGnwxMnJjMgV/R4PRfVnXb2L\nhDJ1ge4qi4puXgf1DDeZUjH3ryHNZv0+ivOzjNoka9/3yAJyNRg6rtZ+7Zz0udGv\n+xY7NnJTMmW3N4ulMTboKeMCxDHE04eY4udc5hDFzZBz1EESdOOA4EpkMkKggTlE\nvRcJMKQRKB03Kf720aG9JVXZreTyQeTwZ4UnHVVQSIzFHPlLYWpXvb9BwsZgeUG7\nUomjC9PRj4eJ6XOt0H1B3vjrwG1uzlwqhDTT9sgqsYEnYn/iuDDwSNwAHfbZTlyp\nBHmVcUbFLMkSU3kEDOHE\n=iaTR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T22:22:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGM5ZGJmOGNkMDkyZDhiNmRkMzg4YTljZmM1ZmM3MjY2YzI1YjRkMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3","sha":"1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3"}],"sha":"c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/c9dbf8cd092d8b6dd388a9cfc5fc7266c25b4d27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T12:17:12Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T12:17:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(observability): collect Web Vitals from production (#13)\n\nSentry.init set tracesSampleRate: 0.1 but registered no integrations, and\nbrowserTracingIntegration is not part of getDefaultIntegrations(). The SDK\ntherefore produced no spans at all: errors kept arriving, which is exactly\nwhat made the setup look complete. No Web Vital was ever recorded.\n\nRegistering the integration turns LCP, CLS, INP, TTFB and FCP into\nmeasurements on the pageload span. Sampling goes to 1.0 because at 0.1 a\nwhole day of portfolio-scale traffic can yield no sampled pageload, which\nreads as \"no data\" rather than \"no traffic\".\n\ntracePropagationTargets is pinned to same-origin. photoUrl and avatarUrl\naccept any host by design, so an unset list would attach trace headers to\nwhatever third party a user pasted in.\n\nThe entry chunk grows 19 kB gzip (119 -> 138 kB, measured), on the critical\npath, which worsens the LCP being reported. Accepted and recorded at the\npoint of use: an unmeasured LCP cannot be improved.\n\nThe tests assert the wiring rather than the values, since the failure mode\nhere is a silent absence, not a wrong number.","tree":{"sha":"2fc1314ab0e4e8b53b1a4cf573e560ddb414bcd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/2fc1314ab0e4e8b53b1a4cf573e560ddb414bcd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 2fc1314ab0e4e8b53b1a4cf573e560ddb414bcd6\nparent abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787228232 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787228232 -0300\n\nfeat(observability): collect Web Vitals from production (#13)\n\nSentry.init set tracesSampleRate: 0.1 but registered no integrations, and\nbrowserTracingIntegration is not part of getDefaultIntegrations(). The SDK\ntherefore produced no spans at all: errors kept arriving, which is exactly\nwhat made the setup look complete. No Web Vital was ever recorded.\n\nRegistering the integration turns LCP, CLS, INP, TTFB and FCP into\nmeasurements on the pageload span. Sampling goes to 1.0 because at 0.1 a\nwhole day of portfolio-scale traffic can yield no sampled pageload, which\nreads as \"no data\" rather than \"no traffic\".\n\ntracePropagationTargets is pinned to same-origin. photoUrl and avatarUrl\naccept any host by design, so an unset list would attach trace headers to\nwhatever third party a user pasted in.\n\nThe entry chunk grows 19 kB gzip (119 -> 138 kB, measured), on the critical\npath, which worsens the LCP being reported. Accepted and recorded at the\npoint of use: an unmeasured LCP cannot be improved.\n\nThe tests assert the wiring rather than the values, since the failure mode\nhere is a silent absence, not a wrong number.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhvBICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhHAQAEliyL3ZJX5YK0xESRPtlAR1\nYLxV4oGvpZggsTSrEZHV0t81RjD5gTYQg0+Q+E8sIRN2QQ/2ET3DmOfeSp6mKUrs\nSsezRls2mY7iy2YWHWmYZRDFh2UxDdUhnE9xGlxzJteV9xGDiaKLKcduNm+HofzM\n1n62yNelWxa5TnRFQ3gLOy8CkYcf5hZ+T410uZZSl6gN6+LsZgPXAISpYqlSElQQ\nB3L0dbGe4Vhntt7YWLBzjP36tBLjH4uIriGquSHQsDN9Fp2LbxP7Q5hDCKjFQKbd\nG9aFL5B+G/jmu2z4KDEfvnJ/FQp8TozxVDPcLdDvHfKlA1Tx5VspXihdboXKbymK\nYi4EdQlC7Un4kTPro1KyYJrUpcuxNTi7BRemMT9Fh4Qn3k9LPyrpKFtshQkk4Nn5\nsYjraUBvNNzZYb5VkuLqJk99g1bYh3HecaUd/D9Ebe8FJuDE0anKorQlCexXd7ds\nwPnpSRk0cRMXOlfzCS+EVvPy7CKFtEKNPRMsGdqnr+6EgUtmP0AHBIDiC2Z15fUT\nnZNWtb6FPibvZ2CIuDfR41qzO7MUZhHkWo/73NgHbNIw2qA2pjnq2TcbXMuVHVSX\nXjyjcaQeoYzDOWHk4i75qb0WVSLbbZoj8gs+NqfISymdm00cdzQpsmVpDWcsQGp0\nUsVcIWXYUmnHBpModQz7\n=7YXB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T12:17:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKDFkZDY4MThhMjM1ZGRjMDNhZjg0NWY0MTkzMzVkZGJjNTMyNDAyZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59","sha":"abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59"}],"sha":"1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/1dd6818a235ddc03af845f419335ddbc532402d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T00:27:27Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T00:27:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(embed): add an embeddable vaccine schedule widget (#12)\n\nAn embeddable widget showing the public PNI schedule, in two distribution\nvariants over one implementation: a script tag that renders a custom element\ninto the host''s DOM, and an iframe served from this origin.\n\nStyle isolation is identical in both — a shadow root with `all: initial`, so the\nhost''s CSS cannot reach in and the widget''s cannot leak out. What differs is\nJavaScript isolation, and that is the whole choice: the script tag integrates\nwith the host''s layout but runs on the host''s origin with access to its DOM; the\niframe shares nothing but must be told its own height, because a host cannot\nmeasure inside a cross-origin frame. That is why a resize message exists at all.\n\nThe message contract is versioned from this first commit. An embed is the one\nartifact whose consumers cannot be redeployed — the tag lives in someone else''s\nHTML — so a host that integrated version 1 keeps version 1''s expectations\nforever. Every message also carries `source`, because a host''s message handler\nreceives analytics, chat widgets and devtools on the same channel.\n\nThe widget never navigates the host. Activating the link emits `navigate` and\ndoes nothing else; a widget that can move the page it sits in is a widget nobody\npastes into their site.\n\nNeither bundle pulls in React, Tailwind or the router: 2.5 kB gzip, because every\ndependency here is one the host inherits without being asked.\n\nTwo build configs rather than one, because IIFE takes exactly one entry and the\nhost needs a plain `<script src>` that survives a CMS stripping attributes.\n\nvercel.json gains a negative lookahead. X-Frame-Options has no per-origin value,\nonly DENY or SAMEORIGIN, so an embeddable page cannot override it — it can only\nbe excluded from it. `frame-ancestors *` on /embed/ is what expresses \"anyone\",\nand it is safe because the widget shows public policy data and holds no session.\nThe embed is cached for ten minutes, not a year: its filename is stable by\nnecessity, so an immutable cache would make a fix unshippable.\n\nAlso fixes something this change exposed: tsconfig.app.json included only src and\n.storybook, so nothing outside them was ever typechecked.","tree":{"sha":"8e16cd356c27d01e482bbed24d4dba21e990b79e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/trees/8e16cd356c27d01e482bbed24d4dba21e990b79e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/git/commits/abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e16cd356c27d01e482bbed24d4dba21e990b79e\nparent b7ec031ed8908974c39a5a9bfc708fef896f7b89\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787185647 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787185647 -0300\n\nfeat(embed): add an embeddable vaccine schedule widget (#12)\n\nAn embeddable widget showing the public PNI schedule, in two distribution\nvariants over one implementation: a script tag that renders a custom element\ninto the host''s DOM, and an iframe served from this origin.\n\nStyle isolation is identical in both — a shadow root with `all: initial`, so the\nhost''s CSS cannot reach in and the widget''s cannot leak out. What differs is\nJavaScript isolation, and that is the whole choice: the script tag integrates\nwith the host''s layout but runs on the host''s origin with access to its DOM; the\niframe shares nothing but must be told its own height, because a host cannot\nmeasure inside a cross-origin frame. That is why a resize message exists at all.\n\nThe message contract is versioned from this first commit. An embed is the one\nartifact whose consumers cannot be redeployed — the tag lives in someone else''s\nHTML — so a host that integrated version 1 keeps version 1''s expectations\nforever. Every message also carries `source`, because a host''s message handler\nreceives analytics, chat widgets and devtools on the same channel.\n\nThe widget never navigates the host. Activating the link emits `navigate` and\ndoes nothing else; a widget that can move the page it sits in is a widget nobody\npastes into their site.\n\nNeither bundle pulls in React, Tailwind or the router: 2.5 kB gzip, because every\ndependency here is one the host inherits without being asked.\n\nTwo build configs rather than one, because IIFE takes exactly one entry and the\nhost needs a plain `<script src>` that survives a CMS stripping attributes.\n\nvercel.json gains a negative lookahead. X-Frame-Options has no per-origin value,\nonly DENY or SAMEORIGIN, so an embeddable page cannot override it — it can only\nbe excluded from it. `frame-ancestors *` on /embed/ is what expresses \"anyone\",\nand it is safe because the widget shows public policy data and holds no session.\nThe embed is cached for ten minutes, not a year: its filename is stable by\nnecessity, so an immutable cache would make a fix unshippable.\n\nAlso fixes something this change exposed: tsconfig.app.json included only src and\n.storybook, so nothing outside them was ever typechecked.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhknvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASIAQAJ9W1JN5UxPFtJO+qd5ZqcLF\nmiquP743NFgn2MLJMf3Kk/zF+Hg4WJEAQYuVImmbzkQTugPSlMMtmqL51CYjJCb5\nJHhus2vtaGeNqM57n33TK5IMvRhVM+CSMaoJ9nJBmXzZKnBXuOjccrq2eCMP/Vb2\ntgVpXmwnIcKyPjXwgKwVCPQMdLGoaa2t3oAdpvCqbHcdlg6NMlb0e9QHj93tvPP8\nKIlHS3CyNuJBmNJ3OjLEI1y5yX9VpGfYfBfmjVFnGH7tetdrWVbtbJCnhn3xvbiA\nQVVSg1/i9VFBaOFiNe7BIOrfdnsTuBmvOGUmlmIYOkEKIfulk4pn/njZI1e9tDgm\nKvpPpLM2Ncm/NTU8zbwwOGxtKiobBdmT2UhHikOiXZ6v46kSX7fkeDrI4Zz5OfCa\nO7uPPAF21HGzPXtzp8yaEJ+4PQ3vNcGLG/CI/xcgotaZmem/J5mAczpWybECwXHJ\nMW9GnaNUCAyWa8cJNtVxFEmPe9t6Fm0GdORi7Ym/athLQ9RzAz7F1hZiqiHq5rts\n4DIF8l4/AIwDRpdwo0iCNtCMDWSfrVLYNDC+WmklNbR8TICyT04/jw3ARWmro3J7\nAw4pnVY313fbD+7gohoWeoiGCHMM4rUubq0r1iGBuKsyKg8SpmF4DdTjuripgonH\nas3cuiIc73kzwhqDAqHh\n=PYyq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T00:27:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59","node_id":"C_kwDOTkG-FdoAKGFiZWM1NWQ3NjIxZjRmZmJiYjVhZmQ4ODkxMzRhMTYxMGM0ZTFlNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commit/b7ec031ed8908974c39a5a9bfc708fef896f7b89","sha":"b7ec031ed8908974c39a5a9bfc708fef896f7b89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/cygnus/commits/b7ec031ed8908974c39a5a9bfc708fef896f7b89"}],"sha":"abec55d7621f4ffbbb5afd889134a1610c4e1e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sa