rs/LuongCongThanh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LuongCongThanh","id":66105517,"login":"LuongCongThanh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MTA1NTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LuongCongThanh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LuongCongThanh/fe-ecommerce-nike-style/commits/191ec40b29da8b0ceb199b856a39394649f98c29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T12:46:22Z","email":"66105517+LuongCongThanh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Luong Cong Thanh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T12:46:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(storefront): wire eslint config to @repo/eslint-config (#41)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Wired `apps/storefront/eslint.config.mjs` to consume\n`@repo/eslint-config/next` instead of duplicating the same\n`nextVitals`/TypeScript-strict spreads inline (tsconfig wiring already\nmerged in #40; this finishes ESLint wiring for the same branch).\n- Fixed two bugs in `packages/eslint-config` surfaced while wiring it\nup: `base.js` hardcoded `tsconfigRootDir` to its own folder instead of\nthe caller''s (now a factory function), and `next.js` re-registered\nplugins (`react`/`react-hooks`/`jsx-a11y`) that\n`eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals` already registers, which threw\n`Cannot redefine plugin`.\n- Removed the shared package''s hardcoded\n`feature-public`/`feature-private` boundaries model — it doesn''t match\nstorefront''s real route-group folder structure and would false-positive\n`boundaries/no-unknown` on nearly every file. Recorded this as Decision\n#83 in the decision log, with `FE-ARCHITECTURE.md`/`FE-EXECUTION.md`\nupdated to match (same precedent as Decision #82: fix docs to match the\napp that''s actually running). Boundaries enforcement is now app-owned;\nstorefront already has its own correct model in its `eslint.config.mjs`.\n\nNote for review against #4''s acceptance criteria: that issue''s checklist\nfor `packages/eslint-config` lists `eslint-plugin-boundaries` as\nrequired content. This PR removes it from the shared package for the\nreason above — see Decision #83 for the full rationale.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pnpm lint` — clean across all 6 workspace packages\n- [x] `pnpm typecheck` — clean across all 6 workspace packages\n- [x] `pnpm test` — 177 tests passing (storefront)\n- [x] Verified `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals`''s actual plugin\nregistrations directly (node script) before fixing the \"Cannot redefine\nplugin\" bug\n- [x] Ran `/review` (standards + spec axes) against the first commit and\nfixed the two real findings it surfaced\n\n## Related\n\nRefs #4\n\n---\n\n- [x] No AI/assistant attribution (e.g. `Co-Authored-By: Claude ...`) in\nthis PR''s commit messages or description.","tree":{"sha":"736d5d43bb5c1d9617002ec49b48a72f00e5cae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LuongCongThanh/fe-ecommerce-nike-style/git/trees/736d5d43bb5c1d9617002ec49b48a72f00e5cae1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LuongCongThanh/fe-ecommerce-nike-style/git/commits/191ec40b29da8b0ceb199b856a39394649f98c29","verification":{"payload":"tree 736d5d43bb5c1d9617002ec49b48a72f00e5cae1\nparent 5ac358cd63a2cf69d9c148a58cb51cd95a62c876\nauthor Luong Cong Thanh <66105517+LuongCongThanh@users.noreply.github.com> 1785761182 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785761182 +0700\n\nchore(storefront): wire eslint config to @repo/eslint-config (#41)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Wired `apps/storefront/eslint.config.mjs` to consume\n`@repo/eslint-config/next` instead of duplicating the same\n`nextVitals`/TypeScript-strict spreads inline (tsconfig wiring already\nmerged in #40; this finishes ESLint wiring for the same branch).\n- Fixed two bugs in `packages/eslint-config` surfaced while wiring it\nup: `base.js` hardcoded `tsconfigRootDir` to its own folder instead of\nthe caller''s (now a factory function), and `next.js` re-registered\nplugins (`react`/`react-hooks`/`jsx-a11y`) that\n`eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals` already registers, which threw\n`Cannot redefine plugin`.\n- Removed the shared package''s hardcoded\n`feature-public`/`feature-private` boundaries model — it doesn''t match\nstorefront''s real route-group folder structure and would false-positive\n`boundaries/no-unknown` on nearly every file. Recorded this as Decision\n#83 in the decision log, with `FE-ARCHITECTURE.md`/`FE-EXECUTION.md`\nupdated to match (same precedent as Decision #82: fix docs to match the\napp that''s actually running). Boundaries enforcement is now app-owned;\nstorefront already has its own correct model in its `eslint.config.mjs`.\n\nNote for review against #4''s acceptance criteria: that issue''s checklist\nfor `packages/eslint-config` lists `eslint-plugin-boundaries` as\nrequired content. This PR removes it from the shared package for the\nreason above — see Decision #83 for the full rationale.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pnpm lint` — clean across all 6 workspace packages\n- [x] `pnpm typecheck` — clean across all 6 workspace packages\n- [x] `pnpm test` — 177 tests passing (storefront)\n- [x] Verified `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals`''s actual plugin\nregistrations directly (node script) before fixing the \"Cannot redefine\nplugin\" bug\n- [x] Ran `/review` (standards + spec axes) against the first commit and\nfixed the two real findings it surfaced\n\n## Related\n\nRefs #4\n\n---\n\n- [x] No AI/assistant attribution (e.g. `Co-Authored-By: Claude ...`) in\nthis PR''s commit messages or description.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcI2eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB88QAClUxuR5HOzTE/MPAe/E9AR1\n7kuo5TZT/1X810mTIV8siJRgrFA4GDVb9uci13tIkOfbbe+NUfr5gVyGjS8O0y2u\nwRcDJf7VLmpdrYQYLksYTxoIHIbohDczLcwn+igYS5wCRJEm+gCUL/vR4oOdHFNc\nL/Fd6MGhg9t8kutxU77Yd6FZE1BvOvnJOJ1rvpt2QqAdNDaauXJNTj5D3Z0FT0Pv\nMqTHhhCp4tsg7klP4QZi048900DTgzl8eDAZzTZ6J/Qc0UuPe+UyJQEmlaqqjlE9\nbkdk8njqHq6rD+ly1UcWJto61ML/L04eEY+jAMlvskgkjF5oU/1oV9ihgob+LuB9\nJfp0yglINlnfpbz4FrkjJtgu09wtslloZol/fZzdAMcV8sWRqy2OPS3LqTQNKVom\noRUXOtrFXTslUPWNr6Q88lPd2+lDkSeYtVOqvUZdMkT79CF3YbzD5rE4MTaGSGZO\nrgCAZEAWs5quI8cOyWqaUIKjca58C5xCRkDRQTByT5QpdMJL+5jtE2jZc3tOsXep\n51XCp4N5bKDhbG2BSR+R41HTEBZEHfuPlJ2OpfZMRSe10Jrq057AEWm4RpAyDJlR\n/Lbgk7jLh2y4GSQkFtkf8P9n3zIFF0JVhFeQMJ7V77VlR9NfB6kx9Po6Kcc5IxAv\njZWfs5a9PQrEXoDkRP5R\n=DsRj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T12:46:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"pub