b.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10","sha":"54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10"}],"sha":"82045687b3b493a1e2b861f65b46a2c0cac6634e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/82045687b3b493a1e2b861f65b46a2c0cac6634e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5040?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valthon","id":5040,"login":"valthon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T01:56:01Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T01:56:01Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"message":"Emit structured island-render diagnostics\n\nIsland failures already carry useful component and route context, but\nworker logs bypass the NDJSON stream consumed by unattended tooling.\nEmit stable codes for SSR, Scripty props, missing sidecars and remaining\nisland-pass failures through the existing locked diagnostic writer.\n\nKeep the wire schema fixed: file identifies the content page, component\nand route details stay in the message, and line/column remain null rather\nthan misattributing a component stack to a page. Format complete messages\nwith explicit allocation ownership so long JavaScript traces survive.\nDisk failure policy and memory placeholders are unchanged.\n\nCarry the render error''s name in the report the island pass hands back.\nThe sink takes a report for every error the renderer returns, not only a\ncomponent that threw, and the others leave the sidecar''s message empty\nand its stack null -- so formatting the message alone emitted a record\nwhose entire payload was a colon and \"(no stack)\", losing the one datum\nthat separates a component throwing from the sidecar dying. Fall back to\nthe name only when there is no JavaScript message, leaving the common\npath byte-identical in both modes.\n\nName both island spellings in the missing-sidecar message. The fast-path\nscan above that branch accepts <island> and <z-island> alike and does not\nrecord which one matched, so a content author who wrote the <z-island>\nalias inside an =html fence was told about an element they never used.\n\nText-mode output therefore changes in exactly those two places, and only\nthere; the docs say so rather than claiming it is untouched.\n\nThe regressions run the real sidecar rather than a stub: concurrent\nfailing pages, an oversized stack, prop errors, invalid markup, an absent\nsidecar, a corrupted channel, and a sidecar that exits mid-build. That\nlast one uses eight pages on purpose -- only one worker observes the\nclosed pipe directly, so a single-page fixture cannot see whether the\nother seven name the failure or their own writer''s state.\n\nThe new pass test is contract 4 and joins the allowlist with its measured\ncause: it leaks eight allocations under the raw testing allocator, five\nfrom the rewrite pass and three from resolveToJson, none from ziggy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019gqeXs2Znr5VyQrKat7M6j","tree":{"sha":"7890eb11310395031ed3412108616b82eec57e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/trees/7890eb11310395031ed3412108616b82eec57e57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/commits/54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5040?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valthon","id":5040,"login":"valthon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10","node_id":"C_kwDOTkRGT9oAKDU0ZWEzNzcxZDdkY2FhZDI3MmE4Mjg3M2EwZWFhMzBhMzA4OGNkMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/9ea17b9885e668309a655251821fb62872d03e5d","sha":"9ea17b9885e668309a655251821fb62872d03e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/9ea17b9885e668309a655251821fb62872d03e5d"}],"sha":"54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/54ea3771d7dcaad272a82873a0eaa30a3088cd10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5040?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valthon","id":5040,"login":"valthon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/9ea17b9885e668309a655251821fb62872d03e5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T01:56:01Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T01:56:01Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"message":"Name sidecar transport failures accurately\n\nEvery failure of the Zig-to-Bun render protocol was reported under the\nname of whatever machinery noticed it, not the name of what broke. A\nsubprocess that exited surfaced as EndOfStream on the one worker that\nhappened to be reading, and as a bare WriteFailed on every worker that\nthen wrote into a pipe with no reader -- std.Io.Writer collapses EPIPE to\nthat and keeps the real cause in the writer''s err field. A response line\nthat was not a protocol frame surfaced as std.json''s own SyntaxError,\nwhich reads as a syntax error in the author''s component and sends them to\ndebug a file that is fine.\n\nThese names were an internal detail while they only reached a log line.\nThey stop being one in the following commit, which puts the error name of\na failed island render into a structured diagnostic record: a build\nconsumer reads it, and so does the author. Fix the names first, so that\nchange has something true to report.\n\nMap a closed pipe to SidecarExited on both sides of it, recovering the\ncause from the writer rather than reporting its buffered state. Split a\nfailed response line by whether it is a protocol frame, not by whether it\nis JSON: console.log(JSON.stringify(x)) is the usual way island code\ncorrupts this channel and it emits perfectly valid JSON, so the test is\nthat the line is an object carrying the request id, which is already the\nprotocol''s only integrity check. A line that is not a frame is a corrupt\nchannel (SidecarBadResponse); a frame whose field types do not match\ncame from the author''s own module, which describe puts on the wire\nverbatim, and says so (SidecarBadResponseShape).\n\nThe classifier re-parses only on the failure path, so the success path is\nuntouched. It takes the RenderArena rather than an Allocator because the\nthrowaway value tree it builds is arena-scoped by NO_SLOP.md''s contract 4.\n\nThe regression covers the direction that is easy to get backwards: an spa\nexport whose field has an unexpected type must be reported against the\nmodule, and must not name a corrupt channel. Its counterpart, that a\ngenuinely corrupt channel still does, arrives with the diagnostics tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019gqeXs2Znr5VyQrKat7M6j","tree":{"sha":"2eb1a54f7cbce6e7feecfe3d99001dafd4960a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/trees/2eb1a54f7cbce6e7feecfe3d99001dafd4960a8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/commits/9ea17b9885e668309a655251821fb62872d03e5d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_ur