l":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/72239de16411358ac43e4013e8fd05fa58c1d97a","node_id":"C_kwDOTkRGT9oAKDcyMjM5ZGUxNjQxMTM1OGFjNDNlNDAxM2U4ZmQwNWZhNThjMWQ5N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/4c879b7661d8a294c9924a641c536cb2df0f1837","sha":"4c879b7661d8a294c9924a641c536cb2df0f1837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/4c879b7661d8a294c9924a641c536cb2df0f1837"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/d07e9bfb53f14fc2b69e0be2455dc39d05710cb6","sha":"d07e9bfb53f14fc2b69e0be2455dc39d05710cb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/d07e9bfb53f14fc2b69e0be2455dc39d05710cb6"}],"sha":"72239de16411358ac43e4013e8fd05fa58c1d97a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/72239de16411358ac43e4013e8fd05fa58c1d97a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5040?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valthon","id":5040,"login":"valthon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/d07e9bfb53f14fc2b69e0be2455dc39d05710cb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T23:21:46Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T23:21:46Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"message":"Prune image caches under an exclusive build lock\n\nDerived variants and abandoned encoder temporaries accumulate forever.\nAdd cache-prune with a required encoded-byte budget, a non-destructive\npreview by default, and explicit --apply. Evict oldest variants after\norphan temporaries, preserving unknown files, links and subdirectories.\n\nHold a persistent exclusive cache lock through derive/install jobs.\nBuilds report lock waits and reuse completed entries; pruners fail\npromptly if busy. Release ownership at the worker barrier.\nReject symlinked cache components and never unlink the lock inode.\nOlder binaries do not use this protocol and must be stopped first.\n\nAn encoder may outlive a killed parent. Use random per-build nonces in\ncompact temporary names so orphan output cannot collide with later\nbuilds, without consuming long source filenames'' NAME_MAX headroom.\nRecognize both legacy and current temporary names during cleanup.\n\nCover byte budgets, dry-run/apply, injected allocation failures, live\nencoder contention, concurrent builds, long filenames and regeneration.\nRemoving the build lock makes the contention regression fail. Cleanup\nis explicit and mtime-based, not LRU. Tolerate entries disappearing\nbetween iteration, stat and deletion; propagate other I/O failures.","tree":{"sha":"dba38d5a6358de67011e5e5e29e21b616fa10259","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/trees/dba38d5a6358de67011e5e5e29e21b616fa10259"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/commits/d07e9bfb53f14fc2b69e0be2455dc39d05710cb6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.