ubusercontent.com/u/5040?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valthon","id":5040,"login":"valthon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/commits/29544130fca66889b91250e41ab116e942eafe74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T21:09:52Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T21:21:55Z","email":"valthon@gmail.com","name":"valthon"},"message":"Reject both quote kinds, and free through the failing allocator\n\nTwo items from the PR #188 review, plus the prose they invalidated:\n\n- `validCustomChoice` rejected `\"` and whitespace while its error message\n  promised \"no quotes\". The single quote is now rejected too: the rule\n  must be at least as strict as its own description. Not a safety fix --\n  the emitters escape correctly either way -- and nothing becomes\n  unexpressible, since a percent-encoded `%27` round-trips to the same\n  URL. The shape test gains the single-quote case, and the doc, its\n  skill mirror and the function''s own comment now state the rule the\n  validator enforces instead of the narrower one it used to.\n- The `contentClaims` FailingAllocator sweep deinit''d through\n  `std.testing.allocator` instead of the failing wrapper that allocated.\n  The wrapped allocator accepts those frees, so nothing catches the\n  mismatch today; freeing through the interface that allocated is\n  correct hygiene, not a pinned behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ceqUz8nDB4ouT3zjGBDR4","tree":{"sha":"5f3f0ff5dae857facc8fa4f1a57e75c5f6406410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/trees/5f3f0ff5dae857facc8fa4f1a57e75c5f6406410"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valthon/zigapagos/git/commits/29544130fca66889b91250e41ab116e942eafe74","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5040?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/valthon","id":5040,"login":"valthon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valthon","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/29544130fca66889b91250e41ab116e942eafe74","node_id":"C_kwDOTkRGT9oAKDI5NTQ0MTMwZmNhNjY4ODliOTEyNTBlNDFhYjExNmU5NDJlYWZlNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/commit/5b8ccd1bf1ef94636ccc4661b77cfcee02093ad8","sha":"5b8ccd1bf1ef94636ccc4661b77cfcee02093ad8